window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2501,"title":"Chapter 2501: Chapter 2453: Men Are All Hideous, Whereas Women Are All Beautiful","paragraphs":["Annoyed by the woman’s request, Zu An had decided to summon Mo Xi.","It had been a long time since Mo Xi last came out. The first thing she did was to demand Ki Fruits from Zu An, but she suddenly froze up when she saw the beautiful woman opposite her. As the two of them stared at each other, Mo Xi’s empty eyes suddenly flickered. She felt as if a spark of flame had ignited inside her, though Zu An didn’t notice a thing at all.","The beautiful woman initially had a playful smile sitting on her lips. She thought that even if the human was speaking the truth, their resemblance could only go this far. To her astonishment, the other party looked just about identical to her. To be fair, there were differences in their appearances, but the overall feeling they gave off was similar. Even their clothes and accessories looked as if they were carved out of the same mold.","“Holy shit!”","The six men were startled by this shocking sight. They first looked at Mo Xi, followed by the princess, and one of them exclaimed, “My grandmother’s arse! They're identical!”","“Are you saying they're identical to your grandmother’s arse?”","“I don’t talk with fools.”","“You looking for a fight?”","...","Two of them began arguing.","The other four men's gazes darted back and forth between the two ladies.","“My princess, she truly resembles you.”","“Yeah. She looks a bit prettier than you.”","Black streaks crossed the beautiful woman’s face. “Shut your mouth if you have nothing better to say!”","But even she had to admit that the woman was more seductive than her in terms of feminine charm. That infuriated her. Hmph, beauty is only skin deep. I dare you to fight me! There’s no way I’d lose to the likes of that woman!","Seeing that he had convinced them, Zu An recalled Mo Xi back into his void space. Perhaps he was overthinking it, but for a brief moment there, he sensed Mo Xi’s reluctance. Still, he didn’t have the energy to think deeper into it.","He turned to the beautiful woman and asked, “Can you answer my question now?”","“Who is that woman? She resembles me a lot,” the beautiful woman said, still shaken up by her encounter with Mo Xi.","One of the men grinned. “She’s prettier than you.”","“Shut up!” The beautiful woman’s eyelids twitched. She had always been proud of her appearance, which won her the title of her race’s number one beauty. She hadn't thought she would lose in the field of beauty. That frustrated her greatly.","I should never have asked in the first place.","Zu An grimly asked, “Shouldn’t you answer my question first? Or do you not plan to keep your promise?”","The beautiful woman huffed in anger, “Don’t talk nonsense. We of the Asura race always keep our promises. We aren’t like you cunning humans.”","“Asura race?” Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected them to be from the legendary Asura race. He first looked at the beautiful woman, followed by the other hideous men, and realization dawned on him.","There were legends that the Asuras were a warring race who often fought with the gods. Asura men were hideous, but Asura women were so beautiful that even gods coveted them. There were also stories that their strength could be determined by how many arms they had. No wonder they had so many arms.","Zu An had never expected to meet members of the legendary Asura race in person. Why would they appear in the underworld?","“I am the current Asura King’s little sister, which is why they address me as princess. I am Ni Huang. Are you satisfied now?” the beautiful princess introduced herself to Zu An.","“What are your ties with the Shaman race? I overheard your conversation, and it sounds like you have a grudge with them?” Zu An asked curiously. The Asura race in the legends had fought with the gods, so why would their rivals suddenly become the Shaman race?","“How rude. I have just introduced myself, so shouldn’t you do the same too?” Princess Ni Huang snorted.","Zu An was stunned.","He didn’t want to reveal his true identity in this time period, but this Asura lady would surely blow up if he concealed his identity the way he had with the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess. They hadn't interacted much yet, but he already had a grasp of her temper. So, he intended to fake an identity, but it had to be a reasonable one.","A thought suddenly surfaced in his mind, and he said, “I am the Necropolis Emperor.”","He assessed their reactions in an attempt to gather some information.","The others were stunned. Princess Ni Huang sneered, “Your name is Necropolis? What a weird name. You are arrogant to proclaim yourself an emperor though.”","Her words confirmed that the Necropolis Emperor didn’t exist in this world, causing Zu An to think, How bizarre.","“Answer my question. Who is that woman to you?” Princess Ni Huang asked, intrigued. “You were ordering her around. Is she your slave?”","She couldn’t help but wonder if he had done anything weird to that woman who looked just like her. Isn’t that almost like me being violated? The thought of that made her uncomfortable.","“Slave?” Zu An frowned. He had no idea why she would think that. “No, she’s my comrade, my companion, and my friend. She is no slave.”","Those descriptors brought a subtle smile to the sleeping Mo Xi’s face. The sleeping Daji revealed a faint smile too.","“Why did she suddenly appear and vanish? It’s almost as if she’s your summon.” Princess Ni Huang frowned. The earlier sight had been a huge shock to her.","“I can summon her because I signed a special contract with her. Rest assured, we are in an equal relationship. There’s nothing else going on,” Zu An replied.","Princess Ni Huang’s face reddened. She felt embarrassed that the other party had seen through her thoughts.","“You haven’t answered my question yet. What’s your relationship with the Shaman races? Why did you... emerge from the Eye of the Ocean?” Zu An asked as he looked at the abyss.","“This involves some confidential information. We can’t share it with you, but our Asura race believes in the sanctity of battle. Before deciding whether to answer your question, let me see if you are qualified to call yourself an emperor.” Princess Ni Huang revealed a charming smile as she drew a spear and thrust it toward Zu An."]},{"number":2502,"title":"Chapter 2502: Chapter 2454: I Like You","paragraphs":["Zu An was put in a tough spot, but the other party’s spear thrust was so fast that he had no choice but to retaliate.","Given the other party’s high standing, he didn’t employ the Tranquility Bell. Judging from the Asura race’s reaction, it was humiliating to them if they failed to breach the bell, and they would even be mocked by their comrades. The Asura race only respected the strong, after all.","It was one thing for the Asura man to be mocked, but Princess Ni Huang was in a lofty position. It'd likely be hard for them to work together if he accidentally humiliated her.","Zu An weighed the pros and cons in the blink of an eye. With a flick of his finger, he thrust the other party’s spear tip aside.","Princess Ni Huang’s eyes gleamed in admiration. “Your skills are not bad.”","Her spear thrust was just a polite probe; she hadn’t used her full strength. For that reason, she wasn’t too angry at having her spear flicked aside by a finger.","She then twisted her spear and flung it toward Zu An’s waist in a sweeping motion.","Zu An was awed by her excellent skills with the spear. The princess had transcended the traditional forms of spearmanship to reach a level of free-flowing moves. Be it a spear, a pole, or her own body, to her, anything could become a spear.","The strike rushed at Zu An with a thunderous roar, distorting even space itself. Even a dragon would have its back smashed if that attack landed. On top of that, her timing was impeccable; she made sure Zu An had no space to dodge. No matter where he escaped, she could continue raining down a barrage of blows on him.","Zu An saw through her and didn’t bother dodging to the side. Instead, he flickered behind her and dodged the devastating attack at the last moment. His hand struck forward to grab her shoulder. All he had to do was to strike her shoulder acupoint, and the battle would be over.","Princess Ni Huang was taken aback by his instantaneous movement, but even so, she still reacted quickly and performed a backward kick to strike his vitals.","Zu An felt a chill between his legs, which left him with no choice but to give up on his attack and retreat. He was getting increasingly impressed with this woman. She's honed her skills to the peak. Anything can be a spear to her.","Little did he know she wasn’t done yet. The princess brought her spear above her head and thrust it against Zu An. Her attack was so swift, precise, and unexpected that it shocked Zu An despite his formidable cultivation.","This attack was calculated. He couldn’t dodge to the sides, and if he chose to retreat, he would be immediately met with a barrage of follow-up attacks. It would be as good as handing over the tempo of the battle into the other party’s hands.","So, Zu An chose to leap upward instead.","But Princess Ni Huang had predicted his countermeasure. Her earlier backward kick happened to strike her spear tip, causing the attack to curve upward. Countless spear silhouettes surged forth, as if igniting the sky with flames.","The Asura men let out awed noises. Our princess’ attack is so beautiful!","Princess Ni Huang stood balanced on a single foot, with her upper body and her other leg forming a perfect curve that flaunted both her flexibility and her beautiful figure. But more importantly, they were impressed by the creative transformations in her attacks.","Everything that followed happened in the blink of an eye.","The spearmanship was incredible, but the dodging was impeccable too. In just a brief moment, they exchanged so many moves that those lacking in cultivation would struggle to understand the ingenuity in their exchange.","It was unlikely that Zu An could dodge the princess’ final strike. Her spear left countless silhouettes that filled his surroundings, leaving him with no room to escape via instantaneous movement. Zu An was impressed by Princess Ni Huang’s calculations. He was left with no choice but to draw his sword.","A brilliant light suddenly shone. It disintegrated the spear silhouettes, revealing a single spear.","The sword clashed with the spear tip. Princess Ni Huang’s body shuddered, and she quickly retreated thirty meters away.","Zu An was just about to conclude the battle when he noticed the excited gleam in her eyes. The princess exclaimed, “Wonderful! Let’s have another go at it!”","More pairs of hands emerged from her back. Zu An did a quick count—there were eight of them, more than the previous Asura man he'd fought with had!","Zu An was speechless. It’s as if a beautiful lady has transformed into a spider fiend... though she doesn’t look hideous with those additional hands. If anything, it adds a unique charm to her. RαNȮ₿Ëṥ","The more hands an asura had, the stronger they were.","A spear appeared in each of Princess Ni Huang’s eight hands before she charged at Zu An once more. Her movements were far faster than before, to the point where the spectators only saw a series of afterimages. It looked as if countless Princess Ni Huangs were ganging up on Zu An.","However, Zu An stood his ground, with one hand on his sword and the other behind his back. He occasionally swung his blade, producing a spark but no sound. That was because the sheer destructive prowess of their clashes obliterated all sounds.","In contrast to Princess Ni Huang’s lightning-fast movements, his legs were rooted to the ground, and his sword moved so slowly that a fool could make out its trajectory. Yet, this incredibly slow swordsmanship somehow neutralized every one of the spear attacks.","Zu An was like a lone boat floating amid choppy waters, refusing to sink no matter how the waves roared. No, it would be more apt to say he was a lighthouse towering on the shore, refusing to budge no matter how the waves crashed down on him.","The Asura men initially cheered for their princess, but over time, their cheers slowly died down, and they began looking at Zu An with grim eyes.","They hadn't thought highly of Zu An at the start, thinking that he was just a weak deadbeat. Even though Zu An was considered tall and well-built among humans, when compared to the highly muscular Asura race, he looked frail.","When Pi Lu failed to breach his defense, they hadn’t been too bothered, as Pi Lu was the weakest one among them. But now that they were watching their princess and Zu An’s battle, it was more than clear to them that Zu An wasn’t using his full strength. He was an unfathomable expert!","When had such an expert appeared in the Human race?","The countless Princess Ni Huangs in the sky suddenly disappeared. Her hands also disappeared, and she reverted to her previous appearance. “Let’s call it quits. I’m no match for you.”","“You’re too kind, my princess. Your spearmanship is incredible. There were a couple of times I struggled to deal with your attacks,” Zu An humbly replied.","“You hypocrite.” Princess Ni Huang spat. “A loss is a loss; I’m not a sore loser. You don’t have to pamper me. I’m satisfied with this battle.”","Zu An smiled. He was satisfied with this battle too. Not only had he preserved harmony, he'd also allowed the other party to experience the bliss of an all-out attack.","Learning from his encounters with Murong Qinghe and the Mermaid Queen, he'd even adamantly avoided physical contact with the other party to avoid spurring unwanted effects.","But while he was feeling good about himself. Princess Ni Huang suddenly exclaimed with a blush, “You’re the first man in so many years to make me experience such a rush. I like you!”","Zu An was bewildered."]},{"number":2503,"title":"Chapter 2503: Chapter 2455: Meeting the Parents","paragraphs":["Zu An panicked. Am I destined to leave love debts everywhere? I've already tried my best to avoid contact with the other side, so why did things still turn out like that?","It wouldn’t be a big deal in his time, but now that he had returned to the past, words like ‘ancestral grandmother’ just kept popping into his mind.","The Asura men looked at Zu An in awe and envy. They were awed because the Asuras respected the strong, and his earlier performance had won them over. They were envious that their princess had just confessed to him.","“So, what did you ask me earlier?” Princess Ni Huang asked, unfazed by her earlier confession.","Zu An quickly composed himself before repeating his question. “What’s your relationship with the Shaman races? How did you end up in the Eye of the Ocean?”","“The Shaman races are our enemy.” Princess Ni Huang’s gaze turned cold. “As for your latter question, we live here.”","Zu An was confused. That answer sparked many questions in his mind.","Princess Ni Huang noticed his confusion and explained, “Our Asura race used to war with the Celestial race, but we lost and were exiled to the underworld. We thought we could kill our way back there as long as we bided our time and trained up diligently, but...”","She suddenly let out a sigh. “That battle was a huge blow to us, but the underworld is so severely lacking in resources that we steadily grew weaker instead of recovering. It doesn’t help that it is also shrouded in death energy. In the end, we had to abandon our plan of launching a counterattack against the Celestial race.”","Zu An fell silent. The underworld was indeed more suited for the dead than the living.","“The Shaman races suddenly arrived later on.” Princess Ni Huang gritted her teeth. “They invaded our territories and plundered the little resources we had left. That’s not something we could tolerate, so a conflict broke out.”","“What’s the situation in that conflict?” Zu An asked.","The Asura men looked awkward. Even Princess Ni Huang looked mildly uncomfortable as she answered, “We initially had the upper hand, but their powerhouses suddenly made a move and pushed us back. Of course, we made the Shaman races pay the price for their aggression too.”","Princess Ni Huang’s hesitation made Zu An chuckle under his breath. The Asura race must have suffered heavy losses in that battle. How intriguing. The Asura race must be fairly powerful to be able to compete with the Celestial race, yet they lost to the Shaman races?","“Who are their powerhouses?” Zu An asked.","“I don’t know their names, but within the Shaman races, they are called ‘Ancestral Shamans’,” Princess Ni Huang replied.","“Ancestral Shamans!” Zu An was taken aback. Back on his Earth, there was a legend that after Pangu severed the sky from the land, his eyes turned into the sun and the moon, his body turned into all creations, and his twelve drops of blood essence morphed into the Twelve Ancestral Shamans. This hinted at how powerful the Ancestral Shamans could be.","In the legends, the Ancestral Shamans easily ranked among the strongest powerhouses. I’d have never expected to meet them here.","He felt a little anxious, but the many trials he had been through over the years helped him to quickly compose himself. He would just have to deal with it when the situation presented itself. Not to mention that so far, this was just his conjecture.","Besides, right now, his strength was likely on par with the legendary figures from his previous world.","“What’s the situation with the Shaman races? Why did they suddenly appear in the underworld?” Zu An wanted to verify if there was a link between this world’s Shaman races and the ones he knew about from legends.","“We did learn a bit about them from many years of battles. Before they were exiled to the underworld, the Shaman races had a massive battle with the Fiend races, but what’s weird is that the Fiend races they speak about dwell in the sky, and they have something called a Celestial Court. Their enemies resemble our ancient foe, the Celestial race,” Princess Ni Huang said.","“Doesn’t that mean you have common enemies? Shouldn’t the enemy of an enemy be a friend?” Zu An asked.","Princess Ni Huang scoffed, “Our Asura race always beats our enemies fair and square; we do not need external help.”","Zu An was stunned. It feels like the Asura race is a bunch of fools.","An Asura man added, “Our enemies might both dwell in the sky, but their enemies are different from the deities we know. Besides, the Shaman races have a lot of stubborn idiots, so there has been a lot of conflict between our races. It eventually culminated into a fight.”","“I noticed that you just came from the underworld. Were you planning to do something outside?” Zu An asked curiously.","“Not really...” Princess Ni Huang’s face reddened. “The Shaman races have always guarded the Eye of the Ocean, but they suddenly stomped out not long ago, only to return with livid faces. Shortly after, they removed the troops stationed near the Eye of the Ocean. We were curious to know what happened, so I brought them here to investigate.”","Princess Ni Huang assessed Zu An. “You seem to be from above. You should know what happened.”","Zu An calmly replied, “I do know a thing or two.”","Overjoyed, Princess Ni Huang quickly pressed for further details. The Asura men also looked at him with expectant eyes.","“They went up to fight with the Ocean races. I'm on good terms with the Ocean races, so I helped them repel the Shaman races...” Zu An quickly filled them in on the situation.","Princess Ni Huang eyed Zu An skeptically. “I know about the Ocean races. They aren’t weak, but they aren’t a match for Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain. You must have been the one to subdue them.”","“I didn’t subdue them; we merely crossed blows. They didn’t reveal all their means.” Zu An offered his most objective evaluation of the situation.","“You’re too hypocritical,” Princess Ni Huang snorted. “That ox has a terrible temper. He would have stood his ground if he thought he could defeat you. Hahaha, it's been a long time since I saw them suffering such humiliation!”","The Asura named Pi Lu exhaled in relief. He'd thought it was embarrassing to have lost to Zu An, but the knowledge that Ox Head, Horse Face, and the others had also been defeated by Zu An allowed him to straighten his back once more.","The more Princess Ni Huang spoke, the more excited she became. She grabbed Zu An’s arm and declared, “I must introduce you to my royal brother. Come with me! Now that you have defeated Ox Head and Horse Face, you’re our Asura race’s most esteemed guest!”","Feeling the squeeze against his arm, Zu An rubbed his nose to stop it from bleeding. Does she not realize that her thin clothes do little to conceal her explosive figure...","In the end, he accepted her offer. He'd been thinking of venturing into the underworld to investigate the situation anyway. It was better to make friends than enemies."]},{"number":2504,"title":"Chapter 2504: Chapter 2456: Asura King","paragraphs":["When they saw their princess grabbing Zu An’s arm, the Asura men raised their eyebrows in envy, and it didn’t help that her body was being squeezed out of shape from being pressed tightly against his.","That fellow has good luck. Our princess doesn’t usually act like this.","Princess Ni Huang pulled Zu An to the cliff and was about to jump in when she suddenly remembered something and exclaimed, “The concentration of death energy in the underworld is far higher than this. We’re only able to survive down there because of a curse. You might be an expert, but going down there might pose a danger to you.”","Zu An chuckled as he began walking forward. “It doesn’t matter.”","The Asura race respected the strong. There was no reason for Princess Ni Huang to stop him since he had already said as much, though she couldn’t resist asking, “Have you reached a level of cultivation where you’re impervious to death energy? Our people will be shocked to hear about that.”","The Asura men looked at Zu An mockingly.","He might be strong, but I bet he’s boasting. Who would be so arrogant as to leap into the underworld with their physical body? Who does he think he is? Aside from the undead, only special races like ours and the Shaman races can enter the underworld.","He’ll regret it dearly once the death energy disintegrates his body!","They were still upset to see their beautiful and noble princess becoming so fond of a human.","However, what happened next left them with widened eyes. They watched in shock as Zu An dove into the Eye of the Ocean and passed through it safely. For some reason, the surrounding death energy opened up to create a path for him.","Princess Ni Huang’s eyes lit up. She smacked Zu An’s chest as she exclaimed, “Incredible!”","Zu An eyed her chest. Why can a woman freely strike a man’s chest, but the opposite is considered wrong?","He quickly severed those thoughts before voicing a question. “Earlier, you mentioned that your race is cursed. What does that mean?”","Princess Ni Huang’s expression turned cold. “That’s the vile curse the Celestial race put on us. It is because of this curse that we are unable to leave the underworld. The only benefit it provides is that it makes us impervious to the underworld’s death energy.”","Zu An’s expression turned grim. A curse that condemned a living race to remain among the dead was indeed vile. He asked, “Who is the Celestial race?”","“It’s a term referring to all the deities in the Celestial World. There are 33 commonly known deities, but there are thousands of deities in total,” Princess Ni Huang explained.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Is the 33 here something related to the 33 layers of heaven?","He wanted to probe deeper, but Princess Ni Huang waved her hand and said, “Words like 'Celestial race' and 'deities' are forbidden among our Asura race. Make sure you don’t mention those inauspicious words before my royal brother, or else it might invoke his wrath.”","Zu An was stunned. Sensing the red-eyed glares from the Asura men, he decided to stop asking for now.","Princess Ni Huang began introducing the scenery along the way to him. “Do you see those flowers? That’s a plant exclusive to our underworld called a red spider lily. Aren’t they beautiful?” ℞aŊÖʙĚṢ","“Yes, They are beautiful.” Zu An smiled at the sight of the familiar flowers. They reminded him of Big Manman. They would appear as a mark somewhere on her body each time she went into heat, and it was beautiful.","“I think they are beautiful too.” Princess Ni Huang was delighted to hear that he liked them. “That is the Yin Mountain, and up ahead is the Oblivion River. You mustn’t come into contact with the water in it. Any living being, no matter how powerful, will lose all their memories and even their wits if they fall into the water,” Princess Ni Huang warned with a pale face as she remembered the plight that had befallen some of her comrades.","As she excitedly introduced the underworld to Zu An, the Asura men trailing behind them looked incredibly frustrated.","My princess, where did your usual loftiness go? Why are you so warm to that human? Fine, I get that he’s strong, dashing, gentlemanly... Ugh!","“Hm? You aren’t reacting much. It's as if you have seen these things before.” Princess Ni Huang sensed something was amiss. Both the Yin Mountain and the Oblivion River held a special significance to all living beings; it was unusual for anyone to be so calm after hearing about them.","“I have indeed seen them before,” Zu An replied.","“You've been here before? Why have I never met you then?” Princess Ni Huang was intrigued.","“I was here in the future.”","“???” Princess Ni Huang racked her brain trying to figure those words.","All of a sudden, Zu An poked her with his elbow and asked, “Is that your army?”","Princess Ni Huang looked over and saw a huge army of asuras in the distance. Their commander was riding on an enormous white elephant. The army was advancing in the direction of Yin Mountain.","“Ah, that is indeed our army. The one riding on the white elephant is my royal brother, Qumodo. He’s our Asura race’s strongest expert,” Princess Ni Huang said with a gleeful smile, showing that she was proud of her brother.","Zu An nodded. Given that the Asura race was warlike and revered the strong, it would take more than blood ties to claim the throne. But what are they planning to do by mobilizing their army?","Feeling too embarrassed to continue holding Zu An’s arm before their army, Princess Ni Huang released her grip and grabbed his hand instead. The two of them flew toward the enormous white elephant.","When they sensed someone approaching, the Asura soldiers vigilantly held their weapons tighter, but when they confirmed it was the princess, they breathed a sigh of relief and stepped aside to open up a path.","Countless eyes fell on Zu An. They were curious to know who he was for their beautiful princess to hold his hand.","Zu An assessed the white elephant. It looked majestic, towering at over thirty meters tall. It was incredible for this white elephant to have survived in a place as treacherous as the underworld.","“Royal brother!” Princess Ni Huang bowed to the Asura riding on the white elephant.","The Asura had a golden crown on his head. He had dark skin, and his physique was three times bigger than the other Asuras. He eyed his little sister and the man beside her and asked, “Ni Huang, who is this fellow?”","“He is the Necropolis Emperor, a friend I met outside,” Princess Ni Huang said.","“Emperor?” The Asura King’s eyes narrowed with murderous intent. “What an arrogant title!”","Sensing her brother’s anger, Princess Ni Huang hurriedly spoke up on Zu An’s behalf. “Royal brother, he is a formidable expert. Not only did he defeat all of us, but he is also the reason Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain retreated from outside.”","“Oh? You defeated Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain?” The Asura King was stunned. He raised his hand, and a black gleam with a force that threatened to sever the world in two abruptly slashed down on Zu An."]},{"number":2505,"title":"Chapter 2505: Chapter 2457: A Great Battle","paragraphs":["“Royal brother!” Princess Ni Huang cried out in shock, but it was too late for her to stop him.","Zu An chose not to dodge the devastating attack, however. He stood his ground as a golden bell projection formed around him. The attack struck the bell, and the two canceled out each other.","Princess Ni Huang quickly stood in front of Zu An and exclaimed, “Royal brother, how can you attack my friend?!”","Zu An interjected with a smile, saying, “Princess, it’s a misunderstanding. Your brother held back. He was merely testing me.”","The other party’s attack had carried no killing intent.","The Asura King nodded in satisfaction. “Indeed. That explains how you defeated Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain. I was worried that my royal sister had been deceived by an outsider due to her lack of experience, but I now see that I was overthinking it.”","Princess Ni Huang was displeased. “Royal brother, do I look that gullible to you?”","The Asura King merely smiled. He knew his little sister was no fool, but as a king, he was carrying too much on his shoulders, so much so that he didn’t have the luxury of unconditional trust. Kings could only trust themselves.","He'd only used 60 to 70% of his strength earlier, but it was enough to prove that the other party was an expert.","Zu An nodded as well. I think I managed to pull it off.","It would be awkward if the Asura King, under the watchful eyes of his army, couldn’t even shatter his defensive layer. On top of that, the Asura race was known to be warlike. It would be terrible if he inadvertently provoked the Asura King to continue the battle. To avoid such a situation, he'd made sure that the Asura King’s attack would perfectly offset the Tranquility Bell.","“Royal sister, bring our guest up here for further conversation,” the Asura King said. It would be a breach of hospitality if his guest had to talk to him while craning his neck upward, after all.","“Come with me.” Princess Ni Huang grabbed Zu An’s hand and leaped onto the white elephant’s back.","It would be more apt to call the platform atop the Asura King’s mount a massive tent. It was very spacious, with several seats neatly laid out in front of his royal throne.","The Asura King gestured for them to take a seat before eyeing Zu An. “You are a human, no?”","Zu An nodded. “Yes, I am a human.”","“What a surprise. I didn’t expect such huge changes to have happened outside while we were trapped in the underworld. To think that the weak humans would have an expert as powerful as you,” the Asura King said.","Most legends depicted humans to be one of the weaker races, sometimes even being reduced to food for other races, though they eventually prospered later on.","The Asura King didn’t spend too much time ruminating, however. “Did you just defeat Ox Head, Horse Face, and the others?”","“We crossed blows, but they suddenly fled shortly after. It would be a stretch to say I defeated them.” Zu An didn’t want to go into detail about his battle with them.","The Asura King burst into laughter. “The lot of them have fiery tempers. That old ox, in particular, has his head in the clouds. He wouldn’t have escaped if he thought he could beat you. I was wondering why the Shaman races were acting as if they had just lost a huge battle. So you are the reason! Well done!”","That compliment brought a beaming smile to Princess Ni Huang’s face. “Royal brother, aren’t I incredible to have found such a friend?”","“Yes, you are incredible indeed.” The Asura King guffawed. “With your friend’s help, our victory would be assured.”","Zu An took this opportunity to ask, “May I know what battle you are referring to?” He had been wanting to ask this since laying his eyes on the Asura army.","“We’re invading the Shaman races' territory, of course. We should take full advantage of their defeat to drive them out of here!” the Asura King said with an excited gleam in his eyes.","The two races had fought for many years now, but neither side had been able to best the other. This was a chance to overcome the stalemate.","Zu An fell silent. Even though the Asura race appeared to have the upper hand, he knew how things happened afterward. The future underworld still had Ox Head and Horse Face, but the Asura race was nowhere to be seen. That made him worried. Did the Asura race suffer a tragic defeat in this battle? But I don’t see how the powerful Asura race could have lost here.","Princess Ni Huang had treated him decently. It would be excessive to call them close friends, but he wouldn’t want to see anything happening to her.","“I was still a little worried, but with your help, I’m sure this battle won’t be an issue!” The Asura King was extremely optimistic about this battle. “If you contribute greatly to this battle, I’ll confer the title of 'Marshal’ onto you and betroth my royal sister to you!”","The smiling Princess Ni Huang’s face immediately turned red. “What are you saying, royal brother? He’s just a friend!” She glanced at Zu An with awkward and apologetic eyes.","The Asura King responded with an annoying ‘I get it’ smile. “Of course, of course. You’re only friends. Hahaha.”","Zu An was stunned. He was only here to investigate what happened to the underworld. He hadn’t expected to suddenly become the Asura King’s brother-in-law.","Worried that his intervention could cause unwanted outcomes, he tried to explain his situation, only for the sounds of battle to suddenly break out ahead. The Asura army had just bumped into the Shaman army, and both sides immediately came to blows.","The Asura King quickly stood up to observe the battle. From time to time, he ordered his guards to signal instructions to the commanders using a flag.","Zu An had fought in a war before, so he was able to follow what was happening. The Asura King would have been a first-class general even in human history. His commanding skill is an art in itself. He’s luring the enemies into their formation before pulling off a divide-and-conquer tactic...","On top of that, the Asura race was a valiant warrior race. Their soldiers were the most outstanding war machines in the world, capable of navigating the battlefield like fish in water. It didn’t take long for the Shaman army’s formation to fall into disarray.","Zu An thus verified that an Asura’s strength could indeed be determined by their number of hands. Most Asuras had three to five hands; very few had six or more. Meanwhile, most Asura generals, like Princess Ni Huang, had eight hands. The Asura King, as the strongest expert of the Asura race, was likely the only one with nine hands.","Just then, a roar echoed. “Qumodo, what do you mean by this sudden assault?”","The world shook. Ox Face, Horse Head, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain’s massive figures were visible as they rushed over from afar with weapons in their hands. The Asura soldiers standing in their path collapsed like trampled vegetables.","The Asura King harrumphed. “Ox Head, what’s the point of venting on the soldiers? I dare you to fight me instead!”","He rose above the battlefield, and a humongous Asura avatar with nine hands, each one wielding a weapon, manifested behind him. He stood there with an air that overpowered even the humongous Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain combined.","Four marshals emerged from the Asura army and took their places next to the Asura King. Similar Asura avatars manifested behind them, but theirs had eight arms and were half the size of the Asura King’s avatar.","Princess Ni Huang took control of the battlefield and continued commanding the troops from the white elephant. Amid this cruel battlefield, her valiant stature was the most beautiful sight."]},{"number":2506,"title":"Chapter 2506: Chapter 2458: Reincarnation Platform","paragraphs":["The Shaman army was at a disadvantage, but Zu An keenly noticed that their soldiers weren’t dying easily. No matter how severely injured they were, even to the point where they lay unmoving on the floor, they recovered shortly after and rejoined the battle.","“That’s incredible.” Zu An remembered the Shaman races displaying incredible regenerative ability at the battle outside the Eye of the Ocean, but somehow, that ability looked to be even greater here.","While directing the troops, Princess Ni Huang explained, “The Shaman races can gain boundless strength just by being in contact with the ground. They can recover no matter how severely injured they are.”","Zu An was taken aback. “Doesn’t that make them undefeatable? No wonder you were at a disadvantage against them!”","He'd found it peculiar that the warlike Asura race had fallen into a disadvantage against the Shaman races, but it turned out that the problem lay here.","“It took us many years before we finally made sense of the Shaman race’s secrets, but we feigned ignorance lest they guard against our countermeasures. We were waiting for the right time to drop them a surprise,” Princess Ni Huang said with a gleeful smile.","Now was the time for them to reveal the tricks they were hiding up their sleeves. Princess Ni Huang waved a flag, and the Asura army swiftly got into formation and worked with one another to hoist their enemies up into the air.","The Shaman soldiers were horrified. They struggled in desperation, but the Asura army had come prepared. Their multiple arms meant that they could continue holding their enemies up in the air while stabbing the latter with their weapons.","The Shaman soldiers bled profusely, thrashing around for a while longer before falling still. But the Asura soldiers still refused to let the deceased Shaman soldiers down, opting to continue fighting while holding the corpses up. Only after a significant time had passed did they hurl the corpses aside.","This time, the deceased Shaman soldiers no longer returned to life. The same situation happened in multiple places across the battlefield; the Shaman soldiers suffered heavy losses.","Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain were horrified. They anxiously charged in with their weapons to rescue their clansmen, but the Asura King blocked their path with a sneer.","“Where are you going? I’m your opponent.”","“Qumodo, are you sure you want to go this far?!” the giant Ox Head roared with red eyes.","The Asura King’s expression turned cold. “You were the ones who invaded our land and massacred our clansmen. There was never any room for reconciliation.”","The underworld was so scarce in resources that it wasn’t even enough for the Asura race, and that was the reason their people were slowly getting weaker over time. At this rate, it was only a matter of time before the Asura race died out. Thus, the Asura King had planned to completely defeat the Shaman race before his people weakened beyond a certain point. Today, when he heard about the Shaman race’s defeat, he'd realized right away that the opportunity had come.","“Don’t blame us for this then!” Horse Face roared as he furiously charged at the Asura King, brandishing his trident.","At the same time, Ox Head attacked with his axe from another direction.","Even so, the Asura King was unfazed. The massive avatar behind him swiftly moved its nine hands to block Ox Head and Horse Face’s attacks.","Zu An was awed. Knowing how strong Ox Head and Horse Face were, he knew it was a remarkable feat for the Asura King to face them in a direct confrontation.","The two races had plenty of intelligence on each other, having been at war for many years. Golden Cangue and Silver Chain knew Ox Head and Horse Face couldn’t defeat the Asura King on their own, so they joined the fray with their weapons.","The Asura King’s four marshals rushed forth to restrain Golden Cangue and Silver Chain from interfering with the Asura King’s battle. Those who could become marshals in the warlike Asura race, needless to say, wielded strength that couldn’t be underestimated. They were individually weaker than Golden Cangue and Silver Chain, but they had no trouble standing their ground against them in a 4-against-2 fight.","Watching the scene from the white elephant, Zu An frowned. At the moment, the Asura race held the advantage; it didn’t look as if they would lose this battle.","The Shaman army’s morale was still low from their crushing defeat against the Ocean races. They were in no condition to deal with the Asura army’s ferocious onslaught. Seeing true death befalling their comrades brought fear to the Shamans’ faces, and their formation began to collapse.","Ox Head and Horse Face were frustrated. They wanted to help their people, but their hands were tied. They were no match for the Asura King in the first place, and their anxiety put them in a worse position. Soon, several glaring wounds appeared on their bodies, although it was no big deal thanks to their tremendous regenerative prowess.","Just then, Ox Head let out a bizarre sound. All the Shamans on the battlefield stopped fighting and began escaping in a certain direction, as if they'd received a certain signal.","Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain unleashed their potential and entered a berserk state to cover their fellow Shamans’ escape. Their current fighting prowess posed a headache to even the Asura King.","The Asura King sneered with a frown, “You already used these techniques earlier when fighting at the Eye of the Ocean. How long can you maintain the ignition of your blood essence? Once you begin to lose momentum, I’ll kill you as easily as slaughtering chickens!”","The four giants had to pay a severe price for the massive temporary boost in their fighting prowess. Needless to say, the Asura King wouldn’t foolishly pit himself against them at this juncture. All he needed to do was to bide his time, and victory would be his.","He felt grateful to the friend his royal sister had brought over. If not for the latter, he couldn’t have defeated the Shaman race so easily. He is the biggest contributor to this war. I shall take him in as my brother-in-law and have him accompany me in expanding our race’s territory.","The thought of their bright future excited him.","Ox Head and Horse Face continued covering their people’s retreat with livid faces, while the Asura King gave chase with his army. The Asura army was overcome with delirium; after so many years of war, there was finally going to be a victor between the two races.","Zu An, who was riding the white elephant with Princess Ni Huang, felt increasingly uneasy. He wondered, “Are they luring us into an ambush?”","Princess Ni Huang smiled. “That can’t be. We have fought for so long that we have a good grasp of each other’s military prowess. Furthermore, we have fought in so many wars that we can tell the difference between a feint and a panicked retreat.”","Zu An suddenly remembered something that had been mentioned earlier. “Doesn’t the Shaman race still have their Ancestral Shamans?”","“Don’t worry, the Ancestral Shamans are already gone. We wouldn’t have waged this war otherwise,” Princess Ni Huang replied with a smile.","Amid the escape and chase, the two armies arrived in the vicinity of the Reincarnation Platform. That was when things started going awry."]},{"number":2507,"title":"Chapter 2507: Chapter 2459: Ancestral Shaman","paragraphs":["Zu An had seen many familiar sights along the way. On the whole, it didn’t look too different from the underworld in the future, though there were fewer buildings around. The Oblivion River Bridge was lacking Grandmother Meng, too. Looking at the raging Oblivion River reminded Zu An of Chu Chuyan underneath the bridge, but now that he was thousands of years earlier in time, there was no way she could be here.","Upon escaping to the Reincarnation Platform, the Shaman races found themselves cornered.","This was the place where deceased souls reincarnated. If they passed through the Reincarnation Platform, living beings would also be forcefully reincarnated. If the Shaman races fled there, the Asura race would be so amused that they could wake up from their dreams laughing.","But the sight of the Reincarnation Platform reminded Zu An of a legend, and his face twisted. Could the Ancestral Shaman protecting the Shaman race possibly be...","The Shamans fled onto the Reincarnation Platform and cried their hearts out.","“Milady, please save us!”","“At this rate, the Asura race will massacre us!”","“Milady, you showed them kindness back then, but they are seeking to obliterate us now!”","...","Perhaps due to the incessant cries and pleas, a terrifying aura that alarmed even Zu An rose from the Reincarnation Platform.","The Asura King was also startled, and he hurriedly halted the pursuit. The Asura army surveyed their surroundings with uneasy eyes.","Princess Ni Huang's eyes suddenly widened. “It’s her aura. How is this possible? Hasn’t she turned into the concept of reincarnation...”","Zu An could already guess the identity of this Ancestral Shaman—Houtu. In the legends, she couldn’t bear to see forlorn souls and ghosts roaming across the world, so she'd embodied the concept of reincarnation so the deceased in the world could be born anew. Her immense contribution led to her being revered as Lady Houtu.","Zu An would have guessed her identity before, but Houtu had already long since embodied the concept of reincarnation. The timeline didn’t fit, so he'd thought the Asura race was talking about other Ancestral Shamans.","In the meantime, a woman’s avatar surfaced from the Reincarnation Platform. Despite her appearance being obscured, one could feel boundless compassion radiating from her, though she also gave off the intimidating air of an expert.","The Asura King’s face darkened. He flew over with gritted teeth and declared, “Houtu, I don’t care whether you’re backing them or not, I’ll be massacring them all!”","The Asura race had spent too long preparing for this battle. If they lost this fight, they wouldn’t have the resources to make a comeback. Rather than spiral into decline and die a slow death, the Asura King would rather stake everything here for the chance of a comeback.","As the Asura King spoke, the avatar behind him grew larger and unfurled another nine arms. His massive avatar had a total of eighteen arms, and they were all either brandishing weapons or forming hand seals. Unlike the other Asura avatars, which were just terrifying, his was dignified like a divine idol. His aura was surprisingly on par with Houtu’s avatar, and that won him the Asura soldiers’ cheers.","But Zu An keenly noticed Princess Ni Huang’s melancholic expression. She was biting her lips, her hands were clenched tightly in her sleeves, and her body was trembling ever so slightly. He made his way over to her and asked, “What’s wrong?”","Having found emotional support in Zu An, Princess Ni Huang’s eyes reddened, and she spoke with a hoarse voice at a volume only the two of them could hear. “My royal brother has used our Asura Royal Clan’s secret art. He has ignited his blood essence. Whether he wins this battle or not... His days are numbered.”","No wonder the Asura King’s number of arms suddenly increased twofold. Zu An felt a surge of respect for the Asura King. The latter was a worthy ruler, willing to put his life on the line for his people’s future.","Judging from the royal siblings’ earlier conversation, he'd gained a rough grasp of the Asura race’s predicament. A second chance was a luxury they didn’t have. Who would have thought that shortly after the Asura King mocked Ox Head and Horse Face for that, it would be his turn to ignite his blood essence?","Fate was truly capricious at times.","Houtu’s avatar suddenly unleashed a swiftly rotating light halo. Upon careful examination, it resembled a miniaturized version of the Six Paths of Reincarnation.","The halo moved extremely slowly, but for some reason, the Asura King was unable to dodge it. He had no choice but to raise a weapon and confront it. However, his weapon was instantly cut in half.","Zu An’s eyes narrowed. The Asura King’s weapon wasn't a divine weapon, but it wasn't far off. Yet, it didn’t survive a single clash. What is that halo?","That wasn't all. The halo proceeded to slice off two of the Asura King’s hands, causing him to roar in pain. In his fury, his remaining sixteen hands struck the halo with the weapons and artifacts they held to strike it down. With his cultivation, the simultaneous movements of his sixteen arms formed an all-encompassing net that nothing could escape from.","And yet, he was unable to contain that mysterious halo.","Wherever it passed, the Asura King’s weapons shattered, and one after another, even his arms were severed. The Asura King roared in pain as he desperately retreated, but the halo chased him as closely as if it was his shadow.","Soon, he had already lost seventeen of his arms. He stared at the approaching halo with eyes filled with despair.","The Asura race had fallen silent. To think that the imposing Asura King would be so helpless against Houtu! The Asuras all felt a mix of despair and fear.","Even Zu An’s body turned cold. Houtu was just too powerful. So this is the prowess of an Ancestral Shaman!","Princess Ni Huang clutched Zu An’s sleeve and pleaded in desperation, “Can you save my royal brother?”","She was cornered too. Her brother was the strongest warrior in the Asura race, and on top of that, he had also invoked their Royal Clan’s secret art. His fighting prowess was currently far above hers. She wouldn’t be able to make a difference in the battle. She racked her brains, and the only one who could be able to turn things around was Zu An.","Zu An flitted onto the Reincarnation Platform and bowed to the blurred avatar, saying, “Lady Houtu, please have mercy!”","The halo stopped just ten centimeters away from the Asura King. By this point, he had already collapsed to the ground, resigned to his death.","Princess Ni Huang was both surprised and overjoyed. He stepped in to save my royal brother for my sake. He truly cares about me... Does this mean he likes me? I also like him a lot too...","A layer of cold sweat had drenched Zu An’s forehead. Houtu was so powerful that he felt greatly threatened by her. He hadn’t stepped up because he was in love with Princess Ni Huang, however. Rather, he wanted to get to the bottom of what was happening in the underworld.","Houtu’s avatar lowered her head to gaze at him, then an ethereal, emotionless voice echoed in his mind. “Who are you? Why do I sense a peculiar aura from you?”"]},{"number":2508,"title":"Chapter 2508: Chapter 2460: Celestial Court","paragraphs":["“Lady Houtu, I am someone who has deep ties with the underworld, but I’m unable to divulge my true identity due to various reasons. However, I have a temporary identity in this world—the Necropolis Emperor,” Zu An replied while assessing Houtu’s reaction.","He hadn't chosen to step up out of recklessness. After taking control of the underworld, he had built up a faint connection with the Six Paths of Reincarnation. With that connection, and the knowledge that Houtu was known for her compassion, he figured it wouldn’t be too dangerous.","“Hm?” Houtu’s avatar suddenly recalled something, and that prompted her to assess him with eyes glowing with different lights. A while later, she finally replied, “So you’re the underworld’s future master.”","Outsiders couldn’t hear their conversation, so there was no need to worry about divulging secrets.","Zu An was surprised. He hadn’t expected the other party to see through his past and future with just a glance. He bowed to her and replied in awe, “Lady Houtu has sharp eyes.”","“Why are you here?” It was impossible to decipher Houtu’s emotions from her impassive voice.","“There's a crisis in the future, so I came to this world to properly resolve the issue. I didn’t expect the underworld of this era to be so vastly different from that in my era,” Zu An replied with a bitter smile.","Houtu’s avatar fell silent for a long time before she finally replied, “My divination revealed many differences too. Why don’t you tell me what the future underworld is like?”","Zu An was taken aback. It would appear that Houtu could glimpse into the future, but she couldn't see the details. He told her about the future underworld without hiding a thing.","Neither the Shamans nor the Asuras dared to interject in their silent conversation.","Princess Ni Huang rushed to the Asura King’s side, supported him to his feet, and fed him all kinds of pills. However, they didn’t dare to leave, as the terrifying light halo was still stopped right in front of them. They feared a reckless move would provoke the halo’s attack once more.","Ox Head and Horse Face were initially delighted to learn that Zu An was the mysterious figure they'd fought with at the Eye of the Ocean. They were convinced that he couldn’t be stronger than their Ancestral Shaman.","He’s courting his death by confronting the Ancestral Shaman. Good riddance!","But as time passed, they gradually realized something was amiss. Why isn’t the Ancestral Shaman making a move on him?","After hearing Zu An’s descriptions, Houtu’s avatar remarked, “I see. That is much more reasonable than how things currently are.”","“I communed with the Six Paths of Reincarnation in the future, but I didn’t sense your existence...” Zu An carefully spoke up.","“I have transformed into the Six Paths of Reincarnation. This is the final sliver of my will. I left it behind because I feared the Shaman races’ bloodline would vanish in the underworld,” Houtu’s avatar replied.","Zu An nodded in realization. I see. The true Houtu has transformed into the Six Paths of Reincarnation, and she probably can’t maintain this sliver of her will for long either. At least, she's nowhere to be seen in the future.","“Are you here to speak up for the Asura race?” Houtu’s avatar suddenly asked.","Zu An glanced at the Asura King and Princess Ni Huang. “I am friends with those two, but it’d be presumptuous of me to intervene in a feud between the two races.”","“That’s good.” Houtu's voice suddenly turned cold. “Back then, I spared those Asuras out of kindness, yet, here they are, trying to end our Shaman bloodlines for good...”","Zu An could tell Houtu’s avatar was planning to decimate the Asura race. He quickly interjected, “Lady Houtu, the Asura race is also one of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. There could be a gap in the Six Paths of Reincarnation if you eradicate them for good.”","Houtu’s avatar was silent for several seconds before replying, “You’re still planning to speak up for your friends.”","“I can’t turn a blind eye to their fate,\" Zu An said. Princess Ni Huang had treated him well, so he couldn’t just watch as she and her race were destroyed. “I've been thinking about the issue. The Shaman races and the Asura race are at war because the underworld suffers from a severe lack of resources, but neither race is native to this place.”","“Can you help them leave the underworld?” Houtu’s avatar asked.","“I know a way to lift the seal outside. As long as Lady Houtu can guarantee they won’t massacre the living, I should be able to bring them out,” Zu An replied grimly.","The Eye of the Ocean’s seal was already half-destroyed. Given his strength and influence, perhaps he'd be able to convince the Ocean races to set them free.","The Shaman races were reckless and violent, but they weren’t as cruel and bloodthirsty as the monsters. There was room for them to coexist with the Ocean races.","Meanwhile, the Asura race was indeed militaristic, but it would not be all bad if their aggression could be channeled toward the monsters. If things went well, they could even potentially take some of the worlds under the monsters’ control.","But Houtu’s avatar sighed. “It’s not that easy. The Shaman races lost to the Fiend races. The Asura race lost to the Celestial Court. Both races have a curse preventing them from leaving the underworld.”","Zu An was taken aback. “Lady Houtu, may I know if the Fiend races you mentioned are the same Fiend races as the ones in this world?”","The Cultivation World’s Fiend races were prosperous, but they had a limit. Given that they couldn’t even defeat the monsters, it was hard to imagine them defeating the legendary Shaman races.","If the legends were true, the Shaman races at their peak had had the Twelve Ancestral Shamans and countless great shamans. Even the monsters out there would struggle to deal with them, let alone the Cultivation World’s fiend races.","“They aren’t the same, but they are related. The Fiend races I mentioned refer to the Celestial Court’s Fiend races. The Fiend races you currently see are merely bloodline descendants they left behind,” Houtu’s avatar replied.","Zu An was shocked. He would never have figured out that the Cultivation World’s Fiend races were the bloodline descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races!","He suddenly recalled a certain matter and asked, “But I heard the monsters proclaiming themselves as the bloodline descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races...”","That was the secret he had heard from the True Demon race’s great elder, and they did have a secret art to activate the Cultivation World’s Fiend races’ bloodline power. They looked more like the real deal here.","“Hmph! Those monsters are merely the bloodline descendants of the pets and mounts raised by the Celestial Court’s Fiend races,” Houtu’s avatar scoffed. She had just divined Zu An’s past, so she had a clear understanding of the monsters too.","Zu An was shocked."]},{"number":2509,"title":"Chapter 2509: Chapter 2461: Six Paths’ Insignias","paragraphs":["Zu An had never expected the imposing monsters to be mere pets reared by the Celestial Courts’ Fiend races, and that the bullied Fiend races would be the latter's true bloodline descendants. Now that he thought about it, however, the monsters resembled beasts more, whereas the Fiend races appeared more normal in comparison.","Zu An couldn’t help but wonder how the True Demon race’s grand elder would react if he learned that those servants’ descendants were actually their master's descendants, and they were the servants instead.","With this thought in mind, he asked, “Where did the Celestial Court’s Fiend races go? Why do they just watch as the pets they reared freely slaughter their bloodline descendants?”","Houtu’s avatar replied, “The battle between the Shaman races and the Fiend races ended with the Shaman races’ defeat, but the Celestial Court’s Fiend races also fell from grace. I have been in the underworld all this time, so I don’t know their whereabouts.”","Zu An recalled what he had heard from the Asura race and asked, “The Asura race mentioned that they fought with the Celestial race but lost, resulting in their exile here. Are the deities they fought with the same as the Celestial Court’s Fiend races?”","“They arrived here earlier than our Shaman races. Based on what I know, it doesn’t seem to be the same group of deities,” Houtu’s avatar replied.","Zu An’s mind churned to action. It seems there was another Celestial race before the Celestial Court’s Fiend races.","His short conversation with Houtu’s avatar was extremely fruitful; it answered a lot of the doubts he'd previously harbored.","He wanted to ask more, but Houtu’s avatar said, “Knowing too much right now may bring you trouble instead.”","Zu An’s heart was chilled. It wasn't his first time hearing those words. In the Myriad Worlds, secrets often represented danger.","“I don’t have much time left. I have to ensure the future of the Shaman races before I dissipate,” Houtu’s avatar said.","A thought popped into Zu An’s mind, and he quickly said, “Just as they were imprisoned here, there must be a way for them to leave this place too. As for what that method is, Lady Houtu, I may need your insight for it.” He figured that someone as knowledgeable as Houtu would have a way.","There was a brief silence before Houtu’s avatar replied, “Are you still hoping to save your Asura friends?”","Zu An’s eyes gleamed with excitement. “Of course. It’d be ideal if we could rescue both races instead of having them fight it out here.”","Houtu’s avatar nodded. “Your talk about the future inspired me.”","Zu An was taken aback. Shouldn’t the future be the result of what happened here? Somehow, the cause and effect seem to be reversed here.","“I may have transformed into the Six Paths of Reincarnation, but I sense its incompleteness. Something is missing in it. I couldn’t figure it out all these years, until I met you,” Houtu’s avatar slowly said.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. She can’t be asking me to complete the Six Paths of Reincarnation, can she?","Sensing his nervousness, Houtu’s avatar said joyfully, “Don’t worry, I just need you to find a few things for me.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. He bowed to the avatar and said, “Please ask anything of me. I’ll walk through fire for you, Lady Houtu.”","“The Six Paths of Reincarnation is incomplete because its connection with the Six Paths is lacking. I need you to find the power insignias signifying the Celestial Path, the Human Path, the Asura Path, the Hell Path, the Beast Path, and the Hungry Ghost Path. I’ll fuse them before imbuing them into the Six Paths,” Houtu’s avatar said.","Zu An was alarmed. This was no easy feat. Each world’s power insignia was often hidden discreetly, not to mention he had no idea where the Celestial World and the others were.","Houtu’s avatar suddenly added, “You don’t need to search for the Hell Path’s power insignia; you have it with you right now—the Netherworld Book of Life and Death. This book governs the fate of all deceased entities in the Hell Path.”","Zu An was worried. The Netherworld Book of Life and Death was of utmost importance to him. Putting aside the powers it harnessed, it was also one of the twelve secret manuals required by the Keyboard System. He didn’t dare to ruin it carelessly.","Sensing his worry, Houtu’s avatar said, “Rest assured, the book won’t be damaged. I’m just borrowing a sliver of its authority. Not only will it be unimpaired, it will also receive benefits from the Six Paths of Reincarnation.”","This doesn’t conform to the law of energy conservation, Zu An retorted in his mind, though he also knew that it would be foolish to apply scientific laws to the Cultivation World.","“What are the other power insignias?” he asked. He knew nothing about those and had no idea where to start.","“You can ask your Asura friends about the Asura Path’s power insignia,” Houtu’s avatar replied.","Zu An glanced at the Asura King and Princess Ni Huang and nodded.","“The Human Path's insignia can be found right outside. Look for the Human Emperor; it shouldn’t be too difficult.","“The Hungry Ghost Path exists between the mortal world and the underworld. They roam the mortal world in confusion, harming the living.”","Zu An couldn’t help but notice that the Hungry Ghost Path resembled the place where Jing Teng had resided when she was the Ghost King.","“As for the Beast Path, after hearing your story about the future, I’m thinking that the Monster World could likely be it.”","Zu An was stunned. Who could have thought that the Monster World was the Beast Path?","However, the Monster World was currently at its peak. It would be nigh impossible to head over and claim their power insignia... though the Lord of Slaughter and his monster army’s invasion of the Cultivation World presented him with a chance.","“As for the Celestial Path...” Houtu’s avatar fell silent for a moment before continuing, “It should be beyond your reach for now, but since the Fiend races out there are the descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races, you might find clues with them.”","Zu An frowned. As the future Fiend races’ regent, he was so familiar with them that he even knew all the details of the minor races, but he had no information about the Celestial Path at all.","Just then, he suddenly remembered the secret dungeon in the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb. There were incomparably powerful beings in there. Could that be the Celestial Path?","He was put in a dilemma. It was unlikely he could obtain any of the power insignias any time soon, and there were other things he needed to do here. As much as he viewed Princess Ni Huang as his friend, he didn’t have that much time to use on this matter.","Just then, Houtu’s avatar said, “You’re looking for the World Law Beacon here, right? I have never heard of a rainbow World Law Beacon, so I can only think of one possibility. The World Law Beacon might still be nonexistent—it could be the item derived from fusing the Six Paths’ insignias.”"]},{"number":2510,"title":"Chapter 2510: Chapter 2462: Asura Valkyrie’s Tear","paragraphs":["Zu An had been wondering where the World Law Beacon was located, but it had never crossed his mind that the World Law Beacon could have not come into existence yet.","Now that he thought about it, this world’s World Law Beacon was indeed unique. Other worlds’ World Law Beacons only had a single color, yet this one was rainbow-colored. He'd thought it was the influence of the Wonderpoint World, but on further reflection, it was probably due to the Six Paths’ fusion.","He'd been reluctant to spend so much time helping Houtu collect the Six Paths’ authority insignias, but if this matter was tied to the World Law Beacon, he would have no choice but to do it. Many things wouldn't align if the World Law Beacon wasn't created. Perhaps the future World Law Beacon would even disappear when he returned to the future.","Having experienced time travel, he now understood that cause and effect was sometimes reversed. Events that happened in this era wouldn't necessarily precede the future; it was perhaps more apt to say that they were happening simultaneously. Since that was the case, he couldn’t turn a blind eye to this matter.","“I’ll help you collect the power insignias, but it might take a long time. Lady Houtu, you mentioned that you won’t be able to sustain your current state for long. I fear...” This was also what Zu An was the most worried about. It had taken him a long time just to obtain the Netherworld Book of Life and Death, so it would surely take him longer to collect all six power insignias.","Houtu’s avatar said, “Since the World Law Beacon exists in the future, it must mean that my forging is successful. That also proves you'll be able to collect all the power insignias before my dissipation. I trust you.”","Zu An was speechless. He was tempted to retort against it, but it wouldn’t change the situation.","“I’ll be going into hibernation to conserve my energy. Summon me after you collect all the power insignias,” Houtu’s avatar said before she began to disappear.","Noticing Ox Head, Horse Face, and the others eyeing him intently, Zu An became anxious. “But the Shaman races...”","“Don’t worry, I’ll talk to them,” Houtu’s avatar said. A divine voice echoed in the surroundings right after. “There shall be a temporary ceasefire between the Shaman races and the Asura race. From this day on, this man, the Necropolis Emperor, will be a friend of our Shaman races. Do your best to cooperate with him.”","Even though Zu An had held a long conversation with Houtu’s avatar, the exchange had happened on the soul level. In truth, only an instant had passed.","Ox Head, Horse Face, and the others had been gleefully waiting for their Ancestral Shaman to crush that brat when they suddenly received the order.","“But Ancestral Shaman...” Ox Head and Horse Face wondered how that brat had enchanted their Ancestral Shaman, but Houtu’s avatar had already disappeared by then, not giving them the time to voice their complaints.","Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain were speechless. They'd never thought they would be forced to smile at an enemy whom they had sworn to destroy just a second ago.","Ox Head was the first to break the silence. He struck his chest and said, “I don’t know why the Ancestral Shaman issued such an order, but we believe in her judgment. From this day on, you shall be a friend of our Shaman races. You may ask anything of us.”","Zu An chuckled. “I think we’ll be friends for a long time.” He thought about Ox Head and Horse Face’s job in the future, and he found himself amazed by fate’s mysticism.","Ox Head was taken aback, not understanding what those words meant.","Zu An flew to Princess Ni Huang’s side and asked, “Asura King, how are your injuries?”","“I’m fine. I just need to recuperate a bit.” With the terrifying halo gone, the Asura King returned to his feet and straightened his posture, looking as dignified as before.","Princess Ni Huang bit her lips as she asked sorrowfully, “Royal brother, why are you still putting on a strong front? After using that secret art, you only have days left to live!”","The Asura King suddenly looked like a deflated ball, and his face started to look much older. “Ni Huang, can’t you leave your royal brother with some dignity?”","Princess Ni Huang bit her lips as she tried to hold back her tears.","Zu An took out an Ice Heart Pill and fed it to the Asura King. “How do you feel now?”","The Ice Heart Pill was the White Jade Sect’s greatest medicine. Even Yan Xuehen only had two pills despite being the sect master, and she'd later given one to Zu An. Later, as Zu An got closer to Yan Xuehen, she'd secretly stolen more from her sect and given them to him to protect himself. However, with Zu An’s current cultivation, he had no use for the Ice Heart Pill anymore.","“It’s an incredible pill. To think that it can extend my lifespan by a month despite the violent nature of our secret art,” the Asura King remarked in awe.","Zu An wasn’t surprised to hear that. How could a technique that the Asura Royal Clan deemed a secret skill be so tame as to have its side effects neutralized by a single Ice Heart Pill?","Zu An let out a sigh. “It’s a pity I depleted my Feather Mountain Spring Water, or else it would have been able to save your life.”","“Feather Mountain Spring Water? What’s that? I’ll find some for my royal brother!” Princess Ni Huang exclaimed.","“I’m afraid that place is beyond your reach.” After saying those words, Zu An suddenly felt dazed.","Now that he thought about it, the secret dungeon in the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb only opened once in a very long while. He had entered the secret dungeon the last time it opened in the future, and it would probably be a long time before it opened once more after that. But now that he was in the past, perhaps it would be near the secret dungeon’s opening time.","Houtu had tasked him to collect the Six Paths’ power insignias, including the Celestial Path’s. He had thought hard about it, and the most likely location of the Celestial World was the secret dungeon he had visited in the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb.","Given that the Fiend races were the bloodline descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races, it wouldn’t be surprising for there to be such a connection between them. Besides, he had seen the Celestial Court inside that secret dungeon.","The thought of that excited him, and he said, “There might be medicine to save your royal brother in the place I’m heading to next.”","“Really?” Princess Ni Huang grabbed his hand in excitement. Is he my fated one?","The Asura King was much calmer in comparison. “Is this related to what you talked to Lady Houtu about?” He could tell the two of them had shared a long telepathic exchange earlier.","Zu An nodded before sharing the summary of what he had discussed with Houtu.","“The Six Paths’ power insignias...” the Asura King murmured.","He reached into his robe and took out a military seal. The seal was carved with glaring, domineering images, but its center was embedded with a beautiful, transparent gemstone that shone with a gentle light, mellowing the seal’s violent aura.","Zu An initially thought the gemstone was a diamond, but he quickly refuted that guess. The texture was different, and the gemstone looked far more mystical, as if it harnessed boundless power.","Sensing Zu An’s gaze, the Asura King explained, “This gemstone is the only teardrop left by a famous valkyrie of our Asura race. It is the Asura Path’s power insignia.”"]},{"number":2511,"title":"Chapter 2511: Chapter 2463: Seal","paragraphs":["“It’s a valkyrie’s teardrop?” Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected that to be the Asura race’s power insignia.","The Asura King nodded. “Our Asura race reveres war, but in our long history, she is the only one whom we deem a valkyrie.”","Zu An hadn’t known the Asura race for long, but he could tell they were proud individuals. A person whom they acknowledged to be a valkyrie had to be truly outstanding.","Princess Ni Huang added, “Our Asura race respects warlike traits like valiance and courage. Tears are deemed to be a symbol of weakness, even for women. Most Asuras never tear up in their entire life, yet she, despite being a valkyrie, shed this teardrop. You can imagine how precious it is.”","Zu An suddenly recalled how Princess Ni Huang hadn’t teared up even though her eyes had reddened. She couldn’t cry even when her close kinsman was facing impending death. This showed just how much of a taboo it was for Asuras to shed tears.","“Then wouldn’t it be considered a disgrace for the valkyrie to have shed a tear?” Zu An asked.","“It is indeed peculiar. There are many speculations about why the valkyrie shed the tear. Some say it was a tear of joy after defeating the Celestials. Some say she was grieving from the death of her lover...” Princess Ni Huang listed several reasons, but in the end, she laughed. “If you ask me, I’d say those are all nonsense. None of these fit the valkyrie’s character. They are all just guesses from nosy people. It’s a pity no one knows the true reason anymore.”","Zu An was more focused on acquiring the Six Paths’ power insignias, so he didn’t probe deeper into the reason behind the valkyrie’s tear. He took the seal and carefully stowed it away. “Rest assured that the forging process won't damage the seal. I’ll return it to you once the forging is completed.”","He had considered collecting the other power insignias first before borrowing this seal from the Asura race, but on second thought, it was possible for something to happen to the Asura race in the meantime, or for the Asura King to suddenly change his mind. It was safer for him to keep it with him.","The Asura King didn’t mind that. “You have saved not only me, but the entire Asura race. If you succeed in your endeavor, our Asura race can be freed from this goddamn place. That is a far greater favor. This seal is nothing in comparison.”","Zu An chuckled. “Put your mind at ease. I’ll do my best to free you from the underworld.”","Princess Ni Huang also spoke up. “Big brother Necropolis, I really want to travel with you, but I think I’ll have to stay behind to take care of my royal brother and ensure no one tries anything funny in the Asura race in the meantime.”","Being called ‘big brother Necropolis’ made Zu An’s eyelids twitch, though he was also glad that Princess Ni Huang couldn’t follow him. “Take good care of your brother. I’ll do my best to find the medicine, though...”","The Asura King revealed a gracious smile. “Don’t worry about it. I was already doomed to die, so I’m already thankful to have a shot at survival. Whether you find the medicine or not is up to chance. If it doesn’t work out, I only have my fate to blame.”","Zu An was amazed by the other party’s magnanimity. “Your words put my mind at ease. I’ll be taking my leave then!”","Princess Ni Huang saw him off. Even when they finally parted ways, she remained rooted on the spot while vehemently waving him off, reluctant to see him leave.","Zu An glanced at her with many thoughts in his mind. He had several words at the tip of his tongue, but none came out.","Leaving the Eye of the Ocean, he heard an ethereal yet familiar melody—it was 'Scenery of Home'. In the distance, he saw a beautiful figure strumming a harp, her movements so graceful that they were a feast for the eyes.","Zu An slowed his footsteps for fear of interrupting her. Mermaids were naturally gifted in music. Despite only having heard the melody once, the Mermaid Queen played it with far greater skill and emotion than him.","It was then that the Mermaid Queen noticed him. She was initially stunned, before tossing her Deep Sea Harp aside to leap into his chest, tightly embracing him. Her usually composed voice sounded hoarse as she exclaimed, “I thought you wouldn’t come back!”","Zu An’s arms hung awkwardly in mid-air. He hadn’t expected her to have such a huge reaction. Feeling her trembling body and the dampness on his clothes, he let out a sigh. Now I know why Gu Long said that a woman’s tears are the most formidable weapon in the world!","Despite knowing it was inappropriate, he couldn’t bring himself to callously push her away. His awkward hands hesitated for a few seconds before gently stroking her back.","However, his reciprocation only brought out the grievances the Mermaid Queen had felt over the past few days, and she cried even harder than before.","Zu An panicked. Why is she crying even harder now?","Little droplets wouldn’t stop falling from the Mermaid Queen’s cheeks, as if she was made of water. She cried for a long time before slowly regaining her composure.","She then wiped away her tears while awkwardly tidying the hair strands sticking to her cheeks. “Was I very ugly just now?”","“No, you were beautiful.” Zu An wasn’t lying. Most beauties looked ugly when they cried, but the Mermaid Queen still looked like an impeccable work of art that could evoke the sympathy of any spectators.","His compliment made the Mermaid Queen’s cheeks redden. She quickly lifted his arms and examined his body, asking, “Did you sustain any injuries while down there?”","Zu An felt warmth in his heart. “Don’t worry, I’m fine. You must have been afraid, waiting here for the last few days.”","“I’m not afraid of those monsters. I was more afraid that you wouldn’t be coming back,” the Mermaid Queen replied as her eyes reddened once more.","“Look, aren’t I back now? It was a fruitful trip. I received many answers to my previous doubts,” Zu An hurriedly replied, fearing she would cry once more.","“What’s beyond the Eye of the Ocean?” The Mermaid Queen’s curiosity got the better of her. “And what’s the background of those monsters from before?”","“They are the Shaman races...” Zu An quickly filled her in about what happened.","But the Mermaid Queen keenly sensed something. “That Princess Ni Huang must be gorgeous, right?”","Looking into her beautiful eyes, Zu An felt flustered, though he quickly shrugged it off as nonsense. It’s not as if she’s my girlfriend, and there’s nothing going on between me and Princess Ni Huang either.","Even so, he didn’t give her a direct answer. “The Asuras pride themselves on their strength and valor. Looks are of secondary importance to them.”","The Mermaid Queen nodded in satisfaction. “So, where do you intend to find those power insignias?”","“I’ll make a trip to the Fiend races' territory first.” Zu An was curious about Yumen Beiqing, and there were many questions in his mind that needed her answers.","He grabbed the Mermaid Queen’s hand and flew up with her. All of a sudden, however, his expression twisted. The previously damaged seals had been repaired from outside!"]},{"number":2512,"title":"Chapter 2512: Chapter 2464: The Shocking Development","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen also realized something was off, and her expression turned grim. “Something must have happened to the Ocean races!”","They knew she and Zu An had ventured into the Eye of the Ocean to investigate the situation. Considering how Zu An had just saved them not long ago, it didn’t make sense for them to seal off their path like that. There was a chance that something had happened to the Ocean races.","Zu An’s face darkened. “The Four Dragon Kings are fickle-minded scum!”","The Four Dragon Kings called the shots in the Ocean races. Without their permission, the others wouldn’t dare to rebuild the seals under their nose.","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “The East Sea Dragon King might be a coward, but he’s not that fickle-minded. The North Sea Dragon King has a candid personality, and you just saved him not too long ago. He’s not an ingrate. Something must have happened to the Ocean races. Could the Incestuous King have invaded us with his monster army...”","Only that could result in such a swift collapse of the Ocean races’ command chain.","“The Ocean races shouldn’t have been completely helpless even if the Incestuous King invaded, and they shouldn’t have been able to repair the seal so quickly either.” Zu An frowned. “Let’s deal with it after we return.”","The Mermaid Queen was worried. “But I fear we won’t be able to get out without anyone helping us from the outside.”","This wasn't the most powerful sealing formation, but its prowess wasn't to be scoffed at. It was with this sealing formation that the Ocean races had imprisoned the Shaman races and the death energy in the Eye of the Ocean for countless years. It was unlikely the two of them could breach it by themselves.","“Leave it to me.” Zu An made his way up to the seal and whipped out a giant saber.","The Mermaid Queen was surprised to find that the weapon resembled a tooth. It was none other than the Lord of Slaughter's mystical tooth.","Zu An’s ‘Steps of Rising Lotus’ had the power to transcend formations. With his enhanced knowledge of formations and spatial laws, he was more than capable of passing through this sealing formation, no matter how formidable it was. But it would be troublesome to bring the Mermaid Queen out with him that way.","Thus, he took out the mystical tooth and swung it. It sliced through the sealing formation as smoothly as cutting through butter.","He then turned back to the Mermaid Queen and said, “Let’s go.”","The Mermaid Queen blinked. This sealing formation had been built on by countless Ocean races’ experts over thousands of years, yet it was sliced through with such ease!","As expected of the man of miracles!","Not daring to dawdle, she quickly passed through the seal. Zu An did the same too.","The Mermaid Queen turned around to take a look. The sealing formation had lost its glow and dissipated.","“I hear fighting noises outside. Let’s head out to take a look.” Zu An grabbed her hand and quickly headed upward.","The Mermaid Queen was too concerned with what was happening outside to immerse herself in the joy of having her hand grabbed, however.","With Zu An’s incredible speed, it didn’t take them long to arrive at the source of the noises.","A group of black-clad Ocean race warriors had encircled another group of Ocean race warriors clad in blue, with the former having a significant manpower advantage. The blue-clad warriors were only holding on thanks to a beautiful woman in their center wielding a powerful artifact, but the situation was still dire for them. The black-clad warriors could afford to slip up many times, but the blue-clad warriors would be goners the moment they made a mistake.","“It’s the Peacock Princess!” the Mermaid Queen exclaimed upon seeing the beautiful woman.","The beautiful woman heard her voice and looked back in disbelief. “Big brother! Big sis queen!”","The black-clad warriors were also stunned to see Zu An and the Mermaid Queen. Without any hesitation, they turned tail and fled.","Zu An harrumphed. “You think you can get away?”","Waves of golden sword ki descended from the sky and pinned the black-clad warriors to the ground. They cried in agony, but they were unable to struggle free from the golden sword ki.","After capturing the black-clad warriors, Zu An finally flew over to the Peacock Princess’ side with the Mermaid Queen. “Princess, what happened here...”","“Big brother!” Before he could finish speaking, the Peacock Princess leaped into his chest and embraced him tightly.","Taking in her youthful fragrance, Zu An awkwardly eyed the Mermaid Queen. The two of them were still holding hands. It was truly a weird situation.","The Xuan-Su guards[1], who had been protecting the Peacock Princess, exchanged looks and saw shock and disappointment in each other’s eyes. They had never seen their princess getting so intimate with a man before.","They could already guess that Zu An was the one who had saved them and their princess. Their princess had been talking nonstop about him over the last few days, so much so that their ears were about to get calluses from hearing about his affairs.","The two of them were the Peacock Princess’ childhood friends, and they secretly adored her. However, neither thought that the other was worthy of the princess. It was only now, when they saw their princess falling in love with a hero, that their hearts finally settled down.","Only a man like that is worthy of our princess... but isn’t it too much for him to be holding the hand of the Ocean races’ number one beauty while hugging our princess?","The Mermaid Queen also had the weirdest expression. She didn’t know whether to continue holding Zu An’s hand or let go. She feared that if she abruptly retracted her hand, Zu An would think she was jealous and angry, but what right did she have to get angry? Not to mention, she had reacted in the same way as the Peacock Princess when she saw him earlier. But given the eyes on them, it would be awkward to continue holding his hand too...","In the end, she chose not to let go. It wasn’t easy to hold his hand. How can I let go that easily?","Unfortunately, the crowd took this as a verification of a rumor that had been spreading among the Ocean races. It was said that a man had appeared out of nowhere and dragged the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess into one bed. Gossips had fervently shared this news as if they had seen it with their own eyes, but many still refused to believe it.","They couldn’t say anything about the Peacock Princess, but they were more than familiar with the Mermaid Queen’s personality. How could someone as proud as her share a husband with other women? Which man in the world had the power to charm her that much?","But this made them realize they were short-sighted.","Such a man does exist in the world!","Zu An patted the Peacock Princess’ back to comfort her. When she finally calmed down, the first thing she said shocked Zu And and the Mermaid Queen. “The Ocean races are no more. There is no one left standing.”","1. Xuanxuan and Susu, the guards who came to the Ocean races' territory with the Peacock Princess ☜"]},{"number":2513,"title":"Chapter 2513: Chapter 2465: Aurora Poison Dragon","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen was stunned. She had guessed that something had happened to the Ocean races, but she hadn’t expected it to be so huge. The Ocean races have been destroyed? Including the Four Dragon Kings?","Zu An’s astonishment matched hers. Mojard is formidable, but surely not to this extent? The Ocean races are a great power. Them being destroyed in a few days seems too much.","Sensing their doubt, the Peacock Princess quickly waved her hands and clarified, “They aren’t dead yet, though they aren’t far from that.”","The Mermaid Queen was getting confused, so she quickly asked, “What happened?”","The Peacock Princess realized there was a huge misunderstanding here and hurriedly explained the matter.","Soon, Zu An and the Mermaid Queen understood what was going on. An illness had been spreading within the Ocean races; those afflicted with it would suffer from nausea and severe diarrhea. The patients were so weakened that they could only lie in bed, looking as if they were about to breathe their last.","Zu An frowned. “That doesn’t sound like an illness so much as a poison.”","The Peacock Princess nodded. “Everyone initially thought nothing of it, but the illness quickly spread across the Dragon Palaces and the rest of the Ocean race territory. It finally dawned upon them that someone had poisoned them, but it was already too late. Most people had already collapsed by then, and the physicians in the Dragon Palace were too busy saving themselves to treat anyone. Only a few lucky ones, like us, escaped the ordeal.”","“Where are the Four Dragon Kings? Did they not step forward to control the situation?” the Mermaid Queen asked.","The Peacock Princess shook her head. “The North Sea Dragon King had fallen into an inexplicable coma, so the other three Dragon Kings visited him. They didn’t find anything amiss, but shortly after, they fell into a coma as well. Rumors began spreading in the Dragon Palaces that recent happenings have evoked the Ocean Deity’s wrath, so he brought divine punishment upon the Ocean races.","“Nonsense!” The Mermaid Queen was infuriated to hear those words. “We are the children protected by the Ocean Deity. Why would she bring such a vile punishment upon us? Someone must be scheming something by spreading these rumors!”","The few remaining Ocean race warriors around them also didn’t think the Ocean Deity would punish them like that.","“What brings you all here? And who repaired the sealing formation over the Eye of the Ocean?” Zu An asked. So many things had happened in his absence that everything felt like a mystery to him. He could only gather as much information as possible to figure the situation out.","“I was discussing an alliance with the Ocean races when something happened to the Dragon Kings and the mysterious illness struck. That delayed our alliance talk. I was planning to help them overcome their current crisis first,” the Peacock Princess said.","“But as more people collapsed, rumors began spreading that it was our alliance with the Ocean races that brought about these troubles. There were even speculations that big brother is the one who brought that illness here. I realized someone was behind all this, so I rushed here to inform you...","“But by the time I reached this place, the seal had already been mended. I had no choice but to return to the Dragon Palace to gather a group of formation masters to remove the seal. Little did I expect to bump into these assassins. They were secretly tailing me to massacre us here.” The Peacock Princess patted her chest. “If not for your timely appearance, we would have been dead.”","Zu An coldly eyed the assassins. “Speak! Who sent you here?”","“Kill us!” The assassins looked away.","Zu An’s golden sword ki had not only pinned them to the ground but also sealed off their ki. They couldn’t even commit suicide. Still, a group that could be dispatched to assassinate the Peacock Princess wouldn't be made up of pushovers.","Zu An frowned. He couldn’t use his powers as the underworld’s master in this world, so he couldn’t drag them down to hell to interrogate them. It would be difficult to force a confession out of them.","Just then, the Mermaid Queen stepped forward. “Hand them to me.”","Zu An was taken aback.","The Mermaid Queen strummed her harp and played a graceful melody. She smiled at the assassins and asked, “Were you trying to harm me?”","The assassins looked both dazed and mesmerized. They shook their heads vehemently as they said, “Of course not. We wouldn’t think of doing so.”","“Do you want to see me upset?” the Mermaid Queen gently asked, looking exceptionally pitiful.","“No, we want you to be happy.” The assassins expressed their love for her.","“But I have so many doubts in my mind that I can’t be happy. Can you answer them for me?” The Mermaid Queen’s beautiful eyes turned an even deeper blue, shimmering with a sapphire-like luster.","“Of course, of course! My queen, please ask us anything!” the assassins hurriedly replied.","“Who sent you here today?” the Mermaid Queen asked with a sweet smile.","...","Witnessing the assassins obediently answering her every question like a bunch of dazed penguins flabbergasted everyone else, including Zu An. It was rumored in the Ocean races that the Mermaid Queen had reached her level of popularity because she was adept at seduction.","There might be some credence to the rumors, after all.","The Peacock Princess looked at the Mermaid Queen with a bizarre expression. I would have thought she was from the Fox race if I didn’t know better. What a femme fatale!","Zu An was amused. She is usually noble and dignified. I didn’t expect such a side of her. That being said, he was certain she had never employed such means on him, which showed that she was serious about getting to know him.","Soon, the Mermaid Queen received all her answers and turned to Zu An.","Zu An’s eyes glowed with intrigue as he heard a familiar name—the Aurora Poison Dragon!","It turned out the Aurora Poison Dragon was behind all these events. Using his aptitude at poison, he'd secretly constructed a plague formation in the Dragon Palace. Everyone in the Dragon Palace had been caught off guard and fallen into his trap.","To make things worse, the East Sea Dragon King had summoned all the Ocean races’ upper echelons to the Dragon Palace to discuss the alliance with the Fiend races, allowing the Aurora Poison Dragon to crush them in a single fell swoop.","“Wait, this can’t be right. The Four Dragon Kings should be strong enough to deal with his plague formation. If he was that formidable, he should have long since risen above the Four Dragon Kings to become the ruler of the Ocean races, right?” Zu An asked.","The Mermaid Queen quickly relayed that question to the assassins.","One of the assassins’ leaders replied, “The Aurora Poison Dragon has defected to the Incestuous King, under the promise that he would be crowned the Ocean races’ new king. The Incestuous King gave him an artifact known as the Soulfall Bell that can put others into a coma. It is with this artifact that he controlled the Four Dragon Kings.”","The crowd widened their eyes in realization. That explained why the North Sea Dragon King was the first to meet with a mishap. The Aurora Poison King was the North Sea Dragon King’s subordinate, making him the easiest target. The unconscious North Sea Dragon King had thus become bait for the remaining three Dragon Kings.","Zu An was amazed by this generation’s Mojard. He’s surprisingly competent."]},{"number":2514,"title":"Chapter 2514: Chapter 2466: Killing the Yellow Dragon","paragraphs":["Zu An was acquainted with Mojard, but he only knew the latter as a perverted old man who was fond of little girls. It was hard to believe that his name had once been spoken alongside that of the Monster Lord. It was only after coming to this era that he truly felt the Incestuous King’s prowess: The latter was both tenacious and farsighted. If not for Zu An’s abrupt arrival, the Ocean races would have been crippled by now. Even now that Zu An was here, there was no guarantee that he could unravel all of the Incestuous King’s schemes.","“The Soulfall Bell must be formidable to bring down the Four Dragon Kings,” the Mermaid Queen muttered worriedly.","Zu An replied, “Let’s rescue the Four Dragon Kings first before the enemy realizes we've escaped from the Eye of the Ocean. Otherwise, things will only get tougher.”","Once they learned that the two had slipped through the seal, Mojard and the Aurora Poison Dragon would prepare more means to deal with them. For the time being, they probably wouldn’t be expecting Zu An and the Mermaid Queen to have escaped from the seal so quickly, so this was an opening for them to capitalize on.","“Ask them where the Four Dragon Kings are imprisoned,” Zu An said.","The Mermaid Queen nodded. She repeated the question to the assassins; the latter, slaves to her charm, divulged everything they knew.","Zu An’s group made their way to where the Four Dragon Kings were imprisoned. The Peacock Princess was worried this would be too reckless, since they were outnumbered. Little did she expect Zu An to say, “I'm a one-man army, anyway.”","The Peacock Princess’ eyes glowed in amazement. That’s true. Big brother might not make a move often, but he always emerges victorious in in every battle. There’s no one in the Ocean races who is a match for him.","The Xuan-Su Guards exchanged looks. As expected of the man our princess fancies. His bragging skills are something we can’t hope to match.","Their group soon arrived at the Dragon Palace. Before Zu An descended into the Eye of the Ocean, the palace had been buzzing with life, but it was hard to spot even a single guard now. The poison formation had to have been truly formidable to have brought down most of the people in the Dragon Palace.","The scenery only changed when they approached the East Sea Dragon King’s sleeping chamber. A melody filled the air from nearby, and beautiful maids could be seen dancing from afar.","However, the one in the main seat wasn’t the East Sea Dragon King, but a black-robed dragon with two horns on his head. He looked younger and more suave than the East Sea Dragon King, but he emanated a coldness that left others feeling uncomfortable. He sat on the royal throne in an unruly fashion, laughing as he said, “Serve me well, and I’ll give you whatever the East Sea Dragon King previously gave you. I’ll also give you what he couldn’t give you.”","“Thank you, master!” The maids bowed before continuing the dance to showcase their most beautiful, graceful selves.","The black-robed dragon lay in the arms of a clam woman, occasionally opening his mouth to allow his female attendants to feed him fruits. He felt blissful, thinking that this was life’s peak.","The Mermaid Queen recognized him and roared, “Aurora Poison Dragon, how dare you?!”","The Aurora Poison Dragon was infuriated to have someone roar at him, but when he realized that the other party was the beautiful Mermaid Queen, he chuckled gleefully. “You came at a good time, Mermaid Queen. I haven’t decided on my wife yet. Just give the nod, and you’ll only be second to me among the Ocean races.”","“Dream on!” The Mermaid Queen was livid. Even the East Sea Dragon King treated her with the utmost respect, yet this lackey of the Nortth Sea Dragon King dared to utter such disrespectful words to her.","The Aurora Poison Dragon licked his lips and sneered, “The Four Dragon Kings have become a thing of the past. I will be the sole king of the Ocean races. My queen, I suggest you lower your head if you don’t want anything to happen to your Mermaid race.”","The Mermaid Queen’s face darkened. No matter how the Ocean races’ experts fancied her, they followed the rules and gave her the respect she deserved on the surface. And yet, this unscrupulous fellow would stoop this low to make her his!","“You 're the Aurora Poison Dragon?” Zu An walked out from behind the Mermaid Queen.","“Hah! How dare you address me by my name? Who do you think...” The Aurora Poison Dragon was halfway through his sentence when he saw Zu An’s appearance and swallowed his remaining words. “How did you get out?”","“You thought you could seal me in? What a pity your seal was insufficient,” Zu An replied calmly.","The Aurora Poison Dragon was horrified. He hurriedly reached for a bell in his robe and rang it.","As the ringing echoed, everyone in the room clutched their heads. Even the Mermaid Queen struggled to stand her ground. She recalled the Four Dragon Kings’ plight. This must be the Soulfall Bell. It’s formidable indeed!","The Aurora Poison Dragon rang it thrice. As he saw everyone stumbling onto the floor, he sneered, “As expected of the Soulfall Bell.”","He walked up to the Mermaid Queen and stared at the latter’s gorgeous face with adoring eyes. “My queen’s beauty knows no bounds. The East Sea Dragon King was a fool to not make you his. Now that I am king, I’ll make you mine.”","He reached for the Mermaid Queen’s face. The latter was in such a groggy state that she was unable to move despite being aware of what was happening. She could only watch as that disgusting hand slowly approached her.","While she was in despair, however, a hand suddenly shot out from the side and grabbed the Aurora Poison Dragon’s wrist.","The Aurora Poison Dragon was taken aback. He turned to Zu An and exclaimed, “How are you still able to move?”","“The Soulfall Bell is a potent weapon against souls, but it has a limit. Mojard would never have given it to you if it were unbeatable,” Zu An pointed out with a smile.","When the Soulfall Bell struck earlier, his Hundredwarble’s skill had activated automatically and neutralized its effect. But with the Dragon Palace under the Aurora Poison Dragon’s control, he'd been worried that the other party had other tricks up his sleeves, so he had decided to play along for a moment. However, he thought, This fellow is too lustful. He made his way straight to the Mermaid Queen. It would be too much if I continued holding back.","The Aurora Poison Dragon’s face darkened. He had heard about Zu An’s prowess and realized that he wouldn’t be a match for the latter. However, his strength had never lay in direct combat anyway.","A thick black fog suddenly puffed out from him and crept down his arms toward Zu An’s body. The Aurora Poison Dragon sneered, “No one dares to touch my body directly. I wouldn’t have been a match for you, but you courted your own death. Don’t blame me for this.”"]},{"number":2515,"title":"Chapter 2515: Chapter 2467: Temptation","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen's eyes widened in astonishment. The Aurora Poison Dragon was known for his lethal poison. Even though she was some distance away, just catching a whiff of his poison’s faint stench had already robbed her of her strength. She couldn’t even take out her Deep Sea Harp to play some poison-expelling melodies.","She regretted getting so caught up with the Soulfall Bell that she forgot about the Aurora Poison Dragon’s poison prowess. That was how he'd taken down the Dragon Palace’s experts in the first place. Now, Zu An was in danger, being so close to the other party’s poison fog.","While she was panicking, however, Zu An chuckled. “Is this the basis of your confidence?” With a wave of his sleeves, he transported the Mermaid Queen, Peacock Princess, and the others backward, out of range of the poison fog.","Both the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess were delighted to see that Zu An was fine. Indeed, how could someone as formidable as him fall to the Aurora Poison Dragon’s poison?","In truth, Zu An wasn’t as relaxed as he appeared.","The Primordial Origin Sutra had made his constitution impervious to a hundred poisons, but there were far more than a hundred poisons in the Myriad Worlds. His consciousness had started drifting off just by coming into contact with the poison fog, as if he was drunk. It finally dawned on him that the Primordial Origin Sutra didn’t make him immune to poisons; it merely granted him an extremely high resistance against most poisons. The Aurora Poison Dragon’s poison was so formidable that even he, despite his current cultivation, was unable to shrug it off.","On the other hand, the Aurora Poison Dragon was so scared that goosebumps covered his body. He was already channeling his poison as much as he could, and he couldn’t believe that someone could be so unfazed by it. Frightened, he hurriedly tried to retreat and put some distance between him and Zu An, but he was unable to shake off the latter’s iron grip.","“What poison formation did you use? Hand over the antidote!” Zu An eyed him coldly. He had noticed formation flags planted around the Dragon Palace, and each of them emanated bizarre poison energy. He had already destroyed the flags he came across, but there had to be more in the Dragon Palace. Furthermore, destroying the poison formation wouldn’t cure the already poisoned Ocean races’ experts.","“Antidote? The only fate awaiting those who are afflicted with my poisons is death!” the Aurora Poison Dragon sneered. He whipped out a dagger and sliced off his own arm before swiftly retreating from Zu An. He unleashed his true form, transforming into a massive black dragon. He bared his fangs at Zu An. “You are formidable, but you can’t save all of the Ocean races. Watch as everyone dies! Hahaha!”","Arrogant laughter followed as his silhouette became faint, and he looked as if he would disappear at any moment.","Zu An’s expression turned cold. “Do you think you can leave?” He directed his palm toward the Aurora Poison Dragon and exerted a powerful suction force that caused the space around the latter to suddenly constrict.","“How is this possible?” The Aurora Poison Dragon was horrified. He had just activated an escape artifact that should have have transported him to somewhere safe. He hadn’t expected the other party to even be able to control space.","Zu An was secretly glad he had learned Secrets of Spatial Distortion from the Monster World, or else he wouldn’t have been able to pull this off.","The black dragon struggled with all his might, but he was unable to break free, it was as if an invisible hand was clutching tightly onto him.","Zu An was worried the Aurora Poison Dragon had other tricks up his sleeves, so he absorbed the other party’s cultivation with the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra before asking again, “Where is the antidote?”","The abrupt loss of cultivation caused the Aurora Poison Dragon to regress from a massive dragon into a withered python. His heart turned cold, but he spat, “There’s no antidote. They will die with me. Hahaha.”","Zu An frowned at his warped smile. He tried to pass the Aurora Poison Dragon to the Mermaid Queen in hopes that her seduction art would work on him too.","The Mermaid Queen discreetly told Zu An, “I would never have used the seduction art if not for the urgent situation. It might not work on the Aurora Poison Dragon; his cultivation is too high.”","“It’s fine. He’s as good as a cripple,” Zu An replied.","The Mermaid Queen was taken aback. Despite witnessing the Aurora Poison Dragon withering from a majestic dragon into a python, she didn’t expect him to lose his cultivation. She composed herself and started questioning the latter.","The Aurora Poison Dragon’s eyes became dazed. “There is no antidote to my poison formation. The only one who can lift my poison is the successor of the Human race’s Firecloud Cave...”","Zu An had been planning to visit the human side to find their power insignia, so he could visit the Firecloud Cave while he was at it.","Hold on, could the Human Path’s power insignia be my Human Emperor Seal?","While he was in a daze, an eerie voice echoed from afar, “How incredible. Not even the seal could hold you in.”","The Aurora Poison Dragon finally regained consciousness and called out, “Save me, Incestuous King!”","Zu An and the others looked over and saw a figure outside the Dragon Palace. Who else could it be other than Mojard? He was accompanied by many monster experts, too.","Zu An’s heart sank. He spread out his divine sense and discovered that the Dragon Palace was filled with monster troops. They had been encircled!","Mojard eyed the Aurora Poison Dragon and sneered, “You’re already a cripple. Why should I save you?”","The Aurora Poison Dragon was stunned for a moment, but then he was overwhelmed with fright. “I can still help you control the Ocean races! You promised to make me the next Ocean races’ king!”","Mojard couldn’t be bothered to look at him. “How can you control the Ocean races in your current state, let alone be crowned their king?”","The others were amazed by how cold-hearted the monsters were, to cast the Aurora Poison Dragon away so quickly.","The Aurora Poison Dragon realized he was no longer of any use to Mojard and exclaimed, “Incestuous King, without my help, you wouldn’t have been able to kill the North Sea’s crown prince, drive a wedge between the Ocean races and Fiend races, and bring down the Dragon Palace so quickly! How can you abandon me like that?!”","The expressions of the remaining Ocean races’ experts turned cold. Mojard was indeed behind all these things. It was finally clear how he had been able to pull them off so easily. It turned out that he'd had the Aurora Poison Dragon as his spy!","Mojard smiled. “What’s the point of saying that? I would have honored my promise to make you the Ocean races’ king if you had the capability to back it up. But you don’t. I can’t prop you up even if I want to.”","He finally turned to Zu An and suggested, “Why don’t you work with us? You can be the next Ocean races’ king and take the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess as your concubines. I’ll even take care of their races on your behalf. All you have to do is nod, and you can have everything the East Sea Dragon King and the Aurora Poison Dragon dreamed about.”"]},{"number":2516,"title":"Chapter 2516: Chapter 2468: A Cloud-Piercing Arrow Brings Forth an Encounter With a Thousand Soldiers!","paragraphs":["“Ocean races’ king?” Zu An laughed. That would have been a decent offer for most people, but there was no reason for him to be interested in becoming a mere Ocean races’ king. After all, he was the king of the world!","He smiled at the Incestuous King and retorted, “Why don’t you defect to my side instead? I’ll help you become the Monster Lord. You must be dissatisfied, having to lower your head to the Monster Lord.”","Mojard was startled. He hadn’t expected Zu An to return those words to him, and in truth those words struck a chord in his heart. In recent years, their master had been showing favoritism to the Monster Lord. When their master went into closed-door training, the Monster Lord had started purging those opposed to him and planted his aides in important positions.","In truth, Mojard had come to the Ocean races to avoid the Monster Lord. He was hoping to bring the Ocean races under his control so he could compete with the Monster Lord in the future. He had never voiced such thoughts aloud, so no one should have known about his intention. How had this man learned about it?","There was no way Mojard would admit to it in front of so many people, especially since the Monster Lord was currently at the peak of his influence, so he sneered, “Since you refuse to listen to reason, you shouldn’t blame me for not showing mercy.”","With a wave of his hand, countless monsters rushed in and encircled Zu An and the others. They pushed in large artifact cannons that clearly boasted tremendous firepower at a glance. These cannons seemed designed to be used on huge armies, and it seemed like massive overkill deploying them for a mere ten people. This showed how much of a threat the monsters viewed Zu An as.","Knowing he had the advantage here, Mojard smiled. “You’re indeed powerful, but there’s only so much you can do alone. Against an army, your only fate is to die.”","He had been secretly using the Aurora Poison Dragon to drive a wedge between the Ocean races and the Fiend races while discreetly deploying his core army here to support him. He hadn’t gone all out in his previous clash with Zu An, but he was still wary of the latter, which was why he'd made thorough preparations this time.","The tight encirclement of the monster army caused the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess to tense up. With most of the Ocean races’ experts bedridden, there was very little they could do against such a huge army. As members of their respective races’ upper echelons, they understood the cruelty of war. No matter how strong an individual was, soldiers could use all kinds of formations to neutralize their attacks. An individual couldn't hope to defy an entire army.","Their bitter expressions further stoked Mojard’s glee. “This is your last chance. You might be able to last a while against my army, but the same can’t be said about your companions. Can you bear to see your lovers die like that?”","Seeing how the Incestuous King was trying to divide them even during a time like this, the Mermaid Queen turned to Zu An and said, “I’ll stand by your decision. Don’t listen to that scum.”","The Peacock Princess said in agreement, “Me too!”","Seeing the conviction in their eyes, Zu An smiled. “The situation isn’t that bad yet.”","The two women were confused. With things having gotten to this point, what tricks do you have to turn things around?","Zu An turned to Mojard and said, “You have an army; however, I have an army too.”","He took out the Valkyrie Tear. It had been placed on a military seal that allowed him to mobilize the asura army. To thank him for saving the Asura race, the Asura King and his little sister had given him this seal and taught him how to use it.","A cloud-piercing arrow brings forth an encounter with a thousand soldiers!","Zu An murmured obscure words that caused the military seal to light up. The surroundings began to quake.","“Be careful!” Sensing the massive spatial turbulence in the surroundings, Mojard ordered his soldiers to remain vigilant.","Countless figures suddenly appeared behind Zu An, accompanied by an occasional elephant roar.","Everyone present rubbed their eyes in disbelief. They hadn’t expected such a terrifying army to appear out of thin air. The soldiers had three heads and six arms, making them look fearsome. However, their leader, seated atop a white elephant, was a beautiful woman dressed in revealing clothes.","The woman leaped down from the white elephant and descended to Zu An’s side. She grabbed Zu An’s arm with a radiant smile. “Big brother Necropolis, I didn’t expect to meet you again so soon!”","The Mermaid Queen was startled by how intimate they were. This must be Princess Ni Huang. She’s beautiful. No wonder he avoided answering my question. Their closeness also suggests that there might be more to their relationship.","But when she thought about how the other party called Zu An ‘big brother Necropolis’, she couldn’t help but smile in triumph. Looks like he didn’t reveal his true identity to her. I’m still ahead of her in the race.","The Peacock Princess was taken aback too. How did big brother hook up with a princess when he was only down there for a few days? Isn’t big sis queen angry? Why is she smiling?","The Xuan-Su Guards stared at the Peacock Princess in astonishment. Why is our princess not angry when another woman hugs the man she fancies?","Zu An smoothly retracted his arm from her grasp and said, “My apologies for bothering you so soon, princess.”","“Your problem is our Asura race’s problem. Besides, there's nothing we like more than war. Only through endless war can we become stronger!” Princess Ni Huang quickly grasped the situation by surveying the surroundings.","Her eyes soon fell on the Peacock Princess and the Mermaid Queen.","The first one is beautiful, but she’s still too young. The other one, though, is in her prime, and I can tell she is interested in big brother Necropolis.","Princess Ni Huang was thinking of having Zu An introduce those two women when she suddenly heard hearty laughter not too far away. Ox Head, Horse Face, Golden Cangue, and Silver Chain had arrived with their shaman army to encircle the monster army.","Those from the Ocean races were stunned to see the shaman army. They were reminded of the battle they'd fought at the Eye of the Ocean.","“Don’t worry, they're my friends now,” Zu An said.","The word ‘friends’ brought smiles onto the faces of Ox Head and Horse Face. “Indeed, we are good friends now. Anyone who bullies our friend will get it!”","Ox Head slammed his massive axe onto the floor, jolting open a massive crevice over thousands of meters long. They had tagged along because they were worried the Asura race would win over Zu An and convince him to turn against the Shaman races. They thought it would be good to have Zu An owe them a favor now.","This put Mojard in a tough spot. His face looked as if he'd smelled something foul. The upper hand should have been his, but in the blink of an eye, he was suddenly the one encircled here."]},{"number":2517,"title":"Chapter 2517: Chapter 2469: This Place Forbids Forbidding","paragraphs":["These enemies were the beings sealed under the Eye of the Ocean, and they were not to be trifled with. To make things worse, the monsters had no intelligence about the multiple-armed race.","There must be another world sealed beneath the Eye of the Ocean. I must report this to my master—there is a new world to be conquered!","The Incestuous King squeezed out a smile and said, “It’s a misunderstanding. There must be a misunderstanding somewhere.”","The Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess were baffled. They were so used to Mojard’s arrogant attitude that they couldn’t believe he could change his ttune that quickly.","While everyone else was in a daze, however, Mojard took back control of the Soulfall Bell and shook it. Everyone who heard the bell lost their balance.","Zu An unleashed the Lion’s Roar before saying, “Be careful. That bell can sway one’s soul.”","Princess Ni Huang snapped out of her daze and sneered, “Easy peasy!”","She waved the command flag, and deep war horns echoed from the asura army, greatly raising their morale. The shaman army also began roaring, as if provoked by the asura army’s war horn. They had fought against each other for so many years that it actually aided their coordination.","Pah!","Under the reverberation of all these noises, Mojard’s Soulfall Bell began to crack. A single artifact could only do so much before an entire army.","Mojard’s face darkened. “Kill them!”","Countless skills were conjured through the army formations and hurled toward the asura and shaman army.","“Get into formation!”","However, in response, the asura and shaman army also conjured skills that neutralized over half of the monster army’s bombardment. The remaining attacks fell on their own army formation’s transparent barrier. This exchange completely lit up the area around the Dragon Palace.","Once again, Zu An confirmed that only an army could deal with an army. Even though the Rune Weapon Chart allowed him to be a one-man army, there were limits to what he could do alone. He wouldn’t fear an average enemy force, but dealing with elites from the Monster World at its peak would still pose some trouble to him. Judging from their bombardment, he could tell that the monster army was filled with experts, and their defensive formations were formidable. Even if he unleashed an airstrike via his Rune Weapon Chart, its prowess would likely be greatly reduced by their defensive formations.","It was fortunate he had won over the Asura race and the Shaman races, or else the situation would have been tricky.","While both sides bombarded each other with skills, the monsters began charging at the shamans and asuras, whipping out their weapons and claws to rip apart their enemies. Their goal was to reach the formation masters. Once the enemy’s formation masters were down, they would be able to easily massacre everyone else. For the same reason, every army always ensured their formation masters were tightly guarded.","The fight intensified. Blood and flesh flew everywhere. The asuras and shamans boasted superior individual fighting prowess, but the monsters were veterans who had conquered countless worlds. It was a surprisingly close fight. There were so many casualties that even the army commanders were startled.","Zu An’s expression turned grim. He couldn’t let the asuras and shamans suffer such severe losses when they were here to help him. Thus, he charged at Mojard.","“This place forbids...” Mojard began using his soulspeak.","Something must be wrong with his head. He dares to use soulspeak despite suffering a huge setback against me.","“What you lookin’ at?”","“...”","“This place forbids teleportation!” Mojard still completed his soulspeak somehow.","Zu An suddenly felt so heavy that his body plummeted from the sky. He stared at Mojard in confusion, not comprehending why the latter hadn’t been compelled to reply ‘ I’m looking at you, shithead! ’ This was the first time that skill had failed.","His gaze soon fell on Mojard’s helmet. He hadn’t paid that helmet much notice as the latter was commanding an army, but from the looks of it now, it was probably the helmet that was making a difference here.","Zu An’s confusion delighted Mojard. “Heh, did you think I would keep falling for the same move? I had this artifact specially forged to tune out external noises and soulspeak.”","Mojard wouldn’t be affected by ‘What you lookin’ at?’ if he couldn’t hear Zu An’s voice. He could decipher what others were saying by reading their lips, so not being able to hear wasn’t an issue for him.","Zu An was stunned, thinking, He looks awfully like Magneto.","He unhesitatingly charged up to Mojard, hoping to interrupt his soulspeak by engaging him in close combat.","The two of them exchanged a blow. While Mojard was being knocked back, he made use of this opening to declare, “This place forbids external aid.”","The Mermaid Queen was shocked to discover that her buffs no longer worked on Zu An.","Zu An’s speed was reduced by almost 20%. Soulspeak sure is troublesome to deal with.","Mojard dodged Zu An’s attack while making another declaration, “This place forbids...”","Soulspeak wasn't omnipotent. Certain conditions had to be fulfilled before it could be used, and more often than not, it could only achieve auxiliary effects. Otherwise, Mojard could have simply ordered his enemies to kill themselves. Also, the effectiveness of soulspeak was greatly dependent on the power disparity between the aggressor and the victim. For instance, he was able to outright forbid the Peacock Princess from retaliating against him, but he couldn’t do the same for Zu An. Not only would it be useless, but he would also suffer a rebound if he tried to do so. Thus, he carefully set up rules one by one. While these rules might not seem like much, they slowly turned the tides in his favor.","He viewed his previous defeat to Zu An as a great humiliation. On top of forging his noise-cancellation helmet, he had also thought hard about how he could subdue this mysterious fellow. It wasn't without reason he was ranked third in the Monster World. He had accrued much combat experience in the years he spent conquering countless worlds. He'd meticulously planned the rules he would impose to avoid backlash while creating the conditions required to achieve victory in the shortest time possible.","If everything went according to plan, he would need just one more rule to ensure his decisive advantage. Once that happened, the enemy could struggle all he wanted, but it would be futile.","But Zu An beat him by declaring, “This place forbids forbidding.”","Mojard was stunned. Do you think we’re playing house? How can you forbid forbidding? Do you take yourself as the God of Creation or something?","He was about to declare the final rule to ensure his victory when he suddenly stiffened up. Much to his shock, he was unable to voicetthat rule!"]},{"number":2518,"title":"Chapter 2518: Chapter 2470: One Man Army","paragraphs":["Mojard was stunned. Unable to believe this to be true, he once again tried to impose his rule, “This place...”","But he was unable to verbalize the word ‘forbids’. This left him dumbstruck.","That fellow is capable of soulspeak too? Ah, that makes sense. If he can stop me with his ‘What you lookin’ at?’, it would make sense for him to be versed in soulspeak too.","On top of that, the other party’s mastery of soulspeak appeared to be above his. With a single rule, the other party had crippled his skill for good.","Hold on! I crafted a helmet just to counter him, so why did I still fall for his trick?","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. It was fortunate he had reacted fast and used his Keyboard Come’s Word Spoken, Order Implemented. He usually avoided using Keyboard Come because he had to pay a significant price for it. Luckily, what he sought to realize through Keyboard Come this time wasn’t too difficult, and his grasp of his powers had gotten much deeper due to his higher cultivation.","Due to Keyboard Come’s side effect, skin fissures appeared all over his body, but he quickly healed up thanks to his formidable regenerative prowess. Others failed to even notice that he had sustained severe injuries for a split second.","Keyboard Come was a high-order power that realized everything he said. It didn’t have to be heard, so Mojard’s specially-forged helmet couldn’t stop it.","Seeing the tragedies happening on the battlefield, Zu An decided to end things quickly to minimize the casualties suffered by the shamans and the asuras. He opened his palm, revealing a droplet of yellow fluid. It was Oblivion River Water!","He gently flicked it, and the water droplet scattered toward the monster army. Despite being just a single droplet, it quickly expanded into a small stream, then a rapid river, and finally a massive tsunami.","The asuras and shamans had lived in the underworld long enough to recognize the Oblivion River Water right away. They immediately retreated in horror.","The monster army, however, was ignorant. They thought it was an ordinary water element skill. Some of the stronger monsters even spewed fiery flames in an attempt to neutralize the water. Their confidence wasn't unfounded, as the flames they spewed looked even more formidable than the massive tsunami.","But the Oblivion River Water showed no signs of evaporating. Instead, the flames were extinguished immediately upon contact. This shocked the monster experts. They couldn’t imagine there being any water in the world that they couldn’t extinguish after combining their powers.","It was a pity they would never know the answer. As the Oblivion Water River crashed down on them, their baleful expressions became dazed. They looked like zombies bathing in water.","Not having expected the water to be this potent, the others in the monster army were horrified. They tried to flee, but it was too late. Meanwhile, the monster formation masters formed hand seals so quickly that smoke almost rose from their palms. In order to stop the advancement of the terrifying tsunami, they unleashed all their skills and formations.","But the Oblivion River Water was impervious to their means. None of their skills and formations could stop its flow. The massive tsunami passed through their barriers and drowned them. In an instant, the sharp-witted monster formation masters turned into idiots.","The monster army crumbled. They had never seen anything like this before. All of them turned tail and fled, not hesitating to trample on their allies just so they could get away a second faster.","But the asuras and shamans wouldn’t let them get away so easily. They swooped in and blocked all the monsters’ paths of retreat, driving them back toward the Oblivion River Water. They were so familiar with the Oblivion River that they knew what to do without having to coordinate with Zu An. They howled in excitement. It had been a long time since they'd had such an exhilarating battle. They didn’t even have to do much; all they had to do was stand in place and reap the prey headed their way.","Mojard was on the verge of breaking down. He hadn’t expected his powerful army to collapse in the blink of an eye. And the culprit behind this is none other than that man!","His eyes no longer contained anger; they only reflected his fear. He had never seen a single person subduing an entire army. Even the Lord of Slaughter would struggle to go against an army head-on, but this fellow had single-handedly wiped out his elites.","What in the world is that yellow water?","He had seen plenty of things from conquering many worlds, but he had never felt the aura of death as vividly from anything other than that water. In the end, he abandoned his army and ran away.","He had previously lost to Zu An, but he'd still challenged the latter again because he thought his specially forged helmet and his elite army of experts who had conquered many worlds together with him would make a difference this time. And yet, everything was lost in an instant. His army was crushed, and his greatest weapon, soulspeak, was sealed off once more. Furthermore, the fact that Zu An had such a powerful artifact in his arsenal suggested that he hadn’t gone all out in their previous battle.","Who knows if he has even more tricks up his sleeves? It would be foolish to fight against someone like that!","Having lost his courage, Mojard fled. His escape caused the monster army’s morale to completely collapse. The monsters frantically fled in all directions, only to be met with the asuras and shamans’ stalwart army formations. In the end, they were all either massacred or washed away by the tsunami.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. It’s a good thing the asuras and the shamans cooperated well with me. The Oblivion River Water alone couldn’t have washed away all the monsters. On top of that, this trick won’t work as well in the future once the monsters are on guard against it.","Looking at the fleeing Mojard, Zu An took out a giant bow.","The weapon drew the attention of the experts on the battlefield. They sensed terrifying energy converging toward the bow. Could this be a deity-grade artifact? How does this man have so many formidable artifacts?","In contrast to the crowd’s fearful gaze, the Mermaid Queen looked at Zu An with gentle eyes. The more powerful he was, the happier it made her. If anything, her admiration for him was growing. She had met many outstanding men over the years, but none had ever won her admiration. Instead, those men fell at her skirt. No wonder my descendant fell in love with this man. I can feel myself succumbing too...","Princess Ni Huang had been observing the Mermaid Queen. Something is wrong with this woman. She’ll be a strong rival in the future.","The Peacock Princess was the only composed one among the three. Her eyes were focused on the bow, as she found it oddly familiar.","An invisible arrow had manifested on the Sun Slaying Bow. Its tremendous energy was causing the space in front of it to distort.","All of a sudden, the arrow morphed into a stream of light that instantaneously struck the distant Mojard. There was a massive explosion of light. Mojard screamed in agony as he exploded into a blood mist."]},{"number":2519,"title":"Chapter 2519: Chapter 2471: Die With Me","paragraphs":["Zu An flitted up to where the arrow exploded. Terrifying shockwaves were still rippling outward from the center of the explosion. He quietly looked at the bloody surroundings.","The Mermaid Queen and the others rushed over too. They were startled by the devastating shockwaves.","“It’s too little blood. He’s probably still alive,” Princess Ni Huang voiced her conclusion.","“He is the renowned Incestuous King, the third-strongest expert of the Monster World. I wouldn’t be surprised if he has some escape method,” the Mermaid Queen said.","“Hmph! So what if he’s the third-strongest expert? He’s lacking a lot compared to big brother Necropolis!” Princess Ni Huang looked at Zu An with an admiring gaze. I’d expect no less from the man I fancy!","The Mermaid Queen rolled her eyes.","The Peacock Princess turned her attention from the Sun Slaying Bow to Zu An’s name. I should ask big sis queen whether Necropolis is his real name.","“This works out too. It’s fate that he escaped.” Zu An chuckled.","The other women were taken aback. Why does he seem happy about Mojard’s escape?","Of course Zu An was happy.","His earlier arrow had been more than enough to kill Mojard, but as he was releasing the attack, it had suddenly dawned on him that the future wouldn’t line up if Mojard died here. Fearing the chain effects that could ensue, he'd held back 30% of his energy. If not for that, Mojard wouldn’t have been able to escape.","That being said, after being struck by an arrow from the Sun Slaying Bow, it was unlikely Mojard would recover anytime soon. Zu An suddenly recalled Mojard’s mention of the severe injury he'd suffered in the past that caused him to lose his memories and his cultivation to regress.","Zu An frowned. Did I leave that injury on Mojard?","He turned to the decimated monster army. If I’m not wrong, they should be Mojard’s core force. With their death, Mojard no longer has the means to compete with the Monster Lord. No wonder he became like that in the future. He lost his pride and his foundation.","Zu An was amazed by fate’s mysticism. He wondered if this was all predestined or his doing.","The next thing they had to do was to clean up the battlefield, but both the asuras and the shamans looked hesitant. Zu An understood their worry and retracted the Oblivion River Water.","Only then did the asuras and shamans excitedly rush in to loot the items. These were the monster army’s elites; there were many experts in their ranks, so the artifacts and resources they had were not to be scoffed at.","Zu An allowed them to take whatever they wanted. I’ll consider this their compensation. Otherwise, they would be no different from slaves if I kept making them fight for free.","Princess Ni Huang approached Zu An and said, “Big brother Necropolis, we can’t stay here for long due to the curse. We’ll have to return soon.”","Her voice betrayed her yearning. She lamented not being able to stay with Zu An. Those two women are lucky!","“I’ll free you from your plight once I gather all six power insignias,” Zu An promised.","“I believe you can do it. I’ll be waiting...” Princess Ni Huang had many more words to say, but she could already feel a powerful summoning force compelling her to return. Fortunately, some things could be expressed without words.","She tiptoed and planted a kiss on Zu An’s cheek.","Zu An was taken aback.","The Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess were shocked.","The two of them were on the verge of exploding. Does that woman think we’re invisible?!","Princess Ni Huang was about to move on to Zu An’s lips when the curse dragged her back to the underworld.","The Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess hurriedly stopped moving. To alleviate the awkwardness in the air, the Mermaid Queen asked, “Where did Princess Ni Huang go?”","“She returned to the underworld. They can’t leave that place for long.” Looking at the disappearing asura army, Zu An made a mental note to take note of the time if he summoned them again in the future.","Ox Head and Horse Face approached Zu An and passed him a round token. “Brother, if you need anything, you can call us with this token. I assure you we’ll do better than those asuras!”","They didn’t want Zu An to get too close to the Asura race. That could be detrimental to the Shaman races in the future.","On top of that, this battle had been fruitful for them. They'd obtained many resources that couldn’t be found in the barren underworld. It was two birds with one stone—they could get on closer terms with Zu An while enriching themselves.","Zu An accepted their token with a smile. He was more than happy to befriend Ox Head and Horse Face, who were going to play important roles in the underworld in the future.","Soon, a mysterious power transported Ox Head, Horse Face, and the shamans back to the underworld.","Zu An examined the round token. It was the size of a mooncake, carved with bizarre human faces. He had seen similar images on the Shaman races’ accessories. It contained faint spatial energy that allowed him to summon the shamans, just like the Asura race’s military seal.","“Why did that woman call you big brother Necropolis?” the Peacock Princess asked.","“I’ll use Necropolis as my name from this day on.” Zu An thought that he still needed an identity. He couldn’t remain unknown in history after doing so many things, so he decided to use an apt name for it.","This was the perfect name for his new identity since he hadn’t met the Necropolis Emperor at the Eye of the Ocean, and no one in the underworld had ever heard of the latter. Thanks to Mi Li’s explanation, Zu An had a rough grasp of how spacetime worked.","It felt mystical to enter history, create it, and become a part of it.","“Alright, big brother Necropolis!” The Peacock Princess was happy to have finally learned his name.","The Mermaid Queen smiled as well. I’m so happy! I’m the only one who knows his real name. Despite their close ties, she wasn’t planning to share this information with the Peacock Princess.","The Peacock Princess wanted to ask about the underworld, the Asura race and the Shaman races, and how he'd won the heart of yet another beautiful princess in just a few days. But with Zu An and the Mermaid Queen focused on saving the Ocean races, she couldn’t bring herself to ask those questions.","“Where are the Four Dragon Kings?” Zu An asked the Aurora Poison Dragon.","The earlier situation had shaken the Aurora Poison King’s nerves. He hadn’t expected the powerful Incestuous King and the invincible monster army to be obliterated just like that. Knowing he was doomed, he laughed madly. “Hahaha, you will never find them! The Ocean races are finished! Everyone shall die with me! My life shall not be in vain!”","He activated his final trick and exploded, causing his poisonous blood to diffuse into the surroundings."]},{"number":2520,"title":"Chapter 2520: Chapter 2472: Refinement Formation","paragraphs":["The crowd was taken aback.","The Aurora Poison Dragon was known for his poisons, with his body containing incomparably lethal toxin. Even a droplet of his poison blood could erode one’s bones and even one's very soul.","Zu An opened his hand, and the light around the Aurora Poison Dragon’s explosion suddenly distorted as if there was a black hole there. The poisoned blood and flesh bits swiftly receded until they were all squeezed into a tiny ball in Zu An’s hands.","The Mermaid Queen and Peacock Princess exhaled in relief as they complimented Zu An’s methods. If not for him, they would all be goners.","Zu An was relieved that he possessed the Taotie’s Heaven-devouring Sutra and was adept at spatial manipulation. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to swiftly control the Aurora Poison Dragon’s self-detonation. He channeled his primordial ki and quickly cleansed that tiny ball of poison, leaving behind a pristine bead.","The Mermaid Queen was overjoyed. “That’s the Aurora Poison Dragon’s inner core! You can finally save your little sister!”","She had initially been worried when she heard that Zu An was looking for the Aurora Poison Dragon; the latter had always been elusive, with hardly anyone ever seeing him. There was also no guarantee that the Aurora Poison Dragon would have an inner core, considering how difficult it was to form one.","Who could have expected the Aurora Poison Dragon to deliver such a pure inner core on his own accord?","Zu An smiled as well. Finally some good news. I wonder if Xiaoxi and the others have found the other ingredient.","The Peacock Princess alternated her gaze between the two of them. To think that big brother has a little sister, and big sis queen knows that he’s trying to save her. I know far too little about big brother. Should I ask big sis queen for more details, or should I talk to big brother more...","Just then, the Mermaid Queen murmured worriedly, “But now that the Aurora Poison Dragon is dead, we might never find the Four Dragon Kings.”","With the Ocean races poisoned, they would be doomed if they lost the Four Dragon Kings too.","Zu An stowed away the Aurora Poison Dragon’s inner core and said, “Don’t worry, I know where he hid the Four Dragon Kings.”","“How do you know?” the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess blurted out in unison.","Zu An chuckled. The Aurora Poison Dragon is too naive. He thinks it’ll all be over just because he’s dead. Little does he know I’m the underworld’s master.","Much of his authority over the underworld was restricted, but he still had no problem tying down a deceased soul. His position granted him natural dominance over the dead. The Aurora Poison Dragon would find him a thousand times more terrifying than when he was alive. That fear originated from the soul, and there was no way to circumvent it.","Soon enough, the Aurora Poison Dragon revealed the whereabouts of the Four Dragon Kings.","Zu An brought the group to a cave around fifty kilometers away from the Dragon Palace. The cave was well hidden amid corals, so much so that it was possible to pass by this place a hundred times without finding it.","“Be careful. There are many vile traps planted in the vicinity,” the Mermaid Queen warned.","She could see through some of the traps and formations, though she couldn’t decipher all of them. Regardless, it was unlikely those traps and formations were there to welcome unwanted guests like them.","Zu An calmly instructed, “Don’t worry. Stay behind me.”","He strutted into the cave as if those traps didn’t exist.","The two women were taken aback. They hurriedly followed him, thinking they could at least protect his flanks.","Then, countless traps suddenly activated. Many skills were blasted in their direction, but they suddenly dissipated halfway through their trajectory.","The Mermaid Queen and Peacock Queen exchanged looks; they could see the awe in each other’s eyes. It looked as if Zu An was casually strutting around, but he had precisely stepped on every trap to trigger them in order to neutralize them.","This made them burst into laughter. Indeed, we shouldn’t need to worry about someone of his caliber.","Behind them, the Xuan-Su Guards sighed. They had finally given up. The gap between Zu An and them was so huge that they couldn’t even gauge how far ahead he was. No wonder our proud princess fell in love with him at first sight. Only someone like that is worthy of her.","For a moment there, they even wondered if their princess was worthy of him.","Soon, they were inside the cave. It looked small outside but was spacious inside. Four naturally-formed stone pillars were present in four different directions, seemingly propping up the ceiling.","The Four Dragon Kings were each bound to a pillar. They displayed none of their usual majesty. Their clothes were unkempt, their heads hung limply, and their faces were ghastly pale.","“Dragon King! Dragon King!”","The Ocean races’ experts rushed up to their respective Dragon Kings, but no matter how they called for them, the Four Dragon Kings’ eyes remained shut. Their faces were warped in pain as if they were in a nightmare.","The Mermaid Queen anxiously warned, “Be careful! There seem to be formations beneath us!”","That alerted the others to the crimson formation marks beneath the stone pillars the Four Dragon Kings were bound to. The formation marks felt malevolent, and they made the crowd feel uncomfortable.","“This...” The Peacock Princess narrowed her eyes. She faintly sensed the vileness of those formations.","“It’s a refinement formation constructed using the Four Dragon Kings’ blood to refine their primordial spirits into pills,” Zu An explained. “They're in pain because their primordial spirits are being refined, but they are still holding on thanks to their powerful cultivation. If we had failed to find this place, eventually, their primordial spirits would have been refined and their blood essences would have been made into pills.”","The crowd was taken aback. The Mermaid Queen exclaimed, “What a vile formation!”","“The Aurora Poison Dragon was ambitious enough, trying to refine the Four Dragon Kings into pills. Had he consumed those pills, his strength would have surpassed the Four Dragon Kings and perhaps even reached a level rivaling the Incestuous King.” Zu An was impressed.","The Mermaid Queen had previously told him about the Aurora Poison Dragon. The latter had been scorned in the Dragon race due to his unique constitution, so he'd received no resources and had to earn everything by himself. It had to have taken tremendous willpower and meticulous planning for an unaffiliated cultivator to come this far. It was unfortunate he had chosen the wrong path.","Zu An instructed the Ocean races’ experts to destroy the refinement formation and retrieve the Four Dragon Kings. After he fed the Four Dragon Kings pills that healed their primordial spirits, they slowly regained consciousness.","They bowed deeply toward Zu An to thank him. “We will never forget the grace you have shown us!”","They had still been able to perceive their surroundings despite being unconscious. They'd resigned themselves to having their primordial spirits refined into fodder for the Aurora Poison Dragon. At most, they could have only lasted half a day more.","Who could have expected Zu An to swoop in at the last moment to save them?","“You’re too polite.” Zu An supported them to their feet. “You should slowly recover after resting for a few days. The four of you are strong enough to survive the Aurora Poison Dragon’s poison formation, but the same can’t be said about the others. We have to save them right away.”"]},{"number":2521,"title":"Chapter 2521: Chapter 2473: Firecloud Cave","paragraphs":["Chapter 2473: Firecloud Cave","“There’s something strange about the poison inflicted by the Aurora Poison Dragon. None of the Ocean races’ doctors know how to treat it,” the Peacock Princess said. She had gotten close to several people from the Ocean races in the past few days, allowing her to obtain information from them.","One of the Ocean race elders affirmed those words. “I have some fame as a doctor in the Ocean races, but there is indeed something strange about the poison. It acts very fast, the symptoms are aggressive, and it spreads widely. It only took days for everyone living in the Dragon Palace’s vicinity to be afflicted with it. I've never seen anything like it before. It doesn’t conform to the usual rules of poison.”","The Mermaid Queen telepathically introduced the elder to Zu An. He was the Dragon Palace’s chief doctor, and others often called him the ‘Divine Physician’. His inability to deal with the poison showed how extraordinary it was. This made the Mermaid Queen feel a hint of despair.","“The poison is formidable, but our first priority should be to destroy his poison formation. Otherwise, even a deity won’t be able to turn things around,” Zu An said.","“We did look into it, but the Dragon Palace is too big, and we don’t have much manpower left. We weren’t able to find much,” the elder replied worriedly.","Zu An stepped out of the cave and looked at the Dragon Palace. “The poison formation constructed by the Aurora Poison Dragon is made up of 108 plague umbrellas planted in the Dragon Palace and the nearby areas. We have to destroy those umbrellas first.”","The Four Dragon Kings were impressed. “To be able to see through that vile dragon’s formation with a glance, your knowledge is impressive. May we ask you to tell us the locations of the plague umbrellas? We’ll remove them right away.”","They wouldn’t dare trouble Zu An with such miscellaneous tasks. They were planning to make a move despite their weakened bodies.","Zu An smiled. “You should rest, since you’re still recovering. I’ll handle it. Those plague umbrellas aren’t that easy to deal with; ordinary people would be afflicted with poison just by approaching those umbrellas.”","The Ocean races didn’t have many people to rely on now. Since he was already helping them, he thought that he might as well go all the way.","The Ocean races’ experts were moved to tears. They kneeled and kowtowed. “You are our Ocean races’ savior. We have no way of repaying such a huge debt to you. Please accept our three kowtows.”","Zu An supported the crowd to their feet with a casual wave of his hand. “You’re too polite. I have deep ties with the Ocean races, so I can’t turn a blind eye to your plight.”","Those words prompted the crowd to look at the Mermaid Queen with deep smiles. Some even regretted being jealous of his relationship with the Mermaid Queen. Now, they would rather the Ocean races had more Mermaid Queens for him to choose from.","It was a pity the Mermaid Queen was one of a kind.","The Dragon Kings even considered picking their most beautiful ladies to present them to him. But will the Mermaid Queen be jealous? Surely not, right? I mean, she’s also a member of the Ocean races.","The Mermaid Queen’s smile looked bitter. Others thought Zu An was doing this because of her, but she knew that the person Zu An truly cared about was his mermaid lover in the future.","Zu An was unaware of the Mermaid Queen’s thoughts. He brought the two ladies back to the Dragon Palace to remove the plague umbrellas. The others remained on standby in the cave to await further orders from the Dragon Kings to stabilize the situation.","Soon, Zu An found a plague umbrella at the fake mountain in the Dragon Palace’s garden. It wasn’t as big as he had imagined; it was only around the size of his palm. It was small and planted amid the bushes. It would have been hard to find unless one was looking closely.","There were strange, disconcerting drawings on the plague umbrella. Skull-like accessories dangled along its edge.","“It’s fortunate we have you here. Otherwise, we probably wouldn’t have noticed these things even if we conducted a thorough search of the Dragon Palace,” the Mermaid Queen said.","“Indeed. Even if we saw these umbrellas, we would have probably just shrugged them off as decorative ornaments,” the Peacock Princess added.","“These umbrellas follow the transformations of the 36 Heavenly Spirits and 72 Earthly Fiends, so there is a pattern to them...” Zu An was going to reveal that he'd arrested the Aurora Poison Dragon’s soul and questioned him, but seeing the admiring looks of the two beautiful ladies, he suddenly thought there was no need to explain everything.","It was only at times like this that he could feel as if his foundation was still the same. Being in a high position for too long had made him deal with things differently from how he previously would. Thanks to the company of the two beautiful ladies, this miscellaneous task wasn’t too boring.","Soon, they removed all the plague umbrellas in the Dragon Palace.","“Does this mean those who were poisoned have been saved?” the Mermaid Queen asked nervously as she witnessed the destruction of the last plague umbrella.","Zu An shook his head. “It only prevents the poison from further spreading and the worsening of existing symptoms, but those who are already poisoned will need the antidote to recover.”","“You previously mentioned something about the Firecloud Cave. Can the antidote be found there?” the Mermaid Queen asked.","“Mmhm. Do you know where the Firecloud Cave is?”","Zu An had looked through the Aurora Poison Dragon’s memories. The Firecloud Cave was rumored to be where Shennong’s successor resided, and the people there were known for their medical skills. However, he didn’t know where the Firecloud Cave was.","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. It was her first time hearing about that place.","“The Firecloud Cave?” The Peacock Princess fell into contemplation. “I think I know...”","“Oh?” Zu An and the Mermaid Queen turned to the Peacock Princess.","“Back when I was younger, I accompanied a clan elder to the Firecloud Cave to visit an old acquaintance of his,” the Peacock Princess replied.","Zu An was overjoyed. “May I know who that old acquaintance was? Does he have a name or any unique traits?”","The Peacock Princess smiled sheepishly. “I don’t remember. I was young and playful then. I found the conversation between elders boring, so I chose to play with other kids outside the cave instead. The only thing I remember is that the place was very hot. There were a lot of flames.”","Zu An and the Mermaid Queen were stunned.","It felt terrible to be presented with a ray of hope, only to have it extinguished like that.","The Peacock Princess quickly added, “But I remember the rough direction. I should be able to find it once we’re there.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. “That’s wonderful. Princess, I’ll be troubling you to lead the way.”","The Peacock Princess’ eyes lit up. She could finally get some alone time with Zu An.","But the Mermaid Queen suddenly spoke up, saying,, “I’ll follow you.”","The Peacock Princess’ smile froze, but she couldn’t complain because she owed her life to the Mermaid Queen. Nevertheless, she still tried to put up a fight. “Everyone in the Ocean races has been poisoned. Big sis queen, aren’t you needed here more than ever?”","The Mermaid Queen blushed. She had blurted those words out because she feared this could be an eternal farewell. Now that Zu An and the Peacock Princess were staring at her, she suddenly felt flustered.","Fortunately, she reacted quickly. “It should be fine now that the Four Dragon Kings have been saved. If I tag along, I can deliver the antidote to the Ocean races.” She turned to Zu An and added, “You’re planning to visit the Fiend races' side, right? If I come along, you won’t have to make another trip back to the Ocean races' side when the time comes.”","The Peacock Princess’ eyes lit up. At least I’ll get some private time with big brother on the way to the Fiend races' side!"]},{"number":2522,"title":"Chapter 2522: Chapter 2474: The Hungry Ghost Path’s Power Insignia","paragraphs":["Zu An thought her words made sense. He had to find the Six Paths’ power insignias, and he potentially wouldn't have time to return to the ocean till he was done collecting all six. Thus, he accepted the Mermaid Queen’s request to tag along.","The three of them returned to the cave to discuss further plans with the Four Dragon Kings.","“The Firecloud Cave? I've heard of it before,” the South Sea Dragon King said.","Zu An was overjoyed to hear that. He quickly probed for more details.","The South Sea Dragon King gathered his thoughts before replying, “I've only heard rumors. It’s said that the Firecloud Cave is where Human Emperor Shennong dwells. Shennong is rumored to be a highly skilled doctor, and there are legends of him testing a hundred herbs to gauge their medical properties. If anyone in the world can treat the Aurora Poison Dragon’s poison, it would probably be him. But...”","Zu An had also heard of Shennong’s legend on earth. He already knew this world had some connection with his previous world, so he wasn’t surprised by the coincidence. If Shennong truly existed, perhaps he'd be able to cure not just the Ocean races, but even Xiaoxi’s peculiar poison body.","Faced with the South Sea Dragon King’s abrupt pause, Zu An urged him, “But what?”","“The legend of Shennong comes from a long time ago. Even if he once existed, he’s likely dead by now. It’s also doubtful whether he truly was the Human Emperor. Humans often inflate their reputation through exaggeration...” The South Sea Dragon King suddenly remembered the person before him was a human too, and an awkward silence loomed.","“What makes you say that?” Zu An asked.","The South Sea Dragon King could only explain, “It’s said that Shennong has an ox head. He likely resembles those shamans more than a human.”","Zu An was taken aback. He did recall Shennong having horns on his head, and many records stated that he had an ox head and a human body. Looking at it from that angle, Shennong wasn't necessarily a human.","“That being said, it’s all a legend. No one has ever met him,” the South Sea Dragon King said. “Also, much time has passed since, so it’s a huge question mark whether the Firecloud Cave is still around.”","“The Firecloud Cave most definitely exists. I went there as a child,” the Peacock Princess said.","“Then there’s probably a successor to the Firecloud Cave.” The South Sea Dragon King didn't think that the Shennong from the legends was still alive.","“Dragon King, do you know where the Firecloud Cave is?” Zu An asked.","The South Sea Dragon King turned to the Peacock Princess and asked, “Princess, I thought you'd gone there as a child?”","The Peacock Princess’ eyes reddened. “I was still young back then. I've forgotten the exact location.”","Zu An patted the Peacock Princess’ shoulder to console her, knowing she was reminiscing about her kin. He had also suggested asking her clan elder where the Firecloud Cave was, but she'd burst into tears. It turned out that the elder had died on the battlefield while fighting against the monsters.","The same thing had happened many times among the Fiend races. Many chieftains, elders, and others in the upper echelons had lost their lives fighting against the monsters. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have had to take on such an important responsibility at such a young age.","Several generations of Fiend races had died fighting against the monsters. Now, it was just each generation filling up the gap left behind by the previous.","Zu An lamented the cruelty of war.","The South Sea Dragon King continued, “What I know about the Firecloud Cave comes from legends, so I don’t know the exact location. However, I have heard that the Firecloud Cave is near the Purple Ganoderma Cliff. Maybe this might be of use to you.”","“Purple Ganoderma Cliff?” the East Dragon King suddenly murmured. “There is a Purple Ganoderma Cliff on the East Sea’s coast. That place is often shrouded by fog, giving rise to rumors about immortals occasionally appearing there. I sent my men to investigate the area, but they failed to find anything. Could that have something to do with the Firecloud Cave?”","Zu An wondered if the fog was the doing of a profound formation. Those whose cultivation was lacking wouldn’t be able to see through the formation even if they were staring right into it. He asked, “May I know where the Purple Ganoderma Cliff is?”","The East Sea Dragon King took out a map. He spent some time studying it before pointing at a peninsula along the coast. “It should be somewhere here.”","The Mermaid Queen’s eyes lit up. “I have been there before. I can lead the way.” This gave her more of a pretext to tag along.","The Four Dragon Kings were counting on the Mermaid Queen to forge close ties with Zu An, so naturally, they wouldn’t stop her from accompanying him. They voiced their approval and offered them all sorts of conveniences. They even gave them a Crystal Boat that normally only Dragon Kings were qualified to ride on.","Zu An thanked them.","Meanwhile, the Peacock Princess ordered the Xuan-Su Guards to return to the Fiend races' side to report on the current situation.","The Xuan-Su Guards couldn’t bear to leave the Peacock Princess, but they knew that she wouldn’t need protecting when she had such an unfathomably powerful companion. Besides, they needed to deliver the report to the royal palace as soon as possible.","Before they left, the Peacock Princess called them over and said, “After we find the antidote in the Firecloud Cave, I’ll be bringing him to the Fiend races's side. I can tell he’s curious about the Saintess, so tell her to make preparations. If we can secure his help, we'll have a much better chance of fending against the monsters.”","The Xuan-Su Guards eyed Zu An with a frown. Is our princess not enough for you? Why are you coveting our Saintess too? Also, how is our Saintess supposed to prepare for your arrival? Prepare to seduce you?","They dared not read any deeper into it.","In the past, they would have thought it was ridiculous for anyone to marry both their princess and the Saintess, but after witnessing what Zu An was capable of, it somehow didn’t seem that ridiculous anymore.","The Mermaid Queen thought of bringing her maid Peach with her, but the latter had also been poisoned and was currently bedbound. Before leaving, Zu An visited her, fed her medicine to protect her life force, and assured her that he would find the antidote.","Peach was moved to tears. I must matchmake him and my queen. He will be my one and only master!","...","Zu An’s group left the Dragon Palace, boarded the Dragon Kings’ Crystal Boat, and began speeding toward the Purple Ganoderma Cliff.","The Crystal Boat glistened radiantly under the sunlight. It even concealed itself while traveling. No wonder it was the Dragon Kings’ default choice of vehicle.","The Dragon Kings had wanted to assign some guards and maids to Zu An, but the Ocean races were severely lacking in manpower. Fortunately, the Crystal Boat was an excellent artifact that would automatically navigate toward its destination if supplied with ample ki stones.","Zu An was delighted to learn that its speed was on par with the Wind Fire Wheels, and there were rooms onboard. That meant the three of them could take a good rest en route.","That night, Zu An returned to his room, took out a pendant, and entered Jing Teng’s cave paradise.","Sensing his arrival, Jing Teng stepped out to greet him. Joy radiated from her usual graceful expression. “You’re here.”","Zu An nodded. He got straight to the point and asked her if she knew where the Hungry Ghost Path was and what its power insignia was.","Jing Teng’s expression turned livid. “I don’t know!”","She went back into her house, leaving Zu An outside to be battered by the wind."]},{"number":2523,"title":"Chapter 2523: Chapter 2475: Awakening","paragraphs":["While Zu An was confused, Jing Teng suddenly walked out of her room once more, but her gait was now exceptionally seductive, a contrast from her previous dignified demeanor.","Zu An glanced at her thighs—they were no longer covered with white stockings, but rather with alluring black ones.","“Big brother Zu, how did you anger big sister?” Black Jing Teng walked over and leaned on him.","Even though Zu An was already familiar with the two sisters, he still couldn’t get used to how they had the same face but spoke and acted completely differently.","“I don’t know either. It was still going well at the start.” Zu An told her what had happened earlier.","“I see.” The corners of Black Jing Teng’s lips crept upward, as if having heard something interesting. “Others laud you as a Love Sage who goes around leaving romantic debts, but it seems you don’t understand women at all.”","Zu An thought about what had happened earlier, and realization struck him. “Was it because I talked business with her right away instead of showing her concern?”","He felt apologetic about that. Too many things had happened recently, and he was in such a huge rush to obtain the six power insignias that he'd overlooked that.","“That’s just one of the reasons.” Black Jing Teng leaned in and licked his ear before saying, “You asked about the Hungry Ghost Path. That’s my field of specialty. She thought you came here to visit me, and that made her even angrier.”","Zu An was startled. I see. While they're sisters, they are two personas occupying a body. There's such a rivalry between them that even in bed... No wonder Jing Teng was so angry.","However, his face soon lit up in delight. “You know about the Hungry Ghost Path?”","“Of course. Have you forgotten that I used to be the Ghost King?” Black Jing Teng tilted her chin upward in glee.","Zu An frowned. “You were the Hungry Ghost Path’s Ghost King?”","He had chosen to ask Jing Teng about this matter because of what he knew about the previous Ghost King. He'd heard that the Ghost King ruled over the wandering ghosts existing between the mortal world and the underworld.","“What Ghost King did you think I was?” Black JIng Teng suddenly transformed from a seductive youth into a domineering queen.","Zu An was surprised and elated. He hadn’t expected such an outcome. He asked, “Is the Hungry Ghost Path filled with hungry ghosts?”","Black Jing Teng shook her head and harrumphed. “Do I look like a hungry ghost to you?”","Zu An looked at her and chuckled. “If all hungry ghosts resembled you, the Hungry Ghost Path would be a paradise everyone looked forward to.”","“That’s more like the player who charmed thousands of innocent girls,” Black Jing Teng said with a satisfied smile.","Zu An was stunned. I feel as if you’re insulting me instead.","He continued asking, “What are hungry ghosts, exactly? Are they just starving ghosts?”","Black Jing Teng pulled him to the nearby garden and sat down on a swing. She pushed herself off and began swinging as she spoke. “They are starving, but the food they seek isn’t what you might be imagining. It refers to their fixation on certain matters. Otherwise, they wouldn’t have refused to descend to the underworld after death, instead lingering on the Hungry Ghost Path.","“That strong fixation creates an unquenchable feeling of hunger in them. Feasting on the blood and flesh of the living is merely a way to temporarily alleviate their hunger. Some hungry ghosts also kill living beings who satisfy certain conditions to dispel their fixation... In summary, they aren’t necessarily kind beings. That’s why the world often speaks about the Hungry Ghost Path with fear and hatred.”","Zu An nodded. He finally understood what the situation of the Hungry Ghost Path was.","On the surface it sounded as if they were vengeful ghosts born from overwhelming resentment, but that wouldn’t be an accurate depiction. Not all hungry ghosts were violent; some were kind. The thing they all had in common was their overwhelming fixation that kept their souls from dissipating.","Other than naturally formed hungry ghosts, there were those born as hungry ghosts too. Indeed, they could mate and reproduce. As the underworld’s master, Zu An had previously investigated the Six Paths and learned it was possible to reincarnate as a hungry ghost.","The underworld decided on a ghost’s reincarnation based on the karma accrued over their lifetime. Only those who had done many evil deeds in their previous life would be reincarnated as hungry ghosts, though it was still less severe than the Hell Path.","Zu An chuckled. Now that he thought about it, in a famous work from his previous life, the female protagonist, Nie Xiaoqian[1], could give birth. No wonder the Old Black Mountain Demon had wanted to marry her.","He turned his attention back to the present and asked the most pressing question on his mind, “What’s the Hungry Ghost Path’s power insignia?”","Black Jing Teng suddenly harrumphed. “Now I know why big sis was so angry. Even I’m getting angry at you. You’re in the company of a gorgeous lady, yet your heart and mind aren’t focused on me at all.”","Zu An smiled bitterly. “This matter is of utmost importance. I won’t be able to relax until I resolve it.”","It was only after hearing her words that he noticed how soft her body was. As they were sitting side by side on the swing, he could even smell her faint body fragrance.","Speaking of which, it was peculiar how even though the two sisters shared a body, they always appeared with different stockings and had different fragrances. White Jing Teng’s fragrance was graceful and noble, whereas Black Jing Teng’s fragrance was wild and seductive.","Black Jing Teng sensed his admiring gaze and nodded in satisfaction. “Forget it. Take a look at this.”","She stretched her fair hand forth, and a ghost mask suddenly appeared on her palm. The mask looked eerie, and the sight of it evoked a cold sensation, as if being gazed at by a lofty ruler.","This was the mask worn by Black Jing Teng when Zu An first met her as the Ghost King.","“Is this the Hungry Ghost Path’s power insignia?” Zu An took the mask in delight.","“You can have it if you like it.” Black Jing Teng didn’t mind giving it to him.","Zu An straightened his posture and said, “I’ll return the mask to you after Houtu forges the World Law Beacon. The process shouldn’t damage the mask.”","Black Jing Teng wrapped her hand around his neck. “I’m already yours. My possessions are naturally yours to take too. You don’t have to be so distant.”","Her sweet whisper and close-up, ravishing face made Zu An gulp down his saliva. She’s such a little imp!","Black Jing Teng leaned closer and breathed on his ear. “I did you a huge favor. How do you intend to thank me?”","“How should I thank you?” Zu An was in a good mood after obtaining the Hungry Ghost Path’s power insignia so easily.","“You know how.” Black Jing Teng raised her head and looked at him with glistening eyes.","Sensing her silent invitation, Zu An couldn’t resist lowering her head and kissing her.","It was then that a familiar, feeble voice echoed from the side. “W-What are you doing?”","1. Nie Xiaoqian is a beautiful female ghost who earns back her humanity through karmic merit and is then able to conceive ☜"]},{"number":2524,"title":"Chapter 2524: Chapter 2476: Epoch","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart shuddered upon hearing that voice. He looked over in disbelief.","A slender figure was leaning against the doorway. She had smoky eyebrows resembling a frown, and her eyes looked as if they would tear up at any moment. Her face was exceptionally pale, and she looked sickly. Her appearance could evoke sympathy from anyone who saw it.","“Honglei!” Zu An was overjoyed to see her.","He'd been planning to first check on Qiu Honglei in the jade coffin after entering the cave paradise, but Jing Teng had appeared right away. He'd gotten so carried away that it slipped his mind.","Who could have expected the awakened Qiu Honglei to stumble upon their imminent kiss?","Zu An was too overcome by joy to bother about the awkwardness of being caught in action.","“You two...” Qiu Honglei murmured feebly, but she collapsed before she could finish her words.","“Honglei!” Zu An flitted to her side to support her. When he saw her collapsing, his soul nearly escaped from his body. He began circulating his ki into her body, making sure to do it slowly as her body was still weak from having only just awakened.","It was fortunate that Honglei had only passed out due to her weakness. With the nourishment of Zu An's ki, she slowly regained consciousness.","“Honglei, you’re awake!” Zu An’s voice quivered as he spoke.","To save him, Qiu Honglei had performed the Dance Offering to the Universe until her body collapsed. She had only preserved a sliver of her life force thanks to the Snow Lady’s ‘sacrifice’. Later, Zu An had found the legendary Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine and saved her.","Even so, Honglei had remained unconscious, and Zu An had feared that the worst would happen. He was overjoyed to see her regaining consciousness.","“Ah Zu~” Qiu Honglei’s lips were pale, but she smiled when she saw how anxious Zu An was. She tried her best to reach for his cheek. “It’s good to see you again.”","Even so, she was so frail that even this simple motion was arduous for her.","Zu An grabbed her hand and pressed it against his face. Just like that, he stared at her with adoring eyes.","Black Jing Teng watched this scene in frustration. Wow, I'm a third wheel here.","She thought about Qiu Honglei’s timely dizzy spell earlier and swore to learn it well. Men seem to love that trick. Ugh, how maddening! We almost kissed! That woman sure knows how to time her appearance!","While Black Jing Teng was seething, Qiu Honglei lay in Zu An’s arms while looking at her lover. She had an uncanny feeling that ages had already passed. “Ah Zu, I thought I’d never see you again.”","Zu An shared the same feeling too. “I was scared out of my wits. Promise me you’ll never do anything as foolish as that again.”","Qiu Honglei smiled. “We would have all died if I hadn’t done that. If I could save you, my death wouldn’t have been in vain.”","Zu An felt warmth in his heart and embraced her even tighter. “Honglei, I’ll never let you put yourself in such danger ever again!”","A voice dripping with jealousy suddenly called out from the side, “Have you forgotten there’s someone else here?”","Qiu Honglei’s face turned red. She tried to push Zu An aside, but was too weak to do so. She surveyed their surroundings and asked, “Ah Zu, this place is...?”","“This is Miss Jing’s cave paradise,” Zu An explained. “It was thanks to her artifact that I was able to bring you wherever I went.”","“Thank you, big sister Jing.” Qiu Honglei tried to get up to bow to Black Jing Teng, but she was so weak that she failed to get on her feet.","“Don’t move around too much. You’re still weak. Someone is going to die of heartache if anything happens to you.” Black Jing Teng had a smile on her face, but she was secretly cursing in her heart.","This green tea bitch has incredible methods. Even a woman like me finds her pitiful, let alone that huge lecher!","To no surprise, Zu An quickly supported Qiu Honglei, saying, “Be careful.”","He took out a ki-nourishing pill and fed it to her. She was still too weak to take anything heavy, so he had to first build up her foundation with gentler medicine.","Qiu Honglei obediently swallowed the pill.","Black Jing Teng’s eyebrows twitched. How am I supposed to learn her coy obedient act?!","She was suddenly reminded of the time she had outright asked Zu An to sleep with her while trying to seduce him. She had to admit there was a huge disparity in their methods. Demonesses from demonic cults are skilled in the art of seduction!","That made her even angrier.","While her mind was shaken, White Jing Teng exploited this opportunity to take control of the body. She was aware of what had just happened, and she felt that she had been thoroughly embarrassed by her silly little sister.","She coldly said, “Miss Qiu’s injuries were severe. The Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine helped a lot, but she has just regained consciousness and needs more rest. My ki-rich cave paradise is a good place for her to recuperate. You can come here and visit her from time to time.”","Zu An noticed her white stockings and realized she had switched personas. “I apologize for my earlier lack of decorum. I was too abrupt...”","Qiu Honglei blinked. Sensing she had missed some huge gossip, she wanted to ask about it, but a sudden wave of exhaustion hit her. She was so tired that she couldn’t keep her eyes open.","“Your body is too weak. You need more rest to recuperate. Don’t force yourself,” Jing Teng said.","“Thanks for your reminder, big sister,” Qiu Honglei mumbled in response before succumbing to her drowsiness.","“Carry her to my room,” Jing Teng said.","Now that she was awake, it wouldn’t be appropriate to put Qiu Honglei back into the jade coffin. Seeing Zu An’s nervous expression, Jing Teng added, “Don’t worry. Now that she’s awake, we can slowly condition her body with pills and spirit food. She’ll gradually recover. I know you’re busy, so I’ll take care of her on your behalf.”","Zu An was grateful. He knew Jing Teng wasn’t the type to take care of others; she was only doing this for his sake. He wanted to thank her, but considering their relationship, such words felt superficial.","So, he wrapped his arm around her waist and kissed her.","“What are you... Wuuu...” Jing Teng was stunned at first, but then shyness overwhelmed her.","She tried to push Zu An away, but his arms refused to move, as if they were forged from metal. After a few attempts, she lost her strength, and her body slowly softened in his embrace.","Some time later, a furiously blushing Jing Teng snuggled in Zu An’s arms. “Tell me what happened recently.”","Once again, Zu An couldn’t help noticing the two sisters’ vastly different personalities. Had it been the young sister, she would have bugged him for all kinds of ‘compensation'. In contrast, the older sister paid more attention to intangible exchanges.","With the beauty in his arms, he shared everything that had happened recently with her.","“The Six Paths, the Asura race, the Shaman races...” Jing Teng murmured those phrases before suddenly saying, “The war between the Asura race and the Celestial race should have happened in the previous epoch. It’s a different epoch from when the Shaman races fought against the Celestial Court’s Fiend races.”","“Epoch?” Zu An keenly noticed her word choice.","“Using your units of measurement, an epoch can range between a hundred million years to several billion years.” Jing Teng’s reply shocked Zu An."]},{"number":2525,"title":"Chapter 2525: Chapter 2477: The Ocean Deity","paragraphs":["“Several billion years?” Zu An was dumbstruck. Earth’s civilization only went back several thousand years, and the Cultivation World’s civilization went back only tens of thousands of years. Recorded history had started only several thousand years back.","While the existence of secret dungeons hinted at past civilizations, most people believed that they would only go back tens of thousands of years, or, at most, hundreds of thousands of years. Even the notion of several billion years sounded ridiculous.","“How do you know that?” Zu An asked out of curiosity.","Jing Teng looked dazed. “I don’t know either. The memory is just there. It popped out when I heard you talking about the Six Paths.”","Zu An remembered her original form had been the Demon-Suppressing Talisman, suppressing countless terrifying experts in that great tomb. Her background itself was already a mystery. He asked, “Were you suppressing experts from that epoch in that great tomb?”","Jing Teng shook her head. “I’m not sure either. My memory is incomplete. My head hurts...”","Zu An was shocked to see her clutch her head in pain and quickly embraced her. He infused a sliver of his ki into her, saying, “You don’t have to think about it if you can’t recall it.”","Jing Teng felt a little better as she turned her attention away from the matter, though she remained in a poor mental state.","Zu An knew she was injured to begin with, and she'd exerted the energy she had recovered with great difficulty to help him in the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons. That had left her in a feeble state. So, he shoved work aside and instead chatted with her about day-to-day affairs.","Jing Teng revealed a rare weak side, snuggling in his arms like a cat. The two of them didn’t do anything more intimate, but the warmth they shared was unprecedented.","Black Jing Teng screamed that it was a huge waste not to exploit this amazing atmosphere to try something. Leave it to me if you’re feeling embarrassed.","But Jing Teng ignored her and continued lying lazily in her lover’s arms. Even though the two of them had often interacted intimately, she had never felt so close to him before. Under this extreme state of relaxation, she quickly drifted off to sleep.","Zu An carried her back to her room. He glanced at Qiu Honglei, who was sleeping on the neighboring bed. His mood felt exceptionally light. Honglei has regained consciousness, I was able to get closer to Jing Teng, and the Hungry Ghost Path’s power insignia is now in my hands. Everything is progressing well.","He planned to stay with the two ladies a while longer, but he suddenly sensed something. He left the cave paradise inside the pendant and returned to his room on the Crystal Boat.","Light knocks came from his door. “Big brother, are you asleep?”","Zu An opened the door and looked at the slightly blushing woman outside. “Princess, do you need me for something?”","“I couldn’t sleep, so I came here for a chat. Is it convenient?”","The Peacock Princess was blushing furiously. It was unlike a demure lady to knock on a man’s door in the middle of the night, but ladies of the Fiend races had always been more daring, and she did have a lot of questions to ask him. That was why she'd mustered the courage to do this.","“Of course it is. Come in.” Zu An tilted his body to let her in.","The Peacock Princess noticed how he didn’t close the door after her and chuckled. Big brother is such a gentleman.","“Big brother, can you tell me what happened in the last few days?” She looked at him with gleaming eyes. Zu An and the Mermaid Queen had mentioned bits and pieces, but she anxiously wanted to know more about him, especially details about that beautiful Asura woman.","I can’t know less than big sis queen.","Zu An told her everything, shocking the Peacock Princess. He then proceeded to ask about the Fiend races.","From her, he learned that when the monsters suddenly appeared, it was the Fiend Emperor who had assembled the Fiend races’ experts to fight back. But the huge disparity in their fighting prowess caused the Fiend races to suffer a series of tragic defeats, and their experts had died one after another. Even the Fiend Emperor had died in battle.","By now, the Fiend races had already lost all their experts from the previous generations. It was the younger ones who were holding the line.","Fortunately, the Fiend races had also been growing throughout the war, and they adapted to the monsters’ fighting style. The appearance of the Saintess and the monsters’ sudden decrease in aggression in recent years allowed them to catch their breath, and they occasionally managed to recoup lost territories.","“The monsters suddenly became less aggressive?” Zu An asked. “When did that happen?”","“It was after we lost our imperial court. It was a tragic battle. The Fiend Emperor refused to abandon our ancestral land and fought to the end. He died to the Lord of Slaughter,” the Peacock Princess said sorrowfully. “They got complacent after conquering our imperial court and killing the Fiend Emperor. Their attacks slowed down, and the Lord of Slaughter hasn’t appeared since. It has been the Monster Lord commanding the troops in his place.”","A thought surfaced in Zu An’s mind.","The Lord of Slaughter must have noticed the Fiend races’ imperial tomb and sensed that there was something more inside. He must be trying to find the Celestial Court, which is why he entrusted other tasks to the Monster Lord.","I don’t know whether he deciphered the Celestial Court’s secret, but his immersion in the investigation gave the Monster Lord a chance to usurp his power and eventually betray him...","Sounds suddenly came from the doorway. Zu An raised his head and saw the Mermaid Queen standing awkwardly outside. She was hesitant about whether to enter or not.","Being discovered by Zu An only made the Mermaid Queen feel even more awkward. “Did I come at a bad time?”","She was also suffering from insomnia, as she knew that the day of parting between Zu An and her was swiftly approaching; they were drawing closer to the Firecloud Cave. She didn’t want to waste any opportunities to interact with him. If possible, she wanted to stay by his side at all times. But she feared that if she approached him in the middle of the night, Zu An would misunderstand her as shameless.","While she was hesitating, however, she'd heard noises from the neighboring room. The Peacock Princess had gone to look for him. Youngsters are so courageous. Maybe I’m thinking too much.","She was curious what the two of them were doing at this ungodly hour. The thought of a suave man and a beautiful woman sharing a room by themselves at night made her heart itchy, as if a kitten were clawing at it. Unable to bear her curiosity, she snuck over to check things out.","She hadn’t expected to get caught right away.","Zu An smiled. “You came at a good time. Come in and have a seat. I have some questions I’d like to ask you.”","The Mermaid Queen’s face heated up. She entered the room and took a seat.","The Peacock Princess felt a surge of envy. Big sis queen’s gestures are so graceful and feminine. I wish I could learn her demeanor.","The Mermaid Queen was grateful for Zu An's thoughtfulness at dispelling her awkwardness. She asked gently, “What do you want to ask me?” I’ll even tell you my three figures if you want.","“The Ocean races don’t seem to be affiliated with the Fiend races. How much do you know about the Ocean Deity your people worship?”","Zu An had always thought the Ocean races were one of the countless races under the Fiend races, just that they were a particularly powerful group. It was only upon coming to this world that he learned that they weren’t the same faction, and they'd even nearly become enemies."]},{"number":2526,"title":"Chapter 2526: Chapter 2478: Destination","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen was dumbstruck. “Of course, the Ocean races and the Fiend races are completely different races. Big brother, what makes you ask such a question?”","The Peacock Princess also stared at Zu An in surprise, not expecting the latter to be confused about what was considered common sense here.","“I had that misunderstanding because in the future, the Ocean races are a part of the Fiend races,” Zu An explained.","The Peacock Princess was delighted to hear that. “It sounds like the alliance went through!”","The Mermaid Queen, however, was worried. “Do the Fiend races annex our Ocean races in the future?” She was opposed to the Ocean races siding with the monsters, but she also didn’t want to be annexed by the Fiend races either.","Zu An smiled. “Don’t worry, the Ocean races remain highly autonomous in the future.”","It now made sense to him why the Ocean races had such a unique standing among the Fiend races, as opposed to the other groups, as well as why the old Fiend Emperor had spent a great amount of wealth and resources to liaise with the Ocean races each year, and why the Ocean races’ Dragon Kings didn’t pale much in comparison to the Human Emperor and the Fiend Emperor.","The Mermaid Queen’s mind was put at ease. She slowly replied, “Our Ocean races were born in the ocean. We came to be together with the ocean. It’s rumored that our history far predates the Fiend races and Human race.","“The Ocean races are diverse, each having their own culture and lifestyle, but we share a common faith—that of the Ocean Deity. It’s said that the Ocean Deity was born because of us, and it is thanks to her protection that we survived to this day...”","Zu An keenly picked up on the pronoun and asked, “The Ocean Deity is female?”","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “The Ocean Deity has no gender, though both the Ocean races and Fiend races are traditionally inclined to see her as a woman.”","Zu An was perplexed. “Don’t you have an idol of the Ocean Deity?”","The Mermaid Queen chuckled. “Different Ocean races have different idols of the Ocean Deity, so there is no way of telling which one is the right one.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. It was similar to how, in his previous life, he had seen idols of the same deity looking vastly different across different temples.","He asked more questions about the Ocean Deity, but the Mermaid Queen didn’t know much. She didn’t even know whether the Ocean Deity truly existed, or was just a pillar of support for the Ocean races.","Zu An chose to end the questions there. After all he had been through, he'd learned that secrets could only be uncovered at a price, and the truth would only come out at a certain time.","The earlier talk about the Ocean races being under the Fiend races piqued the Peacock Princess and Mermaid Queen’s interest about the future, so they implored him to share more.","They had gotten close over the last few days, and the two ladies were using all their persuasive methods to persuade him to talk. Zu An had no choice but to tell them about the future. Of course, he did filter out important things that could affect the past. Even so, the two ladies were still immersed in his stories, and they looked forward to the future.","Time slowly passed, and the three of them drifted off to sleep.","The following morning, the Mermaid Queen found herself sharing a bed with Zu An. She was lying in his arms, with her head resting on his chest. This caused her cheeks to flush, and she anxiously tried to recall what happened last night.","We talked for so long that we started getting tired, so the Peacock Princess suggested for us to continue the conversation on the bed.","The Mermaid Queen had initially found that suggestion ridiculous, but she wasn't averse to sharing a bed with Zu An. There were also other people present, so she didn’t think it was too much.","Zu An had hesitated, but the Peacock Princess had energetically provoked him into accepting it, claiming, ‘What’s there to fear when we're all forthright and open? Could it be that big brother harbors lustful thoughts for us?’","Zu An couldn’t beat her argument, so they'd ended up lying on his bed and talking about the future.","It was a good thing that the bed was wide enough to remain spacious even with the three of them. After overcoming the initial embarrassment, they quickly returned to the conversation.","Hearing his words and taking in his scent, the Mermaid Queen had fallen asleep before she knew it. She was shocked at how lowered her guard was, for her to actually fall asleep next to a man.","However, she soon smiled bitterly. She would never have permitted herself to share a room like that with another man, so such a thing would never have happened with anyone else. Her intact clothes meant that, to her regret, nothing had happened at all.","She tried to carefully move away the hand next to her head, only to feel a soft and smooth texture. That can’t be big brother Zu’s hand. She quickly looked over and frowned in bewilderment.","Sleeping next to her was the Peacock Princess, and the latter’s sleeping posture was much more open compared to her demure one. She was lying on her side, her hands wrapped around Zu An’s neck. Her leg was also resting on Zu An’s body, as if trying to hold him down.","The Mermaid Queen’s face reddened. Fiend race ladies are so open. I would have died of awkwardness if I slept like that.","Feeling a touch on her hand, the Peacock Princess slowly woke up. She instinctively rubbed her eyes before she finally registered the scene in the room. Her fair complexion immediately turned red.","No matter how passionate she was, she was still a young woman. To hug a man to sleep like that—or maybe it would be more apt to use the word ‘clamp’—was embarrassing, and on top of that, someone else was present to witness it.","For a moment, she even considered silencing the Mermaid Queen.","“Morning.”","The Peacock Princess quickly retracted her leg and awkwardly smiled at the Mermaid Queen. The latter responded with an enigmatic smile. That further reinforced the princess' desire to silence her. Hmph, if not because of the favor I owe big sis queen and my inability to defeat her in battle...","She suddenly remembered the excuse Zu An had used against the North Sea Dragon King to rescue her. She'd found it utterly ridiculous then, but in a weird turn of events, they really had ended up sharing a bed for a night.","It was only after the two ladies tidied themselves up that Zu An slowly woke up. “Morning.”","“Morning!” The two ladies’ faces were slightly red.","Zu An had long since woken up. It had been a terrible night for him; which normal man could remain unfazed when there were two gorgeous beauties sleeping right beside him?","The Mermaid Queen was still fine—she had mostly slept peacefully except for the occasional snuggling up to him.","The Peacock Princess, on the other hand, was an unruly sleeper. She had spent a lot of time either hugging or clamping onto him, sometimes even nuzzling against him. Zu An had only managed to hold back due to his self-control being tempered by his rich experiences.","The room descended into inexplicable awkwardness. The Mermaid Queen cleared the air by saying, “We should be near the Purple Ganoderma Cliff now. I wonder if the Firecloud Cave is truly there...”","Before she could finish her words, the Crystal Boat suddenly shook. The two ladies lost their balance and would have fallen down if not for Zu An quickly flitting over to support them.","There was a frown on Zu An’s face. The Crystal Boat appears to have struck something."]},{"number":2527,"title":"Chapter 2527: Chapter 2479: The Gate Has Always Been Open For You","paragraphs":["The trio rushed onto the deck and soon understood why the boat had suddenly started shaking.","A massive octopus monster had wrapped its countless dark-red tentacles around the crystal boat. Its tentacle suckers resembled eyes, and they could send anyone with trypophobia[1] into a panic attack.","“Ugh, how disgusting~” The Peacock Princess couldn’t take the sight and hid behind Zu An.","Zu An examined the octopus monster—its tentacles didn’t have pinkish-red fluid, so it wasn’t the same sea monster Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue had encountered. Speaking of which, he missed that fellow. Its tentacle fluid was a rare medicinal material. It could be used not just for that kind of medicine, but others too.","With Zu An’s deeper insight into formations, spirit food, and alchemy, he had far more ideas about how that fluid could be used now.","Having met monsters from the Octopus race before, the Mermaid Queen murmured with a frown, “That’s weird. The Crystal Boat is the Dragon King’s vehicle; it has a special formation and aura. Most ocean monsters avoid it. Why would this octopus monster attack us of its own accord?”","The octopus monster noticed them and extended two thick tentacles to wrap around them.","Zu An harrumphed. No one saw how he moved, but the two tentacles were severed from the center.","The octopus monster was taken aback. It retracted all its tentacles while crying miserably, but a second later, the tentacles suddenly returned from all directions to lash at the three of them. Each tentacle was around a hundred meters wide and left a sonic boom in its wake. Even a giant ship would be split in two when struck by those tentacles, let alone a body of flesh and blood.","Zu An’s face turned cold. “You beast!”","A barrage of sword ki sliced through the octopus monster’s tentacles, leaving only a giant head floating in the air. Zu An's sword ki was so fast that the octopus monster finally registered the pain only after the tentacles already fell onto the deck. With a cry of agony, the monster dove back into the water, its blood swiftly dyeing the nearby water red.","The Peacock Princess and the Mermaid Queen backed away from the severed tentacles that had dropped onto the deck but continued to wriggle. Women were naturally averse to such things, after all.","Zu An stored the giant tentacles inside the Brilliant Glass Bead’s storage space. He noticed the two women staring at him weirdly and explained with a smile, “I can make hotplate squid out of them. You bet they'll be chewy.”","The two women rolled their eyes. You could feed a village with those massive tentacles.","An angry voice suddenly echoed, “How dare you hurt my little sweetie!”","The crowd looked over and saw a boy walking on waves, heading toward them. The octopus monster head, which had sought refuge in the water, suddenly popped out and shrank until it was the size of a basketball. It nuzzled against the boy with an indignant expression, as if complaining about Zu An and the others.","“Little sweetie?” Zu An and the others frowned. They could tell the octopus monster was the boy’s pet, but they struggled to associate such a cute name with that disgusting giant monster.","“I’m talking to you!” The boy had a clean appearance, a smooth complexion, and hair tied into two buns, but his arrogant gaze and rude tone felt uncomfortable.","“What nonsense are you spouting? It was that monster who attacked us. If we had been any weaker, we would have become its meal. You should compensate us for our emotional distress instead!” the young Peacock Princess retorted indignantly.","The boy was taken aback. He hadn’t expected them to be so good with words. He was unable to find anything to say for a long time.","The Mermaid Queen secretly shot the Peacock Princess a thumbs up. She’s brave and candid, unlike me. I've weathered so many storms that I can’t help but overthink whenever I’m faced with such situations.","“Hmph! My little sweetie was just joking with you! Do you have to deal such a heavy blow to it?” The boy finally recovered and made his comeback. “How vile must your heart be to sever all its tentacles? Who knows whether it can survive this ordeal? I grew up with little sweetie, and I have long considered it a member of my own family! You must compensate us!”","Zu An calmly asked, “So how do you want us to compensate you?”","The boy pointed at the Crystal Boat they were standing on. “Your boat looks decent. My little sweetie must have wrapped its tentacles around your boat because it waws fond of it. It would be fair for you to compensate it with your boat.”","The little octopus head vehemently nodded, agreeing with the proposal.","The Mermaid Queen lost her patience. “Do you know whose boat this is? I doubt you’d dare accept it even if we give it to you.”","“It’s just the East Sea Dragon King’s Crystal Boat. Why wouldn’t I dare to accept it?” the boy sneered.","The trio were taken aback. They'd thought that the other party was just a troublemaking kid, but to think he recognized the Crystal Boat! That complicated matters.","“What’s your name?” Zu An asked. The boy didn’t look weak, but someone at such a young age could only be so strong. The bigger problem was his background—a boy who suddenly appeared in the middle of the ocean and recognized the Crystal Boat was anything but ordinary.","“Are you asking for my great name? Well, wash your ears and listen up! I am...” The boy puffed up his chest and was just about to speak when another voice echoed from afar.","“Stop causing trouble. Welcome our esteemed guests and bring them in,” an aged voice said, sounding as if it echoed from the world itself.","The Mermaid Queen and Peacock Princess were startled. They could tell that the other party was extremely powerful from the voice itself; they were at least above the Four Dragon Kings.","Zu An was the only one who remained calm as he looked in the direction of the voice. An invisible door seemed to open on the water, and an island appeared out of nowhere in the middle of the ocean.","The island was shrouded in fog. Immortal cranes and divine birds flew through the clouds, making the place look like a paradise.","“Hm?” Zu An discreetly asked the Mermaid Queen, “Is this the Purple Ganoderma Cliff?”","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “We should still be a day’s journey away, and the direction doesn’t seem right either.”","The boy harrumphed. “Count yourself lucky. My master hasn’t met any outsiders for many years now. Come with me.”","1. Trypophobia is an aversion to the sight of repetitive patterns or clusters of small holes or bumps. ☜"]},{"number":2528,"title":"Chapter 2528: Chapter 2480: It’s All Fated","paragraphs":["“May I ask your master’s name?” Zu An asked.","“My master is my master. There’s no need for so many questions.” The boy rolled his eyes and ignored them. He fed a pill to the octopus head.","In the blink of an eye, the 'adorable' octopus head suddenly grew dozens of tentacles, reverting to its state before it was injured.","Zu An and the others were astonished. They couldn’t believe a pill could be so potent as to allow for instantaneous full recovery. On top of that, the way the boy casually fed the pill to his pet suggested that he didn’t consider it valuable.","Zu An discreetly told the two ladies, “Looks like the Purple Ganoderma Cliff is a feint; the true Firecloud Cave lies here.”","The sudden appearance of an island here spoke volumes. A highly profound formation had to have been constructed around it, such that outsiders wouldn’t have noticed anything amiss even if they passed by this place a thousand times.","Even Zu An, despite his mastery of formations, had only noticed the formation when the other party revealed it.","Besides, where else could a boy casually bring out a miraculous recovery medicine aside from the medically-renowned Firecloud Cave?","The Mermaid Queen had also arrived at the same conclusion. After seeing how difficult the boy and the octopus monster were, she worried that they couldn’t secure the Firecloud Cave’s help.","The Peacock Princess replied telepathically, “That distant cliff looks familiar, but I don’t remember seeing this boy the last time I came here.”","The Mermaid Queen burst into laughter. “You were still young. That boy might not have been born yet.”","Those words weren't necessarily accurate. In the cultivation world, judging a person’s age by their appearance could lead to grossly inaccurate estimates. For instance, a boy could be older than a white-haired old man. However, the boy didn’t seem to belong to that category.","The boy led the three of them to the island. Mysterious flowers and herbs were scattered around the island, emanating a faint fragrance.","They entered a quiet mountainous path, filled with verdant pine trees and luxuriant green bamboos. Soft emerald grass was coated with glistening dew, and ancient trees of unknown age towered overhead. Stone piles resembled prowling tigers, and the old vines hanging on the trees resembled snakes.","Taking in these details, Zu An told the two ladies that they were walking through a highly profound formation. Had they barged in, these stones and vines would have transformed into ferocious tigers and snakes to attack them.","The crimson cliffs along the way seemed to contain immortal silhouettes. A group of lotuses floated at the bottom of the mountain stream, and their fragrance was discernible even from a great distance. The spring water that splashed on them emanated iridescent light reminiscent of gemstones.","Those lotuses had to be rare treasures. Had they encountered them elsewhere, the trio would have dove right in to harvest them.","The boy brought them to a cave shrouded in iridescent light. Mysterious birds danced amid the clouds.","The Mermaid Queen exclaimed in astonishment, “There’s a melody to their chirping! I wonder if someone trained them, or if they were born with such ability.”","To astound someone as musically talented as the Mermaid Queen, this place was truly extraordinary.","The boy dropped his arrogant attitude and respectfully bowed. “Master, I have brought them here.”","Zu An and the others also bowed toward the cave. “Necropolis (Mermaid Queen/ Peacock Princess) pays respect to the master of the land.”","“Necropolis...” A chuckle came from inside. The person seemed to have found the name interesting,","Zu An looked at the cave. Does he know who the Necropolis Emperor is?","He was curious to know what the other party looked like, but the person had neither left the cave nor invited them in. He tried to extend his divine sense into the cave, but something about the cave prevented it from reaching inside.","“Forgive my discourtesy. It’s not convenient for me to meet outsiders,” the old voice inside the cave said.","The Peacock Princess’ eyes lit up. “I remember it now! This is the Firecloud Cave. I came here once when I was younger!”","The old voice chuckled. “Ah, it’s Little Peacock. You have grown so big in the blink of an eye.”","The boy stared at the Peacock Princess with curious eyes.","“I pay my respects to the elder.” The Peacock Princess quickly bowed once more.","“You’re the child of an acquaintance; there’s no need for so many formalities. How is your uncle doing?” the old voice asked.","The Peacock Princess’ eyes reddened. “My uncle has passed away. Most of our elders have lost their lives on the battlefield...”","She proceeded to talk about the Fiend races’ war against the monsters.","The old voice in the cave was silent for a long time. “Everything is ordained by fate. There’s no need to be too upset, Little Peacock.”","His casual tone only further stoked the Peacock Princess’ sorrow.","Zu An, however, noticed something peculiar in those words. He seems to be looking at things from a higher perspective. Does he mean to say that these events were already decided by fate?","The Mermaid Queen consoled the Peacock Princess before revealing her motive to the person in the cave.","The old voice spent a moment in thought before replying, “I do have the means to treat the Aurora Poison Dragon’s plague formation.”","The Mermaid Queen was overjoyed to hear that. “Elder, I implore you to bestow me with the antidote. The Ocean races will remember your grace.”","The old voice chuckled. “I have no ties with the Ocean races, and that won’t change in the future. I can give you the antidote, but I’ll need the person beside you to agree to my request.”","Taken aback, the Mermaid Queen reflexively turned to Zu An.","Zu An was perplexed. “May I know your request?”","“I haven’t decided on it yet. I’ll let you know when the time comes,” the old voice replied.","The Mermaid Queen frowned.","“I’m afraid I can’t accept such a condition,” Zu An replied.","Accepting this request was as good as issuing a blank check. What if the other party demanded something ridiculous from him in the future?","The old voice chuckled. “I understand your reservations, but you can be assured that I won’t make you do anything against your conscience. When the time comes, you may also decide for yourself whether you wish to repay the favor or not. I won’t force you.”","Zu An was surprised. The conditions were too generous. That meant the other party couldn’t coerce him into doing anything if he refused to repay him in the future. “But that seems very disadvantageous to you.”","“It’s fine. It’s all inscribed in fate,” the old voice calmly replied.","This was the second time the other party had talked about fate. Zu An hesitated for a second before asking, “May I ask if you’re Shennong?”"]},{"number":2529,"title":"Chapter 2529: Chapter 2481: The Human Path’s Power Insignia","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess looked at Zu An in surprise, curious to know why he'd suddenly asked such a question. The Dragon Kings had said that Shennong existed a very long time ago. Could someone live for so long?","Some time passed before the person in the cave replied, “You’re overestimating me. How can I be that person?”","Sensing the other party’s deference toward Shennong, Zu An continued probing, “Are you Shennong’s successor, or his descendant, or the Flame Emperor of the current generation?”","In the legends, the Flame Emperor and the Yellow Emperor had combined their forces, which was why it was said that all humans were ‘descendants of the Flame and Yellow’. Shennong was the first Flame Emperor, though the term 'Flame Emperor' referred to more than just him.","The person in the cave was taken aback. “You know quite a bit. Yes, I am related to Shennong, but I’m not the current generation’s Flame Emperor.”","Zu An had expected that answer. “May I know where the current generation’s Flame Emperor is? Why doesn’t he lead humankind to fend against the invading monsters?”","He had no idea what had happened to the Flame Emperor in this world, but he'd previously encountered Yu the Great. The latter was extremely powerful, and he was the original wielder of the Rune Weapon Chart. The Flame Emperor was at least of the same standing as Yu the Great in the legends, and he should have been able to curb the monsters.","Zu An harbored many doubts in his mind. He had stumbled upon the remnants of different dynasties in the Cultivation World, and these dynasties had all wielded incredible powers, unlike the mundane dynasties in his previous world.","But where did those incredible powerhouses go? It would only take one of them to suppress the monsters. While this Cultivation World from several thousand years back is much stronger than it is in the future, it's still no match for the Monster World.","The person in the cave replied, “It’s all fated.”","Zu An was speechless. He expected to hear more, but that was all. All his talk about fate makes him sound like a con artist.","Knowing there was no point in persisting with this topic, he decided to ask about another, more pressing concern. “I've heard the Firecloud Cave is proficient in medicine. May I ask if there is a way to save someone afflicted with the innate Cruel Poison Constitution?”","The man in the cave was surprised by that question. “I thought the Cruel Poison Constitution was just a thing of legend. That constitution grants one high affinity toward all kinds of poisons, but if it acts up, it can only be suppressed by a more potent poison. That poison can be used in combat, but it only worsens the condition. It’s only a matter of time before the poison becomes insuppressible and destroys the host and the world along with it.”","The Peacock Princess looked at Zu An with worried eyes. Why is big brother suddenly asking about that? Does he have the Cruel Poison Constitution?","The Mermaid Queen knew the truth. Is his little sister’s illness that terrifying? No wonder he hasn’t found a cure for her to date.","The person in the cave continued, “I do know a way to resolve the Cruel Poison Constitution, however. With certain cultivation techniques and rare materials, you can condense the poison into an inner core and achieve a balance. It won’t solve the problem at its root, but it can at least spare the host from an untimely death.”","Zu An found those words weirdly familiar.","“The stronger the cultivation technique used, the stronger the condensed poison core will be. You’ll have to look for a cultivation technique that complements the Cruel Poison Constitution by yourself. It’ll depend on the luck of both you and the host of the Cruel Poison Constitution.","“I am, however, familiar with the rare materials required—Defying Spirit Tears, a Brilliant Pinflower, and an Aurora Poison Dragon’s inner core. Since you are here to treat the poisoned Ocean races, I presume you already have the Aurora Poison Dragon’s inner core,” the man in the cave said.","Zu An was baffled. For a moment there, he wondered if the person in the cave was Salamay. However, he knew that was impossible. How did Salamay learn about this method?","It was unlikely for Salamay to have been to the enigmatic Firecloud Cave, and there was no reason for her to have sought a solution to the Cruel Poison Constitution. If so, there could only be one explanation. This world’s Salamay had to have learned about it from him, the Mermaid Queen, or the Peacock Princess.","After some thought, he thought it was more likely for Salamay to have heard about it from him. He was reminded of what Mi Li had previously told him about spacetime. Is this considered closing the loop too?","For a moment there, he even wondered about the eternal paradox—did the chicken or the egg come first?","He quickly reined in his thoughts and continued asking, “Do you know where I can find Defying Spirit Tears and a Brilliant Pinflower?”","“You can find Brilliant Pinflowers in this world, but finding such rare materials is highly luck-dependent. If it’s not fated, it won’t make a difference even if I provide you with a location. Conversely, if it’s fated, you'll find it even if I don’t say a word,” the man in the cave replied.","Zu An was speechless. Salamay had also previously mentioned that this world could have Brilliant Pinflowers, so he'd thought he could gather more information from this fellow.","“As for Defying Spirit Tears...” The man in the cave suddenly paused as if he was contemplating something. “They don’t exist in the world right now, but you might have a chance to obtain them in the future.”","Zu An was confused.","He tried asking for more details, but the man in the cave gave cryptic replies, such as, “The time isn’t ripe yet. You’ll know when the time comes.”","Ugh, there’s nothing more frustrating than riddlers! I don’t even know what Defying Spirit Tears are, let alone how to obtain them!","Just then, four pills flew out from the cave. “Place these four pills in each of the four seas. They will dissolve in water and neutralize the poison from the plague formation.”","The Mermaid Queen quickly stowed away the four pills. “Elder, thank you for your medicine. The Ocean races will remember this favor.”","“It’s all decided by fate,” the man in the cave replied calmly.","The trio had long gotten used to this answer.","“Our fate is up. Water Boy, send them out.”","The boy nodded. He walked over and gestured for them to leave with him.","Zu An suddenly remembered another matter and asked, “One last question. I heard Shennong was the first Human Emperor. May I know where the Human Path’s power insignia is currently?”","The boy was annoyed. “You don’t know your manners. My master is asking you to leave. You shouldn’t be asking any more questions.”","A chuckle echoed from the cave.","Zu An frowned. He sensed a deeper intent to the laugh, but he couldn’t tell what it was about.","“Why are you searching for the Human Path’s power insignia?” the man in the cave asked.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. Since he’s entertaining my question, there should be a chance. Thus, he told the man in the cave about the Six Paths of Reincarnation. He reckoned that considering his stature, the latter would know something about it. However, he withheld key information concerning Houtu as a precaution.","“Completing the Six Paths of Reincarnation would be a huge merit, but it won’t be easy,” the man in the cave said.","“I still have to give it a try. If I collect the power insignias one at a time, there will come a day when all six power insignias are gathered.” Zu An didn’t reveal that he already had some of the power insignias, because the other party was simply too mysterious.","“That’s a good mindset.” The man in the cave expressed his approval. “All right. You can find the Human Path’s power insignia with the Fiend races.”","“The Fiend races?” Zu An was perplexed. Why is the Human Path’s power insignia not with the humans, but with the Fiend races?","Sensing his doubt, the man in the cave laughed. “Why do you think the Fiend races don’t belong to the Human Path? This world itself is the Human Path. Since the Fiend races are the rulers of this world, it should go without saying that the Human Path’s power insignia is in their hands.”"]},{"number":2530,"title":"Chapter 2530: Chapter 2482: Bitterness","paragraphs":["Zu An was stunned. He suddenly realized that he had unknowingly narrowed the scope of his thoughts too far. He'd instinctively assumed the Human Path’s power insignia was with the humans, and that the humans were the rulers of this world. It was only upon the other party’s reminder that it dawned on him that the Human Path had more than just the human race.","In the future, it was proven that the Cultivation World was the Human Path; it was just that the Fiend races were the stronger ones now. That sparked a thought in his mind, but the thought drifted away before he could clutch onto it.","Nevertheless, it was a fruitful journey. He earnestly said out of gratitude, “Thank you for the enlightenment, elder.”","The man in the cave calmly replied, “If you are truly grateful to me, fulfill my request.”","As if fearing Zu An would ask more questions, the space around them distorted. Before they knew it, the three of them had already returned to the Crystal Boat. They quickly scanned their surroundings, but the island and the Firecloud Cave were nowhere to be seen.","“Was I dreaming earlier?” The Peacock Princess rubbed her eyes in confusion.","“No, it wasn’t a dream,” the Mermaid Queenreplied with a quivering voice as she looked at the pills in her hands.","Zu An looked at the vast ocean and remarked, “What a profound formation.”","All that was left in front of them was the ocean, meaning that someone had moved the island elsewhere. Zu An was awed by the Firecloud Cave’s methods. Speaking of which, is he truly the successor of the Flame Emperor...","The Mermaid Queen was glad that her people could be saved, but the realization that she would have to part ways with Zu An caused her smile to stiffen up.","The Peacock Princess just had to poke the hornet’s nest then. “Big sis queen, shall we first accompany you back to the Dragon Palace?”","The Mermaid Queen could see through her intention, but she shook her head and said, “No, you still have other matters to attend to. I shall not hold you back.” She then turned to Zu An and asked, “May I have a private conversation with you?”","Upon seeing the plea in her eyes, Zu An’s heart softened. He nodded and followed her to the other end of the deck.","The Mermaid Queen had many things she wanted to tell him, but now that their moment of parting had come, she suddenly found herself at a loss for words. They stood in silence for a long time.","It was Zu An who broke the silence in the end. “Stay safe. You should take the Crystal Boat back.”","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “The Crystal Boat is the Dragon King’s gift to you. I can’t take it. Besides, there’s still some distance before you reach land. You’ll need it.”","The corners of her lips curled up. Without this Crystal Boat, big brother Zu might have to carry the Peacock Princess for the rest of the journey. This shall be my little vengeance against her.","“But it’s a long distance for you...” Zu An was worried.","The Mermaid Queen smiled. “Have you forgotten my race? The ocean is my home turf.”","Zu An thought those words made sense. In the water, mermaids are fearsome adversaries.","Silence descended between them once more.","The Mermaid Queen realized it was about time for her to leave and asked, “Can I have a hug before we part ways?”","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected such a request from her. He wondered whether to turn down her request, especially since he wasn’t from this era and didn’t want to influence her.","Sensing his rejection, the Mermaid Queen laughed miserably. “This might be our final parting. After all the time we spent together, do I not at least deserve a friendly hug?”","Tears trickled down her cheeks and landed on the deck, producing crisp knocking sounds. Mermaid tears turned into pearls upon striking the ground, after all.","Zu An knew this could be their final farewell too. His determination wavered. He was about to open his arms to embrace the Mermaid Queen when a trembling body suddenly held onto him tightly.","Zu An fell into a daze. At that moment, he experienced the emotion called bitterness.","He had never believed in monogamy. Under normal circumstances, he wouldn’t have turned the Mermaid Queen down. But the difference in their eras evoked his helplessness. He knew there was no future between the two of them.","Instead of hurting each other, it was better for them to sever ties for good.","It was no wonder that in his previous life’s literary works, love had so many hurdles. He had always scoffed at those tropes, but now, he understood that not all hurdles could be overcome with effort.","Zu An let out another sigh. He was about to speak when he saw the Mermaid Queen’s face approaching him, and a pair of soft lips pressed against his. His eyes widened in astonishment.","It was a kiss most men in the world would have been envious of, but he was in no mood to enjoy it. Instead, his mind was in disarray.","All of a sudden, he felt a sharp pain. He instinctively touched his lips and saw a trace of blood.","The Mermaid Queen had already let go of him and retreated to the corner of the boat. She looked at him with a mischievous smile, saying, “I don’t know if we’ll ever meet again, so I want you to remember that sensation forever. Farewell, my lover.”","She turned around and leaped into the ocean, turning into a beautiful mermaid as she swam into the distance. She didn’t turn around, fearing that she wouldn’t be able to leave anymore if she did.","The setting sun cast glistening specks of light on the ocean's surface. Zu An couldn’t tell if those were just light reflections or her tears.","The Peacock Princess walked up to Zu An and sighed sadly, “Big sis queen has left.”","She regretted playing such a trick on the Mermaid Queen earlier. Big brother doesn’t belong to this era anyway, so what’s the point of competing for him? She thus said, “Big brother, once you’re done with your business in the Fiend races' side, you can return to the Ocean races' side.”","Zu An shook his head. There were too many things he had to do, and the world was always throwing new tasks at him. Who knew if he would have a chance to return to the Ocean races' side?","The two of them continued their journey to the Fiend races’ imperial court. The Dragon King’s Crystal Boat could soar through the sky as well, though it was much slower than traveling on the ocean. Still, it was much faster than the airplanes in Zu An's previous life.","Along the way, the Peacock Princess asked Zu An about the descendant he had gotten close to, whereas Zu An asked her about the Fiend races.","Soon, they arrived at the Fiend races’ temporary imperial court.","The Fiend race experts guarding the perimeter were already expecting their arrival. “Princess, this must be the great hero our Saintess mentioned. The Saintess has been awaiting your arrival!”"]},{"number":2531,"title":"Chapter 2531: Chapter 2483: Saintess","paragraphs":["The Xuan-Su Guards were from the Peacock race and had the ability to fly. They had returned in advance to inform the Fiend races about what had happened in the Ocean races' territory.","The Saintess had quickly gotten to work and built Zu An up as a peerless hero who single-handedly defeated the Incestuous King’s army.","The Fiend races had been oppressed by the monsters for a long time. Even though the Saintess occasionally scored some victories, all that had done was stop the Fiend races from declining further. They had never experienced such a huge victory over the monsters before.","Some had been overjoyed to hear the Saintess’ words, but most took a skeptical attitude. They had fought the monsters for a long time and knew how formidable the Incestuous King was; it was hard to believe a person could single-handedly defeat the Incestuous King and his army.","Despite their skepticism, however, they were tactful enough not to question it in public. The Fiend races were in urgent need of a major victory to boost their morale, and they lauded the Saintess for her wise move. A few did believe that Zu An was a hero, but most were feigning excitement while secretly investigating his background.","Now that they were looking at Zu An in person, they frowned. They knew not to judge a book by its cover, yet he was so dashing that they wondered if he was a moocher; but at the same time, there was an inexplicable aura shrouding him.","Damn, he’s so handsome that even the Peacock Princess is staring holes into him.","Years of warring with the monsters had resulted in the death of the older fiends, and the ones carrying the flag now were the younger generations. Most still had a youthful temperament.","The Peacock Princess was a renowned beauty in the Fiend races, and unlike the Saintess, she didn’t feel out of reach. Countless Fiend race men adored her for that, which was why it irked them to see the Peacock Princess standing so close to Zu An.","Still, even though they were young, they knew their priorities. No one was so foolish as to jump out and antagonize Zu An at a time like this.","A dashing man dressed in golden armor walked over and asked, “Little sister Qingwu, is this the great hero who defeated the Incestuous King? Why don’t you introduce him to us?”","Another man wearing a golden cape voiced his agreement.","These two men appeared to be the leaders of these youths.","Despite their courteous attitudes, Zu An still keenly sensed a faint hostility from the crowd. He noticed the gazes they directed at the Peacock Princess, and the truth became apparent to him. A beautiful lady is bound to have many suitors. That’s perfectly normal. It’d be excessive to make a fuss over this.","But the Peacock Princess frowned in dissatisfaction. “The Saintess is waiting for big brother.”","The words 'big brother’ further fanned the crowd’s jealousy.","The golden-caped man said, “We’re still a fair distance away from the Saintess’ residence. Why don’t we head there together, and you can introduce him to us along the way? We have nothing but admiration for the great hero who single-handedly destroyed the Incestuous King’s army.”","Zu An calmly watched the spectacle. Judging from the other party’s enunciations, he could tell that the latter didn’t believe he could defeat Mojard’s army, but the current Zu An had weathered too many storms to be fazed by something like this. It’s just a bunch of hot-blooded youths.","The Peacock Princess had witnessed Zu An’s prowess in person, and she mistakenly thought others knew about his strength too. That led to the golden-caped man’s sarcasm flying over her head. “This is big brother Necropolis. He might be young, but he is extremely powerful. Even the Incestuous King isn’t his match, let alone you lot.”","Black streaks appeared on Zu An’s face. This young lass speaks her mind. Her words are so candid that it’s drawing hatred for me. But he wasn’t bothered by it. Rather, he was curious to know whether these young fellows would challenge him.","The expressions of the Fiend race youths darkened. “Big brother Necropolis is indeed incredible to have defeated the Incestuous King. May we ask about the details of the battle?”","Zu An looked too young, and he didn’t give off an air of intimidation either. It was hard to think of him as a powerful expert, so it was no wonder they didn’t believe the Peacock Princess’ words.","The Peacock Princess finally sensed the skepticism in the air. “Shoo; my big brother has no time to talk about these things with you.” Fearing that some fools might actually challenge Zu An, she quickly added, “That golden-armored guy who looks like a nouveau riche is the Fiend races’ third prince. That guy with a yellow cloth wrapped around his body is the Golden Peng race’s crown prince...”","She only introduced the important figures around her, and even so, her introduction was extremely brief, as she didn’t think that someone as important as her big brother had time to waste on mere brats.","The Third Prince and the Golden Peng Crown Prince had awful-looking expressions. All of them had grown up together, and the Peacock Princess often talked to them like that. However, they were in the presence of an outsider. It felt as if they were being slighted.","Zu An lamented his ill fate with the Golden Crow race and Golden Peng race. Even now that he had returned to the past, they still viewed each other with hostility.","Fortunately, with the encroachment of the monster army, the only ones left among the Fiend races were the true elites. Despite feeling a little humiliated, they were able to rein themselves in and not cause a fuss.","The crowd escorted Zu An to a palace, though it felt like a stretch to call it a palace, as it only looked marginally better than the houses he saw along the way. The Fiend races had suffered a series of losses, losing even their imperial court. This was the best building they could construct on the spot, since the bulk of their resources would be devoted to fending against the monsters.","A guard at the doorway stopped the crowd. “The Saintess wishes to meet the great hero alone. Please wait outside.”","The crowd was taken aback, but they didn’t dare to defy the highly-esteemed Saintess.","“The Saintess should have personally welcomed you upon your arrival, but for some reason, she called you over instead. Big brother, I hope you don’t mind it. The Saintess must have her reasons for doing so,” the Peacock Princess explained telepathically.","Zu An smiled. “Don’t worry, I’m not that narrow-minded.”","He stepped into the palace. A maid brought him to a serene courtyard and said, “The Saintess is waiting for you inside.”","The maid bowed and took her leave.","Zu An was surprised. The Saintess should have met him in a public space, such as her study, but this courtyard appeared to be her personal residence. For a moment, he felt vigilant. Could the Saintess be scheming something to blackmail me?","On second thought, he remembered that the Yumen Beiqing he'd met at the Sealed Land wasn’t an underhanded person. So, he entered the courtyard, though he continued to keep his guard up lest he fall for the other party’s trap.","“You’re finally here,” a voice echoed from the room, sending shudders through Zu An’s body."]},{"number":2532,"title":"Chapter 2532: Chapter 2484: The Most Familiar Stranger","paragraphs":["A dignified lady stood in the courtyard, dressed in a snowy-white shirt and a loose red skirt. Her clothes showcased no feminine curves, but if the world were a portrait, her ravishing visage would be what made the painting the most beautiful thing in the world. When contrasted with her clothes, her fair skin looked even fairer. Her beauty was slightly beneath that of the Mermaid Queen, and she was also nowhere as vibrant as the Peacock Princess. However, she was graceful and dignified. She emanated a natural air of inviolability just by standing there.","For a moment, Zu An thought he was looking at Kikyo from Inuyasha.","No wonder the Fiend races’ men all compliment the Saintess’ beauty, but her suitors are nowhere as many as the Peacock Princess. She’s a mortal, but somehow she feels divine.","Yumen Beiqing had been crafting talismans when she sensed Zu An’s entrance and lifted her head.","Zu An felt an uncanny sense of familiarity from her, possibly because he had once met her in the Sealed Land. He said with a smile, “Paying respect to the Saintess.\"","He felt the joy of reuniting with an acquaintance, though the latter wouldn’t know that they had once met each other.","Little did he expect the Saintess to suddenly shoot to her feet and quickly walk up to him. Zu An could tell that the body beneath those loose clothes was trembling. She seemed to be exerting a great deal of willpower to hold herself back. That made him frown. What’s with Yumen Beiqing’s reaction?","Both the Ocean races and the Peacock Princess had said that the Saintess was someone who could remain perfectly composed even when in dire straits. It was bizarre for her to display such a blatant breach of etiquette. Is she nervous or afraid because she’s planning something?","Zu An scanned the surroundings with his divine sense, worried that there could be an ambush, but there was no one else in this courtyard other than the two of them. This is weird...","As the other party drew closer, Zu An cleared the air with a cough and called out, “Saintess?”","As she looked at him, Yumen Beiqing bit her lower lip. Her eyes glistened with tears, and she looked as if there were countless words she wanted to tell him.","Zu An’s heart quivered at the sight of such pitiful eyes. Why is she acting as if she's known me for a long time? Does she remember our meeting in the Sealed Land? But that’s supposed to happen in the future!","While he was perplexed, the Saintess suddenly leaped into his chest and embraced him tightly. He was dumbfounded.","He had thought of countless possibilities when the two of them met, but he hadn’t expected the legendary Saintess to leap into his arms. Could this truly be a scheme to blackmail me? Does the Saintess intend to use her beauty to recruit me as a fighter for the Fiend races?","But the genuine emotions in the Saintess’ eyes and her trembling body didn’t seem to be a lie. This didn’t feel like a honey trap.","The Saintess couldn’t have fallen in love with me at first sight, right? Zu An quickly snuffed out that notion as soon as it surfaced in his mind. That was impossible.","Who could have known a pair of lips would press against his the next second?","Zu An was bewildered. His body stiffened up. What in the world is going on?","Feeling the need to get to the bottom of this, he was just about to push the Saintess away when the latter suddenly said, “Big brother Zu, you are finally here to see me.”","Goosebumps rose all over Zu An’s body. The only one who knew his name was the Mermaid Queen. Even the Peacock Princess only knew him as ‘Necropolis’. How had the Saintess learned his name?","Now that he thought about it, the Saintess had also acted as if she'd known him for a long time when they met in the Sealed Land. Did I, at some point in the future, return even further back in time and become acquainted with her?","While he was completely confused, the Saintess realized something and hurriedly explained with a reddened face, “Big brother Zu, I am Ling’er!”","Zu An was shocked. “Little sister Ling’er?”","He stared at the Saintess in disbelief. She is Xie Daoyun?","While there was an uncanny sense of familiarity about her, she looked nothing like Xie Daoyun, though it wouldn’t be right to say there were no similarities at all. Her air of serenity and grace did resemble Xie Daoyun’s.","“In the Monster World’s underground city, I came into contact with a mysterious piece of jade and was transported to this world. I thought I would never see you again!” The Saintess dropped her usual strong front and sobbed like a child.","Those words dissipated all of Zu An’s doubts. He tightly hugged her too. “Little sister Ling’er!”","Back when Xie Daoyun first disappeared, he was horrified, though he had an inexplicable feeling that they would meet again soon. He hadn’t expected them to reunite under such circumstances.","The two of them embraced each other tightly. Before long, their lips were locked together as if these acts of intimacy were the only ways they could let the other party know their feelings.","The Saintess placed her hands on Zu An’s shoulders. Her slender fingers were like ivory tusks, and her forehead accessories gleamed under the sunlight, just like her mesmerizing eyes.","...","The Peacock Princess nervously paced to and fro outside the courtyard. She had no idea why the Saintess had requested to meet Zu An in private. The Saintess had always been transparent, choosing to open everything up for discussion. This was the first time she had requested to meet someone in private.","She wasn't worried about Zu An being harmed by the Saintess; the former could protect himself, whereas the latter wasn't one to do something that foolish. What worried her more was the Saintess falling in love with the perfect Zu An.","However, she quickly shrugged off that thought as soon as it surfaced. The Saintess was called as such because she aligned with what the Fiend races imagined a Saintess to be. She was beautiful yet inviolable, and she displayed incredible charisma as she led the Fiend races in the battle for their survival. She treated everyone with warmth, yet she showed no interest in secular love. Everyone in the Fiend races acknowledged her because they knew she wouldn’t be biased toward any of them.","The discussions of the Fiend youths around her showed as much. They were more worried about Zu An doing something disrespectful to the Saintess.","That angered the Peacock Princess. Big brother isn’t that kind of person!","Most of them quickly realized that their worry was unnecessary. Even if they couldn’t trust Zu An, surely they could trust the Saintess. The discussion thus moved on to speculations about what the two were talking about.","“They are probably discussing a partnership.”","“Regardless of whether his feats are exaggerated or not, it is a fact that he helped the Ocean races defeat the monster army. Securing his help will be greatly beneficial to us.”","Just then, someone meekly asked, “You’re all talking about the Saintess winning him over to our side. Have you considered the possibility of him taking our Saintess away instead? I mean, he is quite good-looking.”","The next moment, silence descended."]},{"number":2533,"title":"Chapter 2533: Chapter 2485: He Is My Man","paragraphs":["After a brief silence, laughter erupted.","“How is that possible?”","“Indeed. Our Saintess wouldn’t be shaken by secular love.”","“So many outstanding youths haveurted her in recent years, but she didn’t even spare them a glance. That’s why everyone was eventually forced to give up.”","...","The Fiend youths laughed as if what they had just heard was the biggest joke ever.","The Peck Princess was delighted but frustrated. She was glad she didn’t have to worry about the Saintess going after Zu An, but she didn’t like how those words made it seem as if her feelings for him were crude.","Our romance transcends spacetime, alright?!","But the reminder that Zu An didn’t belong to this era dampened her mood.","“My princess, can you tell us about the great hero’s battle with the Incestuous King? Did someone as young as him really defeat the Incestuous King?” someone asked curiously.","The others voiced their agreement too. The news delivered by the Xuan-Su Guards was so inceivable that they wondered if they had exaggerated the details because their cultivation was too low to discern the battle’s details. The Saintessuld have only accepted their statements to raise their people’s morale. It would be more reliable to hear the aunt of an expert like the Peck Princess.","The eyes of the Peck Princess lit up. Even three days wouldn’t be enough for her to speak about Zu An’s exploits. She began sharing the details.","Her mention of how the abrupt appearance of the monsters had driven the Ocean races into despair invited nods from the crowd—they had witnessed the monster army’s prowess in person before.","Then, Zu An had appeared. He'd dove into the monster army and wrecked them like a berserker, causing the monsters to scream and blood to flow like a river.","There was no discrepancy between reality and her aunt, but the Peck Princess, due to her rose-tinted glasses, thought that her version was much more awe-inspiring.","Many people voiced their doubts.","“How can an individual rival an army? What about the monster formation masters? Did they not do a thing at all?”","The Peck Princess slowly replied, “Big brother has an ultimate move—henjureduntless weapons out of thin air to decimate the formation masters.”","“What ultimate move can be that formidable?” The crowd found it inceivable. Formation masters were the most protected group in an army. They weren’t just skilled in long-ranged offense, but defensive formations too. Even the Fiend Emperoruldn’t destroy the formation masters in an army single-handedly.","The Peck Princess ffed at their doubts. “The Ocean races’ experts were all present, including the Mermaid Queen whom you all dream about. You canrroborate the details with them if you don’t believe me.”","Those words won her some credibility.","“What about the Incestuous King? Someone as strong as him wouldn’t just watch as the great hero decimated his army,” someone pointed out.","“He made his move. He released his beast form and his body grew to hundreds of meters tall,” the Peck Princess said, then runted what happened then.","The faces of the Fiend youths darkened. They had witnessed the prowess of the Incestuous King’s beast form in the battle where they suffered the greatest loss. They remembered the immense pressure they'd felt, and just the thought of it evoked a hint of despair in them. The Incestuous King had charged into their army and massacred them as if they were mere ants. Their army formation hadllapsed, and it had eventually bme a one-sided slaughter.","The Peck Princess’ eyes gleamed with excitement as shentinued, “But big brother is even more formidable...” As if she had bme a roadside storyteller, she vividly shared the situation with the crowd, occasionally taking some creative liberties to make Zu An seem even greater.","The Fiend youths were flabbergasted. They had thought the previous story was an exaggeration, but whould have thought the truth would be even more exaggerated than that?","The Golden Crow Prince and Golden Peng Crown Prince exchanged fearful looks. It’s a relief we didn’t provoke that guy in the heat of the moment, or else we would have bme clowns.","The crowd was overjoyed to hear that the Ocean races and the mysterious races beneath the Eye of the Ocean were willing to ally with the Fiend races.","“With the Saintess’ leadership and an expert of the great hero’s caliber, we can surely defeat those vile monsters!”","The crowd’s faces beamed with excitement as they dreamed about defeating the monsters and returning to their homeland.","But the Golden Peng Crown Prince pouredld water over the enthused crowd. “It’s too early to celebrate. There’s no guarantee an expert of that caliber will help us. We might not be able to afford his help.”","The crowd’s hearts sank.","There’s no reason for an expert of that caliber to help us. Someone that strong would be celebrated as an esteemed guest no matter where he went, even in the Monster World. He might even be able to usurp the Incestuous King’s position.","There’s nothing he can gain from helping us, especially now that the Fiend races are in their weakest state ever.","The crowd turned to the Peck Princess.","The Peck Princess’ face reddened. “Why are you looking at me?”","“Princess, how far have you progressed with the great hero?” a curious youth asked.","Those words piqued the anger of those who adored the Peck Princess.","The usually sharp-tongued Peck Princess suddenly lost her usual eloquence. “I-it’s not like what you think!”","“Princess, why don’t you sacrifice yourself for the sake of our Fiend races’ future? An expert of his caliber should be worthy of you,” another youth from a major race said. He favored the Saintess more than the Peck Princess, allowing him to objectively decide theurse of action that maximized the Fiend races’ interest.","The Peck Princess sighed. “It’s not that I’m reluctant, but...” She briefly paused beforentinuing, “Even the Mermaid Queen triedurting him, but to no avail.”","“What?!” The crowd was stunned.","If the Peck Princess was only famous in their circle, the Mermaid Queen was a world-famous beauty! It wouldn’t be a stretch to call her the number one beauty in the world, given how she had turned down even the Fiend Emperor. To think that legendary woman wouldurt the man from earlier and fail at that! That would have been a dream for any other man, but he turned her down! Is that fellow still a man?!","Just then, theurtyard doors opened.","“The Saintess is out!”","The crowd looked over, only to freeze in place. Their usually placid Saintess was now resting against Zu An’s chest with flushed cheeks.","The Saintess was embarrassed to have so many gazes on her, but she still gently spoke up. “Let me introduce him to you. He is my man.”","The crowd was speechless.","The Peck Princess was bewildered."]},{"number":2534,"title":"Chapter 2534: Chapter 2486: The Domineering Saintess Is In Love With Me","paragraphs":["Zu An and the Saintess shared such a passionate kiss that they naturally landed on the bed. The last time they met, they had just promised themselves to each other before being abruptly torn apart. Now that they had reunited, they were like newlyweds. Passionate activities naturally ensued.","When their bodies and souls became one, the two of them shed tears of joy... though a large part of the Saintess’ tears were out of pain.","Zu An was taken aback to see that. “Why are you still...”","Xie Daoyun shyly explained, “In this world, I am Yumen Beiqing, the Fiend races’ Saintess.”","Zu An was stunned. “What about your original body?”","Xie Daoyun looked wistful. “I don’t know either. I don’t know how much time passed after I took that jade. I felt as if I was floating in chaos before abruptly waking up in this body. I don’t know if I can ever return to my original body.”","Zu An quickly consoled her, saying, “Don’t worry, Yumen Beiqing should just be your identity in this world. You should revert to your original body once you return to your original era.”","In truth, he wasn’t confident about that. What if Xie Daoyun’s return to the future caused the Saintess’ body to disappear, and her original body didn’t return? Wouldn’t that cause her soul to dissipate?","But I should have regained my position as the underworld’s master by then. Even if she’s only left with her soul, I should be able to find a way to save her.","Xie Daoyun meekly said, “Big brother Zu, let’s not talk about unhappy things. I’m already very happy to be able to see you again.”","It was only upon seeing her reddened face that Zu An was reminded of what they were in the midst of. Still, looking at her familiar yet foreign face felt rather weird to him. “Somehow, it feels as if I'm getting intimate with someone else.”","Xie Daoyun’s face reddened. “But it’s still me. Besides... After realizing that, you seem even more excited.” She was so embarrassed that she averted her eyes. Saying such words was already a lot for her.","Zu An felt awkward. They were in such an intimate position that there was no way to disguise his physical reactions. Looking at her adorable actions and her ethereal aura as a Saintess, he couldn’t resist the urge to kiss her once more.","Xie Daoyun moaned as she tightly hugged her lover’s neck, channeling her yearning to alleviate her pain. Slowly, the pain dissipated into tender sweetness.","...","Some time later, Xie Daoyun crawled up from Zu An’s chest. She looked flustered. “Ah, I forgot there are Fiend race officials waiting outside. This won’t do. I need to talk to them, or else they might do something out of recklessness.”","Her unique disposition, which was an amalgamation of purity and seductiveness, made Zu An reluctant to let her go, but he knew that they had spent too much time in the room. Thus, he got up and dressed himself. “Shall we pretend not to know each other? Otherwise it will be hard to...”","A finger pressed against his lips before he could finish speaking. “No, I don’t want you to suffer any grievances. I want everyone to know about our relationship.”","Xie Daoyun's face reflected decisiveness and courage like never before. This was the leadership she had honed over the years as the Saintess, leading the Fiend races against the monsters.","Zu An chuckled. Am I in a ‘Domineering CEO dotes on her little husband’ script?","He found it interesting, and he wasn’t averse to it either. He followed her out and heard her blissfully introduce him as her man.","A brief, unnerving silence ensued before an uproar exploded. Many people looked desperate.","“Please think thrice, Saintess!”","“Saintess, did he coerce you into this?”","“Just give us a nod, and we’ll slaughter him!”","...","Countless people were caught off guard.","The beautiful Saintess commanded incomparable prestige in the Fiend races. She was beautiful, gentle, strong, and a good leader. There was no one in the Fiend races who didn’t like her. Outstanding youths from distinguished backgrounds had confessed to her but were all rejected. They'd been told that her mind was so devoted to fending against the monsters, that she didn’t have the energy to think about romance.","That further elevated the crowd’s respect for her. From that moment on, they had seen the Saintess with an air of divinity. The Saintess had rejected many princes and young masters from the Fiend races’ upper echelons, but no one saw a problem because they were all rejected equally. If anything, that made them respect her even more. Since then, anyone who dared court the Saintess had become a public enemy. Even though the Saintess’ popularity had shot up, more people courted the Peacock Princess instead.","That was why they were horrified to see the Saintess hugging another man and saying those words. Their first thought was that the Saintess had been coerced into doing the other party’s bidding.","Looking at the hundreds of thousands of Rage points surging in, Zu An was awed by the Saintess’ incredible popularity.","The Saintess was startled to see the crowd up in arms. She anxiously explained, “I am not being coerced. He truly is my lover!”","When she confirmed her stance, the sound of breaking hearts was almost audible.","Many noticed the Saintess’ flushed face and recalled how intimate they had been when they walked out of the courtyard. Their minds couldn’t help but imagine what happened inside the room.","Our sacred, flawless Saintess has just been violated by a man. Crap, an image is forming in my head. No, shut it down! Shut it dooooown!","Everyone, including the Peacock Princess, looked as if they were on the verge of a mental breakdown.","She recalled how she had been telling the crowd about how Zu An had dove into the monster army and wrecked them like a berserker.","Little did I know he was diving into the Saintess and wrecking her in the meantime.","The thought of that nearly drove her mad.","Isn’t big brother from the future? Why is he getting together with the Saintess? He didn’t even sway when big sis queen courted him!","Even though the Saintess boasted incredible popularity among the Fiend races, the only one whose femininity the Peacock Princess admired was the Mermaid Queen. The Saintess felt more like a pillar of support. She was gorgeous, but her air of inviolability made one forget that she was a woman.","Why would big brother get together with the Saintess on their first meeting? Was he lying to us? Was he actually not from the future?","Many people began questioning the Saintess about what was going on.","The Saintess gestured for the crowd to calm down before gently explaining, “We are already engaged; it is just that we were separated due to various reasons. I’m glad the world has brought us back together.” She looked at Zu An with gentle eyes.","Zu An held her hand. “Indeed, we are a couple. I’m thankful to fate for our reunion.”","Looking at the lovey-dovey couple, the Peacock Princess suddenly felt a surge of anger. Saintess, you’re being unfair!"]},{"number":2535,"title":"Chapter 2535: Chapter 2487: I’ll Quit Being a Saintess","paragraphs":["Unable to take it anymore, the Peacock Princess protested, “Big brother, how can the two of you be lovers? Aren’t you...”","Thankfully, she realized it would be unwise to reveal the secret that he was from the future, causing her words to trail off right there. Her face slowly turned bright red.","The others thought that she was just agitated because she had a crush on Zu An. But she wasn’t the only one. Nearly all of the Fiend youths gathered here were agitated. They'd thought a strong ally had arrived to help them defeat the monsters, but the first thing he'd done upon arriving was to snatch away their respected Saintess!","They had only been able to come to terms with the Saintess’ rejection because she did the same for everyone. But now that she was cuddling against the chest of another man, they suddenly felt jealous like never before.","To think that we were still so deeply in love with the Saintess!","The looks of hostility coming from the surroundings left Zu An with a headache. He decided to start with the Peacock Princess’ question. “Princess, we are indeed a couple. It is a long story. I’ll share it with you in private next time.”","The Peacock Princess pouted. She still felt terrible, but Zu An’s consideration of her feelings alleviated her anger a little.","The other Fiend race youths sneered. Is he trying to two-time now? Is snatching our Saintess away not enough for you, and you want the Peacock Princess too?","The Golden Peng Crown Prince reached the limit of his patience and sneered, “I don’t know how you duped our Saintess, but I shall expose you today!”","The Saintess was acting out of character today. It was completely unlike her usual pure, inviolable image. It felt as if she had suddenly plummeted to the secular world and was ravaged.","Did he use an aphrodisiac on the Saintess to take advantage of her? He just came from the Ocean races's side, and I've heard that the North Sea sea monster’s tentacle fluid is the world’s most potent aphrodisiac.","Just the thought of that made him feel like a knife had been plunged into his heart.","I must rip this despicable man to shreds!","Many shared the same thought, as the disparity between the Saintess before and after meeting Zu An was too great! They suspected that Zu An had cast some kind of sorcery on the Saintess to bewitch her.","A crowd followed the Golden Peng Crown Prince when he rushed over. This wasn't a duel. This matter concerned the safety of the Saintess and the Fiend races. Pride and honor were secondary concerns.","A large pair of golden wings emerged from the Golden Peng Crown Prince’s back. He flapped his wings, and the feathers flew toward Zu An like sharp swords.","I was nearly intimidated just now, but the rumors about the great hero were likely the Saintess and the Peacock Princess exaggerating to bulk up their lover’s reputation. How can a human be that formidable?","Today, I shall rip apart that con artist’s mask!","He even paid careful heed to the angle to avoid harming the Saintess.","Other Fiend experts also attacked Zu An from different angles. They clearly had the same thoughts in mind too.","Just then, a massive golden bell silhouette appeared out of nowhere, shrouding both Zu An and the Saintess.","Dong!","The attacks on the bell produced a loud reverberation. The rebound caused the crowd’s heads to spin and their blood flow to go into disarray.","The Golden Peng Crown Prince had it the worst. The feathers he had unleashed toward Zu An shattered upon contact with the bell, causing him to bleed. Then, the ensuing reverberation sent his blood flow into disarray, causing him to plummet from the sky. However, his companion from the Golden Peng race rushed forward to catch him, sparing him from further injuries.","Zu An sneered at the toppled crowd. “I held back on the Saintess’ account. You won’t be as lucky next time.”","Those planning to attack Zu An immediately stopped what they were doing. His words weren’t intimidating, but the cold look in his eyes sent chills down their spines. For a moment there, they felt like they were facing a deity from heaven.","The ones gathered here were all in the Fiend races’ upper echelons. Those who could reach such a high stature were anything but fools. Judging from the brief ‘clash’, it was apparent to them that Zu An was indeed unfathomably powerful.","The Third Prince was relieved. He had considered attacking Zu An too, but fortunately, the Golden Peng Crown Prince beat him to it, sparing him from humiliation.","The Saintess finally snapped out of her daze and roared in anger, “What are you doing?!”","She pulled out a uniquely-designed talisman that crackled with lightning. Her usually gentle eyes were blazing with rage.","Zu An recognized that as Xie Daoyun’s High Firmament Talisman and was heartened. She was gradually gaining control over these divine talismans thanks to the growth in her cultivation.","The crowd was shocked to see the Saintess bringing out her strongest talismans. They anxiously tried to placate her. “Saintess, there’s no need to go this far!”","The Saintess had lost her temper. She looked at them with frosty eyes. “I kindly introduced my lover to you so that you could share the joys of our reunion, yet you seek to kill him?”","The Third Prince quickly stepped forward to mediate, saying, “Saintess, it’s a misunderstanding! We have never heard about your lover, so we thought he might have used underhanded methods to take advantage of you. It’s all a misunderstanding!”","“Do I look as if I was taken advantage of?” The Saintess regretted her actions a little. She was so happy to be reunited with Zu An that she'd let her feelings get ahead of herself. It had been a long time since anyone confessed to her, so she'd forgotten about that.","Ah, it’s my fault. I wanted to introduce them to big brother Zu, but I ended up making a mess of things.","“Of course not, of course not...” the Third Prince sheepishly replied.","The Saintess had rarely brought out these divine talismans, even in the battles against the monsters. It was unlikely that she would bring them out even if she was under someone else’s control. Besides, she looked earnestly angry.","The Saintess coldly eyed the crowd. “After the years we have spent together, I thought we were a family, but I did not expect you to react to my reunion with my lover with such antagonism. I don’t need this Saintess position anymore.” She reached for the wreath representing her Saintess identity, looking as if she was going to toss it away.","“You mustn’t, Saintess!” This time, the crowd was truly flustered. They tried to dissuade her.","The Peacock Princess rushed over and grabbed her hand, saying, “Please calm down, big sister Saintess. They only acted recklessly out of concern. Now that you have proven that you are lovers, there's no way they would oppose your relationship with big brother.”","As she said those words, she looked at Zu An with eyes so aggrieved that it looked as if tears would fall from them.","The others nodded in agreement. If they lost their Saintess, the Fiend races would be doomed.","So be it if she has a man. She can have ten or a hundred men if she wants. We won’t say a thing about it anymore.","The Saintess looked at Zu An and the Peacock Princess with a perplexed frown. She sent a telepathic message to Zu An, asking, “Big brother Zu, don’t you think she resembles Kong Nanwu?”"]},{"number":2536,"title":"Chapter 2536: Chapter 2488: A Shot at Victory","paragraphs":["Zu An took a look at the Peacock Princess. If not for her young age, she would have looked as if she was carved from the same mold as Kong Nanwu.","The Saintess asked with a peculiar voice, “You couldn’t have stolen her heart within such a short time, could you?”","Zu An rolled his eyes. She’s still in the mood to joke even at a time like this.","More people who hadn’t made a move earlier stepped forward to mediate as well. The Saintess heaved a sigh, wiped away the Peacock Princess’ tears, and said, “Little sister Qingwu, I’ll stay.”","The Peacock Princess’ face lit up in joy, though there was still a shadow on her face when she thought about Zu An and the Saintess’ relationship.","After this farce, everyone’s complexions looked terrible.","Soon, some members of the Fiend races’ upper echelons came out to scatter the crowd before respectfully inviting the Saintess and Zu An to their conference room for a discussion. This was an implicit acknowledgment of their relationship.","The Saintess led Zu An to the conference hall. She was still angry due to the earlier incident, so she dragged Zu An in and settled him down beside her. The Fiend races’ upper echelons exchanged looks, but in the end, they could only accept it with bitter smiles.","A youth from the Tiger race stepped forward and bowed to Zu An. “I apologize for the misunderstandings we had. From the looks of it, you indeed defeated the Incestuous King and his army. We were ignorant.”","The other race leaders also stepped forward to apologize.","Their courtesy convinced Zu An to let the matter go. “We're all here to deal with the monsters. Given the high stakes involved, it’s important to be prudent.”","The Tiger youth laughed. “Thank you for your magnanimity.”","That significantly alleviated the tension in the air.","Soon, the topic turned to the Ocean races. The Saintess turned to Zu An and asked, “Based on the intelligence we received, you were the one who convinced the Ocean races to abandon the monsters and ally with us, right?”","“The monsters harbor malicious intent, and there's no lack of wise people among the Ocean races. They understand the importance of huddling in the face of winter,” Zu An replied with a smile. “The Ocean races are currently dealing with a poisoning incident. Once they're ready, they should send an envoy over for further talks about an alliance.”","“I heard the poison was widespread,” the Saintess said.","Worry painted the other faces in the room. They would have less manpower to oppose the monsters if their future ally suffered a heavy loss here.","“Rest assured, big brother has found the antidote, and the Mermaid Queen has transported it back to the Ocean races. They will overcome this crisis.” The Peacock Princess thought about the time they'd spent in search of the antidote, and a smile formed on her lips.","The others cheered in delight as they looked at Zu An with gratitude.","The Saintess shot a contemplative look at the Peacock Princess. Her face lights up whenever she talks about big brother Zu. She's already fallen for him. Haa, it would be hard for a young lady like her to resist big brother Zu’s charms. It had been the same for her too. Thinking about the past made her feel wistful.","The Third Prince spoke up. “Still, the Ocean races suffered a huge blow. It will take some time before they regain their fighting prowess. Our circumstances still aren’t optimistic.”","The Peacock Princess pointed out, “Big brother recently severely injured the Incestuous King and decimated a monster army.”","The Saintess narrowed her eyes at the mention of the Incestuous King. She had met Mojard in the future, after all.","The Third Prince calmly explained, “Mojard is the third most powerful person in the Monster World, but the one calling the shots is the second-in-command, the Monster Lord. Mojard and the Monster Lord have been on bad terms, and there is significant infighting between the two of them. Their rivalrous relationship has benefited us over the years, securing us some victories.”","The crowd looked to be in low spirits. The Fiend races were usually proud of themselves, but years of war with the monsters had shattered their pride. They had to admit that the victories they'd scored weren't clean, and they understood what the Third Prince was driving at.","The fall of the Incestuous King only made the monsters a greater threat, as the Monster Lord could now devote his effort to dealing with them. The crowd even felt angry at Zu An for shattering the fragile balance, causing their circumstances to worsen.","The Saintess could tell that the Third Prince was trying to lead the crowd on, and her face turned cold. “Third Prince, I disagree with your statements. Big brother Zu has eliminated an elite monster army. As numerous as the monsters are, this is still a huge blow to them. Also, you only see the cons but not the pros behind this matter.”","“If I may ask, Saintess, what benefits are there to this?” the Third Prince sneered.","This woman has let her emotions get to her head. It’ll damage her reputation if she can’t justify herself here. This is a good opportunity for me to regain the authority the imperial family has lost and become the new Fiend Emperor.","Due to his respect for the Saintess, he had never harbored such thoughts before today, but seeing the goddess he revered hugging another man with a flushed face had angered and hurt him deeply.","Since the Saintess doesn’t know what it means to have self-respect, I shall take her place then!","He'd liked the Saintess because of the latter’s inviolable halo, but now that she had become another man’s spoil of war, his interest waned. He wasn’t interested in getting together with someone else’s wife. In fact, he was extremely hygienic about that. He only liked the purest woman in the world.","Zu An sent a telepathic message to the Saintess with a frown. “Little sister Ling’er, that fellow harbors bad intentions. Shall I just get rid of him?”","The Saintess shook her head and replied telepathically, “The Third Prince represents the imperial family. If you make a move against him, the harmony within the Fiend races will collapse. At a time like this, the Fiend races can’t afford such a loss. Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I know what I’m doing.”","She cleared her throat and addressed the race leaders. “The Monster Lord has always been ambitious. He dared not run rampant due to the Incestuous King keeping him in check, but now that the Incestuous King has fallen, those shackles have loosened. What do you think his next move would be?”","Zu An smiled. He could guess where she was driving at. It hasn’t been long since we parted ways, but little sister Ling’er has grown a lot.","“Of course it’s to rally his army to eradicate...” The Third Prince suddenly froze halfway through his words as a thought surfaced in his mind.","Some of the smarter ones in the conference hall also fell into contemplation.","The Saintess slowly added, “Think about it. The monsters have occupied our most prosperous lands. Would they still be interested in these barren lands? To the Monster Lord, even though we have launched a couple of successful retaliatory attacks, the war is already over. We can’t turn the tables around anymore. He can destroy us whenever he wants. But there is a much more pressing problem than us.”","“What is it?” someone anxiously asked.","“The Lord of Slaughter!” the Saintess slowly enunciated a name.","As they remembered the horrors associated with that name, the conference hall fell silent.","The Saintess finally continued, “While the Lord of Slaughter was away, the Monster Lord moved to seize authority within the monster ranks. The one who can curb him, the Incestuous King, is out of the picture. The only obstacle left in his way of becoming the true Monster Lord is the Lord of Slaughter.”"]},{"number":2537,"title":"Chapter 2537: Chapter 2489: Clear My Mind","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the Saintess’ words, the quiet conference hall suddenly buzzed into life. Sorrow vanished from their faces, replaced with excitement.","“That’s true. Why didn’t I think of that?”","“As expected of the Saintess. You are able to see through everything!”","“Under the Saintess’ leadership, it is only a matter of time before we chase the monsters out of our world!”","...","No one thought that the Saintess was under Zu An’s control anymore. She was still as wise and astute as ever, seeing things that others overlooked.","The Third Prince was taken aback too, but he pressed on. “Still, there is a possibility that the Monster Lord might first target us to further build his reputation among the monsters. That would give him more leverage against the Lord of Slaughter.”","The crowd frowned. It was evident that the Third Prince was trying to undermine the Saintess, but they couldn’t deny the possibility of what he had just mentioned.","Zu An finally spoke up. He couldn’t let Xie Daoyun shoulder the pressure alone. “There is such a possibility, so I’ll convince the Monster Lord to go for the other option.”","The Third Prince harrumphed. “The Monster Lord is formidable and skilled at psychological warfare. He wouldn’t change his mind over you.”","“It’s impossible for you, but it’s not too hard for me,” Zu An calmly said.","“You!!!” The Third Prince was infuriated. “Do you dare to issue a military ultimatum?”","You have trolled the Third Prince for +444... +444... +444...","The Saintess frowned. “He’s a guest who came to help us. Third Prince, aren’t you going too far by demanding a military ultimatum from him?”","The Third Prince snorted, “Since he said that it’s not difficult for him, why don’t we strike a deal? If he pulls it off, we’ll let him marry our Saintess. Otherwise, our Fiend races would probably find it hard to accept this marriage.”","The Golden Peng Crown Prince quickly voiced his agreement. “The Third Prince is right.”","Anger flared in the Saintess’ eyes. Zu An also spoke up, saying, “Third Prince, you've gotten something wrong. The Saintess and I are mutually in love, and our relationship doesn’t need anyone’s recognition. Your agreement means nothing to me, not to mention you aren’t qualified to accept my betrothal gifts either.”","The Third Prince sneered, “I must question how much you love the Saintess if you can’t even do this much for her.”","“Indeed!” Almost half of the people in the conference hall voiced their support for the Third Prince.","The Saintess’ face darkened. “Third Prince, you have no business in my private life, much less the right to order my man around.”","The Third Prince sighed. “Saintess, don’t let your emotions get the better of you. You are our Fiend races’ Saintess. Your business is our business.”","“Looks like I haven’t made myself clear.” The Saintess stood up. “If that’s the case, you can be the Saintess instead.”","Those words alarmed the other race leaders. They quickly stood up to placate the Saintess. Some said that the Third Prince had gone too far, whereas others said that the Third Prince was speaking from a good place and it wasn’t a bad thing to have Zu An prove himself.","That further frustrated the Saintess. She was about to speak when Zu An said, “Sure, I can go to the Monster Lord and convince him to go against the Lord of Slaughter.”","The Third Prince and the Golden Peng Crown Prince exchanged looks and saw the smirks on each other’s faces.","The Golden Peng Crown Prince was impressed by the Third Prince’s methods.","The Third Prince played him like a fiddle. The Monster Lord is not to be trifled with. No matter how strong that fellow is, it’s unlikely that he’ll survive the journey.","And if he succeeds, it will benefit the Fiend races. Either way, there's nothing to lose.","I am enlightened. No matter how strong a person is, if he doesn’t have a good head, he is nothing more than a tool. I mustn’t be that reckless in the future. I should learn more from the Third Prince.","While the two of them were feeling gleeful, Zu An continued, “But I’m feeling very irked right now. I need to clear my head first before doing this.”","Someone instinctively asked, “How do you intend to clear your head...”","There was a sudden blur before that sentence could be finished. Zu An seemed to have moved, yet he was where he was when everyone turned to look at him.","Zu An wiped off the blood on his fingers as he replied, “My mind is clear now.”","“You...” The Third Prince pointed at him in horror. Blood seeped from his mouth, preventing him from speaking more. Just like that, he collapsed to the ground.","Someone nearby quickly checked on him, only to see that he had fainted. His body was limp, and there wasn't the slightest trace of ki to be felt from him. All his meridians had been severed.","An uproar broke out in the conference hall. This fellow crippled the Third Prince just like that?","The Saintess was taken aback too, but she quickly pulled herself together and calmly declared, “The Third Prince has been attempting to drive a wedge here, weakening the forces we have against the monsters. We need to have a stable foundation before we can fight the monsters. This is also my will.”","Seeing her take responsibility for this matter evoked a laugh from Zu An. Xie Daoyun had clearly warned him earlier, but he'd still gone ahead to eliminate the Third Prince. He knew that this could result in dire consequences, but the Third Prince had been looking at him with resentful eyes, and it looked as if he'd harbored thoughts about the Saintess too. Rather than leaving a ticking time bomb, Zu An preferred to make a decisive move and contain the threat.","“What do you mean by this, Saintess?” Horrified, those who were close with the Third Prince shot to their feet and surrounded her.","The Saintess calmly explained, “At this juncture, infighting mustn’t break out in the Fiend races. I’d rather deal with him on the spot than to let him fracture us.”","“You crippled the Third Prince just because he questioned you? Are you trying to become a dictator?” The Golden Peng Crown Prince was infuriated too. The person he was just admiring a second ago had fallen just like that.","The Saintess had a headache too, but she didn’t blame Zu An for it. The Third Prince had indeed been a threat. Eliminating him was a solution too, not to mention the two of them didn’t have too much time to squander here.","Zu An stepped forward and said, “Crown Prince, since you're on such close terms with the Third Prince, would you like to follow in his footsteps?”","The Golden Peng Crown Prince hurriedly retreated in fear while waving his hands. “No no no, it’s a misunderstanding...”","Upon seeing the Golden Peng Crown Prince’s behavior, the agitated crowd slowly calmed down.","The Third Prince was an expert too, yet he had been crippled before anyone could register what was going on. This showed just how powerful Zu An was. Only a fool would criticize Zu An now.","After a long silence, an older person stood up and said, “The Third Prince indeed erred, but the punishment seems overboard...”","The crowd exchanged looks. They noticed his words were now much more subdued.","Zu An calmly replied, “He offended me time and time again. It’s only on the Saintess and the Peacock Princess’ account that I spared his life.”","The crowd belatedly remembered that this was a world where the strong got their way. It was only normal for an expert who could destroy the Incestuous King and his monster army to be offended when challenged by the likes of the Third Prince. If he had been this arrogant in front of the Incestuous King, the Third Prince would have died a worse death, let alone someone who defeated the Incestuous King. He only had himself to blame for foolishly denying the rumors and underestimating the man he was dealing with.","It was a pragmatic world. No one would oppose a powerful expert for a crippled prince, especially not when the prince had it coming. On top of that, the Third Prince’s enemies and the Saintess’ supporters stepped forward to criticize the Third Prince and affirm the Saintess’ decision. With that, the remaining people didn’t dare to say anything.","Zu An had gone through enough to know how the crowd would react. “Don’t worry. Now that I've cleared my mind, I'll help you deal with the Monster Lord on the Saintess’ account.”","The crowd was delighted to hear that. “We’ll be counting on you. Thank you, Saintess.”","Sacrificing a Third Prince to resolve an imminent threat sounded like an excellent deal.","The Saintess began to deal with the aftermath. The Third Prince had been crippled, but his supporters remained. These supporters needed to be controlled right away, lest they rally together to cause trouble.","Zu An nodded in approval. Xie Daoyun was previously a sheltered young miss, but her methods were now on par with the Empress and Bi Linglong. We might have only parted for a short time, but it looks like you've spent a long time here and grown a lot.","He was waiting for the Saintess to be done so that he could ask her about the Fiend races’ power insignia, when the Peacock Princess went up to him and asked with reddened eyes, “Big brother, were you lying to me?”"]},{"number":2538,"title":"Chapter 2538: Chapter 2490: Whereabouts of the Power Insignia","paragraphs":["Zu An shook his head. “I didn’t lie to you.”","“If you didn’t lie to me, why would the Saintess say that you’re her lover? Aren’t you from the future?” The Peacock Princess’ tears began falling. He’s still lying to me even at a time like this.","A few people noticed their interactions and frowned.","Look at how sorrowful the Peacock Princess is. She must have truly liked him.","That vile man! To think that the Saintess isn’t enough for him; he still wants the Peacock Princess on top of that!","Even so, after what had just happened, the crowd was intimidated by Zu An. No one dared to stand up for the Peacock Princess.","Zu An was distressed. It was hard to explain the details to the Peacock Princess. His silence only made her cry even more sorrowfully.","Just then, a gentle voice spoke up. “Qingwu, he didn’t lie to you. I am also from the future.”","The Saintess was already beside the two of them, and she'd constructed a noise isolation barrier around them before speaking.","“What?” The Peacock Princess was so startled that she stopped crying. She stared at the beautiful Saintess with shocked eyes. However, she soon shook her head and said, “That’s impossible. You’re Yumen Beiqing, the Yumen’s big miss! How could you be from the future?”","“I don’t know the details myself, and I have no way of explaining it.” The Saintess grabbed the Peacock Princess’ hand. “But please trust us. We have no reason to deceive you or everyone else.”","She regretted her reckless decision to flaunt her lover, as she hadn’t expected such a huge mess. She was so happy to be reunited with Zu An that she hadn’t thought things through.","The Peacock Princess thought about everything that had happened in recent years.","The Saintess did seem to have appeared out of nowhere and achieved miraculous feats one after another. That’s very similar to big brother’s appearance. No wonder she’s so outstanding. She’s from the same place as big brother.","She looked at Zu An with a wretched smile. “Big brother, is the Saintess the little sister you want to save?”","“Little sister?” The Saintess pricked up her ears.","Zu An shook his head. “It’s someone else.” He turned to the Saintess and explained, “Xiaoxi has the innate Cruel Poison Constitution. The poison just flared up, and I’m looking for a solution for her.”","“Ah? Is Xiaoxi fine?” The Saintess was taken aback. Anyone who had spent time with Ji Xiaoxi would naturally become fond of that adorable girl.","“She’s fine for the time being, and I have some clues as to how I can solve her problem. You don’t need to be too worried.” Upon seeing how worried she was, Zu An consoled her.","After hearing their conversation, the Peacock Princess had no choice but to concede that the two of them were from the future. She turned to the Saintess and asked, “If you’re from the future, why did you treat me differently all these years?”","She'd initially thought that the Saintess treated her exceptionally well because they got along well. Due to that, they'd become close friends who shared everything with each other. It was only now that she realized things weren’t that simple. Why would someone from the future care so much about her?","The Saintess hesitated before replying, “In the future, I came to know a know a big sister who greatly resembles you, which is why I felt a sense of intimacy with you...”","The Peacock Princess recalled what Zu An told her when they first met, and realization dawned on her. “All this while, I was just someone else’s substitute. No wonder you all treat me so well. It was all my one-sided feelings...” She fled the scene in a fluster, looking forlorn.","The Saintess wanted to chase after her, but Zu An grabbed her and advised, “Give her time to cool down.”","The Saintess bit her lips and chose to give the Peacock Princess some space. She knew there wasn’t much she could say even if she caught up with the latter. She could only pray that time would heal everything. However, after everything that had just happened, she didn’t want to be in the open with Zu An anymore, so she brought Zu An back to her room.","“Big brother Zu, I haven’t had time to ask you why you are here. Is it to save Xiaoxi?”","“That’s one of the reasons...” Zu An told her everything that had happened since he entered this spacetime fragment. “I’m overjoyed to be able to meet you here.”","“There’s a saying that destiny will eventually bring two fated people together, no matter how far they are,” the Saintess replied with a furious blush. Her lover traveling through time and finding her felt like fate to her.","Zu An grabbed her hand, and the two of them smiled. Suddenly, he remembered his reason for coming here and asked, “Speaking of which, do you know what the Fiend races’ power insignia is?”","“The Fiend races’ power insignia? Why do you ask that?” The Saintess was confused, as she struggled to understand what a ‘power insignia’ was.","Zu An summarized the chain of events that had transpired in the underworld and his hunt for the Six Paths’ power insignias.","“I see.” The Saintess nodded in realization. “It should be the Fiend Emperor’s scepter. That's the Fiend races’ symbol of power.”","“Scepter...” Zu An fell into deep thought.","The Saintess added, “The Fiend races had a legendary relic known as the Sun Slaying Bow, but it disappeared a long time ago. No one knows where it went, so they forged a scepter and used it as a power insignia instead.” At this point, she suddenly smiled. “If the Fiend races learn that you have the Sun Slaying Bow, they might just serve you as the chosen one.”","Zu An laughed. “I have no interest in staying with this era’s Fiend races.”","The Saintess’ eyebrows shot up. “Of course, I’m not surprised you miss the future Fiend races more. You have the Medusa Queen, the Empress, the Elf Princess, and so on. Actually, this world also has empresses, medusas, and elves too. Shall I help you find them?”","“Have mercy on me. I already have enough on my hands,” Zu An replied with a bitter smile.","“What can we do when big brother Zu is so charming? You stole the Peacock Princess’ heart away so quickly,” the Saintess said with a sigh.","Zu An was speechless. It was such an awkward topic that he quickly changed the subject. “Speaking of which, do you know where the Celestial World is?”","“The Celestial World?” The Saintess frowned. “Why do you think I’d know that, big brother Zu?”","“The current Fiend races are the descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races,” Zu An said, then told her what he knew.","The Saintess had previously heard the True Demon race claim that their ancestors were the Celestial Court’s Fiend races. “So it turns out those True Demons are just the Celestial Court’s Fiend races’ servants and pets. We were nearly duped by them, though I reserved my doubts toward their claims after what I saw in recent years.”","“Ah, I get it now!” The Saintess’ eyes lit up. “I was wondering why we suddenly fared so well with the monsters, and why the Lord of Slaughter suddenly disappeared from the battlefield. The Lord of Slaughter must have been studying the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb! If there is a way to reach the Celestial World, it has to be the Imperial Tomb! The Lord of Slaughter must be searching for the Celestial Court!”","Zu An nodded. That was what he thought too. As the Fiend races’ Saintess who boasted a deeper understanding of this era’s Fiend races and monsters, if Xie Daoyun had reached the same conclusion too, it would give greater credence to his conjecture.","“Looks like I’ll have to make a trip to the Imperial Tomb...” Zu An said. “Do you know where the Fiend Emperor’s scepter is?”","The Saintess shook her head. “After his death, the scepter disappeared along with the Fiend Emperor. I don’t know where it is, but it has to be with the monsters.”"]},{"number":2539,"title":"Chapter 2539: Chapter 2491: Disappearance","paragraphs":["“What makes you so certain?” Zu An was intrigued.","“The Fiend Emperor always brought the scepter with him. The day he died, he self-detonated in the monsters’ camp to bring down as many monsters as he could. The scepter should have fallen into the monsters’ hands then,” the Saintess explained. “The Fiend races can sense the scepter. We would have known if it was with a fiend, but the scepter remains missing even after so much time has passed. So, it's most likely with the monsters. However, I don’t know whether it’s with the Monster Lord, the Lord of Slaughter, or the other monsters.”","Zu An nodded. It was fine as long as the scepter really was with the monsters. He was going to visit the Monster Lord anyway, so he could take a look around while he was there.","The Saintess suddenly asked, “Big brother Zu, you previously mentioned that you came to this spacetime fragment with a few other big sisters. Where are they?”","“I was about to ask you.” Zu An looked grim. “Have you not seen Big Manman?”","“Big sister Pei?” The Saintess was taken aback. “I haven’t. What makes you ask that?”","Zu An’s heart sank. “We split up to deal with different matters. Jiang Luofu and Yun Yuqing took Xiaoxi to search for the Brilliant Pinflower. Suolun Shi stayed behind to guard the future Mojard, Salamay, and the others. Big Manman’s mission was to contact the Fiend races’ surviving army. Back then, she mentioned that she intended to reach out to you, the Saintess.” He realized that Xie Daoyun would have recognized Pei Mianman if they met and would have told him about it by now.","The Saintess was stunned. She asked him about the time and location of where they'd parted. Doing a rough calculation, Pei Mianman should have long since arrived here. She wondered, “Did something happen to big sister Pei?”","Zu An shook his head. “Manman is quite strong now, and she’s carrying many protection artifacts. She should have no trouble protecting herself. She might have been tied down by other matters along the way.” Despite saying so, he was still worried.","“Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I’ll send my men to look into it.” The Saintess called her subordinates in and ordered, “Send some men to search the vicinity. I’m looking for a human woman with the family name of ‘Pei’. Miss Pei is extremely beautiful, and...” She almost blurted out that Pei Mianman was big, but that would have been distasteful, so she said, “She leaves a strong impression. Anyone who has seen her would remember her.”","“Yes, Saintess!” The subordinate rushed over to relay her order.","The Saintess turned to Zu An and gently consoled him, “Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I’m sure big sister Pei is fine.”","Zu An nodded, though he remained nervous. He wasn't in the mood to set off and visit the Monster Lord anymore.","Fortunately, the subordinate swiftly returned with updates. “Saintess, there are sightings of a woman who fits your description in a small town 150 kilometers southwest. She was looking into you.”","“Where is she?” Zu An hurriedly asked.","The subordinate shook his head. “I’m afraid I don’t know. She should have been heading in our direction, but no one saw her afterward.”","Zu An frowned. While 150 kilometers would be a long distance for mortals, Pei Mianman could cover it within a short time. What could be preventing her from coming here?","“Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I’ll send someone to investigate it. There’s no way a living human could disappear into thin air. It’s only a matter of time before we find her whereabouts,” the Saintess consoled him.","Zu An shook his head. “It’s fine. I’ll investigate it myself.” He asked about the town’s location before rushing in that direction.","The Saintess rushed out as well. “Big brother Zu, I’ll go with you.”","Zu An noticed the fiends following below them and said, “You’re currently an important person in the Fiend races. Your abrupt departure could have ripple effects.”","“The town isn’t too far away. It should be fine for me to take a small trip there. Still, I should give them a heads up. Big brother Zu, can you wait for me?” the Saintess asked apologetically.","Zu An nodded. As anxious as he was, he could afford to wait a bit. He had clashed with the Fiend races earlier in the day, so they could misunderstand if he suddenly left with the Saintess without giving them a heads up. If the unity among the Fiend races unraveled at this juncture, it would become exceedingly hard to deal with the monsters.","The Saintess quickly descended to explain the situation to the panicking crowd. Shortly after, she returned to Zu An’s side and said, “Let’s go, big brother Zu.”","“Thank you, little sister Ling’er,” Zu An said.","“Big brother Zu, you’re being distant. I'm worried about big sister Pei too, and she disappeared in my territory. It’s only right for me to do my part,” the Saintess said.","Looking at ethereal moonlight reflecting off the Saintess’ face, Zu An could understand why the Fiend races revered her. There is something divine about her.","Zu An grabbed her hand and rushed toward the town. With his traveling speed, it didn’t take long before they reached their destination.","The town was small but prosperous, possibly because it was en route to the Fiend races’ main camp. It was already nightfall, but there was still a number of people on the streets. They came from different races, and their occupations ranged from merchants to cultivators, adventurers, and treasure hunters.","Zu An frowned. This place feels chaotic. It won’t be easy to investigate.","They made their way to the town’s largest inn. Zu An headed straight for the manager and asked about Pei Mianman’s whereabouts.","The manager shook his head. “How could I remember every guest when we have so many people coming in each day?”","Zu An detected dishonesty in his words, and his face darkened. He was about to exert his methods when the Saintess took off her veil and gently said, “Manager, please give it some thought. Miss Pei is very important to us.”","When she took off her veil, the dimly-lit hall visibly brightened up. Her beautiful and pure face surprised the manager, prompting him to point a trembling finger at her. “Y-You are...”","The other patrons recognized her and exclaimed in delight, “It’s the Saintess! It’s the Saintess!”","A huge commotion followed. Everyone rushed over and surrounded Zu An and the Saintess, but at the same time, they kept a meter away from her, as if they were worried about sullying her. It wasn't Zu An’s first time witnessing this, but he was still awed by the Saintess’ high standing in the Fiend races.","The Saintess nodded. “I came here because a friend of mine went missing. Have any of you seen her?” She proceeded to describe Pei Mianman’s traits.","Zu An was worried about not being able to find clues, but to his surprise, many people raised their hands and exclaimed, “I’ve seen her! I’ve seen her!”"]},{"number":2540,"title":"Chapter 2540: Chapter 2492: Overlooked","paragraphs":["Zu An and the Saintess exchanged looks. The Saintess pointed to a person and asked, “May I know where you met her?”","“I met her outside town. She was about to enter the town when she encountered a foreign adventurer party,” the person said, feeling honored to be selected by the Saintess. “That adventurer party was mesmerized by her beauty and stepped forward to tease her, but that woman made quick work of them.” Fear flickered across his eyes as he recounted the chain of events.","Zu An asked about the details of the battle. The person replied with a pale face, “She unleashed a black flame. It was terrifying. The adventurers came into contact with it and couldn’t put it out. They were burned to ashes.”","Looks like it really is Manman. That’s her unique black flame. Those adventurers must have deserved death for her to go that far.","“What happened next?”","“I fled because I dared not watch any further. I don’t know where she went next,” that person replied sheepishly. “Given how powerful she is, she should be fine.”","“I know where she went next. She entered the town and bought a stick of candied hawthorn,” someone else added.","Zu An smiled. Despite Manman’s mature appearance, she has a childish side too.","“She went to the bridge and asked about the Saintess, but we didn’t tell her anything because we were wary about her unknown background.”","“That afternoon, she came to our inn and ordered a few dishes.”","“I saw her south of town...”","The sudden influx of clues felt suspicious, so Zu An asked, “Why do so many of you remember her?”","Usually, one would have been lucky to stumble upon one or two of such clues in their investigation, but a huge bunch of them suddenly sprouted out here. Something felt amiss.","Someone meekly replied, “That lady is so beautiful and... And...”","The Saintess’ face turned cold. “And what?”","Intimidated by the Saintess, the person quickly finished his sentence, “And big! No one could possibly forget about her!”","The Saintess and Zu An were speechless.","Considering Pei Mianman’s curvaceous figure, those words made perfect sense.","Through further questions, Zu An was able to map out Pei Mianman’s movements after entering the town. By the same afternoon, she had already figured out where the Saintess and the Fiend races’ resistance army were. She'd left town and was about to head there when she suddenly received a letter and reversed course, traveling in the opposite direction instead.","Zu An frowned. What could have been in the letter to make her change her route? More importantly, who sent that letter to Big Manman? She doesn’t have acquaintances in this timeline, so it doesn’t make sense for her to receive a letter.","The Saintess suddenly spoke up. “Big brother Zu, what do you think big sister Pei saw that made her leave right away? Could someone have told her you were in danger?”","Zu An shook his head. “No, that wouldn’t work.”","He and Pei Mianman knew each other very well, and they had codes to verify each other’s identity too. It was unlikely for anyone to be able to deceive her about him. Besides, she knew how powerful he was. The odds of him encountering danger so quickly were slim.","“I can only think of one possibility—she must have left because she found clues about the Brilliant Pinflower, Defying Spirit Tears, or the Aurora Poison Dragon,” Zu An said. Only when it came to the matter of rescuing Ji Xiaoxi would Pei Mianman stray from the plan.","“Ah!” the Saintess suddenly exclaimed. She noticed Zu An looking at her with perplexed eyes, so she explained, “I don’t know about the other two, but there are Brilliant Pinflowers growing near the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb.”","“The Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb?” Zu An was taken aback. “I was there in the future, but I saw no such flower.”","The Saintess gave the matter some thought before replying, “There are Brilliant Pinflowers in this world, but there are very few of them. Each generation’s Fiend Emperor cultivates them to offer them to heaven. If they're no longer there in the future, they must have gone extinct at some point. The existence of Brilliant Pinflowers is a secret, but there are fiends who know about it. Someone might have told big sister Pei about it while she was gathering information.”","Zu An nodded. That was the most plausible explanation. He said, “I’ll make a quick trip to the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb.”","He was worried about Pei Mianman. The Lord of Slaughter was at the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb; Pei Mianman could be in danger if she headed there recklessly. Besides, Ji Xiaoxi and the others were also looking into the Brilliant Pinflowers’ whereabouts. They could be on their way to the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb too. If so, they could reunite there.","The Saintess exclaimed, “I’ll go with you!”","Zu An advised her otherwise. “Little sister Ling’er, as the Fiend races’ Saintess, you have many responsibilities on your shoulders. The resistance army needs you. Chaos will break out if you arbitrarily leave your post.”","“But...” The Saintess knew he was right, but she couldn’t bear to part ways with him.","Just then, a female elf scout descended from the sky and said, “Saintess, there’s an urgent report from the frontlines. We have detected anomalous movements from the monster army. Everyone is worried that the monsters are preparing for an attack, so they sent me here to invite you back to discuss this matter.”","The Saintess was stunned. She looked at Zu An with a conflicted expression. “Big brother Zu...”","Zu An patted her shoulder. “Little sister Ling’er, you should return. I can settle things on my end. Besides, you'll be indirectly helping me by drawing the monster army’s attention.”","The Saintess nodded. “All right, I’ll return for now to make arrangements. I’ll find you as soon as I’m done. You must take care of yourself.”","Zu An was startled. “You mustn’t go to the Imperial Tomb alone. You’re probably at the top of the monster army’s bounty list now, and the Imperial Tomb is under the monsters’ control. You would be delivering yourself into the enemy’s clutches.”","The Saintess revealed a sweet smile. “Rest assured, big brother Zu. I'm not a reckless person. The monsters won’t be able to capture me that easily.”","Zu An belatedly remembered that the Saintess had already fought with the monsters for many years now. His worry was unfounded. Thus, he stopped the nagging and instead stepped forth to embrace her. “Little sister Ling’er, I’ll take you back to our original time period once we settle everything in this spacetime fragment.”","The Saintess nodded. “I believe that you’ll be able to do it, big brother Zu.”","The two of them hugged for a long time.","“Little sister Qingwu will likely ask about your whereabouts when I return. Should I tell her?” the Saintess suddenly asked as they separated from each other’s arms.","Zu An shook his head. There’s no point in prolonging the pain. I should use this opportunity to make the Peacock Princess forget about me.","The Saintess nodded, knowing any relationship between those two couldn't bear fruit.","With that, they finally bade each other farewell and left.","While leaving, the elf scout couldn’t help but glance at Zu An. She was curious about the man to whom the Saintess had given her heart.","Zu An wondered if this female elf scout was related to Xue’er. Considering how elves had a long lifespan, she could be Qiao Xueying’s elder from three to four generations ago. However, he quickly reined in his thoughts. His priority at hand was to find Pei Mianman.","A bone-chilling wind blew against him. He had a feeling he had overlooked something, but he couldn’t figure out what it was."]},{"number":2541,"title":"Chapter 2541: Chapter 2493: Pit Them Against Each Other","paragraphs":["Something seemed to have surfaced in Zu An’s mind, but it slipped past his clutches, and no matter how he racked his brains, he simply couldn’t remember what it was anymore. Still, he knew there was no point panicking at a time like this; he could only wait for the epiphany to arrive once more later on.","He headed off in the same direction as Pei Mianman when she left the town. Along the way, he tried gathering information about her, but it was to no avail. Pei Mianman’s appearance and distinctive physique were bound to leave a deep impression on anyone who saw her, similar to what had happened in the town. However, the monster invasion had left most areas desolate and barren. He didn’t meet a single person along the way, so there was no way to gather information.","Quite some time had passed since Pei Mianman left the town, and there was no guarantee that she would drop by the other towns along the road to the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb. With that in mind, Zu An thought it would be best to first head to the imperial tomb to take a look.The intelligence he had received suggested that Pei Mianman had likely changed course because she received information about the Brilliant Pinflower.","Earlier, he'd received intel from the Saintess that the monsters could be broadly divided into four groups.","The first group was stationed in the imperial tomb with the Lord of Slaughter; it was likely the Lord of Slaughter’s army. The second group was under the Incestuous King; most of its troops were veterans, but the bulk of them had been obliterated from the face of the world. The third group consisted of powerful and influential military commanders who waged war and conquered new lands. The last group was the Monster Lord’s army; it was the strongest of the four groups, and it was tasked with the mission of conquering the Cultivation World. It had the power to mobilize other armies, except for the Lord of Slaughter’s army stationed at the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb.","The Monster Lord’s army was stationed 100,000 kilometers away from the Fiend races’ resistance army, sandwiched between the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb and the resistance army. That would have been a long distance in Zu An’s previous world, but in this world full of cultivators, it was no big deal.","Zu An decided to first pay a visit to the Monster Lord.","Even though he had once defeated the Monster Lord, it was largely because the other party’s cultivation had been suppressed by the world’s barrier, and Zu An had communed with the world using the World Law Beacon. In this ki-rich world, the monsters’ cultivation wouldn’t be suppressed, and he didn’t have the World Law Beacon here. Facing off against the Monster Lord would be dangerous to him.","However, the strongest entity in this era was still the Lord of Slaughter, or else the Monster Lord would have long since revolted. Even in the future, despite the Lord of Slaughter having been suppressed for millennia, they were only able to vanquish him when Qiu Honglei carried out a Dance Offering to the Universe to summon an unfathomable being. She'd had to pay a heavy price for that.","The Monster Lord wouldn’t be a match for the Lord of Slaughter now that the latter was at his peak. Zu An had to find a way to turn them against each other.","The high concentration of ki in this world and his unique cultivation technique allowed Zu An to maintain his peak condition even when traveling without rest. Along the way, he occasionally entered the pendant’s cave paradise to visit Qiu Honglei and the Jing Teng sisters and tell them what was happening outside.","Qiu Honglei was amazed when he told her that he had gone back thousands of years in time, but once she learned that he could have to face off against the terrifying Lord of Slaughter again, she quickly became nervous.","Zu An embraced her tightly. “Don’t worry, Honglei. Things are different now. I won’t put myself in a desperate situation, and I won’t endanger anyone around me either.”","Qiu Honglei lay on his chest. “You've been through so much in recent days. With your capabilities, I’m sure you’ll be fine.”","While exchanging sweet nothings, Qiu Honglei slowly drifted off to sleep. Her complexion looked much better than before, though she remained weak from having just recovered. Even a short conversation could invoke her drowsiness. Zu An knew that it would be unwise to rush things; they would have to slowly condition her body with spirit medicine over time.","With Qiu Honglei and the Jing Teng sisters’ company, the journey wasn’t boring. Time passed in a flash, and Zu An soon arrived at the monster army’s camp. He calmly surveyed the barracks that stretched for thousands of kilometers.","There are indeed a lot of monsters. The Fiend races’ troop count was one of the reasons they were so difficult to deal with in the future, and the monsters outnumber even that. On top of that, I can sense the auras of countless experts even from a distance away. I’ll be dead meat if they discover me.","Now that he didn’t have the World Law Beacon, Zu An didn’t dare to let his guard down. He first constructed a formation at the barracks’ outer perimeter before making his way in. He continued to construct dozens more teleportation formations to ensure his safety along the way.","“Hold it right there. Who are you?” Two patrolling monster soldiers discovered him.","Zu An brought out Daji, who immediately took control of the two monster soldiers with her Charming Voice. He eliminated the two monster soldiers, put on a set of their attire, and continued advancing into the barracks. As he walked, he began transforming into a monster soldier.","Most military barracks were protected by defensive formations and sentry posts, making it difficult for a cultivator, no matter how powerful, to sneak in. However, Zu An, with his Myriad Transformations, could turn into a monster while concealing his aura. He kept changing his appearance along the way, making it nigh impossible for anyone to see through him.","In a majestic tent deep in the barracks, the Monster Lord sat on a tall throne made out of white bones. A bizarre three-headed bird lay at his feet as a plump servant made a report to him.","“Master, the Ocean races have wiped out the Incestuous King and his army. No one can hold you back anymore. We should march eastward to destroy the Fiend races and make that Saintess or something your maid!”","If Zu An were here, he would recognize the servant as the underground city’s Manager Pi.","“Mojard has truly disappointed me! How could he and his elites be destroyed by a nobody? Others might think I’m of the same caliber as him!” the Monster Lord spat through gritted teeth.","“Master, how could Mojard be worthy of being your rival? He was only able to tie you down because of the one above,” another servant said.","If Zu An were there, he would recognize this servant to be the War Priest. He was highly respected among the monsters, and he participated in most large-scale wars. That was why his downfall in the Cultivation World in the future was a huge shock to the Monster Lord, prompting the latter to send blood pool clones to invade the Cultivation World.","The Monster Lord stopped the War Priest with a raised hand. “It’s not over yet. We should practice utmost prudence. Hmph! Now that Mojard is finally gone, I can go all out. Conquering the Fiend races and capturing their Saintess should grant me enough prestige to do it.”","Just then, a voice echoed outside. “I disagree. Now is the best time to do it.”","“Who is it?!” The monsters in the tent were horrified. It could bring them endless trouble if outsiders were to learn about what they had said.","The Monster Lord thrust his palm forth, unleashing a formidable force that decimated a section of the tent."]},{"number":2542,"title":"Chapter 2542: Chapter 2494: Betrayal","paragraphs":["“There’s no need to be so angry, Monster Lord. I come in peace.” A figure slowly emerged from the hole in the tent.","Manager Pi and the War Priest narrowed their eyes. Even they would have struggled to deal with the Monster Lord’s earlier attack, but this fellow overcame it with such ease. This told them how powerful he was.","Hm, he’s wearing our uniform. Whose subordinate is this? Why don’t we know about him if he possesses such strength?","They scanned the intruder from head to toe. The latter was astonishingly emaciated for a monster, and he wore a mask that covered his appearance. It was also impossible to figure out his background from his aura and cultivation technique.","Needless to say, the intruder was Zu An. He was shocked when he saw the people inside the tent. He hadn’t expected them to be familiar faces. Manager Pi was one thing, but he hadn’t known that the War Priest served the Monster Lord as well.","“I find it hard to believe that someone who refuses to reveal his identity bears no ill will.” The Monster Lord was alarmed, gazing sharply at Zu An. He hadn’t put his full strength into the earlier attack, such that a fair number of top-notch experts could have dealt with it, but he couldn’t think of anyone who could neutralize it so quietly.","“Skin is superficial. I didn’t mean to deceive you, and I seek your understanding. I came here today to discuss your future.” Zu An had put on a mask because the Monster Lord didn’t recognize him in the future, so he figured he had to not reveal his true face now.","“Our master doesn’t need the likes of you to discuss his future. Men, capture this scoundrel!” Manager Pi roared.","Monster guards rushed up and surrounded Zu An.","“Step down!” the Monster Lord suddenly roared. That surprised the guards, but they quickly bowed and backed off.","Manager Pi didn’t look awkward despite having his order superseded. Instead, he exclaimed with a fawning smile, “Our master is wise and farsighted.” He then glared at Zu An. “Our master has given you a chance to talk! You better cherish it!”","The War Priest rolled his eyes. This bootlicker.","The Monster Lord, however, was satisfied with Manager Pi’s bootlicking. He turned to Zu An and said, “Tell me what your earlier words meant.”","Zu An first cast a glance at the crowd before saying, “What I’m about to say might be improper. Would it be fine to speak openly in front of them too?”","The Monster Lord could roughly guess what Zu An was going to say. “It’s fine. Go on.” He wasn't a patient man, but he thought that the intruder was strong enough to be worth listening to his words.","Zu An calmly spoke, “The Incestuous King’s army has been destroyed, and the Lord of Slaughter has lost his most loyal subordinates. This is a good opportunity for you to take his position.”","The War Priest, Manager Pi, and the others turned to look at the Monster Lord. They were ready to kill the intruder on the spot as soon as the Monster Lord gave the signal.","The Monster Lord coldly sneered, “What a crude way of sowing dissent. Did you think it would work?”","Zu An smiled. The Monster Lord’s decision to not kill him right away spoke volumes. “You misunderstand. It doesn’t matter whether my motive is to sow dissent or not. What's more important here is what is aligned with your interests.”","“I can guess your background,” the Monster Lord sneered. “We were just discussing the decimation of the Fiend races’ resistance army and capturing the Saintess when you suddenly appeared and made such a suggestion. You must be the Fiend races’ ally, though it baffles me why I have never met you before.”","Zu An didn’t deny it. “Yes, I have ties with the Fiend races’ Saintess. As a token of my sincerity, I can tell you that I was the one who defeated Incestuous King Mojard and his army.”","The War Priest, Manager Pi, and the Monster Lord straightened up in shock. “It’s you!”","“Indeed. That’s why we have a common enemy,” Zu An explained. “The Incestuous King is the Lord of Slaughter’s aide. If he learns about this matter, the Lord of Slaughter will not spare me. That’s why I wish to forge a partnership with you.”","The Monster Lord sneered, “You’re mistaken. I am loyal to my master. Men...”","Zu An sighed. “The Lord of Slaughter has secluded himself in the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb to decipher its secrets, so he doesn’t know that you have usurped his power. If he hears about the Incestuous King’s death, he will investigate the matter and learn that you have removed his men from important positions and replaced them with your aides. How would he respond to that?”","The Monster Lord was startled. “My master is wise. He can distinguish between a normal reshuffling of manpower and an attempt to usurp power. I have never done anything disloyal. I shall take you down right now to avenge the Incestuous King!”","Terrifying pressure suddenly crashed down on the tent. The War Priest and Manager Pi, having received the Monster Lord’s signal, blocked Zu An’s path of retreat.","The Monster Lord rushed up to Zu An at an incredible speed and thrust his palm down on the latter's head, causing Zu An’s figure to shatter as if it was an illusion.","“A teleportation formation?” the War Priest exclaimed in shock.","The Monster Lord’s complexion darkened. “It’s no ordinary teleportation formation. It bears some resemblance to our world’s technology.”","“Is he from the Monster World too?” the War Priest asked, but he couldn’t think of anyone who had those unique traits.","Manager Pi stepped forward and volunteered himself. “Master, I’ll lead our men to capture him!”","The Monster Lord shook his head. “Don’t bother. Given his cultivation and aptitude in teleportation formations, you won’t be able to capture him.”","“Are we going to let him off just like that?” Manager Pi was indignant.","The Monster Lord fell silent.","The War Priest suddenly remarked, “To be honest, his proposal is an appealing one. Should we accept it first?”","The Monster Lord sneered, “You don’t even know his background. The Lord of Slaughter could have sent him here to test us. We can’t give ourselves away that easily. But he delivers a timely reminder. It looks like we’ll have to bring our plans forward.”"]},{"number":2543,"title":"Chapter 2543: Chapter 2495: Girl","paragraphs":["Manager Pi was taken aback. “Master, you don’t intend to attack the Fiend races’ resistance army anymore?”","The Monster Lord shook his head. “His words make sense. The Fiend races barely have a breath left in them. We can clean them up afterward. That person poses a greater threat to us.”","Manager Pi had a fair complexion, but the Monster Lord’s words left him even paler. He found the Lord of Slaughter much more terrifying than the Fiend races’ remnant army.","The War Priest looked worried. “Master, how confident are you in defeating that person?”","There was a prolonged silence before the Monster Lord replied, “If it’s a 1-on-1, my odds should be 40:60.” His true evaluation of his odds was closer to 30:70, but he inflated the number to inspire confidence in his aides.","The War Priest and Manager Pi were tactful enough not to ask who was 40 and who was 60. “Should we ally with that man and borrow his strength? That may further skew the odds in our favor.”","That mysterious man had left a deep impression on them. He'd easily neutralized the Monster Lord’s attack and safely escaped from their encirclement. His strength and wits were top-notch.","The Monster Lord shook his head. “We don’t know his motive. He could turn against us at a critical moment. We can’t use him.”","“What should we do? Once that person learns about Mojard’s defeat and begins investigating, he will quickly learn that we have replaced all his old subordinates.” The War Priest was fearful. If this matter came to light, the cruel Lord of Slaughter would bring terrible fates upon them.","The Monster Lord chuckled enigmatically. “Don’t worry. Sometimes, strength is not everything.”","...","Light suddenly distorted in a remote area of the barracks, and Zu An appeared out of thin air. Unlike what the Monster Lord thought, he didn’t escape right away. Having previously interacted with the Monster Lord, he knew how cunning the latter could be. He knew that the other party wouldn’t trust him easily. Still, it was paramount to take that trip to bury a seed in the other party’s heart. When the time came, that seed would sprout.","He made his way to another tent. Judging from its prime location, flags, and elegant decor, the tent hinted at its master’s extraordinary position. Zu An hesitated at the tent’s entrance, but he still entered it in the end.","The tent was guarded, though the security wasn't as tight as in the Monster Lord’s tent. There were still lapses in the defenses that Zu An could exploit. With his Myriad Transformations, he easily slipped into the tent and entered a courtyard.","A long sigh came from within. A girl sat on a swing, basking in the orange glow of the setting sun. She looked adorable despite the bits of scales on her body, though it was bizarre to hear a young child letting out an aged-sounding sigh.","The sight of that young but familiar face left Zu An in a daze. The girl was Salamay as a child. He had known beforehand that she was already born in this era, though she was still young. The first thing he'd done upon arriving at this barracks was to locate little Salamay before paying a visit to the Monster Lord.","Zu An wondered what would happen if the future Salamay saw her, though that was impossible. The future Salamay had been restrained and was currently under Princess Suolun’s watch.","“Who are you?” The girl noticed his presence and eyed him with curiosity.","“Aren’t you afraid?” Zu An asked in surprise. He'd been prepared to subdue her in case she panicked and called for her guards, but the latter merely looked at him with blinking eyes.","“Why should I be afraid?” The girl couldn’t understand the question. “Are you here to play with me? I’m bored.”","Zu An belatedly recalled that she was the Lord of Slaughter’s daughter, an exalted entity in the monster army. Given that the Monster Lord had yet to rebel, he had to treat her with the greatest respect. Salamay had never needed to fear anyone. On the contrary, it was others who had to fear her.","“Are you very bored, first miss?” Zu An noticed her frown and asked.","“Yup. My daddy went to some imperial tomb a few years back and I haven’t seen him since. Uncle Mojard has been missing since two years ago, and Uncle Monster Lord is too polite and busy to play with me.” The girl pouted. “Other people are too afraid of me. You are one of the few people who aren’t scared of me.”","Zu An sighed.","Salamay had a tough life. She never enjoyed happiness despite being the monsters’ first miss. Later, the Monster Lord usurped her father’s position, forcing her to go into hiding with his father’s old subordinates while plotting vengeance. No wonder her heart became so warped.","As much as Zu An pitied her, he wasn’t going to let it hinder him from doing what he had to do. “I’m not here to play with you, first miss. I’m a friend of the Incestuous King, and I came here to deliver news to you.”","“Uncle Mo?” The girl’s eyes lit up. She leaped off the swing and ran over. “Did you bring me a present from Uncle Mo?”","Zu An sighed before speaking with a heavy tone, “The Incestuous King and his army were ambushed in the East Sea Dragon Palace and were defeated.”","“What? That’s impossible! Aren't the Ocean races planning to surrender to us? How could they have the strength to defeat Uncle Mo and his army?” The girl was young, but she was no fool.","Zu An was surprised. It won’t be that easy to fool her. Thus, he explained, “It could have been a feint, and the Ocean races weren't planning to surrender in the first place. On top of that, I heard a mysterious expert has joined forces with the Ocean races.”","Little Salamay panicked. “Where is Uncle Mo now?”","“We don’t know whether he is alive or not, but the odds aren’t in his favor. That’s why I risked my life to come here to inform you of the matter, first miss,” Zu An said with sorrowful eyes.","“Risk your life?” Little Salamay stared at him in confusion, not understanding why it was dangerous for him to report this matter to her.","Zu An sighed. “The Monster Lord should have already heard about the Incestuous King’s defeat, but has he shared the news with first miss?”","Little Salamay’s eyes widened. Indeed, no one had informed her about this matter. Her earlier innocence vanished without a trace, replaced with grimness. “What you have just mentioned is too huge. I’ll have to verify it.”","“First miss, you mustn’t confront the Monster Lord!” Zu An exclaimed. “I came under the Incestuous King’s request. He told me to warn you about the Monster Lord if anything happened to him.”"]},{"number":2544,"title":"Chapter 2544: Chapter 2496: The Imperial Tomb’s Secret","paragraphs":["Little Salamay narrowed her eyes. “Are you telling me that the Monster Lord had a hand in Uncle Mo’s mishap?”","Zu An shook his head. “I don’t know. I am just relaying words from the Incestuous King.”","Telling a person something outright was more likely to pique their suspicion. Instead, it was more effective to lead their train of thought toward the truth. They would be more inclined to believe it if they arrived at the conclusion themselves.","Unsurprisingly to Zu An, Little Salamay soon frowned as a thought surfaced in her mind.","“There’s another matter I need to ask first miss. Did our people recently capture an extremely beautiful woman with a very... unique figure?” Zu An decided not to reveal Pei Mianman’s name in case Salamay remembered her name. That could have ripple effects on the future.","Little Salamay shook her head. “I haven’t heard of anyone like that. What’s your relationship with that woman?”","“We met by coincidence,” Zu An answered. There was no reason to stay here if Pei Mianman wasn’t here. “I have fulfilled the mission entrusted to me, so I shan’t disturb your rest anymore, first miss.”","“Hey...” Little Salamay tried to stop him, but Zu An’s figure blurred before vanishing into thin air.","“Hm?” Despite her young age, Little Salamay could tell that Zu An had incredible abilities. “Does Uncle Mo have such a formidable friend?”","After some thought, she decided to verify the matter. As she made her way out of her tent, her guards and servants asked her where she was heading.","“I’m going to look for Uncle Hulu,” Little Salamay said innocently.","“Lord Hulu isn’t in the barracks. He was recently dispatched to the frontlines to deal with the Beast races,” a guard replied.","“Then I’ll look for Aunt Jyan,” Little Salamay replied.","“Lord Jyan has gone to the South Sea’s shores to curb the rebellion there,” someone replied.","“Ah!” Doubt was starting to fester in Little Salamay’s mind, but she didn’t let it show. “I’ll go play with Uncle Ajue then!”","“Lord Ajue has been imprisoned for committing some wrongdoings.” The guards began to look nervous, wondering if they had inadvertently revealed the secret.","“What a bummer! I’ll play by myself then.” Little Salamay harrumphed before hopping back into her courtyard like an easily distracted child.","The guards wiped off their sweat. Thank goodness she didn’t probe any further, or else the Monster Lord might punish us for this. I guess she’s just a child, after all.","Little Salamay returned to her courtyard and frolicked with a ball. Some time later, she stretched her back as if she was tired, before returning to her room. She murmured under her breath, “I’m tired. Time to sleep.”","Several maids followed her to prepare her for bedtime. Shortly after Little Salamay lay on her bed, her breathing became long and deep.","The maids looked envious. Children fall asleep so easily. They tucked her into her blanket, lit a fragrant incense stick, and quietly retreated from the room.","As soon as the door closed, little Salamay’s eyes shot open. She carefully got up from her bed and took out an artifact. The artifact lit up and formed a small sound-isolation barrier around her. She made sure to confirm that the formation was working. Next, she reached into her storage bag and took out a mirror. She stuffed several ki stones into the mirror, and its surface rippled like water.","Soon, a figure appeared in the mirror. His bloodthirsty aura could be felt even through it. He was none other than the Lord of Slaughter! He initially looked worried, but when he saw little Salamay, he heaved a sigh of relief. “My good daughter, I thought something happened to you.”","“Daddy, when are you coming back?” Little Salamay asked with a pout, sounding a little tearful.","That sent the Lord of Slaughter into a panic. He felt an urge to wipe off her tears even across the screen. “Don’t cry, my good daughter. Who bullied you? I’ll rip him into shreds!”","“No one bullied me.” Little Salamay shook her head. “I miss you.”","“My good daughter, daddy is too busy to leave right now. Once I’m done with things here, I’ll return right away to spend time with you,” the Lord of Slaughter said gently. He took some time to coax his daughter before asking, “I told you not to contact me unless something urgent cropped up. Did something happen?”","His daughter was young but sensible. It was unlikely for her to contact him for no reason.","“I don’t know if it’s urgent or not.” Little Salamay took a moment to gather her thoughts before saying, “I think Uncle Mo’s army was recently decimated, and we don’t know if he is dead or alive.”","“What?!” The Lord of Slaughter was enraged to hear that. “How can Mojard be that unreliable? How did he lose his army when we have already eradicated the Fiend races’ main army? I knew the Monster Lord was more reliable!”","Little Salamay looked hesitant to speak further.","“What’s wrong, my good daughter?” The Lord of Slaughter noticed his daughter’s unusual behavior.","Little Salamay hesitantly spoke up. “The Monster Lord didn’t tell me about this.”","“Then where did you hear the news from?” The Lord of Slaughter frowned, as it suddenly occurred to him that no one had reported this matter to him.","“It was a mysterious man. He says he was sent by Uncle Mo...” Little Salamay proceeded to tell the Lord of Slaughter about her encounter with Zu An.","The Lord of Slaughter was bewildered. “Does Mojard have such a friend?”","“That’s not all. I was thinking of verifying the news with some of the uncles and aunts, but I learned that they were either demoted or imprisoned. There is no one here I can talk to,” Little Salamay said.","The Lord of Slaughter’s face warped in anger. He had ruled long enough to immediately understand the implications of what he had just heard. He told Little Salamay, “Don’t tell anyone about this, especially not the Monster Lord. Keep everything to yourself and wait for my return!”","Little Salamay was overjoyed to hear that. “That’s wonderful! I can meet daddy again.”","The Lord of Slaughter tried to smile, but he couldn’t lift the corners of his lips, as if there were weights attached to them. How dare the Monster Lord betray my trust and pull tricks behind my back?","...","The Monster Lord was busy scheming with his aides when his eyes suddenly widened. He shot a glance at his aides before taking out a recording mirror. The Lord of Slaughter soon appeared in the mirror.","“Paying respects to master!” The Monster Lord quickly bowed.","“You may dispense with the ceremony. Get up,” the Lord of Slaughter said amicably.","“Thank you, master. Do you have any command for us?” the Monster Lord asked respectfully.","The Lord of Slaughter looked to be buzzing with excitement. “After years of research, I have finally deciphered the secret of the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb. The gates are about to open. Come here right now to witness history with me. I have found the legendary Celestial Court!”"]},{"number":2545,"title":"Chapter 2545: Chapter 2497: Caught","paragraphs":["“Celestial Court?” The Monster Lord’s face beamed with joy. “Congratulations, master! You have finally found the legendary Celestial Court!”","The Lord of Slaughter laughed heartily. “You don’t need to hold back with me. I wish to share this joy with you. I have heard about the prowess of the elusive Celestial Court, so I will need your help too.”","“Thank you, master. I’ll make some arrangements before rushing over,” the Monster Lord said with a beaming face.","“Yes, you should. The Fiend races and the Ocean races still have one last breath in them, so we mustn’t give them the chance to make a comeback. Quickly make arrangements and come within the next few days,” the Lord of Slaughter instructed.","“Yes, master!” The Monster Lord bowed respectfully.","As soon as the recording mirror was switched off, Manager Pi stepped forward with a fawning smile and exclaimed, “Congratulations, master.”","“Why are you congratulating me?” The Monster Lord’s smile disappeared.","Manager Pi was shocked by the Monster Lord’s sudden change in attitude. “It’s naturally because the Lord of Slaughter trusts you so much that he’s willing to share the secret he has deciphered with you.”","The Monster Lord sneered, “You’re wrong. He is planning to kill me.”","Both Manager Pi and the War Priest were stunned.","The Monster Lord explained, “That old thing spent years in the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb, but to no avail. What a huge coincidence it is for him to find the Celestial Court the moment something has happened to Mojard!”","“Master, is that person sounding you out?” The War Priest was taken aback.","“Isn’t it obvious?” the Monster Lord replied grimly. “He wouldn’t have neglected to mention Mojard otherwise. His ties with Mojard might have become strained in recent years, but he wouldn’t leave that fellow out for something this important. He must have learned about Mojard’s defeat and the power shifts in the army. He’s fearful of me, which is why he is summoning me. It’d be easier for him to take me down once I’m isolated from my troops and aides.”","The War Priest was shocked. “That old thing is a sly one! The slightest carelessness would have resulted in us falling for his trap!”","Manager Pi took this chance to fawn over the Monster Lord. “No matter how sly that old thing is, our master still saw through him right away. Try as he may, but he will never be able to pull one over us!”","The group burst into laughter.","The Monster Lord’s eyes gleamed. “I shall prepare a huge surprise for him then.”","...","Zu An spent some time wandering around the barracks and subduing almost a hundred monsters of different ranks, but none of them had news about Pei Mianman. Pei Mianman’s traits were so conspicuous that the monsters would have remembered her if they had seen her.","Did she avoid the monster barracks to head straight for the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb? Or could there be another possibility?","Unfortunately, Zu An was lacking in intel, so his best bet was to pay a visit to the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb.","He traveled day and night without rest and eventually arrived in the Imperial Tomb’s vicinity. It felt nostalgic to return to the same place. The last time he was here, he'd been accompanied by Yan Xuehen, Yun Jianyue, and Yu Yanluo, but this time, he was here alone to look for Pei Mianman.","The Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb looked vastly different from how it was in the future. The buildings outside were much more majestic and densely packed. Many of the buildings had likely eroded and disappeared over time.","Zu An quietly stared at the many monsters stationed around the Imperial Tomb.","What would Big Manman do upon arriving here?","She’s not a reckless person. Knowing that the Lord of Slaughter is here, she wouldn’t risk her life to obtain the Brilliant Pinflower. She would instead find a way to inform me, so we could come here together to obtain it.","Could she be on her way to the Ocean races, but we missed each other? If she meets the Mermaid Queen, she should be able to find out what happened.","That quelled some of Zu An’s worries. To be safe, he still decided to infiltrate the monster army. He spent some time walking around before entering a monster commander’s room. He suppressed the latter and asked, “Did you capture a woman...”","He briefly shared Pei Mianman’s traits, though there was no need for too many details, as those who met her would remember her easily.","“N-No, I haven’t met her.” Fearing that Zu An wouldn’t believe him, the monster commander anxiously added, “Who would infiltrate this place when our master is here...” His words suddenly trailed off as he realized the man before him was one such intruder.","Zu An thought those words made sense.","The monster commander continued, “I advise you to free me. Our master is invincible. You won’t be able to survive his wrath even if you have nine lives. If you leave on your own accord, I’ll pretend this never happened.”","In truth, the monster commander was scared out of his wits. He'd been caught off guard, but the intruder was strong enough to subdue him before he could react. That meant the intruder was at least on par with the War Priest.","As soon as I scare this fellow off, I’ll alert my comrades and have him captured. Who knows? I might even be rewarded for this!","Zu An could tell what the monster commander was planning from his gaze, but he didn’t expose the latter. Instead, he asked, “Where’s the Lord of Slaughter?”","“How dare you call our master’s name?!” The monster commander paled in horror.","“Answer my question.” Zu An grabbed the monster commander’s shoulder and exerted a powerful suction force.","The monster commander was horrified. He sensed that the intruder had the power to reduce him into a withered corpse at will. Left with no choice, he replied, “Our master is in the Imperial Tomb.”","“What is he looking for?\"","“I don’t know. I only know he recently found a treasure and was extremely happy. He hasn’t been this happy for a few years now. I suspect that the treasure contributes greatly to what he’s looking for.”","Zu An was surprised. Did the Lord of Slaughter find a way to enter the Unknown Region?","Just then, he raised his head.","Footsteps echoed outside, and someone shouted, “Lord Aku, our master has summoned everyone who is of commander rank and above to the Imperial Tomb!”","The monster commander was overjoyed. He tried to call for help, only to be horrified to learn that he couldn’t speak at all. On top of that, his surroundings suddenly distorted, isolating the space around him from light and sound. Then, he felt his ki gushing out, causing his body to quickly weaken.","“Pl... ease...” He tried to speak, but hardly a sound came out before his consciousness faded.","Zu An lay his carcass down before replying in his voice, “Give me a moment. I’ll be right there.”","This monster commander named Aku carries a strong stench of blood. He must have many lives on his hands. He deserved to die.","To Zu An’s dismay, the monster camp was in an uproar over something. If he barged into the Imperial Tomb at this juncture, the odds were that he would be discovered quickly. So, he had no choice but to take on Aku’s appearance, wear his clothes, and enter the Imperial Tomb first to observe the situation."]},{"number":2546,"title":"Chapter 2546: Chapter 2498: The Lakeside Assault","paragraphs":["After putting on Aku’s clothes, Zu An produced a spark of flame and burned the corpse into ashes. He left the room and saw several monster guards waiting outside. They were all Aku’s subordinates.","“Sir, the other commanders have already headed over,” the guards said worriedly. They were worried that his tardiness in responding to the Lord of Slaughter’s summon could implicate them. That would put them in a bad position.","Zu An looked up and saw countless figures rushing toward the imperial tomb. The Monster World is indeed at its peak. None of these commanders are weak, and there are even a few who are exceptionally powerful.","Knowing that he would draw unwanted attention if he tried to escape right now, he decided to head over and observe the situation first. He made his way to the imperial tomb together with the monsters. The gates to the tomb were wide open, and many sculptures of the Fiend races’ ancestors had been destroyed. Only the most majestic Fiend God sculpture remained intact.","Now that he was back here, Zu An couldn’t help but notice a peculiar aura shrouding the Fiend God’s sculpture that made it seem solemn and powerful. Beneath the sculpture was a giant stone bench that had bloodthirst lingering on it, likely left by people who had sat on it.","Zu An took a look around; there were almost a hundred monsters gathered here. Aku was one of the weaker ones. The conspicuously stronger monsters in front had all surpassed earth immortal rank.","Soon, a brawny figure walked in. His eyebrows stood at forty-five degrees, looking as if they would pierce through the sky. He looked at the monsters before him with sharp eyes.","“Paying respect to master!” The monsters bowed.","Zu An secretly sized up the Lord of Slaughter. The latter was indeed stronger than the one who had been suppressed for millennia in the future. His bloodthirst was so overpowering that it almost felt palpable. -Those beside him trembled uncontrollably before the Lord of Slaughter’s presence.","“He’s too powerful.” Zu An didn’t dare to check the Lord of Slaughter’s cultivation with his divine sense, lest the latter detect it. He could only fathom a guess. The latter was undoubtedly stronger than him and the Monster Lord.","I wonder how the Monster Lord suppressed him in history.","“Master, may I know why you have summoned us urgently?” one of the monsters in front asked.","“Something is happening among us,” the Lord of Slaughter said.","The commanders were perplexed. Some whispered among themselves as they tried to figure out what those words meant.","“Incestuous King Mojard and his army were recently wiped out by the Ocean races,” the Lord of Slaughter said.","“What?!”","The commanders were taken aback, but there were also a few who exchanged glances with each other.","“I was shocked when I first learned this news. But what shocked me more was...” The Lord of Slaughter stared at the commanders with eyes as frigid as winter, causing them to shudder in fear. “Why has no one reported this matter to me?” His voice sounded like the roar of a primal beast.","Pah! Pah! Pah!","One after another, several monsters exploded into bloody mist. A powerful monster in front cried miserably as he tried to get up and flee, but he was unable to suppress the destructive energy rampaging inside him and exploded.","Blood and flesh splattered on the other monsters, causing them to shudder even more fearfully. The survivors were frightened and confused, and they dared not move lest the Lord of Slaughter turn his wrath upon them.","Goosebumps rose all over Zu An’s body. He had only come here to weather the crisis and escape as soon as everything calmed down. He hadn’t expected to stumble upon the Lord of Slaughter massacring his subordinates. It was a relief he wasn’t one of the targets.","The ‘fireworks’ killed a third of the monsters gathered here. The remaining ones were trembling, looking as if they wanted to fight back yet dared not.","If we’re going to die anyway, we might as well try fighting back.","The Lord of Slaughter is too strong. I’ll surely die if I attack first. I should wait for others to make a move.”","What’s going on? Has our master lost his mind?","Different thoughts floated in the monsters’ minds. Fortunately, the Lord of Slaughter spoke up. “Calm down, I was only purging the traitors. I know that the rest of you are loyal to me, and I don’t mistreat those who are loyal to me.”","“Traitors?”","Most of the monsters were stunned. The Monster World was at its prime, and it was already on the verge of conquering the Cultivation World. Who were these traitors defecting to?","A few smart ones had already figured out what was going on, though.","The Lord of Slaughter harrumphed. “The Monster Lord even dares to bribe my subordinates.”","A huge commotion broke out.","The Lord of Slaughter had gone into seclusion to uncover the secrets of the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb, and he'd entrusted all military affairs to the Monster Lord. The Monster Lord had always enjoyed great prestige because of his strength and commanding prowess, and years of monopolizing power had elevated his standing to be almost on par with the Lord of Slaughter. However, the two of them still fell out in the end.","“We vow to serve master to our deaths!” the remaining monsters roared. As the Lord of Slaughter’s aides, it was in their best interest to continue serving him. Even if they tried to defect to the Monster Lord’s side, it was unlikely that the latter would trust them.","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up. Looks like my visit to little Salamay paid off. She does have a way to communicate with the Lord of Slaughter.","The Lord of Slaughter continued, “The Monster Lord removed my aides and put his people in power. I now see that my trust in him was misplaced. That ambitious bastard dreams of overthrowing me! It’s about time for an internal purge.”","One of the commanders anxiously spoke up, “Our army is now under the Monster Lord’s control, and the Incestuous Lord has fallen in defeat. The other troops loyal to our master are stationed in the distant borders and won’t be able to make it back in time. Master, I beseech you to calm down and think things through!”","The Lord of Slaughter laughed. “Relax, I am not a reckless fool. I played a little trick. The Monster Lord will be coming to the imperial tomb within the next few days. We’ll take him down while he is on our turf.”","The monsters were overjoyed to hear that. “We will fight him to our dying breath!” It would be advantageous to them if they were fighting on their home turf, especially since the Lord of Slaughter’s cultivation was higher.","Zu An was awed. The Lord of Slaughter was indeed a formidable individual, to concoct a scheme against the Monster Lord so quickly. I wonder what he used as bait to lure the Monster Lord over. Is it the imperial tomb’s secret? He looked contemplatively at the imperial tomb.","The Lord of Slaughter proceeded to craft a detailed plan to deal with the Monster Lord.","Zu An nodded in approval. It would be hard for the Monster Lord to deal with such arrangements. I wonder how he turned the tables on the Lord of Slaughter in history.","To prevent news from getting out, none of the monsters were allowed to leave the imperial tomb until this matter was settled. The monsters spent the next few days constructing all kinds of formations in the imperial tomb. If they were tired, they would simply find a place to lie down and rest. There was plenty of space inside the imperial tomb anyway.","Zu An thus found a chance to sneak into the imperial tomb. He remembered that this place was structured as a Yin Yang Tomb. The Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb was merely a distraction to conceal the Unknown Region hidden below.","He made his way to a deep lake. Back then, the entrance to the Unknown Region had been located at the bottom of the lake, but he had no idea whether the gates were currently opened or not. He was thinking of taking a look when he suddenly heard a sharp whiz.","A black shadow flew toward his neck. At the same time, a small formation appeared underneath his feet, causing the surrounding air to become viscous. It was a slowing formation, hindering him from dodging the attack."]},{"number":2547,"title":"Chapter 2547: Chapter 2499: Reunion","paragraphs":["Zu An frowned. He sidestepped with the Steps of Rising Lotus. Given his deep understanding of space, very few formations could hope to trap him now.","“Hm.” The black figure was surprised to see how easily Zu An struggled free of her formation.","Hearing that gentle voice and looking at the figure's delicate frame, Zu An quickly stopped his attack and called out, “Little sister Ling’er?”","“Hm?” The black figure was about to attack with another talisman when a shudder ran through her body. She stared at him in disbelief. “B-Big brother Zu?”","Looking at her joyful yet skeptical expression, Zu An suddenly remembered he was still disguised as a monster, so he quickly reverted to his original appearance with a smile.","Upon seeing his face, the black figure also took off her veil to reveal a gentle and pure face. Who else could it be other than Xie Daoyun? Or perhaps it was more apt to call her this world’s Saintess Yumen Beiqing.","Zu An was delighted too. “What brings you here?”","The Saintess’ lips crept up. “After parting ways, I returned to the Fiend races and made arrangements. As soon as I was done, I rushed here to look for you. I couldn’t gather any information about you, so I disguised myself and snuck in. I didn’t expect us to reunite under such circumstances. This must be fate.”","Zu An was worried. “You’re the Fiend races’ Saintess, the most wanted person by the monsters. It’s too dangerous for you to be here.”","The Saintess quietly looked at him. “But I was worried about you, and we have been separated for so long that I don’t want to be away from you anymore.”","Her pitiful appearance squeezed Zu An’s heart. He pulled her into his arms and said, “We’ll never be separated from each other again.”","To him, he had only been away from Xie Daoyun for a few months, but to her, they had been separated for many years now. Like newlyweds who were forced to part for years right after their marriage, what woman could control her yearning for her lover?","They embraced each other tightly for a long time. By the time they let go, the Saintess’ cheeks were already flushed. Big brother Zu is still as naughty as before.","“What are you doing here, big brother Zu?”","“I came here to see if the Unknown Region has opened.”","The Saintess was taken aback. “Big brother Zu, you know the secret of the imperial tomb?”","Zu An laughed. “Have you forgotten? In the future, I once entered the Fiend race’s dungeon. The Unknown Region was hidden in the imperial tomb. I heard rumors that the Unknown Region opens once every few millennia, and we have returned a few millennia in time. It might be opening soon.”","The Saintess was awed. “Big brother Zu is indeed overflowing with luck. Most people wouldn’t see an Unknown Region in their entire lifetime. Even the Lord of Slaughter couldn’t find a clue despite having investigated this place for many years. Yet, you stumbled upon the opening of the same Unknown Region twice!”","Zu An embraced her slender waist and chuckled. “I have always been lucky. How else did I meet you?”","The Saintess’ cheeks were completely red. She rested her head on his shoulder and said, “Big brother Zu, I feel so blissful now.”","Zu An wrapped his hand around her. “Let’s return to the future once we settle things here. This bliss shall continue till the end of time.”","The conversation soon turned toward their current plight.","“It doesn’t look like the Unknown Region is open yet.” The Saintess frowned.","“Let’s head down to take a look.” Zu An grabbed her hand and brought her toward the lake.","The Saintess was about to take out a water repulsion talisman when the lake suddenly split open, revealing a path for them to pass through. Big brother Zu is incredible.","They flew around the lake twice.","Zu An was confused. “Hm? The gate isn’t there despite the powerful ki pulsations in the vicinity.”","The Saintess pondered the situation, wondering, “Is the teleportation gate not open yet?”","Zu An nodded. “From the current looks of it, that’s the most likely explanation.”","“Earlier, you mentioned that the Lord of Slaughter claimed that he had uncovered the Imperial Tomb’s secret. Do you think he’s telling the truth or lying?” the Saintess asked.","“It should be true.” Zu An thought about the Lord of Slaughter’s earlier behavior. “He's been obsessed with the Imperial Tomb’s secret for years now, yet he was calm for the last few days. He must have discovered something.”","“A pity that it doesn’t matter anymore,” the Saintess said. “He’s probably summoning the Monster Lord here to get rid of him, but based on the trajectory of history, he’s doomed to fail and be replaced by the Monster Lord.”","“Indeed. It’s going to be an intense battle.” Zu An fell into deep thought.","Speaking of which, where’s the Time Scribe? Shouldn’t he be with the Monster Lord or the Lord of Slaughter? Why didn’t I see him? I don’t think he’d miss such an important historical event.","They didn’t linger around the lake for fear of being discovered. Zu An quickly brought her back to his accommodation.","Fortunately, the imperial tomb was massive, and only monsters of commander rank and above had been summoned, so everyone had chosen a room or cavern of their own. Aku, whom Zu An was disguised as, was one of the weakest monsters; so he could only pick the most remote, smallest location. However, it was also the perfect place to hide the Saintess, as it was unlikely that other monsters would find her.","“Who should we side with when the time comes?” The room was simple, with a piece of rock serving as a makeshift bed. The Saintess’ face reddened with embarrassment at being alone with Zu An, and she scrambled for a topic to discuss.","“We’ll go with the flow. Whatever we do should align with the progression of history.” Zu An had initially thought that he would stay out of it, but in their history, the Lord of Slaughter was the loser. If the Monster Lord faltered, he could end up having to lend the latter a helping hand. Of course, he would have to be prudent about the extent of help he offered. Otherwise, the Monster Lord could just turn around and destroy him. That would be the worst-case scenario.","The two of them lay on the makeshift bed as they shared their experiences after parting ways. They hadn’t had much private time in the Fiend races' camp so there were many things they hadn’t shared yet.","Zu An wanted to ask the Saintess about how she had fared in the last few years, but the latter was more interested in his experiences. He didn’t hide anything from her, though he wasn't so foolish as to divulge his relationship with the Mermaid Queen and so on of his own accord.","At some point, however, Zu An’s hands began to wander.","The Saintess quickly became angry and grabbed his hand. “Big brother Zu, now that we’re surrounded by enemies, we should be warier than ever.”","Zu An looked at her with a smile. “Little sister Ling’er, I feel like we've drifted apart since our reunion.”","Fluster flickered across the Saintess’ eyes, and her cheeks soon became flushed. “Nonsense! There’s no such thing~”"]},{"number":2548,"title":"Chapter 2548: Chapter 2500: The Showdown","paragraphs":["The Saintess’ usually gentle and elegant voice carried a hint of coyness, and that stirred something in Zu An’s heart. He kissed her cheeks as he said, “I didn’t see any signs of the Brilliant Pinflowers in the imperial tomb. Are they really here?”","He had been searching the imperial tomb, but there were no signs of Brilliant Pinflowers.","“I remember there being some here, but I don’t know the exact location.” The Saintess looked apologetic. “I was in a rush to look for you, so I forgot to look up more information.”","“I probably just haven’t found them yet,” Zu An murmured.","He didn’t dare to search openly under the Lord of Slaughter’s watch. Given how big the imperial tomb was, it would take more time for him to cover more ground. It was also possible that the Brilliant Pinflower wasn't inside the imperial tomb but rather outside; it was just that he currently couldn’t head outside to take a look.","Just then, a pair of soft lips suddenly pressed against his. The desire in the Saintess' eyes lit up Zu An’s lust. The two of them embraced each other and tossed everything else to the back of their mind. The only thing they were interested in now was exploring each other’s bodies.","Zu An constructed a voice isolation formation around them, lest the Lord of Slaughter or other monster commanders hear them while their feelings were at their climax.","His action caused the Saintess’ face to redden further. She bit his shoulder and scoffed, “It’s all your fault.”","Zu An chuckled. “Who knew that there was such a side to the pure and dignified Saintess?”","“You’re so bad~” the Saintess moaned. She wrapped her hands around his neck, and the two of them soon melted in each other’s warmth. All kinds of unspeakable pleasures followed...","The following day, Zu An’s eyes suddenly shot open, and he sat upright. “That’s not right!”","“What’s wrong?” The Saintess leaned against him, revealing her impeccable body.","“Something is amiss about the situation outside.” Zu An quickly put on his clothes.","“What’s amiss?” the Saintess asked as she put on her clothes too.","Zu An removed the voice isolation formation and spent a moment listening before he replied, “It’s too quiet.”","There were powerful monster armies stationed outside the imperial tomb. They paled in comparison to the Monster Lord’s main force, but they were still a force to be reckoned with.","Just then, a terrifying howl echoed, “There’s a change in situation. Hurry up and gather!”","“It’s the Lord of Slaughter,” Zu An told the Saintess. “Find somewhere to hide. Don’t move around in the meantime.”","The terrifying roar caused the Saintess’ reddened face to turn pale. “Be careful.”","Zu An nodded. He quickly put on his clothes before rushing outside. As he headed off, his appearance slowly transformed into Aku's. The Saintess was awed by his transformation.","By the time Zu An arrived, most monsters were gathered and were staring at the Lord of Slaughter in confusion. The Lord of Slaughter looked infuriated, but no one knew what was going on.","“Master, what happened?” a monster standing at the forefront asked.","Zu An had learned his identity over the last few days. He was the Warped Monster, one of the Eighteen Monster Generals of the Monster World. In the Monster World, the Eighteen Monster Generals’ influence and strength were only beneath that of the three behemoths—the Lord of Slaughter, the Monster Lord, and the Incestuous King.","“The Monster Lord is already here,” the Lord of Slaughter said grimly.","“What?” The Warped Monster was taken aback before his face lit up in delight. “It’s good that he arrived early. We can use our home turf advantage to suppress him with our army outside!”","The Lord of Slaughter’s complexion looked awful. “Our army outside is gone.”","The commanders were all flabbergasted. How could so many troops disappear overnight without them noticing?","Zu An was awed. As expected of the Lord of Slaughter. His senses are keener than mine. I merely noticed that it was abnormally quiet outside, but he already confirmed that his troops were gone.","But how did the Monster Lord do it?","The troops stationed outside were a force to be reckoned with—they were the Lord of Slaughter’s elite army. How could they be massacred in a single night without any noise?","The commanders voiced their doubts too. They couldn’t believe that their subordinates were killed so easily.","The Lord of Slaughter sneered coldly, “It looks like the Plague Monarch has betrayed us.”","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up. The Plague Monarch?","He had clashed with the Plague Monarch in the future. The other party’s fighting prowess was nothing impressive, but his ability to spread plague was a potent weapon in large-scale battles. Even those with higher cultivation would struggle to match his destructive prowess.","Many monsters gasped upon hearing the Plague Monarch’s name. The latter was capable of rendering an entire army powerless overnight. To make things worse, the commanders were trapped inside the imperial tomb, leading to a collapse in the command chain outside. This hindered the troops outside from rallying together and putting up a fight. Of course, none dared to point that out, as it was the Lord of Slaughter’s idea to keep them here. The Lord of Slaughter was a proud man who didn’t take criticisms well.","Just then, a voice echoed outside. “Master, I request an audience with you.” Those words were uttered softly, but they echoed to every nook and cranny of the imperial tomb, sending chills down the commanders’ spines.","The Monster Lord was here.","The Lord of Slaughter narrowed his eyes. He glanced at the commanders in the imperial tomb, telling them to follow the plan. The commanders quickly flitted off to their respective hiding spots to lie in ambush.","The Lord of Slaughter turned to the gates and said, “Come in.”","The gates opened. Sunlight spilled into the imperial tomb, bringing it some life.","The first to enter was the Monster Lord, followed by a large group of monsters.","Zu An recognized the monsters gathered around the Monster Lord. On his right was the War Priest, and on his left was the Shadow Monster King. The Shadow Monster King’s incredible prowess had left a lasting impression on him in the Sealed Land. The War Priest and the Shadow Monster King were likely the Monster Lord’s strongest subordinates here.","There were also others whom Zu An had clashed with in the future, such as the Demonic Motherbug, Manipulator of Death, Iron Fist Rock, Scorpion King, Thousand-Footed Elder, Shadowhorror Devil, Plague Monarch, Doomsday Spirit... He had crossed blows with them in the future, but he hadn't thought that they were all the Monster Lord’s subordinates in this era.","The Lord of Slaughter turned grim. “I didn’t expect half of the Eighteen Monster Generals to have defected to your side.”"]},{"number":2549,"title":"Chapter 2549: Chapter 2501: Making An Example to Intimidate","paragraphs":["Having spent days with the monster commanders, Zu An knew that the Eighteen Monster Generals were eighteen renowned experts in the Monster World. Not only were they strong, they also each commanded great power and ruled over a territory. It could be said that anyone supported by these eighteen powerhouses was the true ruler of the Monster World.","The Monster Lord had ten of the Eighteen Monster Generals on his side, whereas the Lord of Slaughter only had the Warped Monster. There was a huge disparity in their fighting prowess. To make things worse, the latter's loyal subordinate, the Incestuous King, could potentially be dead. Things didn’t look optimistic for him.","The other commanders also had awful looks on their faces. After seeing the other side’s lineup, their earlier confidence had shattered.","While Zu An had fought these experts before, that was when they were weakened by the world barrier, whereas they could all exert their full strength now. He had previously been thinking of supporting the Monster Lord if the latter was at a disadvantage due to the ambush, but now, his priority shifted to how he could escape from this ordeal.","The Monster Lord’s lips crept upward as he spoke with his uniquely feminine voice. “You’re pulling our legs, master. They are only here so that we can serve you better.”","The Lord of Slaughter felt infuriated. That fellow is still putting on an act even at this point!","In truth, he had enjoyed such bootlicking in the past, or else he wouldn’t have trusted the Monster Lord so much as to even neglect his old subordinates like Mojard. And yet, in just a few years, the Monster Lord had already revealed his claws.","He suppressed his anger and put on an amicable face. “You came at a good time. I have just comprehended the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb’s secret and need more manpower to aid me. With all of you here, even the Celestial Court won’t be a threat.”","The Monster Lord maintained a respectful tone. “May I know where the Celestial Court is?”","“This concerns the biggest secret of our Monster World. I can’t divulge it in public.” The Lord of Slaughter spent a moment in thought before beckoning him over. “Follow me. We’ll discuss this further in the secret chamber.”","The Monster Lord was moved. He was tempted by the secret of the Celestial Court as well. However, in the end, his rationality got the better of him, and he stood his ground. “Master, you don’t need to fool me. You have laid a trap in the Imperial Tomb. I will be dead if I head over.”","The Lord of Slaughter’s face darkened. “Brother, what do you mean?”","The Monster Lord laughed. “Master, those are tricks I have used for a long time. Don’t you think you’re underestimating me too much by using them against me?”","The Lord of Slaughter’s cheeks twitched. He had always been an arrogant man. This was the one time he'd lowered his pride to lure his opponent into a trap, only to have the latter mock him for it. It made his cheeks sting.","However, he let out a hearty laugh. “Yes, I am beneath you in terms of schemes and ploys, but do you think you have won? Only the strongest is worthy of taking this seat!”","His laughter reverberated deafeningly in the hall. The weaker ones among those present had to clutch their hearts to pull themselves together, but even the stronger ones felt their blood flow going into disarray.","Zu An had to concede that the Lord of Slaughter was terrifyingly powerful, but it didn’t change the fact that the odds were stacked against him.","The Lord of Slaughter understood there was no turning back once the battle began, so he held back the full strength of his voice. He wasn’t as decisive as when he'd reduced a third of his commanders into a blood fog.","The Monster Lord and his aides were startled by the terrifying pressure coming from the Lord of Slaughter’s laughter. However, the Monster Lord let out a harrumph, neutralizing the laughter’s bloodthirst with his feminine voice. That greatly reduced the pressure caused by the laugh.","“Times have changed, master. Individual prowess can only go so far. I am now in control of most of the Monster World’s army, while the soldiers loyal to you are all gone. You are alone, and I am surrounded by talents. Do you still not understand where you have gone wrong?” The Monster Lord sighed. “Let me offer you words I have learned from the new world—those who win the hearts of the masses win the world!”","“Pui!” The Lord of Slaughter spat in anger. “You’re nothing more than a dog I reared. You desperately tried to climb up the ranks while I was investigating the imperial tomb’s secret.”","He turned to the Monster Lord’s aides and said, “Upon my word, I have never mistreated you. If you side with me now, I won’t pursue this matter and will even share the Monster Lord’s territory and wealth with you, as well as the Celestial Court’s secret. You should know how important the Celestial Court is to our Monster World.”","That left many of the experts wondering if the Lord of Slaughter had truly deciphered the Celestial Court’s secret. In the Monster World, there was a legend that their origin was tied to the Celestial Court, and their founding ancestor was the master of the Celestial Court. There were rumors about how powerful the Celestial Court was, and that finding the Celestial Court would allow them to fully awaken their bloodline powers and become many times stronger than they currently were.","Sensing that his aides were beginning to waver, the Monster Lord interjected, “Master, you are still pulling our legs. If you have found the Celestial Court, you would have long sinceawakened your bloodline’s powers. All of us combined wouldn’t have been a match for you. There would have been no need for you to negotiate with us.”","The monsters widened their eyes in realization. That’s true. We were almost duped by that old thing!","The Plague Monarch snickered, “Others might consider surrendering to you, but I wouldn’t dare do so after having just poisoned your personal army outside. I wouldn’t dare believe your words even if you promised me the world.”","The Lord of Slaughter’s face distorted in anger and he roared, “So you were the culprit!” He wouldn’t have been in this predicament if not for his personal army falling for the Plague Monarch’s poison.","The War Priest stepped in front of the Plague Monarch and said, “Rest assured, Plague Monarch. We are on the same side. We all know that old thing is arrogant and hot-tempered. If we continue working under him, it’s only a matter of time before he kills us in a fit of anger.”","The other experts nodded. The Lord of Slaughter was known for his cruelty. It was unlikely for things to end well for them if they defected to his side.","Seeing that his plan had failed, the Lord of Slaughter was infuriated. “Bastard! I’ll kill you!”","He dashed over to the War Priest and swiped his claws at the latter’s head. He was so fast that the other experts had no time to react at all.","He intended to first eliminate the War Priest to intimidate the others!","The War Priest was prepared for his attack. He quickly whipped out a pitch-black Soul Summoning Banner and unleashed a surge of black aura at the Lord of Slaughter.","However, the aura that could repel countless beings failed to stop the Lord of Slaughter. The latter’s claws gripped the War Priest's face like the death god’s scythe."]},{"number":2550,"title":"Chapter 2550: Chapter 2502: Lord Against Lord","paragraphs":["The stronger a cultivator was, the tougher their body would be. Someone of the War Priest’s cultivation would have a head tougher than metal. And yet, the Lord of Slaughter’s claws sliced through it as easily as tofu before crushing it.","The surrounding monsters were horrified. The War Priest was ranked second among the Eighteen Monster Generals, making him one of the top experts of the Monster World. And yet, the Lord of Slaughter had killed him in an instant. Quite a few monsters regretted their decision. They had underestimated the Lord of Slaughter’s strength, and now felt it was unwise to have made such a risky move.","Only Zu An remained calm. Having fought the War Priest in the future, he knew that the latter wouldn’t die that easily.","As expected, the Lord of Slaughter was frowning, but he didn’t stop there. With a casual strike, he smashed the monster commanders beside the War Priest into bloody mist.","The Eighteen Monster Generals reacted fast and quickly escaped while the War Priest was being attacked.","The Lord of Slaughter charged at the Plague Monarch, perhaps due to the latter’s slower speed or the fact that he harbored great hatred toward the latter for poisoning his personal army.","The Plague Monarch could only barely keep the attacks from striking his vitals. A punch struck his shoulder, and he spurted a mouthful of fresh blood. His body crashed into a stone sculpture like a tattered sandbag, causing the sculpture to crumble. He was so weakened that he couldn’t return to his feet despite several attempts to do so. He had temporarily lost his ability to fight.","However, a grayish mist had enveloped the Lord of Slaughter’s hand and was relentlessly creeping upward. The Plague Monarch was one of the Eighteen Monster Generals, after all. His poisons weren't to be scoffed at.","Iron Fist Rock’s eyes lit up at the opportunity.","The Lord of Slaughter had just killed the War Priest and severely wounded the Plague Monarch. Those attacks had to have severely depleted his ki. Furthermore, the Plague Monarch had managed to inflict his poison on him. This was a rare opening.","So, Iron Fist Rock hurled his renowned iron fist forth to strike the Lord of Slaughter’s back. He released a punch so fast that it produced a sonic boom and caused the surroundings to light up with iridescent colors; the light was caused by the intense friction between ki and air.","The Lord of Slaughter harrumphed. With a flick of his fist, he expelled the grayish poison aura out of his body before confronting Iron Fist Rock’s punch head-on.","Boom!","A miserable cry of agony emerged, accompanied by the sound of fracturing bones. Iron Fist Rock anxiously retreated while clutching his right arm. Cold sweat was dripping down his face. His fist was now hanging limply. It looked as if the bones inside had all shattered.","The monsters were horrified. Iron Fist Rock was known throughout many worlds for his iron fist. His punch could even shatter a city into ruins, or break apart a mountain. And yet, he suffered such a tragic loss against the Lord of Slaughter! Those thinking of exploiting the situation dropped those thoughts and determinedly retreated.","This greatly boosted the morale of the Lord of Slaughter’s group, including the Warped Monster. They charged out to battle with the Monster Lord’s subordinates.","While the Lord of Slaughter's group had fewer top experts, these commanders were all elites among the elites. They were far stronger than ordinary monsters. With the formations they had prepared beforehand, they were surprisingly able to match the ten Monster Generals’ army.","The Lord of Slaughter didn’t continue his onslaught, instead eyeing the Monster Lord. He sensed the latter trying to make a move several times, only to hold back because he couldn’t find a good opening to exploit.","“Master, your strength is indeed unparalleled. You killed the War Priest in a single blow and severely wounded the Plague Monarch and Iron Fist Rock,” the Monster Lord said flatteringly, but his eyes reflected fear.","“Hmph, the War Priest wouldn’t die that easily. Are you hiding there in hopes of finding a chance to assault me?” the Lord of Slaughter sneered.","The light at the corner of the hall distorted, and the War Priest slowly reappeared. “I see that it’s impossible to deceive your sharp eyes, master.”","The Lord of Slaughter said in praise, “You survived my all-out attack. You do live up to your reputation as the number two of the Eighteen Monster Generals.”","He could only unleash his full force in his first surprise attack. When he was dealing with the Plague Monarch and Iron Fist Rock afterward, he'd had to keep an eye out for the Monster Lord, lest the latter backstab him. Due to that, the pressure faced by the three Monster Generals was vastly different.","The other Monster Generals shot awed looks at the War Priest. He’s stronger than I expected.","Even the first-rank Shadow Monster King felt wary. This fellow is a threat to me.","“It’s my honor to receive master’s recognition.” The War Priest relished in the other Monster Generals’ admiring eyes, although he felt pained by his loss.","He'd had to use his precious war puppet to survive the ordeal. The puppet was extremely valuable, having strength on par with the main body. Not only was it his second life, it was also a powerful offensive tool. If he brought it out in battle, his enemy would have to simultaneously deal with two of him. Even if the Shadow Monster King was stronger than him, could he be two times stronger?","It was the War Priest's greatest trump card, and he would never have revealed it unless cornered. He hadn’t expected the Lord of Slaughter to destroy it right away. His heart was bleeding, but he had to feign composure as if it was nothing. I’ll have to find another trump card.","Not long ago, he'd found a secret dungeon rumored to contain the legendary Oblivion River Water. He had refrained from entering due to the risks, but it looked as if he had no choice now. Only by refining the Oblivion River Water would he stand a chance against the Shadow Monster King.","The Lord of Slaughter noticed the fear in the War Priest’s eyes and harrumphed. He turned his attention back to the Monster Lord. “Scheme all you want, but you can’t scheme your way out of a fight with me. Ultimately, you still have to speak with your strength.”","The Monster Lord knew that the Lord of Slaughter’s sudden assault had intimidated the ten Monster Generals, so they wouldn’t charge ahead for him anymore. However, he laughed. “You’re too arrogant. Do you think that you’re invincible?”","He suddenly charged at the Lord of Slaughter with speed that was on par with the latter’s earlier surprise attack. Very few people in the hall could see his movements. Flickering red marks revolved in his eyes. With a black aura in his right hand and a green mist in his left, he unleashed his attack upon the empty space right beside the Lord of Slaughter.","Both the Shadow Monster King and the War Priest were startled. Why was he attacking the air? Isn’t he exposing his opening to the Lord of Slaughter?","Only Zu An understood what was going on.","The Lord of Slaughter suddenly vanished in the next moment, only to reappear where the Monster Lord was attacking. It almost looked as if the Lord of Slaughter was running into the latter’s attack!"]},{"number":2551,"title":"Chapter 2551: Chapter 2503: Tricked","paragraphs":["The monsters were all shocked, be it those allied with the Lord of Slaughter or the Monster Lord.","Those on the Lord of Slaughter’s side were appalled to see their master in danger, whereas those on the Monster Lord’s side hadn’t expected him to have become so much more powerful as to anticipate the Lord of Slaughter’s reaction.","Only Zu An understood, having previously crossed blows with the Monster Lord. The latter possessed special eyes that could see his opponent’s openings. Often, he only had to strike the opening, and most enemies would crumble and fall into deep fear. Having one’s every move perfectly read and countered was enough to drive most cultivators into a mental breakdown. Only those with tremendous willpower could retain their sanity.","Needless to say, the Lord of Slaughter was no ordinary person either. He was stunned for a moment, but he quickly snapped out of it and sliced through space with his sharp claws.","The surrounding space collapsed, and the opening vanished. The Monster Lord had no choice but to change his move. They traded dozens of blows in the blink of an eye. Their movements were so fast that most monsters in the hall couldn’t keep up.","“I hadn’t expected you to acquire that legendary eye technique, but did you think you can defeat me just because you can see through my openings?” the Lord of Slaughter said mockingly.","“Master’s cultivation is formidable. Not only do you reveal few openings, but you move so fast that your openings vanish in an instant. Naturally, you wouldn’t be afraid of my eye technique,” the Monster Lord replied, but he didn’t sound disappointed at all.","The Lord of Slaughter harrumphed. He also knew it wouldn’t be that easy to deal with the Monster Lord’s eye technique, though the earlier clash gave him some confidence. Despite the latter's swift growth, the Monster Lord was still lacking compared to him. Even at the expense of incurring severe injuries, he was determined to end the Monster Lord right here. Once the ringleader was dead, his subordinates would have no choice but to return to his side.","Sensing their intensifying auras, Zu An knew that both sides were about to get serious.","All of a sudden, the Monster Lord said, “Master, I have prepared a gift for you to thank you for the years you have spent nurturing me.”","The Lord of Slaughter’s heart quivered. He thought the other party had acquired a formidable artifact or potent poison.","Little did he expect the gate to suddenly open, upon which a girl exclaimed, “Daddy~”","“Salamay!” The Lord of Slaughter flew into a rage.","It turned out that the Monster Lord’s subordinates were holding his daughter hostage at the entrance. In truth, he had already guessed as much when the Monster Lord arrived with his subordinates, but he'd still harbored hope. After all, Salamay was still young and didn’t pose a threat to the Monster Lord. Furthermore, in the Monster World, she was a well-known princess.","He'd figured that if the Monster Lord didn’t want everyone to know about his traitorous behavior, he wouldn’t lay his hands on Salamay. But the Monster Lord was more despicable than he'd expected.","He had always doted on his daughter, so he couldn’t turn a blind eye to this.","“Let her go!”","The Lord of Slaughter’s roar caused all the monsters in the hall to tremble; it was as if they were confronted with an enraged primal beast. The terrifying sonic boom sent the commanders holding Salamay hostage into shock, causing them to lose control over their bodies. If not for the Lord of Slaughter holding back for fear of hurting his daughter, they would have been reduced to bloody mist by now. He made use of the opportunity to fly over to rescue his daughter.","But the Monster Lord wouldn’t give him a chance to do that. He persistently stuck to the Lord of Slaughter as if he was the latter's shadow.","Even though the Lord of Slaughter was stronger than the Monster Lord, the gap wasn’t significant enough for him to quickly suppress the latter. With the Monster Lord persistently hounding him, he wasn’t free to save Salamay.","“Master, why are you in such a rush? Aren’t you snubbing me too much?” the Monster Lord sneered. “Master, why don’t you surrender? I promise to spare you and the little princess. Otherwise, I can’t guarantee the little princess’ safety.”","The Lord of Slaughter was both alarmed and furious. If he ignored the Monster Lord to save his daughter, the chances were that the latter would deal him a heavy blow. That would be the end of him. But if he didn’t head there now, the opportunity he had created with great difficulty would be squandered. The other party wouldn’t give him such a chance again.","All of a sudden, another figure charged at Salamay.","“Warped Monster!” The nearby Scorpion King and Thousand-Footed Elder noticed the other party and rushed forward to block his path.","However, the Warped Monster squeezed through the gap between the two of them like a slippery snake, charging straight toward Salamay. The commanders holding her hostage were just starting to recover from their shock when he snapped their necks.","“Princess!” The Warped Monster picked up Salamay and freed her from her restraints.","“Uncle Warped!” Salamay was moved too.","The Shadow Monster King sneered, “You’re courting death!” His eyes glowed as two rays of light shot toward the Warped Monster, who froze on the spot.","It was the Shadow Monster King’s ultimate skill—Paralysis Ray!","A massive corpse ball rolled up to the Warped Monster, and the countless skeletons stuck to the ball gnawed at him. It was the Manipulator of Death!","Even though the Warped Monster was paralyzed by the Shadow Monster King, as one of the Eighteen Monster Generals, he had his own survival methods. His body warped once again, causing the attacks to miss his vitals.","However, he was unable to dodge the attacks coming from his left. The massive corpse ball managed to latch onto him, and a miserable cry followed. The entire left side of his body vanished into thin air, and his exposed innards wriggled. A closer look at his wounds revealed bite marks, as if they had been chomped off by countless mouths.","The Lord of Slaughter was infuriated. He shook off the Monster Lord and hurled a punch at the Manipulator of Death. The latter's countless mouths shrieked in agony as the sheer force of the punch exploded his countless corpses.","However, the Lord of Slaughter’s face still looked grim. He knew that the Manipulator of Death was made out of countless corpses, and he had incredible regenerative abilities. Despite having received a heavy blow, it wouldn’t be long before he recovered.","The Lord of Slaughter thus quickly cast a skill on the Warped Monster, allowing his ruined left body to regrow flesh and blood. “Take Salamay away!” he shouted as he stood in front of the Warped Monster to block the onslaught of the Monster Lord, Shadow Monster King, War Priest, and the other experts.","“Master, you should run! I’ll cover your escape. Rally your army to eliminate these traitors,” the Warped Monster said anxiously.","That was indeed the Lord of Slaughter’s initial plan, but he laughed. “You don’t have the means to cover my retreat. Let me do it...”","He was about to say that he could easily find an opening to escape when his face suddenly darkened. Without any hesitation, he thrust a palm strike behind himself.","The Warped Monster spurted blood as he was sent flying, but there was a smirk on his face as he gleefully waved a pitch-black spike.","The Lord of Slaughter felt a numbing sensation spreading from the back of his waist to the rest of his body. He turned his sharp eyes toward the Scorpion King. “Your stinger!”","The Scorpion King snickered. “Master, there are few in the Myriad Worlds who can withstand my stinger’s poison. How does it feel?”"]},{"number":2552,"title":"Chapter 2552: Chapter 2504: Someone Who Shouldn’t Be There","paragraphs":["Zu An was surprised. He had also collected the Scorpion King’s stinger after killing him back then. He had known that the stinger contained a lethal poison, but he hadn’t expected it to be so potent as to even get the better of the Lord of Slaughter.","“Very well, very well!” The Lord of Slaughter’s complexion looked awful. “You have planned this out meticulously. Not only did the Scorpion King hand his greatest weapon to someone else, but you even put on a perfect show to deceive me. I am impressed.”","The Monster Lord smiled. “Master, you have always been mistrustful. We had to go this far to convince you.”","He thus surrounded the Lord of Slaughter with his subordinates while waiting for the poison to spread through the latter’s body. He opted for a defensive posture lest the Lord of Slaughter dragged one of them down with him in his desperate counterattack.","The Lord of Slaughter turned to the Warped Monster and asked, “What did that fellow promise you to turn against me?”","The Warped Monster had not only lost half of his body, but also faced simultaneous attacks from the Shadow Monster King and the Manipulator of Death. Had the Lord of Slaughter not intervened, he would have been dead. Even so, after losing half his body and receiving such a heavy blow, he would be weakened for many years.","Thus, the Lord of Slaughter couldn’t understand what the Warped Monster was after.","The Warped Monster wiped off his blood and chuckled. “Master, you are cruel and despotic. You are nowhere as virtuous as the Monster Lord. When so many of your old subordinates have turned against you, shouldn’t you reflect on yourself...”","Before he could finish speaking, the Lord of Slaughter rushed up to him and smashed a palm down on his head.","The Warped Monster was horrified. He anxiously lifted Little Salamay up as a shield while warping his body to dodge the attack. However, due to his severe injuries, his reaction was much slower than usual. There was no way he could dodge the Lord of Slaughter’s vengeful attack.","Pah pah pah!","The Warped Monster was shredded apart before exploding into a bloody mist. The Lord of Slaughter took this opportunity to snatch Little Salamay back from his hands. It happened so fast that no one had time to react.","The Monster Lord was stunned. “Master’s cultivation is unrivaled in this world. You remain as valiant as ever despite being inflicted with lethal poison. But channeling your bloodline power will only cause the poison to spread faster. Is there a need for that?”","“Traitors have to die!” the Lord of Slaughter spat with gritted teeth. Due to the effects of the poison, however, his breathing sounded more ragged.","The Monster Generals surrounded him while keeping their distance. Despite knowing that the Lord of Slaughter was severely poisoned, none of them dared to confront him. The Monster Lord had won this battle, but anyone who made a reckless move at this juncture could end suffering the same fate as the Warped Monster.","“Daddy, are you okay?” Little Salamay asked tearfully as she anxiously grabbed the Lord of Slaughter’s robe.","Zu An, who had been watching from the shadows, was perplexed. At this point, the Lord of Slaughter’s defeat was guaranteed, but in history, the Fiend races had suppressed him under the Sealed Land’s snow mountain. Also, according to history, Salamay was supposed to have escaped.","Furthermore, when he first came into contact with her, she'd been deceived by the Monster Lord, and it was only later that she learned about her father. But now that she had witnessed everything, how could she still be deceived by the Monster Lord even if the latter spared her life?","Were her memories altered by some method?","Zu An was worried that the alteration in history could affect those around him.","“Rest assured, I’m fine,” the Lord of Slaughter replied with a strained smile as he gently patted his daughter’s hand. Then, he turned to his enemies.","How can I escape? I'm at a disadvantage here, but I can put up one last fight. I can sacrifice my commanders to stall the enemies while I escape from here. If I gather my old subordinates, there's still a chance I can turn the tables around...","While he was thinking of a way to survive this ordeal, his body suddenly shuddered. He looked down at his chest. A bloodied little hand had pierced through it to grab his heart.","All the Monster Generals were stunned. They couldn’t understand what was going on.","The Lord of Slaughter arduously turned his head around, only to see little Salamay looking at him with an eerie smile.","Zu An was speechless. This time, even he was confused as well. The future Salamay had always been saying that she would exact vengeance for her father, but it turned out that she was the culprit instead?","However, he quickly rejected that thought. He had crossed blows with the Lord of Slaughter in the Sealed Land, so there was no way the latter would die here.","“Why?” the Lord of Slaughter asked as blood gushed out from his mouth, accompanied by bits of his innards. His eyes reflected his shock and sorrow.","Instead of answering the question, little Salamay ripped out his heart and retreated from him. Her expression began to change. “In the end, the renowned Lord of Slaughter only amounts to this much.” Her physique began to enlarge as she transformed into a blue-skinned man.","Realization dawned upon the Lord of Slaughter. “The Lord of Myriad Transformations!” He turned to the Monster Lord and exclaimed, “So this is your true hand!”","The Monster Lord chuckled. “Master, you are indeed smart, but you realized it too late.”","The Lord of Slaughter sighed in desolation. “I hadn’t expected you could win over someone as elusive as the Lord of Myriad Transformations. I deserve my loss.”","Zu An was taken aback too. The Warped Monster’s betrayal was ingenious, but to think that even that was a feint! The true killing blow was the Lord of Myriad Transformations disguised as little Salamay!","But how would the Lord of Slaughter escape this?","“The heart of an expert. Ahh, I can’t wait!” The Lord of Myriad Transformations was so excited that he swallowed the heart on the spot.","The other Monster Generals looked at him in envy, knowing that he would grow much stronger assimilating such a powerful heart.","The Lord of Myriad Transformations initially had a look of absolute bliss, but a hint of confusion soon surfaced in his eyes. “Hm?”","“What’s wrong?” The Monster Lord frowned. He instinctively sensed that a variable beyond his control had emerged, and he would hate it if anything went wrong at this point.","“I can’t put my finger on it.” The Lord of Myriad Transformations was perplexed. “I should have eaten his heart, but it doesn’t feel like it. It somehow feels... empty.”","The Lord of Slaughter harrumphed. A peculiar light suddenly shone from his body as a heart reappeared in his previously empty chest, and then his wounds began healing at a visible pace.","“Quick, let’s attack him together! He might have a way to retrieve his heart, but he should now be in his weakest ever state!” The Monster Lord lost his composure. He didn’t dare to hold back in case something went wrong.","Just then, a woman’s voice echoed from the entrance. “Bastard Zu, save my father right now if you don’t want anything to happen to your women!”"]},{"number":2553,"title":"Chapter 2553: Chapter 2505: Threat","paragraphs":["Zu An was stunned. He had been leisurely watching the show while wondering how the Lord of Slaughter would escape from this deathtrap. He hadn’t expected to be dragged into the conflict.","The monsters in the hall were taken aback. They turned toward the source of the voice and saw a man and a woman standing at the entrance.","The Monster Lord was taken aback to see the man. It’s Mojard?","Many years back, Mojard had been an expert who stood on the same pedestal as him. Even though the Monster Lord’s cultivation had advanced significantly in recent years, he was still wary of Mojard.","I thought he died against the Ocean races? Why is he here? He feels... different. He doesn’t have his usual confidence, and he looks much older.","Who is the woman next to him? Why is she looking at me with eyes filled with hatred? She looks familiar, but I can’t put my finger on it.","...","The other monsters were confused too.","“Brother Mo!” The Lord of Slaughter was delighted to see Mojard, but at the same time, he felt regret. Many years ago, Mojard had warned him about the Monster Lord’s swelling ambitions, but he'd thought that Mojard was merely trying to put down his rival and ignored him. It was only now that he understood who was truly loyal to him.","After hearing about the latter's tragic defeat to the Ocean races, he'd thought that Mojard was dead, so he was heartened to see the other party safe and sound.","“Incestuous King.” When he saw Mojard, the Monster Lord initially thought everything had gone wrong, but with a quick scan using his divine sense, he realized that the two of them had come here alone. On top of that, Mojard’s aura was extremely withered. That put his mind at ease. “I was worried sick when I heard about your defeat against the Ocean races. It’s good to see you safe and sound.”","“You scum. Drop your hypocritical act!” Mojard’s complexion looked terrible.","“Yes, you’re right. There’s no point continuing the act. I've been sick of it for a while.” The Monster Lord turned to the woman next to him and asked, “Who is this lady? She looks familiar.”","“Of course she looks familiar, for she is...” Mojard was about to reveal her identity when Salamay stopped him. Her coming from the future was a useful card, and she didn’t intend to squander it just like that.","Salamay looked at the Lord of Slaughter with a rapidly beating heart. After so many years, she was finally able to see her father once more. However, she suppressed her excitement and instead looked around while shouting, “I know you’re here. Let’s all die together if you refuse to come out.”","Zu An reverted to his human form and slowly emerged from the shadows. He made sure to wear a mask to avoid any complications in the future.","The Monster Generals were startled. They hadn’t noticed a human hiding there.","The Monster Lord was unsurprised. “I thought that master had an expert hidden in the shadows, but it looks like my worry was unfounded.”","He had been guarded against Zu An, worried that the latter would spring a surprise attack on him. That was why he hadn’t gone all out against the Lord of Slaughter. He was aware that this was the same person who had approached him for an alliance against the Lord of Slaughter.","Similarly, the Lord of Slaughter had thought that Zu An was the Monster Lord’s subordinate.","Due to their reservations, the two top experts had chosen not to reveal his existence despite both having noticed him.","Zu An ignored the two monsters and instead addressed Salamay with an awful look on his face. “How did you escape? Where’s the princess?”","Her presence here suggested that something had happened to Suolun Shi. To avoid affecting history, he took care not to reveal Suolun Shi’s name.","“That foolish woman is in my hands,” Salamay replied with a gleeful smile. “And why are you only worried about her? You should also be worried about the others. You haven’t been able to contact them, right?”","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn't received any messages from Pei Mianman, Ji Xiaoxi, and the others for quite a while. Ji Xiaoxi has Jiang Luofu and Yun Yuqing with her, so they should have no trouble protecting themselves.","That thought allowed him to calm down a little. “You’re trying to trick me. I won’t fall for it.”","“You can believe whatever you want to. Just don’t regret it when the time comes.” Salamay was in no hurry to explain herself. She seemed to be confident.","Zu An frowned. Could she have something to do with Manman’s disappearance?","“Give me more details, and I’ll decide whether to help or not.”","Salamay’s expression turned cold. “You don’t have a choice, whether it’s for your lovers or to ensure that everything... corresponds with the future.”","Zu An understood what she was driving at. In their world’s history, the Lord of Slaughter didn’t die in the Monster Lord’s hands. Conversely, that meant he had to ensure that the Lord of Slaughter survived this ordeal to prevent history from affecting the future. And the only one who had the power to pull that off now was him.","He was dazed for a moment. It was often said that history shaped the future, but why did it look as if history was determined by the future too?","“Who are you?” The Monster Lord’s face quivered. He had never been ignored like that before.","Zu An smiled. “We're merely passers-by.”","“Passers-by or not, you aren’t getting away scot-free!” The Monster Lord shot a glance at his subordinates, and the Demonic Motherbug and Thousand-Footed Elder, who were nearest to Zu An, lunged at him from his flanks.","The Thousand-Footed Elder had a head on each of his his feet, and these heads simultaneously opened their mouths and spewed a poisonous black fog at Zu An from all directions, shrouding him in it in an instant.","The other Monster Generals breathed a sigh of relief. The Thousand-Footed Elder was a giant centipede, and his black fog contained lethal poison. Even the other Monster Generals would be reduced to pus when enveloped in the black fog.","However, their smiles quickly stiffened.","The thick black fog suddenly began dissipating. An instant later, the mysterious man dashed out of the black fog. There was a cold gleam, and dozens of the Thousand-Footed Elder’s feet were suddenly severed. The heads on the severed feet screamed in misery as they dropped to the ground before swiftly withering into bones and falling silent.","The Demonic Motherbug launched her attack too. She was extremely fast, morphing into four silhouettes to attack Zu An from different directions at the same time. It looked as if red flashes of lightning were tearing through space. Despite having witnessed the setback faced by the Thousand-Footed Elder, she wasn’t worried in the slightest. Her talent put her in an increasingly advantageous position the longer the battle dragged out. As she generated more clones, she would eventually become undefeatable. The only way to defeat her was to simultaneously destroy all her clones.","The Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord might be able to pull that off, but they don’t know that the key is to destroy all my clones at once. This fellow doesn’t feel strong. I doubt that he can end me instantaneously.","As soon as those thoughts surfaced in her mind, she suddenly found herself faced with a massive black fog. That was the Thousand-Footed Elder’s poison!","Her surroundings were immediately enveloped by the poison. She couldn’t avoid it entirely no matter how fast she moved. As a result, all four of her clones plummeted from the sky and dropped dead."]},{"number":2554,"title":"Chapter 2554: Chapter 2506: Chaotic Battle","paragraphs":["All the monsters in the hall couldn’t believe what they were seeing. Both the Thousand-Footed Elder and the Demonic Motherbug were top experts of the Monster World, so how could they be defeated in an instant?","In particular, the Demonic Motherbug was so strong that she was close to coming on par with the War Priest and the Shadow Monster King. She was well-known to be a difficult opponent. The longer the battle dragged out, the stronger she became. And yet, she was defeated right away. That was a feat only the Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord were only supposed to be capable of.","The Shadowhorror Devil was excited. He could sense the fear lingering in the air, and some of it came from experts of the same caliber as him. Fear from experts was the greatest tonic to him in the world. He felt better than ever.","In contrast, the Monster Lord was frowning. Sensing his subordinates’ low morale, he roared, “That fellow has an evil art that allows him to absorb energy. Be careful!”","Those words snapped the Monster Generals out of their daze. Now that they thought about it, the other party had merely absorbed the Thousand-Footed Elder’s poison fog and used it against the Demonic Motherbug. The Demonic Motherbug had been caught off guard and fallen for it.","The Demonic Motherbug must have been vulnerable to area-of-effect attacks right from the start. Now we know how to deal with her in the future.","The monsters smiled in glee. They were on the same side now, but they were still rivals. That was why they avoided revealing their trump cards and weaknesses, lest the others take advantage of them. It was a good thing for them to learn about a renowned expert’s weakness.","Salamay looked at Zu An in awe. He’s a capable one. It’s a pity I can’t use him...","The Lord of Slaughter was delighted by the twist in the situation. He'd thought that he was doomed, but several helpers had suddenly appeared out of nowhere.","Where did Mojard find this helper from? Who is that woman?","Most important of all, who is that mysterious expert? His strength appears to be be on the same level as the Eighteen Monster Generals, yet he’s able to curb them with ease. It’s almost as if he knew about their weaknesses beforehand.","The Monster Lord noticed the same thing too. He turned to his remaining subordinates and warned them with a frown, “Something is off about that fellow. Don’t let your guard down. Attack him together and bring him down as soon as possible.”","He had to watch the Lord of Slaughter to stop the latter from escaping. Even though the Lord of Slaughter had sustained severe injuries from the earlier surprise attack, the Monster Generals still weren’t a match for him. Thus, he couldn’t make a reckless move.","Quite a few top experts had been taken out, leaving just the Shadow Monster King, War Priest, Shadowhorror Devil, Doomsday Spirit, and a few others. After seeing how easily he'd defeated the Thousand-Footed Elder and the Demonic Motherbug, they were hesitant to fight Zu An one-on-one. More than that, they were worried that they would be forced to reveal their trump cards. That would be a huge loss to them.","The monsters exchanged looks and soon arrived at a consensus. They would attack Zu An together and settle this as quickly as possible.","The Shadow Monster King was the first one to make a move. He floated into the air and began emitting light like a miniature sun, but unlike a sun, his body at the very center was pitch black.","The black sun suddenly shot out two beams of light. Many in the hall recognized it to be the Shadow Monster King’s ultimate skill—Paralysis Ray! Those struck by it would find their bodies stiffening up, rendering them completely helpless.","Wary of the bizarre movement skill Zu An displayed earlier, the Shadow Monster King utilized soulspeak on top of that. “This move will hit its target.” He wasn’t afraid of letting others know about his soulspeak, as some here already knew about it, and his soulspeak was inferior to Mojard’s anyway.","Zu An’s movement immediately halted, allowing the two Paralysis Rays to strike him squarely.","Salamay was appalled. Why is that fellow so useless? He fell for the Shadow Monster King’s tricks so easily! Isn’t he a tenacious bastard who even killed the Monster Lord?","Zu An had clashed with the Shadow Monster King in the future, so he knew about the other party’s tricks. He could have used ‘Whatcha lookin’ at’ to interrupt the other party’s soulspeak, but he decided against that. He was concerned that the Shadow Monster King and the Monster Lord would recognize him right away as soon as he used the skill against them in the future. He was weaker back when he faced them, and their heightened vigilance could make things dangerous for him. Thus, he'd decided to take on the other party’s control skill instead.","The Monster Lord’s group was delighted to see that. The Shadowhorror Devil and the Doomsday Spirit charged at Zu An. It was the perfect opportunity for them to snatch the kill while the latter was paralyzed by the Shadow Monster King. This would give them more leverage later when discussing contributions and rewards.","The Shadowhorror Devil briefly paused halfway through his charge, as he couldn’t sense any fear from Zu An. This left him confused. He still isn’t panicking yet. Does this mean he has other tricks up his sleeves?","Out of vigilance, he slowed down and allowed the Doomsday Spirit to overtake him. He was thinking of using the latter as fodder to probe the other party’s hand for him.","The Doomsday Spirit did notice the Shadowhorror Devil’s little movement. He’s still as cowardly as ever, even at this point. Looks like I’ll be getting this head.","All of a sudden, however, he heard a bell, and it induced inexplicable fear in his heart.","Isn’t that the Shadowhorror Devil’s renowned artifact—the Horror Bell? Why is he making a move against me?","Ah! He must be a spy from the Lord of Slaughter. That’s why he’s turning against me at this critical moment! No wonder he intentionally slowed down. He was planning to get behind me so he could cooperate with that mysterious man to launch a pincer attack on me!","That raised the Doomsday Spirit’s fear. Without any warning, he turned around and unleashed his attack on the Shadowhorror Devil instead.","The abrupt attack startled the Shadowhorror Devil. He anxiously put up his defense while exclaiming, “What are you doing? Are you out of your mind?”","“I’m out of my mind?” The Doomsday Spirit was infuriated too. “You traitor who defected to the Lord of Slaughter! How dare you turn against us right now?!”","The Shadowhorror Devil was stumped. “What nonsense are you spouting? Why would I defect to the Lord of Slaughter’s side?”","Even the Lord of Slaughter was dumbstruck. Huh, is the Shadowhorror Devil on my side? Why don’t I know that?","The Monster Lord frowned. “Do you have evidence, Doomsday Spirit?”","“Why don’t you ask him where his Horror Bell is?” the Doomsday Spirit roared.","“Of course it’s with...” The Shadowhorror Devil was about to take out his artifact when he suddenly froze in place. Eh? Where’s my Horror Bell?","That evoked the Doomsday Spirit’s sneer, prompting him to attack with greater fervor.","Zu An smirked. He dared to take the Shadow Monster King’s Paralysis Ray head-on because he had made preparations beforehand. He had killed the future Shadowhorror Devil and obtained the Horror Bell from him. He usually didn’t have much use for the Horror Bell, but it was the perfect tool to divide the Monster Generals in this tense moment.","However, he was surprised to see the Shadowhorror Devil unable to produce his own Horror Bell. Could it be that duplicates of an item can't exist at the same point in spacetime, and the moment one is taken out, the others will disappear?","While Zu An was wondering about that, a desolate war horn echoed. Countless cavalrymen appeared out of nowhere and charged at him.","The shocked monsters in the hall hurriedly leaned against the walls to dodge the cavalrymen’s charge. Not even the Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord would confront a charging army of such scale.","With the cover of his comrade, the War Priest had unleashed his ultimate skill—Invincible Army!"]},{"number":2555,"title":"Chapter 2555: Chapter 2507: Closing the Spacetime Loop","paragraphs":["Confronting thousands of charging cavalrymen was a truly terrifying prospect. Even the Lord of Slaughter’s surviving commanders despaired at the situation.","The War Priest required a long channeling time to summon his army, but if he succeeded, he could easily crush any enemy. The only one who could potentially be able to escape from his army was the Lord of Slaughter. The others wouldn’t stand a chance.","The Monster Lord felt chills. The War Priest is too powerful once he unleashes his full prowess. I must never let him summon his army if I ever fight with him in the future.","By the time the cavalrymen charged over, however, Zu An had already regained his mobility. He brought out his Human Emperor Seal. The golden seal revolved as it floated into the air, and then suddenly enlarged until it was the size of a mountain and crashed down on the cavalrymen.","Boom!","A loud explosion ensued. The cavalrymen at the forefront were crushed into mincemeat.","“Human aura?” The Monster Lord frowned. He sensed emperor ki from the seal, and it made him wonder if the humans of this world had a Human Emperor or something.","However, he quickly rejected that guess. The emperor ki was weak, which showed that its connection with the humans of this world was faint. It hadn’t received the recognition of the humans. Nevertheless, it still showed that this mysterious man had connections with the human race.","“Don’t worry, his seal doesn’t contain enough faith. Its prowess is lacking,” the Monster Lord said upon seeing the War Priest lurching in shock.","The War Priest snapped out of his shock and chuckled. “I was wondering why that thing felt off. Turns out it only looks formidable on the surface.”","He waved a flag, and the formation masters in his army unleashed their skills on the massive Human Emperor Seal. A black aura enveloped the Human Emperor Seal, and the ground under it turned into a black bog. It was as if the area had turned into a marsh. The Human Emperor Seal began sinking into it.","Zu An sighed. The Human Emperor Seal lacks legitimacy here, so it’s unable to unleash its true prowess.","The corruption of the Human Emperor Seal was eroding his connection with it, so he quickly took it back without any hesitation.","The War Priest lamented Zu An’s swift reaction. Just a bit more, and I could have erased the seal’s divine sense imprint and taken it for myself. He could tell that the seal was growing, and once it matured, it could potentially exert prowess comparable to a deity-grade artifact.","At this point, he decided to stop holding back. He waved his flag once more, and his army encircled Zu An. Even though his vanguard had suffered heavy losses due to the bizarre seal, he could easily conjure more soldiers as long as his army formation wasn’t breached. Even ants could devour an elephant in sufficient quantity, let alone his strong soldiers.","Seeing Zu An in a predicament, the Lord of Slaughter advised him, “You have to defeat the War Priest himself, or else he can resummon his army.”","He couldn’t let his powerful helper die just like that. Unfortunately, he was severely injured by the Warped Devil and the Lord of Myriad Transformations, and the Monster Lord was keeping a close eye on him now. He couldn’t intervene in Zu An’s battle.","Hearing his father’s concern for that fellow, Salamay’s eyes drooped. Father doesn’t know how powerful he is. He’s strong enough to slay the Monster Lord, so how could the War Priest stand in his way?","In the entire hall, it was probably her who had the most confidence in Zu An. The only worry was that this world didn’t have world laws that imposed restrictions on intruders, so the Monster Lord and his subordinates were far stronger than they were in the future. This could lead to variables.","In the center of attention, Zu An calmly faced the army charging toward him. With a flick of his hand, a turbid yellow water droplet appeared on his palm. There was a hint of blood red hidden in the droplet.","“Go!”","With a wave of Zu An’s hand, the Oblivion River Water flew out and quickly expanded into a stream, then a river, and finally a massive tsunami.","The charging army didn’t have time to dodge, although it wasn't as if they planned to. Why would they dodge when they were strong enough to disperse even a rapid river?","Only the War Priest felt uneasy. Looking at the turbid yellow water tinged with bloody red, he was suddenly reminded of the water from the legends. He anxiously waved his flag to order his army to avoid the tsunami, but it was already too late.","The Oblivion River Water washed through the hall, devouring the War Priest’s army. Some of his soldiers weren’t afraid of the tsunami at first because they were adept in water skills. However, when they came into contact with the Oblivion River Water, their bodies jolted and they forgot all their skills. Their memories had faded into oblivion.","The War Priest’s army was devastated.","Some of the Lord of Slaughter’s commanders and the Monster Lord’s subordinates failed to dodge in time and were touched by the Oblivion River Water, causing them to lose their wits and become floating corpses.","“It’s the Oblivion River!” The Monster Lord recognized the origin of the water. Even with his strength, he had no choice but to dodge the tsunami.","The Monster Generals fled in a fluster, having heard about the Oblivion River Water’s legend.","Salamay and Mojard seized the opening to cover the Lord of Slaughter and escort him to Zu An’s side.","The Monster Lord’s face darkened. The only silver lining was that he had sealed off the entrance, so the Lord of Slaughter wouldn’t be able to escape just yet. However, if the Oblivion River continued rampaging, more variables could emerge.","Thus, the Monster Lord tossed a copper coin toward the raging Oblivion River Water. It was none other than the Treasure Sinking Coin.","Zu An had been curious to know what would happen if he took out the Treasure Sinking Coin before the Monster Lord, but out of consideration for the future, he decided against it.","However, the Monster Lord seemed to be lacking understanding of the Treasure Sinking Coin. This artifact could only nullify created artifacts; it was completely useless against intrinsic items. The Oblivion River Water was an intrinsic item.","Zu An suddenly recalled Mi Li’s talk about spacetime. This was a good opportunity, so he pretended that the Treasure Sinking Coin had worked on the Oblivion River Water and severed his connection with it. Without his control, the rampaging Oblivion River Water reverted to its initial droplet, and by some stroke of fate, it landed in the War Priest’s vicinity.","Without any hesitation, the War Priest rolled up his sleeves and stowed away the droplet. He nearly burst into laughter, gladdened by the windfall. This mysterious fellow must have beaten me to that dangerous dungeon, but his gains only ended up benefiting me.","The other Monster Generals looked at the War Priest in envy. They had suffered heavy losses, whereas the War Priest had gained something valuable instead.","Even the Monster Lord looked at the War Priest with envious eyes. He was interested in the Oblivion River Water, and he hadn’t expected it to fall into the War Priest’s hands. It was a pity he still needed the Monster Generals, so he couldn’t snatch it in public, lest he lose their support.","Salamay scoffed at Zu An. How can he be this careless as to lose such a valuable treasure?","The Lord of Slaughter consoled Zu An, saying, “Don’t worry, my friend. As long as you escort me to safety, I’ll find an even more formidable artifact for you in the future.”","Zu An smiled. He had done all that merely to ‘return the item to its master’. Only by entrusting the Oblivion River Water to the War Priest now could he snatch it away from the War Priest in the future. Through this, he was closing the spacetime loop.","“Let’s get him now that he doesn’t have the Oblivion River Water anymore. We mustn’t give them any chance to make a comeback!” the Monster Lord roared as he charged at the Lord of Slaughter.","The other Monster Generals charged at Zu An, hoping to get something on par with the Oblivion River Water from him."]},{"number":2556,"title":"Chapter 2556: Chapter 2508: Losing the Catch and the Bait","paragraphs":["Both sides’ subordinates had been mostly wiped out by the Oblivion River Water. The only ones alive were experts of the Eighteen Monster Generals’ caliber.","But despite the fewer monsters present, the battle only grew more intense. There had been too many distractions earlier, and some of the experts had been using the cover of the commotion to slack off. But now that the distractions were eliminated and both sides were done probing each other’s capabilities, it was time for them to get serious.","The Monster Lord was no longer holding back; every attack he unleashed was a killing blow. He was determined to kill the Lord of Slaughter for good. When everything had been under his control, he'd prioritized safety and opted for a war of attrition to wear down the latter. However, the appearance of this mysterious but powerful expert left him with a feeling of danger.","If he manages to rescue the Lord of Slaughter, it will be the worst-case scenario.","The Lord of Slaughter had ruled for so long that he had many old subordinates loyal to him. Furthermore, those in the middle and lowest echelons, oblivious to his true nature, revered him. It had taken the Monster Lord years of scheming to dispatch the Lord of Slaughter’s subordinates to rural places, thus temporarily isolating the latter. But if the Lord of Slaughter escaped and gathered his old subordinates, the tables could turn. Considering what was at stake, the Monster Lord didn’t dare to hold back anymore.","The Lord of Slaughter charged at the Monster Lord with a furious roar. His hatred for the Monster Lord ran so deep that he wanted nothing more than to rip the latter to shreds. Unfortunately, he had suffered two consecutive blows, such that he struggled to even protect himself from the Monster Lord. It would be hard for him to take down the Monster Lord here.","Seeing the two bosses going all out, the Monster Generals felt a tremendous boost in morale. They unleashed their strongest skills, and even those who were severely injured climbed to their feet to help out. Experts of their caliber, as long as they weren’t killed on the spot, boasted incredible regenerative prowess. By now, those who had been injured were ready to fight once more.","Of course, the Shadowhorror Devil and the Doomsday Spirit were still fighting with each other and didn’t have the time to join the battle.","The Monster Generals wouldn’t dare to intervene in the battle between the Monster Lord and the Lord of Slaughter. Now that the Lord of Slaughter was a beast trapped in a cage, there was no telling what he could do out of desperation. It was unwise to provoke him right now.","Thus, they turned their attention to Salamay. They didn’t know who she was, though she had mentioned ‘Father’ when she first entered. It was perplexing, as they knew that the Lord of Slaughter didn’t have a daughter of that age better than anyone else.","The stronger a cultivator was, the lower the leakage of their spirit would be, thus making it tougher for them to have a child. The Lord of Slaughter only had an extremely young daughter, and the Monster Lord had stationed her tens of thousands of kilometers away from here. So, who was this woman?","In any case, her weakness made her the perfect target.","Mojard tried his best to protect Salamay, but with his current strength, he was no match for so many Monster Generals. Soon, he started receiving injuries.","“Hm? When did you become so weak, Incestuous King?”","“Where’s the soulspeak you’re so proud of?”","“Is he feigning weakness?”","...","The Monster Generals were perplexed, but they weren’t too worried. They had the absolute advantage here. It wouldn’t change a thing even if Mojard was feigning weakness.","“Save me!” Salamay was no weakling, but this was a battle involving the top experts of the Monster World. She was severely outclassed here.","The Lord of Slaughter didn't know her identity, but he could tell she was on her side. Furthermore, he felt an inexplicable sense of intimacy toward her, so he howled in her direction.","A terrifying sonic boom jolted the Monster Generals’ bodies, causing their blood flow to go into disarray. That gave Mojard and Salamay a chance to regain their footing.","The Monster Lord harrumphed. “I’m your opponent!”","He summoned a three-headed bird to attack the Lord of Slaughter.","The Lord of Slaughter’s eyes reddened. He revealed his true body, which resembled an enlarged T-rex, and both of them fought each other even more intensely. Wherever they passed by, the sculptures in the Imperial Tomb shattered into dust.","Surprisingly, the Fiend God sculpture and the Imperial Tomb’s overall structure remained untouched despite the powerful shockwaves emanated by the two bosses. The Monster Lord and the Lord of Slaughter couldn’t resist looking at the towering Fiend God sculpture, wondering if there was a secret hidden in it. However, this wasn’t the time for their minds to be wandering. They had to prioritize eliminating the enemy before them first.","Without the Lord of Slaughter’s help, Mojard and Salamay soon fell into a disadvantageous position once more. Salamay could only shout for Zu An to help her.","Zu An dodged the Shadow Monster King’s attacks while replying telepathically, “Tell me how they're faring, and I’ll save you.”","Salamay understood that she couldn’t reveal her relationship with the Lord of Slaughter, or else the enemy would use her as a hostage to threaten her father. She gritted her teeth in anger, but this brief moment of hesitation caused another attack to land on her. Left with no choice, she replied telepathically, “Don’t worry, Suolun Shi is still alive. I merely temporarily imprisoned her elsewhere. If you don’t save me, she'll go down with me.”","“What about the others?” Zu An remained unmoved.","“I don’t know their whereabouts. I was lying,” Salamay replied helplessly.","Zu An had figured as much, and he breathed a sigh of relief. That being said, he couldn’t turn a blind eye to Suolun Shi’s plight, so he performed an instantaneous movement to appear at Salamay’s side and dragged her away from the Scorpion King’s incoming giant pincers.","Before the two of them could exchange words, a flash of light appeared beside Zu An. “Your opponent is me!”","The light and shadow surrounding the Shadow Monster King began to distort. He was confident that he was within the top three of the Monster World. With the downfall of the Incestuous King, he even thought about having a showdown with the Monster Lord. His confidence was rooted in his ability to slow down the time around him. The space around him was folded to such an extent that his opponent couldn't attack his main body. That made him undefeatable. On top of that, he had another trump card up his sleeves.","He'd noticed that when the War Priest acquired his droplet of Oblivion River Water, Zu An didn’t look regretful at all. That suggested the latter had more valuable artifacts with him. He was determined to acquire them while the Monster Lord was distracted, or else he wouldn’t get this chance again.","As the Shadow Monster King pressed closer, Zu An remained on his guard, knowing that he was a fearsome adversary. Fortunately, there was an information disparity between both sides. Zu An knew the tricks the former had up his sleeves.","Breaching the Shadow Monster King’s distorted space was easy enough for him—the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra did the job perfectly. That was how he'd pull it off in the future. But to avoid digging holes for himself in the future, he had to give up on that easy solution.","It was a good thing that Zu An's grasp of spatial transformations had greatly deepened. He unleashed the Star Shattering Imprint, using his tenfold attack power to penetrate the folded space around the Shadow Monster King to strike the latter’s main body.","The Shadow Monster King was horrified. He couldn’t understand how Zu An’s attack had reached him. But there was no time for him to think further. He could already feel death encroaching on him. Without any hesitation, he activated his survival skill—Time Severing—to stop this deadly attack. Then, he took this opportunity to quickly retreat. Fear lingered on his face, and he hesitated to confront Zu An once more.","What’s with that fellow? How is he this formidable? More importantly, it feels as if he knows my abilities.","It’s a huge loss this time. Not only did I fail to acquire any of his artifacts, but I ended up using Time Severing once. I can now only use it once more.","He felt so regretful that he thought his intestines would turn green.","Zu An was startled. When he'd first fought the Shadow Monster King in the Sealed Land, the other party had revealed that he had once encountered a powerful enemy and was forced to use Time Severing, resulting in him only having one use left. Could that powerful enemy be me?","A blue light suddenly glowed from the hall, and a massive formation emerged from beneath the crowd’s feet."]},{"number":2557,"title":"Chapter 2557: Chapter 2509: Gate of World Crossing","paragraphs":["“What’s going on?” The Monster Generals were stunned.","Did the Lord of Slaughter prepare a trap beforehand? But we already defeated his commanders and unraveled his formations.","The blue light enveloped Zu An, the Lord of Slaughter, Salamay, and Mojard.","“This isn’t good. It’s a teleportation formation!” The Monster Lord recognized the nature of the light right away and thrust his palm on the ground. A destructive force rippled forth, causing the blue formation to flicker.","Mojard anxiously pushed Salamay toward the Lord of Slaughter. “Master, you leave. I’ll cover your back!”","“Brother Mo!”","“Uncle Mo!”","The Lord of Slaughter and Salamay were horrified.","Mojard looked at them with a smile. “Otherwise, none of us will be able to get away. To be able to help master and first miss in my final moments, I have no regrets.”","He lunged forward to tightly embrace the Monster Lord. He used a secret art that intensified his aura severalfold, such that even the Monster Lord struggled to shake him off.","“Let me go!” The Monster Lord was infuriated. One of his hands turned completely green and the other turned completely black as he smashed them ceaselessly into Mojard’s body.","The areas struck by the green aura instantly decomposed until only bloodied white bones were left, whereas the areas struck by the black aura turned into puddles of pus.","Normal enemies would have been destroyed by that, but Mojard had once an expert on the Monster Lord’s caliber. Even though he was severely weakened, the prowess he could exert out of desperation was still not to be underestimated. Lights surfaced from his body, swiftly healing the injured areas.","Unfortunately, the Monster Lord attacked so quickly that the lights slowly dimmed. Mojard's rate of recovery was unable to catch up with the rate he was receiving damage. It wouldn’t be long before his body was reduced to a bloody mist.","Tears streamed down Salamay’s eyes. The Lord of Slaughter’s eyes reddened as well. He felt bitter regret. Had he listened to the Incestuous King years ago, he would never have ended up in this state.","Zu An was impressed. Mojard was truly loyal to the father and daughter, though Zu An wondered how much the latter's twisted love contributed toward that.","In the blink of an eye, all of them vanished into thin air. Before they knew it, they were already beside the lake in the Imperial Tomb.","“Are you all right?” the Saintess asked anxiously. She only breathed a sigh of relief upon confirming that Zu An was safe and sound.","“I’m fine. Were you the one who teleported us here?” Zu An quickly scanned his surroundings. There was no one on their tail yet.","“Mmhm. I saw the Monster Lord bringing so many of his subordinates along and realized that I wouldn’t be able to make a difference in the battle. So, I took the time to construct a formation here instead.” The Saintess patted her chest in relief. “I’m glad you managed to hold on.”","“You’re the Fiend races’ Saintess?” The Lord of Slaughter was astonished to see Xie Daoyun. He had naturally met the legendary Saintess before, considering how they had been adversaries for so many years. He'd never thought that the day when he was saved by her would come.","The Saintess nodded, to which the Lord of Slaughter quickly replied, “I’ll remember this favor, Saintess. If I curb the rebellion, I’ll make peace with the Fiend races.”","Zu An and the Saintess didn’t think much of it. That old thing is just making empty promises. In any case, he was strongly suggesting for them to help him, since his promise could only be fulfilled if he emerged victorious.","“We aren’t out of danger yet. We’re still inside the Imperial Tomb. It won’t be long before our enemies find us, and that would be the end of us,” the Saintess said.","The Lord of Slaughter knew she was right. He had received severe injuries from the earlier two betrayals, and the subsequent battle with the Monster Lord only worsened his injuries.","While the mysterious man was formidable, he was only marginally stronger than the Monster Generals. He was only able to get the better of the Monster Generals due to his special methods and the Monster Generals’ reluctance to reveal their aces. If it came down to a desperate fight, two or three Monster Generals could take him down.","Suddenly, there was a loud explosion in the distance, causing the Imperial Tomb to tremble.","Tears trickled down Salamay’s eyes. “It’s Uncle Mo. He must have self-destructed.”","The Lord of Slaughter’s complexion looked awful. He was about to console her when a white light suddenly shone from her waist pouch.","A bead flew out from the pouch. Mojard emerged from it and fell to the ground. His face was ghastly pale.","“Flesh Puppet?” The Lord of Slaughter quickly made sense of the situation.","Mojard revealed a bitter smile. “Master is knowledgeable. Yes, this is my means of survival.” He then bowed apologetically to Salamay and said, “I seek first miss’ forgiveness for placing my life bead with you.”","Salamay was overjoyed. She quickly supported him to his feet. “There’s no need to seek my forgiveness. I’m more than happy to see you alive.”","The two of them had weathered storms together for many years. Mojard had continued to stay by her side even after she had fallen from grace. As a sentimental being, how could Salamay not have any feelings for him? She'd long been aware of Mojard’s feelings for her, but she'd feigned ignorance and instead used it to control him. However, his decision to sacrifice himself to buy time for their escape had moved her profoundly. She realized that she wasn’t as heartless as she thought.","“You call her first miss?” The Lord of Slaughter was perplexed.","“She is First Miss Salamay, albeit from the future. We are all from the future,” Mojard knew they were in a predicament, so he didn’t hide anything and quickly explained the situation.","“Hahaha! No wonder I feel a sense of closeness to her! No wonder she called me father!” The Lord of Slaughter was overjoyed. He pulled Salamay into his embrace. “My good daughter, you have grown so big!”","“Father!” Salamay was moved too. She had been searching for a way to save her father for millennia now, and it was only now that they were finally reunited.","The Saintess interjected with a cough. “I don’t want to interrupt your reunion, but our priority should be to escape from here. The Monster Lord will find this place very soon.”","The Imperial Tomb was filled with the Monster Lord’s subordinates. There was nowhere for them to escape to.","The Lord of Slaughter laughed. “I was hesitant, but since Brother Mo has returned alive and my good daughter has reunited with me, I shall take you to the legendary Celestial Court!”","Zu An was surprised. “You found a way into the Celestial Court?”","“Of course,” the Lord of Slaughter replied proudly. “The Monster Lord only got the better of me because I spent years devoted to investigating the secret of the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb. My effort wasn’t in vain.”","He turned to Zu An and the Saintess and said. “Even though you have just helped me, the Celestial Court is of grave importance. I can only take you with me if you promise to help me defeat the Monster Lord in the future.”","Zu An and the Saintess exchanged looks. The Saintess told him telepathically, “Big brother, since we couldn’t find the Brilliant Pinflower in the Imperial Tomb, it might be in the Celestial Court instead.”","Zu An had been planning to make another trip into the dungeon anyway, so he nodded. “All right.”","The Saintess also spoke up. “His will is my will.”","The Lord of Slaughter looked at Zu An in surprise. This human wields such influence over the Fiend races’ Saintess.","Salamay looked at Zu An in disdain. This fellow flirts with women no matter where he goes.","Suddenly, the Monster Lord’s roar echoed. He was already not too far away from them.","Without any hesitation, the Lord of Slaughter took out a transparent box. Zu An and Salamay’s breathing quickened. They had seen this item before—it was the Nature Jade Case!","As he opened the box, their surrounding space rippled. The lake before them began revolving swiftly until a glowing door manifested."]},{"number":2558,"title":"Chapter 2558: Chapter 2510: Anomaly","paragraphs":["“Master, we haven’t determined the victor in our battle. Why did you flee like a coward? If news of this gets out, you’ll become the world’s laughingstock.” The Monster Lord suddenly appeared in the distance, taunting the Lord of Slaughter as he swiftly approached.","“Bastard!” The Lord of Slaughter was infuriated. He wanted to step forward to confront the Monster Lord. He had been a conqueror for a good half of his life; it had been a long time since he last suffered such a grievance.","Salamay and Mojard quickly held him down. “Father (Master), you mustn’t fall for his provocation! You can always make a comeback in the future!”","The Lord of Slaughter took a deep breath. “Forget it. You went through so much trouble to find me. I can’t let your sacrifice be in vain.” He beckoned Zu An and the Saintess over. “Hurry up and enter the gate. It’ll close very soon.”","He grabbed his daughter’s hand and Mojard’s shoulder before charging into the light gate.","Zu An grabbed the Saintess’ hand and said, “Hug me tightly.”","The Saintess was confused, but she still did as she was told with a reddened face. Ah Zu, this is too much. Do we need to get affectionate in public?","Just as they entered the gate, the massive energy ball hurled by the Monster Lord arrived and blasted the lake. Unfortunately, the gate had already disappeared by then.","The Shadow Monster King and the other Monster Generals arrived a second too late. Upon learning what had just happened, their faces darkened. They asked, “Master, what should we do?”","They were beginning to regret their decision. Despite having prepared such an elaborate trap, the Lord of Slaughter had still escaped from their encirclement. If the latter recovered and made a comeback, they would be in grave danger. They hadn’t forgotten how brutal the Lord of Slaughter had been over the years.","The only one who was in a celebratory mood was the War Priest. He had made a killing by acquiring a droplet of the legendary Oblivion River Water.","The Monster Lord could guess what the Monster Generals were thinking. “What are you panicking for? We’ll start by encircling the Imperial Tomb, then we'll take this time to purge that old thing’s loyal subordinates. Even if he escapes, what can he do alone?”","“But that’s the Celestial Court! What if that old thing awakens his bloodline power inside? By then, we might not be a match for him even if we join forces,” the Shadowhorror Devil said, gulping in fear.","The others shared the same worry. The Celestial Court was the Monster World’s most elusive legend. It was the dream of every monster, but it was a pity they'd missed this golden opportunity.","“How can a person grow stronger that easily? Don’t worry, everything is still within my grasp,” the Monster Lord said with a confident sneer.","The Monster Generals exchanged looks. They initially thought that the Monster Lord was saying those words to console them, but his confident expression made them wonder if he had a trump card that they didn’t know about.","...","Right after Zu An and the Saintess passed through the light gate, it vanished. The Monster Lord’s howl was vaguely audible behind them.","The Saintess released Zu An’s waist, only to realize they were in the middle of a large body of water. There was nowhere for her to step on, causing her to plummet. She was horrified. She had never felt so helpless before.","However, a warm hand grabbed her in time, keeping her from plummeting deeper. The water around her parted, creating a bubble-like space.","Zu An chuckled. “I told you to hold me because there’s something weird about the water here.”","He'd remembered that what was on the other side of the lake was the legendary Weak Water, which was water that offered so little resistance that not even a feather would float in it. It was fortunate that the powerful Fiend Emperor had been with them, or else he, Yan Xuehen, Yun Jianyue, and Yu Yanluo would have drowned. Recalling the past brought a smile to his face. How I wish to return and see them again...","Just then, he sensed something was off. He lowered his head and saw the Saintess’ face was pale, and she was shivering a lot. He asked anxiously, “What’s wrong?”","“I’m afraid of water,” the Saintess replied with a strained smile.","Zu An embraced her tightly. He patted her shoulder while consoling her. “Don’t worry, I have the power to control water now. I won’t let any water near you.”","The Saintess buried her head in his chest. It might have been his words or his warm embrace, but her shivering reduced.","Zu An quickly ascended through the water together with her. In the past, he had been completely helpless against the Weak Water, but the growth in his cultivation and the water control ability he'd acquired from fusing the Crown of the Ocean Deity and Hundredwarble allowed him to deal with the Weak Water with ease.","When he reached shore, he was surprised to find that the Lord of Slaughter and the others weren’t there. He searched the shore, but they were nowhere to be seen. He eventually turned his gaze back to the Weak Water. Did they drown in there?","He quickly rejected that thought. The Lord of Slaughter would no doubt be strong enough to overcome the Weak Water, even if he was weakened. Besides, he had Mojard and Salamay to help him.","“We might have been teleported to different places,” the Saintess said. Now that she was out of water, her complexion recovered. She sat on a stone next to the shore. The cold wind tugged at her clothes and left her hair unkempt, making her look a little pitiful.","Now that he had grasped the secrets of spatial transformations, Zu An knew her words made sense. Given that they had entered the light gate at different times, it wouldn’t be surprising for them to have been teleported to different locations. The last time he came here, he and the others had been inside the Fiend Emperor’s sleeves, which was why they were teleported to the same destination.","“What a pity. I wanted to get more information from Salamay.” Zu An sighed. He was curious how Salamay had escaped, and how Suolun Shi had been reduced from a warden to a prisoner.","“Don’t worry. Now that we're allies, she won’t hurt the princess. They still need our help to deal with the Monster Lord,” the Saintess consoled him.","“Let’s hope that’s the case.” Seeing that the Lord of Slaughter wasn’t here, Zu An grabbed the Saintess’ hand and led her deeper in.","Along the way, he passed by familiar sights, such as the giant stone tortoise sculpture and the towering Feather Mountain. What surprised him, however, was the absence of the stone tablet carved with the words ‘Feather Abyss’.","He initially didn’t think much of it, but as he ventured deeper into Feather Mountain, his expression slowly turned grim. Why isn’t there resentment that's so intense it's almost corporeal?","Back when the Fiend Emperor forced him, Yan Xuehen, and the others to lead the way, they had begun sprouting black scales under the effects of the resentment. If they hadn’t taken turns holding onto Yu Yanluo’s Lord Sui’s Pearl, they would have become a part of the resentment too.","“What’s wrong?” The Saintess noticed something amiss with Zu An’s expression.","Zu An didn’t reply. He grabbed her hand and began rushing up to the mountain peak. With his current cultivation, the aerial monsters no longer posed a threat to him. Soon, they arrived at the peak.","Zu An was stunned. Where’s the Feather Mountain Spring Water?"]},{"number":2559,"title":"Chapter 2559: Chapter 2511: Appearance","paragraphs":["Zu An had a deep impression of the Feather Mountain Spring Water. While it was incapable of truly reviving a dead person, its effects were very close to that. He had already consumed all the spring water he obtained the first time, and he often regretted not procuring more.","Now that he was here again, he'd wanted to gather more spring water. He was surprised to not find it here.","“What are you looking for?” the Saintess asked.","Zu An told her about the Feather Mountain Spring Water. “I've noticed that there are many differences from the last time I entered this place. I’m even starting to wonder if it’s the same place.”","The Saintess chuckled. “Other than the points you have mentioned, the rest is the same, right?”","Zu An thought about it. “Yes, most things remain the same except for those details.”","“The divergence could be caused by the difference in spacetime.” By now, the Saintess had already recovered from the shock of falling in the water. “The last time you entered this dungeon was millennia in the future. Much could have changed in the meantime.”","Zu An thought that was a sloppy explanation, but he couldn’t find any explanations for the anomaly.","“Speaking of which, when talking about this dungeon, the Monster Lord and the Lord of Slaughter mentioned the Celestial Court. Where is the Celestial Court?” he wondered as he looked upward. He remembered seeing a brilliant light in the sky back then, and then the Celestial Emperor had gifted him the Sun Slaying Bow. If there was a Celestial Court here, that was the only sign of it he'd seen during that trip.","Unfortunately, he'd seen neither the Celestial Emperor’s face, nor the Celestial Court. He only remembered that the sky had been covered in colorful, auspicious clouds.","The Saintess was perplexed. “I don’t know why the monsters thought there was a Celestial Court here, but they must be disappointed now.”","Tens of thousands of kilometers away from where Zu An and the Saintess were, the Lord of Slaughter looked at the vast world before him in a daze. “Where’s the Celestial Court? Where’s the Celestial Court?!”","He had no idea what the Celestial Court looked like, but he didn’t think it would be like this. The world around him was completely barren. How could this be the Celestial Court?","Salamay also knew about the legends concerning the Celestial Court. “This world’s ki is richer than our original world. The Celestial Court might be hidden here somewhere.”","The Lord of Slaughter’s eyes lit up. “Yes, you’re right. I lost my nerve for a moment there. I should have thought about that. Let’s take a good look around. We should be able to find the Celestial Court.”","Salamay nodded. From time to time, her eyes would scan the surroundings.","“Are you looking for the Fiend races’ Saintess and that mysterious man?” the Lord of Slaughter asked.","Salamay nodded. “Mmhm. Uncle Mo is missing too.”","The Lord of Slaughter spent a moment in thought before replying, “It could be because we entered the light gate at different times, resulting in us being transported to different places.” As the leader of the Monster World, he had also grasped the secrets of space. It wasn’t difficult for him to deduce what was going on.","“I see...” Salamay looked both regretful and relieved at the same time. It would be troublesome if Zu An interrogated me while my father is injured. Once my father recovers from his injuries, I won’t have to fear anyone anymore.","“Earlier, you mentioned that you came from the future. Tell me more about it,” the Lord of Slaughter said.","He had already secretly brought up matters that only he and his daughter knew about to test her, and he could also feel his bloodline aura in her. That convinced him that she was his daughter as an adult. But this matter still sounded inconceivable to him. He was also curious to know who that powerful, mysterious man was. There were too many questions in his heart.","Salamay knew that for them to work together, she had to share her information with her father, so she told him about everything that had happened.","Despite everything the Lord of Slaughter had been through, he was still shocked to hear Salamay’s story. His face darkened. “You’re saying that the Monster Lord successfully replaces me in the future?”","Salamay assessed her father’s expression and carefully replied, “But the Monster Lord didn’t meet with a good end either. He eventually died to that fellow named Zu An.”","The Lord of Slaughter frowned. “That mysterious fellow is strong, but he’s still lacking compared to the Monster Lord. How did he defeat the Monster Lord?”","“If I’m not mistaken, the Monster Lord was weakened by the world’s law...” Salamay explained the situation then. In truth, however, she was also unsure how Zu An had defeated the Monster Lord.","“It must be the compounded effect of the world barrier and that Zu An’s possession of the World Law Beacon. By weakening the enemy and strengthening himself, he gained an advantage over the Monster Lord and killed him,” the Lord of Slaughter sneered. “I didn’t expect the Monster Lord’s real body to be his mount. Even I was fooled. If I didn't know that, I would be at a huge disadvantage if I fought a life-and-death battle with him.”","Salamay looked hesitant to speak.","The Lord of Slaughter laughed. “You may speak frankly. Your father is not that weak-hearted.”","Salamay thought it was best for him to know about how he'd ended up so he could guard against it, so she said, “Father, you’ll be sealed inside a formation in a place called the Sealed Land in the Cultivation World. The culprit seems to be the Fiend races’ Saintess.”","“Her?” The Lord of Slaughter frowned. “How did she have the power to seal me?”","Salamay added, “But now that you know, as long as you tread carefully, that woman won’t be able to get her way. We should kill them after we’re done using them, lest they become a threat.”","The Lord of Slaughter nodded, but he still felt uneasy.","Meanwhile, Zu An was discussing their next destination with the Saintess. He was thinking of heading somewhere he could obtain useful information.","“Why don’t we go to Kunlun Mountain?” the Saintess proposed.","“Kunlun Mountain?” Zu An was surprised. That wasn't one of his options. “Why Kunlun Mountain?”","“Kunlun Mountain is said to be the ancestor of all mountains. There are legends about Kunlun Mountain in ancient fiend records. Such renowned places tend to have rare herbs. If the Brilliant Pinflower exists in this world, the odds are that it’s at Kunlun Mountain,” the Saintess explained.","Zu An nodded. Even if not for the Brilliant Pinflower, he would still decide to stop by Kunlun Mountain to gather some clues about the Celestial Court. After all, in the legends, Kunlun Mountain had intricate ties with the Celestial Court.","“I’m feeling uneasy. Where did the Time Scribe go?” Zu An frowned. Such an elusive expert had gone completely silent. He was worried that the Time Scribe was scheming something.","“He might have infiltrated the Monster Lord’s faction. After all, he is the true master of the Monster World millennia in the future,” the Saintess said.","“Let’s hope that's the case.” Zu An was still feeling uneasy, however.","Soon, sunset arrived. The many ferocious beasts in this world made traveling at night very dangerous, so the two of them found a cave to rest in.","There were too many things to worry about, so Zu An wasn't in a mood to fool around. Instead, he spent his time in thought.","Just then, the Saintess shyly whispered something into Zu An’s ears.","Zu An burst into laughter. “Don’t go too far away. Call me if anything happens. I’ll rush over.”","“All right. You mustn’t sneak up on me!” the Saintess said coyly.","“I’m not so perverted as to pounce on someone relieving themselves.” Zu An laughed.","The Saintess glared at him before rushing out with a reddened face.","A moment later, Zu An shook his head. She sure is shy to run so far away. Oh well, she’s no longer a sheltered miss, but the renowned Fiend races’ Saintess. She can protect herself now, and I can rush over if anything happens too.","Thus, he continued racking his brain to remember the details of what he'd seen when he came here millennia in the future. He felt as if he had overlooked something.","Meanwhile, the Saintess glanced back at the cave coyly, as if she was afraid that her lover would follow her. But as she walked further away, the coy expression on her face slowly disappeared. Suddenly, she sped up and began traveling rapidly toward the mountain. Some time later, she halted her footsteps and coldly called out, “Isn’t it about time for you to reveal yourself? You have followed us for so long.”","Applause echoed from behind. If Zu An were here, he would have been surprised to learn that Mojard had been following them.","Mojard looked intrigued. “I’m curious. Even Zu An didn’t notice me. How did you know?”"]},{"number":2560,"title":"Chapter 2560: Chapter 2512: Only the Dead Can Keep Secrets","paragraphs":["The Saintess eyed Mojard and said. “You don’t look anywhere near as injured as you were before.”","Mojard had barely escaped from the Monster Lord, but invoking his Flesh Puppet came at a steep cost. His earlier condition said it all. Otherwise, the Lord of Slaughter wouldn’t have believed him so easily. And yet, the Mojard here looked perfectly fine.","Mojard chuckled. “I used to be the Incestuous King. I’m bound to have hidden aces.”","“Is that so?” The Saintess chuckled, though her usually gentle smile looked cold. “Zu An was still wondering where the Time Scribe had gone, but I see that he has accompanied us here.”","Mojard’s eyebrows shot up. “Saintess, are you suspecting me to be that Time Scribe or something? I am Mojard! Surely the first miss and my master can tell the difference?”","“The one who risked his life to stall the Monster Lord should have been the same Mojard, but...” The Saintess intentionally paused to scrutinize Mojard with her gaze. “The same can’t be said about the one who followed us in here.”","Mojard laughed awkwardly. “My master should be powerful enough to tell the difference.”","“The Lord of Slaughter doesn’t know about the Time Scribe, but even if he knew, both he and Salamay were hoping that Mojard can escape alive. You used their subconscious against them and crafted some story about a Flesh Puppet to convince them. WIth that, you could infiltrate our midst openly using Mojard’s identity.” The Saintess eyed him coldly. “I was initially fooled by you too. It was only when Zu An mentioned the Time Scribe that I realized there was something off about you.”","Mojard sighed. His body began to distort until he reverted to his original appearance. He was now wrapped in a huge black cloak. His face was hidden by the shadows of the cloak, making it impossible to discern his true appearance. “Our disguises collapse once someone suspects the plausibility of our identities. Yesterday, I was in such a rush that I forgot to make proper arrangements.”","The Saintess understood what he meant.","The Time Scribe had been in a rush because the Lord of Slaughter was about to take them through the light gate, and the only one the Scribe could impersonate was the recently deceased Mojard. None of them had witnessed Mojard’s death, so there was room for him to maneuver. His story about the Flesh Puppet sounded plausible, so no one had doubted him. But no matter how plausible his story sounded, there were bound to be gaps when scrutinized.","“Weren’t you recording events beside the Lord of Slaughter? What are you doing here?” the Saintess asked.","Zu An had told her that the Time Scribe would only follow ‘the protagonist of the world’. Both the Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord had a far greater impact on the world than anyone else. That was why the Time Scribe had left Zu An’s side to follow those two and record the major events surrounding them. The Time Scribe could have impersonated Mojard because he wanted to record the legendary Celestial Court, but it was extremely suspicious how he had abandoned the Lord of Slaughter to stalk her and Zu An.","“I discovered that the one who has the greatest luck and influence in this world is not the Monster Lord, nor the Lord of Slaughter, and not even Zu An.” The Time Scribe looked at the Saintess with heated eyes. “It’s you!”","The Saintess’ gaze turned even colder.","The Time Scribe took out a book and quickly flipped through it. “According to history, you’re the Yumen clan’s first miss, and the Yumen clan is merely a minor clan in the Fiend races. How did they groom an outstanding talent like you?","“History states that you suddenly rose to prominence just as the Fiend races were about to meet their end and performed an incredible comeback. In the end, you even sealed the Lord of Slaughter. I can’t imagine how you were able to perform all these feats.”","“I don’t know about any such history,” the Saintess scoffed. “I’m merely doing my best to lead the Fiend races against the monsters. Perhaps big brother Zu might have helped me to accomplish many of those feats.”","“Are you trying to say that you’re Miss Xie who transmigrated into this era?” The Time Scribe chuckled. “Yes, I initially believed that story. I thought Zu An worked together with you and the Monster Lord to seal off the Lord of Slaughter. But after I met you and interacted with you close up, I realized how ridiculously wrong I was.”","The Saintess suddenly smiled. “Oh? How were you ridiculously wrong?”","“You have far greater weight in this timeline than anyone else. That Miss Xie doesn’t have such capabilities.” The Time Scribe closed his book. “I found no records of you in history before you became the Saintess. So... Who are you?”","“Did you follow us just to speak utter nonsense?” The Saintess looked calm, as if none of this was related to her.","“I didn’t want to reveal myself either. We Time Scribes should remain quietly in the background, recording every major event that happens in the world. But you insisted on calling me out.” The Time Scribe smiled. “Since that’s the case, I thought I would ask you in person.”","“Aren’t you afraid of being silenced?” The Saintess’ eyebrows shot up.","The Time Scribe shook his head. “Don’t worry, Saintess. I don’t bear any ill will. We Time Scribes merely record history. We don't intervene in secular affairs, so you need not worry about your identity being leaked.”","“Is that so? But I recall you intervening unnecessarily when I was in the Monster World’s underground city.” The Saintess eyed him coldly, unconvinced by his words.","“Hm? You inherited that lady’s memories? That’s weird...” The Time Scribe picked up his brush and scratched his head. “Is it possession? But it doesn’t look like it. Ah, it could be...”","The Saintess raised her hand. “Only the dead can keep secrets.”","The Time Scribe revealed a mocking smile. “I see you’re about to do something useless, so let me remind you that we Time Scribes, unlike low-tier entities, have transcended physical bodies so we can traverse spacetime and the world. We are indestructible. You can’t kill me.”","“Is that so...” A light suddenly shone from the Saintess’ hand. It was so blindingly bright that it outshone even the sun. This omnipresent light instantaneously engulfed the Time Scribe, causing his body to dissipate.","The Time Scribe’s horrified voice could be heard from the light. “How’s this possible? You are able to hurt me! This power... I know who you are! You are...”","He was reduced to ashes before he could finish speaking."]},{"number":2561,"title":"Chapter 2561: Chapter 2513: Tolerating the Humiliation For Greater Things","paragraphs":["The Saintess watched everything with calm eyes as if she had done something insignificant. Under the brilliant light, her face looked exceptionally cold. It felt as if there was a light halo around her. Unlike the Shadow Monster King, who was dark at his core, she felt like a divine entity emanating auspicious light. If the Fiend races were to see her, they would once again kneel and kowtow to her, thinking that she was the Saintess chosen by heaven.","Only when the Time Scribe was completely eradicated did the Saintess turn around to leave. Her movements appeared leisurely and slow, but it only took a step for her to leave the forest. She soon returned to the cave’s vicinity. She rubbed her face to erase its coldness, replacing it with her usual gentle smile.","Zu An happened to rush out then, and he looked visibly relieved to see her. He rushed forward to give her a big embrace. “That scared me. I sensed something happening outside and rushed out to take a look, but I didn’t see you. I thought something happened to you.”","The Saintess' body stiffened up at his embrace, her lifted hand freezing in midair. Hearing the other party’s concern, her expression mellowed, and she naturally hugged him back too. She gently replied, “Don’t worry, I’m fine. I was surprised by the light too.”","Zu An looked in the distance and said, “Wait here for me. I’ll check it out.”","“Don’t go. It could be dangerous.” The Saintess held his hand.","Zu An smiled. “Don’t worry, I'm strong enough to stay safe.”","The Saintess insistently shook her head. “We could be in the Celestial World. There are too many powerful entities that we don’t know about here. We can’t be too cautious.”","Zu An frowned. “Danger is no reason for us to stay still. We're already lacking intelligence about this world. If we don’t gather as much information as we can, we could die without even knowing why.”","The Saintess stared at him, amazed by his mental fortitude. “I’ll go with you then. I can at least cover you.”","Zu An thought it would be worse to leave her here and risk being separated in this foreign world, so he replied, “Alright.” He wrapped his arm around her slender waist and flew into the air.","The Saintess glanced at the hand on her waist and felt the warmth coming from it. It made her cheeks redden. Zu An had so many things on his mind that he didn’t notice anything off about her, though.","The two of them soon arrived at where the Saintess had previously met Mojard. Zu An put the Saintess down and scanned the surroundings.","“Did you find anything?” the Saintess carefully asked.","Zu An squatted down in front of a hole and pinched the soil. “There were two people here just now. Both of them were very powerful.”","“Is that so?” The Saintess looked at him from behind with sharp eyes.","“I sense traces of fire and light element ki lingering in the air. Those two people must have fought with each other.” Zu An’s face turned grim. “How weird. I only sensed an instantaneous burst of power. Was the victor determined in a single move?”","The Saintess walked up to him. “Who do you think they were? Were they humans or beasts?”","“There’s too little information to say for sure.” Zu An shook his head. “I don’t think they were beasts, as there are no traces of wildlife activities here or within a fifty kilometer radius. It’s as if the beasts dare not approach this place because they're afraid of something.”","Zu An had tried to use the jade badge’s communication ability to gather information from nearby animals, only to find that there was not a single animal within fifty kilometers.","Upon hearing his answer, the Saintess retracted her hand and said, “If we can’t find anything, we should leave quickly to avoid complications. I feel uneasy. This place is dangerous.”","Zu An nodded. “I feel uneasy too.” He considered talking about the inexplicable unease he had felt in recent days, but he decided against that to avoid worrying her. Seeing that there were no other clues around, he brought the Saintess back to the cave.","While he was pondering with a frown, he suddenly felt a pair of fingertips gently massaging his temples, and a voice saying, “I think you have been too nervous recently. You should relax a little.”","Zu An looked at her with a helpless smile. “I don’t want to, but we’re treading on thin ice. The slightest mistake could cost my life and implicate the rest of you.”","Suoluo Shi had been imprisoned by Salamay. Ji Xiaoxi and the others were unreachable. On top of that, something seemed to have happened to Pei Mianman.","“Are you worried about big sister Pei?” the Saintess asked while massaging him.","“Mmhm. I didn’t find any traces of her outside the Imperial Tomb,” Zu An said. “I’m beginning to doubt whether she was really heading to the Imperial Tomb.”","The Saintess’ hands paused. “Once we’re out of here, let’s return to that town to gather more information. Perhaps there are other clues there.”","“I guess that’s all we can do now.”","The Saintess continued the massage. “You don’t need to be too worried. Sometimes no news is the best news.”","Zu An grabbed her hands and pulled her into his embrace. “Little sister Ling’er, you’re so understanding. After hearing your words of consolation, I now feel much calmer.”","The Saintess was embarrassed. “Big brother Zu, you’re making fun of me.”","Her coy demeanor stoked Zu An’s desire. He couldn’t resist the urge to lower her head and kiss her.","The Saintess was taken aback. She instinctively tried to look away, but at the same time, she was worried that the other party would notice something. Her hesitation resulted in her lips being captured. Shock flashed across her eyes, but she quickly controlled her emotions to show only embarrassment and confusion.","It was only when Zu An’s hands began reaching into her robes that she regained her clarity. She coyly grabbed his hand and grumbled, “You said that this place is filled with the unknown. How can we do something like this here?”","“But you just said that we should take things in stride and not worry too much.”","“I was consoling you... Wu...” The Saintess wanted to protest, only to find her lips sealed.","Anger flickered across her eyes. She placed her fingertip behind his head. It would only take a simple jab for her to claim this fellow’s life. But she quickly remembered her ploy and gave up on it. Forget it. It’s not our first time anyway.","In her moment of hesitation, she suddenly felt Zu An squeezing into her with unstoppable momentum. Her face reddened, and she bit down hard on his shoulder. It’s all for that...","“Be gentler!”"]},{"number":2562,"title":"Chapter 2562: Chapter 2514: Conditions","paragraphs":["The following day was sunny.","Zu An and the Saintess traveled westward to Kunlun Mountain. It wasn't hard to find—it had a high mountain peak that rose into the clouds, making it visible from all parts of the world.","Zu An was astounded. How high must that mountain be to be visible even from this far away?","This world’s Kunlun Mountain was vastly different from the Kunlun Mountain he was familiar with in his previous world, both in terms of height and size. He even wondered if this world’s Kunlun Mountain was connected to heaven, linked to the Celestial Court. Or maybe the Celestial Court is on Kunlun Mountain?","Meanwhile, the Saintess secretly glanced at his side profile, and a red tinge occasionally appeared on her cheeks. This bastard has too much stamina!","She'd initially endured it, thinking of it as a necessary sacrifice. However, it had eventually reached a point where her head blanked out, and she succumbed to the relentless waves of attacks. Just how many loads did that fellow shoot in me last night?!","The Saintess had been both embarrassed and angry in the moment, but she had to suppress her emotions because Zu An seemed to have the ability to detect someone’s anger. And yet, when she thought back about it now, she somehow no longer felt anger. The process had been sweet... and for some reason, her cultivation had advanced a fair bit. It was as if his load was a rare tonic in the world. I guess it isn’t a loss for me. Maybe I can find him again later for more...","She quickly shook her head to rid herself of inappropriate thoughts.","“What’s wrong?” Zu An asked, noticing her actions.","“It’s nothing.” The Saintess’ face was burning.","Zu An looked at her side profile under the sunlight. Her hair and skin were coated in golden radiance, highlighting her fair complexion and beautiful features. He gently hugged her and said, “Little sister Ling’er, you’re beautiful.”","The Saintess sensed that she no longer stiffened up when embraced by him, as if she had grown accustomed to it. “Am I more beautiful now, or was I more beautiful before?”","Zu An’s smile froze. Why do women like to ask such deadly questions?","“As long as it's you, you're always beautiful.”","“Tsk. What an insincere answer.” The Saintess rolled her eyes, but she didn’t ask any further. Instead, she was appalled that she'd asked such a meaningless question.","The two of them chatted while flying and avoiding aerial beasts. All of a sudden, however, a beam of light came from the surface.","“Be careful!” Zu An grabbed the Saintess and dodged the attack.","But that wasn't the end of it. Several bursts of bizarre, mysterious energy flew at them right after. The two of them dodged the attacks while descending on a nearby mountain. It was only then that they realized that the aggressors were six old men dressed in bizarre clothes.","“Who are you? Why did you attack us without reason?” the Saintess asked with a cold gaze. She had already brought out her High Firmament Talisman, and lightning crackled around her.","The old men wore colorful clothes made out of different bird feathers and beast skins stitched together. Their faces were obscured by bizarre golden masks, and giant necklaces made up of assorted bones hung around their necks. They didn’t look like as if would be easy to talk to.","“You can control lightning? Are you related to that person?” The bizarrely-dressed old men were astonished.","“Calm down, everyone. We know each other.” Zu An was delighted. He recognized the old men as some of the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans. He had met them the last time he came here, and they had even helped him.","“You know them?” The Saintess was taken aback.","Before Zu An could answer the question, a hot-tempered old man scoffed, “Who the hell are you? What do you mean we know each other?”","Zu An’s smile stiffened. He only now recalled that he had met them in the future, meaning they weren’t acquainted yet. He could only switch to another angle. “Are you the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans? I've heard a lot about you.”","The old men exchanged looks, but their faces remained cold. “You’re mistaken. We aren’t the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans.”","Zu An was startled. It was only after he took a closer look at the old men that he noticed some discrepancies. He smiled sheepishly and said, “Ah, I apologize for the misunderstanding, but you must be Wu Peng, and this must be Wu Di. I don’t think I've met the other four before.”","Astounded, one of the old men said, “We are indeed Wu Peng and Wu Di, but we don’t remember ever meeting you.”","Zu An was at a loss. He didn’t know how to explain to them that they were friends in the future, so he spent a moment in thought before replying, “I received a dream from an immortal about the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans...” He shared some details about the Spirit Mountain he saw in the future with them.","Wu Peng and Wu Di were dumbstruck. “There’s no way to lie about those details. To think there could be such a mystical dream in the world!”","The shamans lowered their hostility toward the two, and the Saintess stored away her High Firmament Talisman too.","Zu An took this chance to ask, “Why did you suddenly attack us earlier?”","The six shamans looked a little awkward. Instead of answering the question, they asked, “Why did you come here?”","Zu An suddenly remembered that the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans were skilled in medicine and had a broad knowledge of herbs. They might know where the Brilliant Pinflower is. “My little sister has a constitution that threatens her life, and we’re looking for a Brilliant Pinflower to save her. Do you by any chance know where I can find it?”","The six shamans exchanged glances as if communicating with one another. Some time later, Wu Peng said, “I know where the Brilliant Pinflower is.”","Zu An was overjoyed. “I’ll be grateful if you can tell me where it is.”","There was finally a lead after searching for so long!","Wu Peng grimly replied, “Don’t be too quick to thank us. The Brilliant Pinflower is a valuable, rare herb. We can’t give it to you for free. You’ll have to do us a favor first.”","Zu An wasn’t surprised. Even though he was friends with the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans in the future, in this time, they had only just met. He had dispelled their doubt, but that didn’t mean they would be willing to share such a valuable herb with him. Thus, he asked, “May I know what you need my help with?”","Instead of answering the question, Wu Peng said, “You should think it through. You won’t be able to turn down our request once you hear it. We can’t risk our secret getting out.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He knew too little about this world to guess what they needed his help with. He didn’t dare to accept their request recklessly in case it was too convoluted or dangerous. It would be terrible if he got embroiled in a fight between major powers.","The Saintess gently spoke up. “Big brother Zu, it’s worth taking this risk to save little sister Xiaoxi.”","Zu An thought that made sense. If they failed to find the Brilliant Pinflower, Xiaoxi would be a goner. He let out a sigh as he pointed out, “It’s just that I’ll be putting you in danger too.”","The Saintess chuckled. “What are you saying, big brother Zu? We have been through so much together. I’ll be with you no matter what happens.”","Zu An was moved. He grabbed her hand before turning to Wu Peng. “All right, we agree.”","Wu Peng nodded. “I’ll need you to draw away some guards for us. There’ll be some danger, but with the skills you showedearlier, you should be fine as long as you’re careful.”","Zu An and the Saintess exchanged looks and saw the worry in each other’s eyes. “May I know which guards you are referring to?”","Wu Peng pointed to a nearby mountain. His expression looked tense. “They're from Shushu Mountain!”"]},{"number":2563,"title":"Chapter 2563: Chapter 2515: Celestials","paragraphs":["“Shushu Mountain?” The Saintess’ eyes narrowed, but she quickly lowered her head to conceal her reaction. However, her hands remained firmly clenched. I still arrived late in the end...","Zu An found that name familiar, but he couldn’t remember where he'd heard it. So, he asked, “What kind of place is that? Who are the guards? How strong are they?”","Wu Peng pointed to a nearby mountain, “The mountain five kilometers away from us is Shushu Mountain. Most of the guards are snakes. They aren’t too powerful, so you should be able to handle them. The other guards, however, are more powerful. There is a bat, a fire boar, and a swallow lady. The swallow lady is the strongest, so you must be careful of her...”","The more Zu An listened to their intelligence, the stranger he felt it to be. “It sounds no different from delivering my head to them on a silver platter.”","Wu Di replied, “We’re not asking you to fight them. You just have to cause a commotion to draw their attention while staying safe. You can run if things get dangerous.”","The Saintess spoke up, asking, “What will you do while we distract them?”","Wu Peng shook his head. “We can’t tell you. However, you can be assured that we are not planning to do anything evil.”","The Saintess sneered, “Look, we are in a cooperative relationship now. Your refusal to share intelligence with us puts us at a disadvantage. We’ll still do our part even if you tell us nothing, but we will have to tread more carefully to compensate for it. We might end up not attracting enough attention to help you with what you seek to achieve.”","Zu An was impressed. Little sister Ling’er has grown from the sheltered young miss she used to be. This must be a skill she's honed in the years she spent as the Fiend races’ Saintess.","Wu Peng and Wu Di were taken aback. They were worried that Zu An and the Saintess wouldn’t pull their weight. In the end, they decided to speak up. “All right, we’ll tell you the truth. We’re hoping to take advantage of the chaos to steal a corpse from Shushu Mountain. Shushu Mountain’s master is extremely powerful. It’s unlikely that you’ll be able to draw his attention, but you should take this with you in case you catch his notice. You’ll at least still have a chance to survive.”","They tossed over a massive tortoise shell carved with mysterious marks.","Zu An was taken aback. “Is Shushu Mountain’s master someone who can take our lives with just a gaze?”","He had encountered such entities before. That kind of gap in strength was impossible to bridge. If that were the case, he would rather break his promise and fight with these six shamans than march to his death.","“Not to that extent,” Wu Peng explained. “Shushu Mountain’s master is Er Fu, a celestial with a human head and snake body. While he is powerful, he is incapable of taking someone’s life with a gaze. With the tortoise shell’s protection, you should be fine. Also, the odds of you catching his attention are extremely low.”","“A celestial!” Zu An shuddered. This could be his chance to meet a deity.","It finally dawned on him why the name ‘Shushu Mountain’ sounded so familiar. He had heard it from the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans the last time he was here. Back then, he'd encountered a monster named Yayu in the Weak Water. It turned out that Yayu had once been a celestial and was Er Fu’s brother, but Er Fu was jealous of his prestige. To make things worse, Er Fu’s subordinate had sown seeds of discord between the two. In the end, Er Fu killed Yayu.","Later, the Celestial Emperor had tasked someone to deliver an immortal medicine to revive Yayu. The medicine had brought Yayu back to life, but it hadn't brought back his soul. As a result, Yayu devolved into a mindless beast. Later, he'd fallen into the Weak Water and turned into a dragon-headed monster who feasted on mortals. These shamans were likely planning to steal Yayu’s corpse.","When he first heard about it, Zu An had found it lamentable, but he hadn’t expected to one day be involved in it. To think that he would be dragged into such a huge scheme! He was beginning to regret accepting the offer.","The Saintess read his mind and said, “This matter concerns a celestial; it is far beyond our means to deal with it. We won’t do it.”","The hot-tempered shaman roared, “Now that you know our secret, you have to go whether you like it or not. The only other option is for you to die!”","Before addressing Zu An and the Saintess, Wu Peng stopped the hot-tempered shaman with a raise of his hand. “You are mortals, right? I understand your fear of celestials, but you don’t have to put them on a pedestal. They are merely stronger entities. Given the strength you have displayed, you aren’t powerless against them. Still, we won’t make things difficult for you if you are truly intimidated. All we ask is that you keep this matter a secret.”","Zu An and the Saintess exchanged doubtful looks. The other party was being suspiciously nice.","Just then, Wu Peng added, “Ah, I forgot to tell you that I am the only one in the world who knows where the Brilliant Pinflower is. You might never find it if you miss this opportunity.”","Zu An was speechless. I bet this fellow’s heart is black through and through.","The Saintess sent a telepathic message to Zu An, “Big brother Zu, why don’t we give it a try? This might be little sister Xiaoxi’s only hope.”","Zu An nodded. He was thinking of giving it a try too, not just to obtain the Brilliant Pinflower, but also to meet the celestial named Er Fu. He also wanted to understand the difference between a mortal and a deity. Through that, he could figure out how mortals could transcend their limits to become deities.","“Alright. Does the celestial named Er Fu have any skills I should take note of?” Zu An decided not to tell the shamans that he knew about the story between Er Fu and Yayu. He could tell that these shamans weren’t kind, innocent beings. It would be wise to be careful around them.","Wu Peng was delighted to see Zu An accepting their request. “You need to be wary of his incredible speed. He is known to be the fastest creature in the world.”","Zu An was speechless. Fuck. How can I escape from him if he’s the fastest in the world?","Having guessed Zu An’s thought, Wu Peng consoled him. “That tortoise shell can block an attack from Er Fu. You can use that opportunity to escape. The moment we steal the corpse, he will sense it and pursue us instead. That will free you from danger. I’m not saying that there is no risk, but it’s up to you whether you think it is worth taking it on or not.”","“Very well, we’ll accept your request,” Zu An said. “But how can I trust you to tell us the Brilliant Pinflower’s whereabouts once we accomplish our mission?”"]},{"number":2564,"title":"Chapter 2564: Chapter 2516: Palace","paragraphs":["Wu Peng puffed up his chest and proudly declared, “We, the Kaiming Six Shamans, have at least this bit of credibility. You should know that from the dream you received from the immortal.”","Zu An thought about how they had kept their promise in the future, so he decided to trust them. But what are the Kaiming Six Shamans? Aren’t they the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans? So, he took this opportunity to ask about it.","Wu Peng and Wu Di exchanged looks before explaining, “Someone once put our names with eight other great shamans and called us the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans, but that title is merely an acknowledgment of our standing. Instead, we are closer to these friends. We share the same interests and values, and we often gather in the east of Kaiming. Over time, the world began to call us the Kaiming Six Shamans.”","He introduced the other four shamans—they were Wu Yang, Wu Lu, Wu Fan, and Wu Xiang. The hot-tempered one was Wu Yang.","Zu An widened his eyes in realization. I guess it’s similar to North Qiao Feng South Murong. Those two don’t hang out even though their names are mentioned together. Looks like Wu Peng and Wu Di are only friends with these four.","They quickly settled the details before Zu An and the Saintess made their way to the Shushu Mountain ahead of the Kaiming Six Shamans.","As expected of the ki-rich ancient era. Even the mountains here are far taller than in the future, Zu An thought as he looked at the massive mountain before him.","“Big brother Zu, is there a chance the shamans are lying to us?” the Saintess asked softly.","Zu An shook his head. “I met them when I came to this world in the future. On the whole, they are still trustworthy people. I heard about this incident too.” He told the Saintess about how Yayu was killed by Er Fu and turned into a monster.","“Isn’t it meaningless if he eventually turns into a monster?” The Saintess was confused.","Zu An smiled. “We’re just doing our best to ensure that history corresponds to the future to minimize its influence on us. Besides, it's a chance for us to find the Brilliant Pinflower and meet a deity. All these things have meaning.”","“Big brother Zu, will everything unfold as it did in the future, no matter what we do?” the Saintess asked with a pale face.","Zu An didn’t think deeply about that question. The same thought had occurred to him before, and it made him feel pessimistic and powerless. “It’s impossible to change major events, but it’s possible to change the details of how things unfold. For instance, there's plenty of room to maneuver unrecorded history...” He shared what he had previously heard from Mi Li with her.","The Saintess’ eyes glowed with spirit. “Big brother Zu, your interpretation has opened my mind. Thank you.”","“What’s there to thank me for?” Zu An thought she was making a big deal out of nothing. Given their relationship, there was no need for thanks between them.","They began secretly scaling the mountain. To their surprise, the place wasn’t tightly guarded. There were very few sentries and patrols. They only encountered some snake monsters now and then, although the latter more closely resembled lizard-people. It didn’t feel as if they were guarding the mountain; rather, they felt native to the mountain. As long as they were avoided, there would be no danger in scaling the mountain.","Zu An and the Saintess soon arrived at the mountain peak, where they saw a majestic palace. Along the path leading to it were sculptures and pillars with bizarre snakes carved into them. It looked eerie.","If Yu Yanluo were here, could she play the kin card with Er Fu?","In terms of height and area, this palace was far larger than the Cultivation World’s palaces. Only the structures Zu An had seen in the Monster World’s underground city could compete with it.","Its master must have a huge physique to live in such a huge palace.","In most worlds, there was a correlation between strength and size.","Zu An’s expression turned grim. He could already sense faint pressure despite not having entered the palace yet. So, he constructed several teleportation formations out of precaution. He wasn’t about to entrust everything to the tortoise shell.","The security around the palace was much tighter than on the outskirts of the mountain. It looked as if even the reptilians feared this place, as there wasn't a single one within a three kilometer radius. Eight brawny guards stood at the palace entrance. From time to time, armed snake guards patrolled the square in front of the palace gates. It seemed impossible to approach the gates in such an open space, let alone to infiltrate the area.","“Should we cause a commotion here and retreat?” the Saintess proposed. That was their agreement with the Kaiming Six Shamans.","Zu An shook his head. He didn’t want to miss this good opportunity to see a deity in action. He didn’t want the Saintess to risk her life with him, so he said, “Stay here to cover me. I’ll go take a look.”","But the Saintess rejected his proposal. “No, I’m coming with you. It’s too dangerous for you to go alone. I’m not going to part ways with you here.”","Upon hearing her words, Zu An hesitated. He thought about the many teleportation formations they had prepared beforehand and eventually agreed to take her along. He summoned Daji and had her play her pipa not too far away from the square.","The Saintess' eyes widened in shock. She hadn’t thought that Zu An could summon a person out of thin air, not to mention one so beautiful.","Daji followed Zu An’s instructions, and soon, a melodious tune drifted into the square. Zu An wasn’t planning to have her control the guards with her ‘Voice of the Devil’, however. These guards were stronger than Daji; she couldn't control any of them.","Nevertheless, the guards patrolling the square were drawn to the melodious tune and marched over to take a look. Even the guards at the entrance glanced over as well. They were mesmerized by Daji at first sight.","Beauty transcended race. Zu An noticed that even among the Fiend races, the Ocean races, or the monsters, they had a tendency to morph into humans, and they found the human physique beautiful. The guards couldn’t resist someone as beautiful as Daji.","While the guards were distracted, Zu An grabbed the Saintess and dashed through the palace gates with Grandgale. With a few instantaneous movements, he breached the palace defense and entered the premises.","The Saintess stepped away from his embrace to tidy up her hair, using this chance to conceal her furious blush. “Won’t the lady outside be in danger?”","“It isn’t a problem,” Zu An replied with a smile. He recalled Daji back into his mysterious space.","The guards outside were on the verge of catching Daji when she suddenly vanished into thin air. That caused a huge commotion.","The Saintess’ astonishment deepened. He’s not particularly strong, but he has all kinds of rare abilities.","Zu An scouted the path while making a beeline toward the palace depths. To avoid getting noticed, he used the Unshakable Daoist Manual’s ki concealment ability and plastered several concealment talismans on both of them.","Soon, they arrived at a hall and saw a massive silhouette swimming inside.","Indeed, the being within was swimming. His incomparably thick snake body moved between tall pillars, but his head was human. In the center of his forehead, he had a yellowish-brown mark that resembled an eye. He gave off a dignified yet solemn air.","He was staring at a stone platform at the center of the hall, where another snake body lay. However, the latter was completely stiff—it was a corpse."]},{"number":2565,"title":"Chapter 2565: Chapter 2517: Divine Halo","paragraphs":["Zu An figured that they had to be Er Fu and the deceased Yayu. But why did Er Fu leave his brother’s corpse here after killing him?","He gently grabbed the Saintess’ hand, worried the latter would be intimidated by a massive snake body paired with a human head. It was a sight that could swiftly erode one’s sanity. But to his surprise, the Saintess’ hand was warm. She wasn’t afraid in the slightest.","The snake body coiled around the pillars moved slowly as a human head bent down from the ceiling to examine the corpse lying on the stone platform. There was an irrepressible smile beaming on his face. He murmured obscure, ancient-sounding words. Fortunately, Zu An had been to this world, so he could comprehend 70% to 80% of the words.","“Yes, you’re so noble and incredible. Our father likes you. The other celestials like you. The shamans and the people like you. Everyone likes you. What about it? Aren’t you still a cold corpse now?”","Frenzied laughter followed. Afterward, however, Er Fu’s face suddenly darkened. “Don’t blame me. You were asking for it. Why did you have to compete with me over everything? Our parents’ love when we were younger, and later other people’s love too.","“They could compliment you, but why did they have to compare us? The kinder and more virtuous you were, the more despicable and detestable I looked! My dumb little brother, didn’t you know those compliments would come at a price? It was those compliments that led you to your death!”","...","Zu An frowned. He'd wanted to experience a deity's divinity close up, but what he got instead was a mentally warped monster. He was greatly disappointed.","Just then, a woman’s voice echoed, “Congratulations, master. You have finally gotten rid of your greatest threat.”","Only then did Zu An notice a skinny woman standing by the corner. Er Fu’s massive body was so visually striking that he'd failed to notice the much smaller woman right away. Zu An looked over and was flabbergasted.","The woman wore a white inner garment with a black robe reminiscent of a dress over it. The black-and-white coordination accentuated her curves. If it had been placed on the internet in Zu An's previous world, the netizens would comment that with such a beautiful figure, it would be fine even if they didn’t look at the face.","But her face was indeed a problem, as she didn’t have a human head. She was literally a birdbrain!","No wonder the monsters believe they're the descendants of the Celestial race. I can see the resemblance. Given her swallow-like head, I bet she must be the legendary Wei Yueyan.","In the future, when the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans told him about Yayu’s death, they'd mentioned something about Er Fu being manipulated by his subordinate, Wei. This birdbrained woman seemed to be that same Wei.","Er Fu’s cold voice boomed in the hall. “My brother is dead. What is there to congratulate?”","The birdbrain woman’s expression stiffened. What shamelessness! He wants to pretend to be a paragon of virtue despite having killed his brother?","Of course, she didn’t dare to express those thoughts aloud. She mustered her courage and replied, “Yayu deserved his plight for provoking master in all sorts of ways. Now that he’s dead, there is no one to steal faith from master anymore. That is something worth congratulating.”","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up. Faith? Sounds like faith is important to celestials.","His heartbeat hastened slightly, but that unfortunately caught Er Fu’s attention. The latter raised his massive head and looked over. “Who is it?”","Zu An was alarmed. He immediately tried to leave with the Saintess, but much to his astonishment, a tremendous burst of energy suddenly appeared before him. He hadn’t seen any traces of Er Fu making a move! It was as if the attack had just suddenly manifested around him. It was beyond comprehension!","Despite being on his guard, he couldn’t protect himself from the attack. The terrifying energy was already on the verge of striking him. All he could do in the spur of the moment was to drag the Saintess behind him and gather his ki to tank the attack, but he wasn’t sure if he could endure an attack from a deity.","Just then, a sliver of light shone. A massive tortoise shell suddenly appeared in front of him, shielding him. It was the shell he had received from Wu Peng!","Kacha!","The tortoise shell shattered into dust, but it also neutralized half of the terrifying attack. That bought enough time for Zu An to react. He grabbed the Saintess and performed instantaneous movements to flee outside.","The earlier clash couldn’t have made it clearer that Er Fu was far stronger than Zu An. Even the Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord at their peak wouldn’t have been a match for him!","Even though Zu An hadn't experienced a deity’s divinity, he had most definitely experienced a deity’s terrifying prowess.","“The familiar yet hateful aura of the shamans.” Er Fu’s expression turned cold. “Take down the intruder.” It was beneath him, a celestial, to personally make a move.","“Yes!” The birdbrained woman bowed. She gently leaped off the ground and transformed into a delicate swallow. Despite her small size, she was as fast as lightning.","Zu An used Grandgale consecutively to escape. Mo Xi’s Celestial Jade Palace skill reduced the cooldown time of his instantaneous movements, but it wasn't omnipotent. While his skill was on cooldown, he was shocked to see a swallow appear on his back. Having heard of Wei Yueyan’s name, he didn’t dare to underestimate her.","The swallow swooped in front of the two of them and transformed back into that bird-headed, human-bodied woman. She sized up the two of them with surprised eyes. “Hm, two mortals? Are you here to seek death? Come with me to meet my master.”","Zu An smiled. “What if I say no?”","Wei Yueyan’s lips curled in disdain. “You must be confident in yourself to dare intrude on this place. I can tell you’re different from other weak mortals, but you are completely oblivious to the gap between a mortal and a celestial!”","She released a burst of intertwined black and white light.","Zu An was alarmed. He didn't know the fundamental difference between a mortal and a celestial, but his danger instinct was tingling. He'd intended to make a preemptive move, but he couldn’t possibly be faster than light.","As the black and white light shone on him, he felt his body becoming heavy as if he was submerged into a viscous marsh. Not only was moving difficult, but even breathing became hard. He murmured, “Domain?”","Wei Yueyan scoffed, “Is that the limit of your comprehension? How can a divine halo be something as lowly as a domain?” She casually waved her wide sleeve, flicking it toward Zu An and the Saintess. She was planning to capture them alive and bring them to her master.","However, in the next second, she froze up. To her astonishment, the other party had somehow regained his ability to move and dodged her sleeve. “How is that possible?”","Then, her face twisted. “The Taotie’s ability!”"]},{"number":2566,"title":"Chapter 2566: Chapter 2518: Ritual","paragraphs":["Zu An was taken aback. He had used the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra—it was inspired by his fight with the Shadow Monster King in the Sealed Land. The Shadow Monster King had also been shrouded in light, and had warped the space around himself. Back then, Zu An was able to unravel the warped space with the Heaven-Devouring Sutra.","Wei Yueyan’s divine light reminded him of that experience, which was why he'd tried using the Heaven-Devouring Sutra, turning his body into a black hole to absorb the surrounding energy. Much to his surprise, he successfully overcame the divine light.","It wasn't the first time someone recognized the Taotie’s power. Their words also suggested that the Taotie they spoke about was different from the little Taotie monsters he had previously met in the Yinxu secret dungeon.","I wonder if I’ll meet the real Taotie one day.","Wei Yueyan snapped out of her daze and said, “You have tricks, but you can’t escape death.”","Not daring to let her guard down anymore, she went all-out and morphed into a black bolt of lightning. Her sharp wings turned the surroundings into a lethal trap, performing thousands of cuts within the blink of an eye. She didn’t think that anyone could escape unscathed from her concentrated attacks.","However, her smile soon stiffened. To her shock, Zu An and the Saintess had disappeared into thin air.","“A teleportation formation?” Despite being Er Fu’s subordinate, she was still a deity; she could sense a disturbance in the surrounding spatial ki.","With a sneer, she slipped into a spatial crack and soon arrived in a room. However, Zu An and the Saintess were still nowhere to be seen.","“They prepared multiple teleportation formations? You’re too naive if you think you can shake me off like that!”","She slipped into the cracks of space once more and performed ten consecutive teleportations, stopping by forests, cliffs, and quarries along the way. The final teleportation brought her back to the room she'd reached in her first teleportation.","Her face finally darkened. It was now clear to her that the other party had tampered with the spatial ki disturbance to mislead her, leaving behind a fake trail of teleportations to render her effort useless. Chances were that those two had already fled in the meantime.","A terrifying pressure suddenly bore down on Wei Yueyan.","Er Fu’s massive snake body appeared on the room’s ceiling. He lowered his human head and said, “You seem to have lost the targets.”","Wei Yueyan anxiously half-kneeled on the ground and said, “Forgive me, master. The intruders were too cunning. Their grasp of the spatial laws surpasses that of ordinary people.”","“You have disappointed me.” Er Fu’s eyes turned cold.","Wei Yueyan shuddered in fear. Goosebumps rose all over her body as Er Fu slowly approached her with a widened mouth. She trembled in fear, but she didn’t dare to avoid her master.","All of a sudden, Er Fu raised his massive head and looked back at the hall. “How dare you!”","His massive snake body abruptly vanished into thin air. Shortly after, furious roars came from the distance as terrifying ki pulsations rippled from the palace at the mountain peak.","Zu An and the Saintess observed the commotion from a tree outside the palace.","“It’s a huge relief that little sister Ling’er reminded me to set up that trap in our teleportation formations, or else she would have caught up with us,” Zu An remarked in awe. The Saintess’ grasp of spatial formations seemed to be above his.","The Saintess smiled shyly. “I just thought that deities could have the ability to slip through space, so it would be good to prepare countermeasures. I didn’t expect it to be of use either.”","She didn’t want to dwell on this topic, so she naturally diverted the conversation toward the ongoing battle in the palace. “Big brother Zu, those shamans are stronger than I thought.”","“Indeed, they are stronger than I thought,” Zu An said with a frown. His brief encounter with Er Fu had left a deep impression on him, so he was surprised that the Kaiming Six Shamans could fight the latter on equal grounds.","“It doesn’t seem as if there’s anything different about deities other than them being stronger than mortals,” the Saintess said.","Zu An shook his head. “No, that’s not right. I didn’t see Er Fu move when he attacked us earlier. It’s as if he can control the surrounding ki with his will. I'm familiar with that feeling. I could do the same in the Cultivation World when I had the World Law Beacon.”","The Saintess was taken aback. “Does Er Fu have this world’s World’s Law Beacon?”","Looking at her nervous face, Zu An chuckled. “I don’t think so. If he had this world’s World Law Beacon, we would have been long dead, and he wouldn’t have had to murder his little brother out of envy either.","“I think deities have the ability to freely control ki within a set radius. It’s not as powerful as the World Law Beacon, which can control an entire world’s ki and will. However, this world is far stronger than the Cultivation World, so even utilizing a small portion of its ki can make one very powerful.”","“No wonder he exerted such terrifying pressure,” the Saintess murmured contemplatively. “What else did you figure out?”","“Deities also have an ability known as divine halo,” Zu An deduced. “Now that I think about it, there were iridescent lights when the Celestial Court bestowed me with the Sun Slaying Bow the last time I was here. I thought it was just a special effect, but it might have been a divine halo.","“Wei Yueyan isn't a strong deity; that’s why her divine halo is only black and white. I’m not sure if I could have broken free if it had been a stronger deity with an iridescent divine halo.”","The Saintess lowered her gaze in contemplation.","Zu An continued, “Aside from those two factors, I think faith is also very important to deities. It may directly determine their fighting prowess.”","The Saintess looked at him with conflicted eyes. He’s formidable, to be able to deduce so much despite the brief encounter.","“Let’s go. It looks like the Kaiming Six Shamans have succeeded,” Zu An said. The fighting in the palace had died down, leaving Er Fu to rage alone.","He and the Saintess made their way to the meeting spot with the Kaiming Six Shamans and found them surrounding a stone platform. A human-faced, snake-bodied corpse had been placed on the platform.","The six shamans murmured an obscure chant, and blue lights began glowing from the formation beneath their feet. The blue lights converged on the stone platform, causing the corpse to glow with a faint light. The surroundings were suffused with tremendous life force.","Zu An wanted to walk over and ask about the Brilliant Pinflower, but the Saintess stopped him. “They are conducting an important resurrection ritual. You mustn’t interrupt them now, or else they might blame it on you.”","Zu An looked at the formation and sighed. “They won’t succeed.”"]},{"number":2567,"title":"Chapter 2567: Chapter 2519: Searching For Her a Thousand Times in the Crowd","paragraphs":["“Why?” the Saintess anxiously asked.","Zu An glanced at her in surprise. Why is she so concerned? “I once used an immortal medicine to save Honglei. Aside from the immortal medicine, you have to find the person’s soul as well. Neither can be missing in the equation.”","“You seem to have deep ties with the underworld. Is there a way to find someone’s soul?” the Saintess asked.","Zu An shook his head. “I’ve checked. For some reason, the netherworld doesn’t exist in this world.”","The Saintess widened her eyes. She seemed to have thought of something and decided not to probe further.","Zu An continued, “In the absence of the netherworld, deceased souls wander the world aimlessly without anywhere to go. Some dissipate swiftly, and some morph into vengeful spirits. It’s nigh impossible to find Yayu’s soul.”","While they were talking, the Kaiming Six Shamans had already concluded their ritual.","Wu Di exclaimed in excitement, “He’s moving, he’s moving! The immortal medicine works!”","Zu An regretted not asking to see what their immortal medicine was. It hadn’t been easy for him to find a Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine in the future. It would be great if he could find another immortal medicine in this world.","The surrounding life force gushed into the corpse on the stone platform. The corpse’s hands and legs shook before it slowly opened its eyes.","“He has been revived!” The Kaiming Six Shamans cried tears of joy.","“Yayu, we have rescued you from Er Fu, and the Celestial Emperor was gracious enough to bestow an immortal medicine to you. That’s why we saved you.” The shortest shaman, Wu Fan, walked up to Yayu to explain the situation with a smile.","Yayu initially looked confused, but a vicious glint soon flashed through his eyes. Without any hesitation, he gobbled Wu Fan up whole, shocking everyone present.","The remaining Kaiming FIve Shamans quickly retreated. Their leader, Wu Peng, was enraged. “Yayu, what are you doing?”","Yayu clutched his head and groaned in pain. He was unable to speak at all.","In the meantime, Wu Peng and the others snapped out of their daze and rushed forward to rescue their comrade. They knew that Wu Fan was likely dead by now, but they had to at least give it a try.","However, the charge of the Kaiming Five Shamans alarmed Yayu. With a roar, he fled outside and disappeared in the blink of an eye.","Zu An and Saintess were dumbfounded. They quickly followed the Kaiming Five Shamans out.","It was a pity that Yayu was too fast, just like Er Fu. Much to the Kaiming Five Shamans' despair, they soon lost sight of their target.","“How did this happen?” Wu Peng murmured in disbelief.","The others were too shaken up to utter a word.","“Could the immortal medicine be fake?” the hot-tempered Wu Yang growled.","They had succeeded in reviving Yayu, but the latter had devolved from a gentle, compassionate deity into a vicious monster. They felt indignant and enraged to have lost their comrade like that.","Wu Peng shook his head. “That can’t be. It was a bestowment from the Celestial Emperor, and we inspected it. There’s no way to fake it.”","“Could the Celestial Emperor have tampered with the pill in a way that eludes our...” Wu Yang muttered.","Wu Peng interjected, “Watch your words!”","Wu Yang belatedly realized the outrageous words he had muttered.","Zu An took this opportunity to ask, “You've met the Celestial Emperor? May I ask what kind of deity he is?”","He had too little information about the Celestial Court. This was a good opportunity to gather some intelligence.","“The Celestial Emperor is the Celestial Emperor, the ruler of all deities.” Wu Peng didn’t look interested in this topic. “We have only seen the Celestial Emperor from afar, and we didn’t dare to raise our heads to look at him. We don’t know much about him either.”","“Didn’t you receive the immortal medicine from the Celestial Emperor?” Zu An was surprised. He'd thought that both sides would be close.","“How could we be qualified to meet the Celestial Emperor? We received the immortal medicine from Celestial Bao Jiang. He manages the Celestial Emperor’s immortal medicines.” Wu Peng replied with a shake of his head. He hadn’t recovered from his confusion, shock, and sorrow yet.","Looking at how crestfallen he was, Zu An explained, “Yayu didn’t intend to eat your comrade. His soul hasn’t returned yet. What you revived with the immortal medicine is an undead monster.”","“Soul...” Light slowly returned to Wu Peng’s eyes. “Yes, yes! That’s where we went wrong!”","But his excitement quickly deflated into sorrow, as he realized that everything they'd done was meaningless. Not only had they failed to save Yayu, they'd even lost a comrade in the process too.","The Saintess suddenly asked, “Do you know where we can find Bao Jiang?”","“Are you looking for immortal medicine? It’s useless. No one can obtain an immortal medicine without the Celestial Emperor’s permission.” Wu Peng shook his head. “However, the Brilliant Pinflower you asked about can be found on his Treasure Origin Mountain. We’ll uphold our promise even though we failed to save Yayu. We’re grateful for your help.”","Zu An was overjoyed to receive news about the Brilliant Pinflower.","“We should be bringing you there, but we’ll have to pursue Yayu. I’m afraid we can only point the location of Treasure Origin Mountain out for you...” Wu Peng took out a tortoiseshell and drew on it. “Here’s a map to Treasure Origin Mountain and a letter. Once he sees the letter, Bao Jiang will know you are my friend and will hand the Brilliant Pinflower to you.”","Zu An accepted the tortoiseshell. “Thank you, elder.”","Wu Peng waved his hand in disinterest. He wasn’t in the mood for pleasantries.","Zu An knew Wu Peng wouldn’t be in the mood to answer his questions, so he decided to head to Treasure Origin Mountain to obtain the Brilliant Pinflower first. The thought that he was going to obtain another material to save Ji Xiaoxi lifted his spirit.","“Big brother Zu, we should make haste,” the Saintess reminded him.","Zu An was taken aback. “Why?”","“Have you forgotten about the story you heard in the future? Bao Jiang, who manages the immortal medicine, was assassinated,” the Saintess replied grimly.","Zu An’s face darkened right away. He anxiously dragged the Saintess with him to Treasure Origin Mountain as fast as he could. It felt as if Wu Peng’s drawing was equipped with a navigation system; it persistently pointed in the direction they should head to reach their destination.","Zu An and the Saintess made no stops along the way. They continued to fly full speed ahead, occasionally popping a pill into their mouths to replenish their stamina and ki. Fortunately, Treasure Origin Mountain was only around 500,000 kilometers away. Had it been any further, they would have had to travel via teleportation formation.","After days of travel, Zu An and the Saintess arrived at Treasure Origin Mountain. It was extremely near Spirit Mountain, which he had visited the last time he was here; but he was in no mood to check if his old friends, the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans, were around.","He made his way to a cave and shouted, “I have come to seek an audience with Deity Bao Jiang under the guidance of the Kaiming Six Shamans.”","“The Kaiming Six Shamans?” a seductive voice echoed from the cave.","Zu An and the Saintess were taken aback. Is Deity Bao Jiang a woman?","A woman slowly made her way out of the cave. Her sentimental peach blossom eyes, mesmerizing face, and curvaceous figure drew their eyes.","Zu An was delighted to see her. “Manman!”","He had been extremely worried about Pei Mianman in recent days, and his failure to find any clues about her had been causing his unease to reach its peak. Seeing her safe and sound made his heart burst with excitement, and he leaped forward to embrace her."]},{"number":2568,"title":"Chapter 2568: Chapter 2520: Goddess","paragraphs":["When she saw the woman’s face, the Saintess’ face twisted in shock. She opened her mouth several times, but no words came out.","A terrifying aura suddenly burst forth from the woman. “How dare you!”","Zu An was jolted a great distance back.","The woman’s hair and robes fluttered as her body emitted an iridescent light. With a reddened face, she glared furiously at Zu An.","Zu An was taken aback too. He hadn’t expected Pei Mianman to be so vehemently opposed to his embrace. What’s going on?","You have trolled Yaoji for +999... +999... +999...","Who is this Yaoji?","Zu An stared confusedly at the woman in front of him. With those portrait-like eyebrows, an enchanting face, and that distinctive talent, who else could she be if not Pei Mianman?","The Saintess noticed that the woman was exploiting Zu An’s daze to channel a huge move, so she quickly raised her hands to stop them. “Big sister Pei, why are you so angry? Big brother Zu merely got too excited after not having seen you for such a long time.”","The woman was taken aback. “Big sister Pei?”","The Saintess quickly replied, “That’s right, big sister Pei. Big brother Zu has been searching all over for you, from the resistance army camp to the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb. He even risked his life to fight with the Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord for you!”","“The Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb? The Lord of Slaughter and the Monster Lord?” The woman frowned. The killing intent in her eyes faded a little.","“What’s wrong, Manman?” Zu An could fathom a guess about the situation, but he would rather believe that Pei Mianman was suffering from amnesia.","The woman’s face turned cold, and her killing intent flared again.","The Saintess glared at Zu An as she quickly explained, “We came here under the Kaiming Six Shamans' guidance to seek an audience with Deity Bao Jiang to obtain a Brilliant Pinflower to treat little sister Xiaoxi. You went missing searching for this flower. I didn’t expect we would be reunited here. How did you get here?”","She spoke quickly but clearly, concisely revealing their relationship with Pei Mianman while highlighting their relationship with the Kaiming Six Shamans.","The beautiful woman could roughly figure out what was going on, and she coldly replied, “I’m not your big sister Pei or Manman or whatever. You got the wrong person.”","Zu An was stunned. His mind went blank when his suspicions were confirmed. How could two people in the world look so identical?","But he quickly recalled the Mermaid Queen and the Peacock Princess; they were identical to the future Shang Liuyu and Kong Nanwu. From that angle, it wasn’t impossible for someone to resemble Pei Mianman too. However, losing another lead to Pei Mianman’s whereabouts made Zu An uneasy.","The Saintess had thought as much, but she feigned astonishment and exclaimed, “You aren’t big sister Pei? How is that possible? There’s no way we would fail to recognize her!”","The woman lost her patience. “You have the wrong person. But what are these Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb, Lord of Slaughter, and Monster Lord? Why have I never heard about them before?”","Upon hearing that she didn’t know about those things, Zu An had no choice but to give up. “It seems we indeed had the wrong person. I apologize for my earlier discourtesy.”","His earnest attitude placated the beautiful woman’s anger. In truth, she was perplexed too. Given her temperament, she wouldn’t have hesitated to kill any men who dared to suddenly embrace her. But for some reason, she felt no killing intent toward him despite her anger. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have held back even with the Saintess’ intervention. It was weird how she felt intimate toward him despite having never met him before.","“May I know if you are Deity Bao Jiang?” the Saintess asked.","The beautiful woman shook her head. “I am not Bao Jiang. I am his neighbor, and I came here because I have business with him.”","“Neighbor?” Zu An looked at the neighboring spirit mountains and wondered where she resided.","“This is big brother Zu An, and I am Yumen Beiqing. May I ask what your name is?” Seeing that Zu An was in no state to socialize, the Saintess had to step up and gather more information.","The beautiful woman was hesitant to reveal her identity, but the inexplicable intimacy she felt toward Zu An made her relent. “You can call me Yaoji.”","“Yaoji?” The Saintess was surprised. “Are you the Flame Emperor’s little daughter, the Goddess of Wu Mountain?”","Zu An was taken aback. He finally remembered why that name sounded so familiar. The Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans had mentioned this neighbor of theirs the last time he was here, but he hadn’t expected the other party to bear such a striking resemblance to Pei Mianman.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at the Saintess. “You know me?”","Zu An was perplexed as well. Even he took time to recall this piece of information; it was puzzling how quickly little sister Ling’er reacted here.","“I have long heard about your legend. You are indeed as ethereal as others claim,” the Saintess threw a compliment over.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was unfazed, having heard many such compliments before. “You said the Kaiming Six Shamans sent you here. Do you have evidence of that?”","As soon as Zu An took out Wu Peng’s tortoiseshell, it abruptly flew into the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s hand. She said, “Yes, this is indeed Wu Peng’s aura. You must be trustworthy to have earned their recognition.”","The tortoiseshell floated back to Zu An. The light fragrance that lingered on it left him dazed. Is she really not Pei Mianman?","“You came at a bad time. He has already left,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said.","“He left? Toward where?!” the Saintess anxiously asked.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain calmly replied, “I was looking around and saw a note saying that he left. He must have reported back to the Celestial Court.”","“Am I still a step too late...” The Saintess fell into a daze. She looked as if someone had sapped her energy dry.","Zu An looked at her contemplatively before asking, “Goddess, is there a way to find him? There’s something I need his help with.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain impatiently replied, “Do you think you would be more important to him than the Celestial Emperor’s orders?”","Zu An detected disdain in her voice and explained, “He is in danger right now. He could die if we don’t get to him right away. Goddess, you must be his friend to freely wander around his cave. I’m sure you wouldn’t want anything to happen to him either.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. “What makes you say that?”"]},{"number":2569,"title":"Chapter 2569: Chapter 2521: Chance Encounter","paragraphs":["Instead of directly answering the question, Zu An asked, “Goddess, does anyone in the world know where to find immortal medicine as of late?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head. “Immortal medicines are supreme treasures. Many covet them but to no avail, as they are highly elusive.”","“Someone was fanning conflict between Er Fu and Yayu, prompting the former to kill the latter. Er Fu and Yayu are both deities, which makes that an extremely risky move where a misstep could result in eternal damnation. What could drive someone to take such a risk? Surely it couldn’t be because they have a personal vendetta against Yayu?”","Zu An chose not to reveal the final outcome of the matter. There was no way he could explain why he knew so much if the other party asked about it. Revealing that he was from the future in a world filled with deities could lead to unforeseen complications, so he decided to guide the other party’s train of thoughts with questions instead.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was no fool. She understood what Zu An was driving at and asked, “You think the person behind this wishes to make use of this opportunity to figure out the whereabouts of an immortal medicine?”","“That is the most likely possibility, now that Bao Jiang has left his cave to report to the Celestial Court. If the mastermind plans to make a move, now is the best time,” Zu An said.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was startled. She quickly took out a cloud-shaped mirror with a wave of her hand, and its surface rippled.","“I can’t reach him.” She stowed away the mirror with a grim expression.","Zu An figured that the mirror was something similar to the Cultivation World's recording mirrors.","“Do you know which path he took? Is there a chance we can still make it in time if we make haste?” he anxiously asked, thinking that this could be a good opportunity to gather some intelligence about the Celestial Court.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain paced around the room. Even the Saintess had to concede that she was a charming woman. “Deity Bao Jiang recently mentioned that he needed to harvest a special herb, which can be found on the way to the Celestial Court. It might be possible to catch up with him if you give chase now.”","Zu An was taken aback. “Goddess, aren’t you coming too?”","He instinctively felt close to her because of her striking resemblance to Pei Mianman, and he also wanted to see if she was related to Pei Mianman in any way. He was disappointed that she showed no inclination to travel with them.","“I can’t stray too far away from Wu Mountain,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain calmly replied without explaining too much.","Zu An could tell that the other party was reluctant to share more information, so he turned the topic back to Bao Jiang. “Which road should we take to find Deity Bao Jiang?”","This world was so huge that blindly looking for Bao Jiang would be even tougher than finding a needle on the ocean floor.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain swirled her finger in midair. Clouds gathered at her fingertip and formed a simple map. “Follow this map. You should be able to find him in the vicinity of Kunlun Mountain.”","“Kunlun Mountain?” Zu An glanced at the Saintess. Back then, the latter had suggested heading to Kunlun Mountain. Who would have thought that after so many twists and turns, they would still be heading there in the end?","“All routes to the Celestial Court pass through Kunlun Mountain,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain explained.","Zu An nodded in realization. No wonder Kunlun plays a significant role in so many folktales and legends.","He took this opportunity to ask more about the Celestial Court, but the Goddess of Wu Mountain's expression turned cold. “I don’t like that place, and I don’t want to talk about it.”","She flung her sleeves and left, leaving behind a graceful silhouette.","Zu An was stunned. Is she angry because of my earlier brash behavior?","The Saintess tugged his sleeves and said, “Stop looking. She’s already gone.”","Zu An replied with a sheepish smile, “Little sister Ling’er, is it possible for two people to look so identical in the world?”","“There are similar-looking people in the world, but for them to bear such great resemblance to each other...” The Saintess fell into deep thought. There’s only one possibility...","Worried that Zu An would continue probing, she changed the topic. “We should quickly head over. It’ll be terrible if we don’t make it in time.” She grabbed Zu An and headed out of the mountain.","Her urgency moved Zu An. Little sister Ling’er truly cares about Xiaoxi. She’s worried that we won’t be able to find the Brilliant Pinflower.","While they were leaving, a stone peak vaguely peeked out amid the fog. It slowly morphed into a woman with a fluttering skirt. If Zu An and the Saintess were here, they would be able to tell that she was none other than Yaoji.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at their departing silhouettes with a slight frown. “That’s weird...” She couldn’t understand why that strange man evoked a sense of familiarity in her. At the same time, she also detected an aura she didn’t like from the woman next to him.","As the fog drifted past, the woman’s silhouette slowly vanished before morphing back into a mountain peak.","While they were traveling, Zu An noticed a hint of exhaustion on the Saintess’ face and apologized, “I've burdened you, little sister Ling’er. We've been traveling without rest for the last few days.”","It was a hilarious situation. They had rushed to Treasure Origin Mountain, only to have to rush to Kunlun Mountain right after. As long as they were careful, the aerial monsters no longer posed a threat to them, but this world was so vast that even Zu An was starting to feel tired despite his cultivation.","The Saintess chuckled. “Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I can still hold on. We can’t lose time now, or else we might lose Bao JIang.”","Zu An nodded. “Yes, we need to hurry.” But worry filled his face right after as he continued, “Even so, we might not be able to make it in time with our current speed.”","Kunlun Mountain was still far away. It would be ideal to travel via a teleportation formation, but Zu An had never been there and didn’t know its terrain and coordinates, so he couldn’t construct a teleportation formation even if he wanted to.","“If only we had a mount...” The Saintess lowered her gaze. She looked conflicted.","Zu An took out the Crystal Boat he 'd gotten from the East Sea Dragon King. “This boat is slower than us, but we can recover our stamina while riding on it. Otherwise, we won’t have the strength to rescue Bao Jiang even if we arrive on time.”","The Saintess frowned. She found the Crystal Boat too slow, but she couldn’t find a pretext to refute him. In the end, she boarded the Crystal Boat with him and rested in a room.","Zu An took out a couple of pills for them to consume. While recuperating via meditation, he said, “There’s another matter I’m worried about. Judging from our encounter with Er Fu, the deities are extremely powerful. Even if we make it in time, will we be able to save Bao Jiang?”","The Saintess chuckled. “Big brother Zu, you’re thinking too much. Bao Jiang is a deity himself. Back then, he probably only died to his assailants because his guard was down. He should be able to survive the ordeal as long as we make it in time to warn him. Furthermore, he has the Celestial Emperor’s backing. I reckon the conspirators wouldn’t dare to go too far.”","Zu An was awed. “Little sister Ling’er, your analysis is spot-on. You've grown a lot over the years.”","The Saintess blushed. “I took big brother Zu’s teachings to heart and put them into practice.”","Zu An’s heart twinged at her coy appearance. He was about to touch her face when they heard a masculine voice outside asking, “Friends on that crystal boat, may I hitch a ride?”"]},{"number":2570,"title":"Chapter 2570: Chapter 2522: Celestial Heaven, Houtu","paragraphs":["Startled, Zu An and the Saintess made their way to the deck and saw a tall, muscular man flying not too far away. He wore a tigerskin cloth covering only half of his upper body, along with a pair of shorts. His thighs and arms bulged impressively. Despite his muscular stature, he didn’t seem heavy. Rather, his muscles seemed to be pulsating with explosive prowess.","Such a physique would win the reverence of the gym rats in my previous world.","Zu An quickly pulled himself together and apologized, “I’m sorry, but we're rushing to Kunlun Mountain. I’m afraid we can’t take you along.”","Had it been any other occasion, he would likely have invited the other party onto the Crystal Boat. This was a rare opportunity to interact with a native and gather intelligence. However, they were in a rush to rescue Bao Jiang, so they dared not lose any time.","Unexpectedly, the man laughed. “What a coincidence! I’m heading to Kunlun Mountain too. We’re going in the same direction, so I won’t hinder you.”","Zu An was conflicted.","The Saintess glanced at the man’s bow before sending a telepathic message to Zu An. “This man is strong and skilled at archery. If we offend him with our rejection, we might run the risk of him secretly sniping us with his arrow.”","Zu An nodded. “Since it’s convenient, please come aboard.”","As long as it didn’t hinder their journey, it didn’t matter whether they had an additional person or not. Anyway, this was a chance to interact and learn about this world. So, Zu An released the Crystal Boat’s defensive formation and allowed the man on.","The man flew onto the deck. “Thank you!” He examined the boat and remarked in awe, “This flying boat is exquisite. I sense a dragon’s aura. Are you two descendants of the Dragon race?”","Zu An was amazed by his keen discernment. “We aren’t from the Dragon race, though this boat is a gift from a dragon friend.”","He dared not reveal it was from the East Sea Dragon King, as he didn’t know if this world had the concept of the Four Dragon Kings or not.","The man nodded. “You must be an extraordinary person to receive such a valuable gift from the Ancient Dragon race.”","Zu An was stunned. Ancient Dragon race? And he appears to harbor great respect for the Dragon race too.","Such a remark would have been understandable if it happened in the future when the Dragon race was at the peak of its power. But it was hard to believe that the Dragon race still enjoyed such an exalted standing in this world filled with deities.","“How should I address you?” the Saintess suddenly asked.","The man clasped his fist and replied, “I am Yi from the Shaman races. How can I address the two of you?”","The Saintess and Zu An froze up.","Yi?","In Zu An’s previous life, this man's legend was extremely famous. The last time he came to this world, Zu An himself had simulated the other party’s heroic journey. Could this be the legendary man who shot down the nine suns?","“You can call me Necropolis. She is my girlfriend, Yumen,” Zu An introduced themselves.","“Girlfriend?” The man was initially confused, but he quickly picked up on the air of intimacy between them. “Ah, I get it. She’s your woman.”","The Saintess was speechless.","Seeing that the man had a candid personality, Zu An asked, “I see you're carrying a huge bow, so you must be proficient at archery, no?”","“I have learned it before,” the man replied with a smile in an unexpected show of humility.","Just as Zu An was wondering how he could verify the other party’s identity, the Saintess suddenly asked, “If I could ask, what do you intend to do at Kunlun?”","The man’s face reddened. “I am heading there to propose to a woman.”","“Propose to a woman?” Zu An and the Saintess exchanged looks. They hadn’t expected such an answer.","The man had no notable possession other than his bow. Even his clothes were tattered. It would be much more credible if he said he was heading to Kunlun to hunt instead.","Seeing the doubt in their eyes, the man laughed awkwardly. “I encountered a bunch of detestable fiends along the way and fought them. My comrades lost their lives, and the betrothal gifts I brought were destroyed in battle. Of course, the fiends didn’t have it any better. We massacred them all despite being outnumbered.”","Killing intent flared from the man as he recalled the situation back then.","“Fiends?” Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. This fellow seems stronger than I thought.","The man snapped out of his recollection and quickly reined in his aura. “It’s the bunch you mortals refer to as celestials.”","“Celestials!” Zu An was shocked. He hadn’t expected the celestials to be fiends. Did this mean the Celestial Court was filled with fiends too?","No wonder Mi Li mentioned the Celestial Court’s Fiend races! And this fellow just massacred a bunch of celestials?","He had no idea how strong those celestials were compared to Er Fu, but he had clearly underestimated the man’s strength.","“What sparked the fight?” the Saintess asked. As she assessed the man before her, she stayed a step behind Zu An.","“What other reason is there? We fought because we saw each other as an eyesore,” the man casually replied.","The Saintess seemed to understand that, but Zu An was shocked. “Is that it?”","“Of course.” The man was surprised by Zu An’s reaction. “The Shaman races and the Fiend races have fought for so many years that there is a deep-seated grudge between both sides. The relationship has become so convoluted that no one can untangle it anymore. So, we just come to blows whenever we see each other.”","“The war between the shamans and the fiends...” Zu An murmured. “Does the Celestial Emperor not intervene in this battle?”","“The Celestial Emperor is merely the Fiend races’ Celestial Emperor. He has no power over us.” The man harrumphed. “We shamans worship Lady Houtu. We formed a pact in the past, stating that one would govern the heavens, and the other would govern the earth. That reduced the conflict between our races, but if both sides encounter each other, a fight is still inevitable.”","Zu An was taken aback. He was starting to get a grip on this world’s power balance. It was fortunate that he'd met this fellow on the way. The latter had provided him with too much useful information, especially concerning Houtu. He'd had an idea of how powerful Houtu was, but he hadn't thought that it would be to the extent of opposing the Celestial Emperor.","I hope I haven’t offended her in any way.","“May I know which lady is fortunate enough to be your lover?” the Saintess suddenly asked.","The man’s face reddened in shyness. He raised his head toward the sky as his eyes gleamed expectantly. “She’s the Chang clan’s Saintess, as well as their most beautiful woman.”","Zu An gasped. “Is that Saintess Chang'e?”"]},{"number":2571,"title":"Chapter 2571: Chapter 2523: Chang’e","paragraphs":["Surprised, the man stared at Zu An with widened eyes. “How do you know?”","The Saintess also looked at Zu An with questioning eyes, perplexed by how he knew that name.","Zu An was stunned. It really is Chang’e. This man must be the legendary figure who shot down the suns.","Zu An’s lack of response caused the man to narrow his eyes dangerously. “Brother, are you after Chang’e as well?”","Sensing the other party’s growing hostility, Zu An snapped out of his thoughts and smiled. “You misunderstand! You mentioned that she’s the Chang clan’s most beautiful Saintess. Her name spreads far and wide. It’s only normal for me to have heard about her.”","“Is that so?” The man breathed a sigh of relief. He scratched his head and laughed. “I didn’t expect her to be this famous. To think you've heard of her despite not even knowing about the grudge between the shamans and the fiends.”","Zu An wiped away some cold sweat. “Haha, it’s a coincidence.” He took the opportunity to gather more details. “You two must be very close, for you to be proposing to her.”","The man looked at Zu An as if he was talking nonsense. “I haven’t even met her yet.”","It was Zu An’s turn to be dumbstruck. “You’re proposing to her despite having never met her?”","“Of course! The most beautiful woman should be with the strongest man!” the man declared as he flexed his bulging biceps. He turned to the Saintess and awkwardly added, “Your woman is beautiful too, but to me, the most beautiful woman is my future wife.”","The Saintess rolled her eyes. You might as well just stay quiet.","Zu An could relate to him, saying, “Brother, I can tell that you’re a sentimental person. I am in awe.”","That compliment brought a wide grin to the man’s face. Fueled by excitement, he began sharing his history with Chang’e. “Actually, it’s not as if we're completely unrelated. My clan elders have made an agreement with the Chang clan to betroth us to each other.”","“Ah, so it was an arranged marriage!” Zu An and the Saintess nodded in realization.","The man heaved a big sigh. “But shortly after we were betrothed, our clan encountered a disaster and suffered great casualties, resulting in our clan’s decline. I reached the age of marriage long ago, but I didn’t want my future wife to suffer any grievances, so I decided to make a name for myself before proposing to her. That way, her reputation wouldn’t be sullied.”","This reminded Zu An of a webnovel trope in his previous life—a destitute young man slowly rising through the ranks with his own capabilities, eventually reaching the top of the world.","The Saintess pointed out, “You must be famous then.”","The man patted his bow and proudly replied, “I dare say that if I proclaim myself second in the world at archery, no one will dare take the first spot.”","A gleam flickered across the Saintess’ eyes. “What a coincidence. My big brother happens to be skilled in archery too.”","That piqued the man’s interest. “Oh? What a coincidence! Brother Necropolis, where’s your bow? Shall we have a duel?”","Zu An glanced at the Saintess, surprised by her remark. Is it because she doesn’t want me to be overshadowed? But he was in no mood to have a duel when he had more important matters at hand. “She’s pulling your leg. I’m merely an amateur.”","The man frowned. “Your archery must be outstanding for her to say so. A man shouldn’t disappoint his woman. You don’t have to feel stressed. It’s just a friendly competition. Let’s keep things light-hearted, all right?” He casually gestured toward a flock of birds in the distance. “Those vultures are extremely cruel. They are fond of feasting on infants’ brain matter. Let’s shoot an arrow each and see who can shoot down more birds.”","It would be impolite to continue rejecting him now, so Zu An took out the Sun Slaying Bow. However, he immediately regretted his decision. He belatedly recalled that the man had a deep tie with the Sun Slaying Bow in history, having used it to shoot down the nine suns.","Upon seeing the red bow, the man’s eyes lit up out of enthusiasm. “What a wonderful bow!”","Zu An was worried that the man would covet the Sun Slaying Bow, but the latter was simply appreciating its craftsmanship. He heaved a sigh of relief and suggested, “Brother, why don’t you go first?”","The man frowned. “You’d be at a disadvantage if I went first. Why don’t you go first?”","Zu An smiled in embarrassment. “You’d be at a disadvantage if I went first too...”","“Then let’s go together.” The man laughed heartily. He nocked his arrow and released it like a shooting star.","The Saintess was dumbstruck.","The arrow pierced through a vulture’s eye before striking another, and another. It was baffling how the released arrow could twist and turn, catching up with the flustered vultures no matter where they fled to. In the blink of an eye, half of the vultures were already shot down.","It was then that Zu An’s arrow arrived. There was a brilliant flash of light, and all the remaining birds, be it near or far, were blasted to cinders.","The man was dumbstruck before bursting into laughter. “You shot down one more vulture than me. It’s your victory.”","Zu An shook his head. “Your archery skills are clearly superior to mine. I merely took advantage of this bow’s superior prowess.”","The man wasn’t bothered by that. “It’s also a skill to be able to acquire a good bow. Since that’s the case, why don’t we call it a draw?”","Zu An respected Yi’s hearty and magnanimous personality.","While the two men were bonding with each other, the Saintess lowered her gaze. Her face was pale, and her fists were clenched tightly in her sleeves.","Amid chatter, they finally arrived in the Chang clan’s vicinity. The man clasped his fist at Zu An and said, “Thank you for the ride. I've reached my destination. May we meet again.”","Zu An was curious to meet the legendary Chang’e, but he had more important matters at hand. Besides, he already considered Yi his friend now, and it wouldn’t do for him to steal his friend’s wife.","“Brother Yi, may you return home with your bride!” Zu An clasped his fist as he bade farewell.","“Hahaha! You can be sure that I’ll invite you to our wedding!” While embracing Zu An, the man took the opportunity to send a telepathic message over. “Be careful of your woman. She carries a fiend’s aura.”","Zu An was stunned. Before he could process what he had just heard, the other party had already leaped off the Crystal Boat with a hearty laugh, leaving behind a waving silhouette.","Zu An turned to the dazed Saintess. Yi has sharp eyes. He’s able to tell that little sister Ling’er is from the Fiend races.","Needless to say, Yumen Beiqing, as the Fiend races’ Saintess, was a fiend. It was inevitable for Yi, due to the war in this era, to harbor prejudice toward fiends.","“What did he say earlier?” the Saintess asked as she walked over.","“He wished us a blissful marriage,” Zu An replied with a smile. There was no need to trouble her with such trivialities.","The Saintess laughed awkwardly. Her face was slightly flushed, but her eyes were tinged with confusion and fear.","Meanwhile, the man made his way to the foot of the mountain, where a town lay. He was about to report his background when he noticed that the Chang clan was in chaos, searching for something. He grabbed a random passerby and asked, “What happened?”","“You...” The passerby was about to flare up when he sensed the man’s intimidating aura, so he obediently answered, “The Saintess had gone missing.”","“What?” The man was stunned. “Why would she suddenly go missing?”","The passerby replied, “I heard that the Saintess’ childhood fiancé is going to propose to her today. There are rumors he is three meters tall, his waist is three meters wide, and he devours ten cows each meal. How can our delicate Saintess marry such a brute? She must have fled to escape him.”","The man widened his eyes in disbelief. “What bullshit are you spouting?!”"]},{"number":2572,"title":"Chapter 2572: Chapter 2524: Someone Who Shouldn’t Be There","paragraphs":["“It’s not bullshit. Everyone is saying that!” the passerby exclaimed indignantly. However, he suddenly assessed Yi’s clothes and widened his eyes in fear. “Y-You can’t be...”","Yi had black streaks all over his face. “That’s right, I am your Saintess’ fiancé, the brute you speak of!”","The passerby felt a rush of awkwardness. “It’s all a misunderstanding, bro! That’s not what I meant.”","“Then what did you mean?” Yi replied with a livid face.","The passerby was speechless. Why are you asking when you know the truth?","Yi looked at the bustling town in the distance. “Did your Saintess really escape?”","The passerby replied with a strained smile, “Our Saintess is indeed missing, but it might not be because of you. There could be other reasons at play.”","Yi’s complexion looked terrible. He had come with a heart brimming with excitement, his head filled with the image of his gorgeous fiancée welcoming him with a shy smile. Who could have thought that she would be intimidated by him instead?","The commotion on their side caught other people’s attention. Many Chang clansmen thought he was a troublemaker and rushed over with weapons in hand.","Yi could only explain himself, but that only made the Chang clansmen’s eyes turn more hostile. Chang’e was adored by all the youths in the Chang clan, so they were already dissatisfied with her fiancé despite having never met him before. Who could have thought that the Saintess would disappear because of him? That further stoked their anger.","Fortunately, a Chang clan elder rushed over to defuse the situation and led him into the inner hall to explain the situation.","“What? The Golden Crow Third Crown Prince!” Yi was infuriated. He hadn’t expected there to be such a twist.","The elder took out a golden feather that was still crackling with flame. “That’s right. The Saintess’ sudden disappearance caught us off guard. Many nosey folks have been speculating about her disappearance, thus the rumors about her... escaping from her marriage. We were worried that the truth could lead to an irreconcilable conflict, so we didn’t clarify the rumors.”","Yi was both delighted and worried. He was glad that Chang’e hadn’t run away because she detested him, but at the same time, he was worried because her disappearance appeared to be related to the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince.","“We found this golden feather near the Saintess’ residence. He must have been here. Who knows what the Golden Crow race is plotting,” an elder muttered worriedly.","“What else could they be plotting? Those fiends are trying to undermine the bonds within our Shaman races!” Yi slammed his hand on the table and shot to his feet. “I shall rescue Chang’e from the clutches of the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince!”","Ignoring the elders’ shouts for them to think things through, Yi rushed outside. The thought of his fiancé being in the Fiend races’ clutches made him feel as if ants were gnawing at his heart.","If she loses even a strand of hair, I’ll go to the Scalding Valley [1] to settle the score with those Golden Crows!","...","After sending Yi off, Zu An continued maneuvering the Crystal Boat toward Kunlun Mountain. At the moment, he was in a room with Yumen Beiqing, discussing their analysis and speculations about Yi. However, Yumen Beiqing appeared to be distracted.","When Zu An asked her what was wrong, they suddenly heard a surprised exclamation outside. “Big brother Zu, is that you?”","Zu An’s body shuddered. He instantly teleported to the deck outside.","A beautiful woman floated in midair, looking as if she had emerged from the fog. Her appearance made the dim sky light up a fair bit. This woman could enchant anyone no matter how many times they saw her. Her curvaceous figure was wrapped in a sea-colored dress, and her fair skin glowed radiantly like the moonlight.","Zu An was both surprised and delighted to see her. He hadn’t expected to meet her here.","It was the Mermaid Queen, Gong Suyin!","“Big brother Zu, it really is you!” Her voice sounded a little hoarse. Unable to hold back her excitement, she leaped right into his arms.","Had it been in the past, Zu An would have avoided her. But sensing the intense feelings she harbored for him, he couldn’t bring himself to do that. He embraced her, and that made him realize that her body was trembling. “Yes, it’s me. You don’t have to be afraid.”","Yumen Beiqing arrived on the deck slightly later than Zu An. The first thing she saw was a ridiculously beautiful woman leaping into her lover’s arms as if their love transcended life and death. That made her feel a rush of jealousy. Where did this hussy come from?","That thought alarmed her. Why would I feel jealousy? Do I truly have feelings for this fellow? How is that possible?!","She quickly consoled herself. It’s normal to be angry if someone takes my toy away without my permission.","It was then that the Mermaid Queen noticed Yumen Beiqing and anxiously tore herself away from Zu An’s embrace. “Big brother Zu, she is...”","“She’s the Fiend races’ Saintess, whom you were full of praises for and have been wanting to meet, Yumen Beiqing.” Zu An figured that there was no point in saying too much, since she wouldn’t know Xie Daoyun. “Saintess, this is the Ocean races’ Mermaid Queen, Gong Suyin.”","“As expected of the Ocean races’ number one beauty. How gorgeous!” Yumen Beiqing remarked as she eyed the other party’s chest. She’s big. They're almost on par with mine.","“So you’re the Fiend races’ Saintess! I have heard a lot about you.” The Mermaid Queen was surprised too. She had heard a lot about this legendary woman and had been wanting to meet her, but who could have thought that they would meet under such circumstances?","Their exchange of pleasantries was a little awkward.","Yumen Beiqing could guess their relationship from their intimate embrace. This playboy! The last time I saw him, he had three gorgeous women with him. Now, he has yet another one here. And how can all of them be so beautiful?!","Despite only being in this world for a short time, he's already gotten together with even the famed Mermaid Queen. Is he an incubus?!","The Mermaid Queen was perplexed too. She could tell that something was going on between Zu An and the Fiend races’ Saintess—the intimacy between lovers was obvious.","Isn’t big brother Zu from the future? Why is he together with the Saintess? Was everything he told me before a lie? Does he not like me at all?","Her face darkened. The clouds gathered, as if lamenting alongside her.","“What brings you here?” That was the biggest question in Zu An’s mind. Given that they had entered this place via the Fiend races’ Imperial Tomb, it was baffling that the Mermaid Queen was here too.","The Mermaid Queen was about to speak when countless figures charged out of the forest. “The Saintess is there! Capture her!”","Zu An instinctively glanced at Yumen Beiqing. The latter looked bewildered too. Why is someone after me in this world?","“Chang’e, you aren’t getting away!”","Those words, along with the anxiously hiding Mermaid Queen, evoked an utterly ridiculous thought in Zu An’s mind. “You can’t be Chang’e, can you?”","1. In Chinese folklore, the Scalding Valley is where the sun rises from. ☜"]},{"number":2573,"title":"Chapter 2573: Chapter 2525: The Victim Comes Knocking","paragraphs":["The Mermaid Queen was stunned. “Big brother Zu, how do you know that? I don’t know what’s going on either. Ever since I arrived here, everyone has been calling me Chang’e.”","Zu An and Yumen Beiqing were speechless.","Zu An slapped his forehead. How could something so cliche happen here? I was just wishing Brother Yi and Chang’e a blissful marriage, only to learn right after that Chang’e is the Mermaid Queen. How am I supposed to earnestly wish them happiness now?","While he had been keeping his distance from the Mermaid Queen, he couldn’t turn a blind eye when she was forced to marry a man she didn’t like. The thought of Yi angrily confronting him over this gave him a splitting headache.","However, this wasn’t the time to be thinking about such things. He turned to the soldiers and saw them encircling the Crystal Boat, their eyes focused on the Mermaid Queen.","Zu An frowned. He sensed auras similar to Er Fu coming from those people. According to Yi, these people were likely from the Fiend races. The good thing was that these fiends were nowhere as powerful as Er Fu or Wei Yueyan. However, the bad news was that their auras weren’t weak; they were at least at the level of the strongest of the Eighteen Monster Generals.","“Why are they pursuing you?” Yumen Beiqing asked with a frown.","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “I don’t know either. I learned that Chang’e is betrothed to someone, and her fiancé is going to propose to her today. There was no way I could accept the marriage, so I escaped. However, these people suddenly appeared out of nowhere and began hunting me down. It took everything I had to flee here.","“I was in despair until I noticed the Crystal Boat. I thought I was dreaming, so I tried calling out to you. I didn’t expect it to truly be big brother Zu!”","As she looked at Zu An with deepening feelings, her eyes began to brim with tears. She felt that this was all decided by fate. If the world is already helping me, how can I back off like I did before?","Zu An and Yumen Beiqing felt sympathy for Yi. However, they turned to the crowd encircling the Crystal Boat.","“Is there some kind of misunderstanding here? My friend doesn’t know you.”","Those people exchanged looks. The pig-headed leader standing in front said, “That's the Chang clan’s Saintess Chang’e; we wouldn’t mistake her for anyone else. Our Golden Crow Third Crown Prince wishes to meet her. You better not stick your head where it doesn’t belong.”","They noticed how extraordinary the Crystal Boat was, not to mention it was tinged with the Dragon race’s aura. They couldn’t figure out Zu An’s background on the spur of the moment, so they chose to bring out their backing to intimidate the other party.","“The Golden Crow Third Crown Prince...” Zu An’s face turned cold. My eight characters [1] must clash with the Golden Crow race. Why do I get into a conflict with them at every turn?!","Yumen Beiqing harrumphed coldly. “Nonsense! How can you be the subordinates of the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince?”","Zu An was taken aback. Little sister Ling’er’s reaction is weird. Has she gotten on close terms with the Golden Crow Imperial Family in the years she spent as the Fiend races’ Saintess?","Even though the Celestial World’s Golden Crow race was bound to be different from the Cultivation World’s Golden Crow race, there were still bloodline ties between them.","The pig-headed chief eyed Yumen Beiqing with greedy eyes. “Beauty, there’s no need to prove to you that we are the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince’s subordinates. Who in the world would dare to use his name in vain?”","He was surprised to see that someone could rival Chang’e in beauty.","Yumen Beiqing coldly sneered, “Chang’e is the fiancée of the Shaman races’ powerhouse, Yi. There have been many conflicts between the shamans and the fiends over the years, and their relationship has gotten so tense that a war can easily break out at a moment’s notice. If the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince kidnapped Chang’e at this juncture, he would not only offend Yi but the Chang clan as well. That’s bound to stir a massive war between the races.","“The Golden Crow Third Crown Prince is famous in the Celestial Court; he would have surely thought of that. Taking a thousand steps back, even if he was interested in Chang’e, he would capture her quietly instead of announcing his identity in public.”","The fiends exchanged awkward looks.","The Mermaid Queen was awed by Yumen Beiqing. As expected of the legendary Saintess. She is truly wise.","Even Zu An was surprised. Little sister Ling’er has changed a lot.","The pig-headed chief was infuriated. “A woman like you can’t begin to fathom a celestial’s thoughts. Hand Chang’e over right now, or don’t blame us for getting violent!”","His comrades raised their weapons, ready to make a move at his command.","Just then, a crisp bell rang—it was the Horror Bell! The surroundings fiends felt a surge of fear. They were worried that their master’s plan had been unraveled.","At the same time, a massive black flag emanating a ghostly aura appeared in midair. With a slight sway of the flag, the surrounding fiends suddenly felt their mental states being rattled. It was the Fallen Soul Banner!","These two artifacts were Zu An’s spoils of war from the Monster World’s top experts. As the trump cards of those top experts, their prowess wasn't to be scoffed at.","But while the artifacts had shaken up the fiends, they weren’t enough to claim their lives. Zu An also hadn't been expecting the artifacts to do that much; it was good enough as long as the items at least sent them into a temporary daze.","He was about to make a move when he suddenly frowned. Without any hesitation, he transported the Mermaid Queen into the cabin using a teleportation formation and instructed, “Don’t make a noise.”","In the next moment, a red light shot over from afar. Just as it had impaled the vultures in the sky, it easily claimed the heads of the fiends surrounding the Crystal Boat. It was so fast that the fiends didn’t have time to react before their heads burst apart.","Only the pig-headed chief had time to raise his weapon, but he was still too late. The red light pierced through his forehead, and he plummeted from the sky.","Soon, Yi flew over from afar. He lowered his head and saw the pig-headed chief’s body dissipating as a light wisp of smoke, and that made him frown. “That fellow still has some ability. To think that he escaped with his primordial spirit.”","This reunion left Zu An feeling conflicted. “Brother Yi, thank you for your help.”","At the same time, he was astounded. Even though the Horror Bell and the Fallen Soul Banner had delayed the fiends’ reaction, it was still shocking to see Yi massacring all of them from afar with a single arrow. It looked as if the latter hadn’t gone all out in their previous friendly duel.","“Brother Necropolis, you could have easily dealt with them even if I didn’t make a move. It’s just that I’m not in a good mood now, so I’m taking it out on them,” Yi huffed.","Zu An smiled. “Why are you so angry, Brother Yi? Weren’t you in high spirits when we parted? Oh right, I thought you were going to propose to Chang’e?”","Yumen Beiqing rolled her eyes. This fellow is good at feigning ignorance.","“Don’t mention it. Just thinking about that makes me angry,” Yi grumbled indignantly. “The Golden Crow Third Crown Prince kidnapped Chang’e. I’m chasing after him now. Did you see anyone suspicious along the way?”","Zu An pointed to the corpses on the floor. “Those people are plenty suspicious...”","Yi was confused.","Zu An quickly explained the situation. “They claim to be the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince’s subordinates, but they might not be trustworthy.”","He quickly shared the Saintess’ earlier analysis.","“I won’t refute that possibility, but the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince is still the likeliest suspect. We found his feather at Chang’e’s residence.” Yi clenched his fists.","Yumen Beiqing’s face stiffened.","1. The Eight Characters indicate the year, month, day and hour of a person's birth, which are often used in fortune-telling in China. ☜"]},{"number":2574,"title":"Chapter 2574: Chapter 2526: I’m Willing to Pay Any Price","paragraphs":["“Could someone be framing him?” Yumen Beiqing asked.","Yi waved his hand. “That’s unlikely. Given the lofty stature of the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince, how can he not know if someone steals his feather?”","Yumen Beiqing fell silent. His words made sense.","Yi clasped his fist and said, “Thank you for your intelligence. I’ll pursue that pig head’s primordial spirit now. If you find Chang’e, please inform me or the Chang clan.” He passed a piece of jade to Zu An. “You can contact me through this jade if you find anything.”","Zu An stowed away the jade and replied with an awkward smile, “Alright.”","Before leaving in a hurry, Yi thanked the two of them again. He was anxious to find his missing fiancée.","“You seem to be very concerned about the Golden Crow Third Crown Prince?” Zu An asked Yumen Beiqing with an ambiguous smile.","Yumen Beiqing chuckled naturally. “I have fought alongside the Golden Crow race for many years. The thought that someone might be framing them bothers me.” She quickly added, “Do you not plan to tell Yi about Chang’e’s whereabouts? If he learns that you have been lying to him, he might turn against you.”","Zu An was in a dilemma. “I can’t hand the Mermaid Queen to him. I can only take things one step at a time.”","He dared not call the Mermaid Queen to the deck because of her prominent identity in this world, so he headed down into the cabin to look for her.","The Mermaid Queen was sitting nervously on a chair. It was only upon seeing him that she revealed a faint smile. “So that’s Yi. You are acquainted with him?”","“It was a coincidence. We bumped into him along the way and took him with us.” Zu An still found this situation ridiculous. “So, how did you come here?”","The Mermaid Queen’s face reddened as she stuttered, “I don’t know either. One day, I suddenly heard a woman’s voice, saying that she could fulfill my wish, but she asked if I was willing to pay the price for it...”","Zu An got agitated. “What price did you pay?”","The Mermaid Queen pursed her lips. “I didn’t pay anything. Perhaps it was because she pitied me. When I opened my eyes, I was already in this world. Then... I met you.”","After parting ways with Zu An back then, she'd returned to the Ocean races to distribute the antidote to her people. The Ocean races had returned to their former strength, but she felt lonelier than ever.","One day, she'd gone to a sandbank on the surface of the sea and gazed at the moon while silently murmuring her feelings for Zu An. However, as they weren’t from the same spacetime, she knew that they didn’t have a future together. The more she thought about it, the more depressed she became. In the end, she couldn’t hold back her tears.","After crying for a long time, she'd suddenly heard a faint woman’s voice asking her if she truly wanted to be together with her big brother Zu. The Mermaid Queen had naturally replied with a nod.","The woman had then asked her, “Will you pay the price if I realize this wish for you?”","“I will!” It sounded reckless in hindsight, but back then, she'd answered that question without hesitation.","The woman had been surprised. “You answered despite not knowing the price you have to pay?”","“I’m willing to pay any price as long as I can be with big brother Zu.” The Mermaid Queen knew that there was no way they could be together, so she'd wanted to hear the woman out even if she was lying to her.","“What a fool...” The woman sighed. “You’ll suffer long years of loneliness just for a brief reunion with him. Are you still willing to do so?”","The Mermaid Queen had been stunned. She wasn't hesitant because of the price, but because the other party’s offer was starting to sound credible. Perplexed, she asked, “Who are you?”","“You need not care who I am. You just have to answer my question,” the woman had replied.","The Mermaid Queen had hardened her determination. “I’m willing to pay the price!”","She'd thought that the woman was lying, but even if she wasn't, she was willing to pay the price to be with big brother Zu.","Shortly after she answered the question, she suddenly fell into a daze. By the time she snapped out of it, she had already become the Chang clan’s Saintess, and she had a fiancé who was waiting to propose to her. This had shocked her. She had no idea why she had suddenly been transported into this foreign world.","However, she had no time to think too much about it. The imminent arrival of her fiancé had stoked her sense of urgency. It had crossed her mind to wonder whether that fiancé named Yi was big brother Zu, but she hadn’t dared to bet on it. If her bet was wrong, it would all be over. So, she'd chosen to escape.","Little had she expected to encounter a group of assassins shortly after she fled. She'd had to exhaust all her methods before she managed to temporarily shake them off her trail.","She'd thought she wouldn’t have a chance to see big brother Zu again, but the familiar Crystal Boat suddenly appeared in front of her. She'd called out to him with some skepticism, but the big brother Zu whom she'd been thinking about day and night really had appeared in front of her. At that moment, she'd felt so blissful that she could faint.","She shared everything that had happened with Zu An, though she did leave out some of the more embarrassing details, including the exact price she had to pay.","I wouldn’t mind telling everything to big brother Zu if there were no one else around, but the Fiend races’ Saintess is right there. They seem to be lovers. It wouldn’t be good for me to say those words here.","Even so, Zu An and Yumen Beiqing were still stunned.","“Who was that woman? To think that she has the power to directly transport you to this world!” Yumen Beiqing was far more shocked than she let on. Even she at her peak didn’t possess such powers.","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “I don’t know who that woman is. I tried contacting her after arriving in this world, but I never heard that voice ever again.”","“A woman’s voice...” Zu An could already fathom a guess. “Can you imitate that voice?”","“I should be able to.” The Mermaid Queen was a born musician. She had extreme sensitivity toward melodies and voices. She closed her eyes to recall the situation back then before slowly imitating the woman’s words.","Others could have struggled with the details, but the Mermaid Queen, with her impeccable skills, was able to fully recreate the woman’s voice.","Yumen Beiqing widened her eyes. To think it was her!","Zu An also looked conflicted. Seconds later, he let out a sigh. “I have an idea of who it is.”","Yumen Beiqing was surprised. She looked at Zu An with questioning eyes, not expecting him to know who that woman was.","“Who is it?” the Mermaid Queen anxiously asked. That was the thing she was the most curious about. Who could have the power to fulfill her wish?","Zu An took a deep breath before slowly revealing a name. “Lady Houtu.”"]},{"number":2575,"title":"Chapter 2575: Chapter 2527: Everything Is Fated","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the name, Yumen Beiqing looked grim.","“Lady Houtu...” The Mermaid Queen was initially confused before she was overtaken by shock. “Is that the person you met in the underworld?”","Zu An nodded. He would have wondered if Houtu was capable of such a feat in the past, but after learning that Houtu was a being on par with the Celestial Emperor, he realized that she was far stronger than he had expected. Not to mention she governed the Six Paths of Reincarnation. It shouldn’t be an impossible feat for her to transport someone across worlds.","The true question was why she'd done that. Furthermore, she had chosen not to reveal her identity. If not for the Mermaid Queen perfectly emulating her voice, they wouldn’t have known she was behind this.","She didn’t send me any messages even though I promised to find and deliver the six power insignias to her. Instead, she suddenly sent the Mermaid Queen here. What is she planning?","And what could the price the Mermaid Queen mentioned be?","Many doubts popped into his mind. He felt as if he'd been dragged into a massive conspiracy, and that there was a pair, or even many pairs, of eyes staring at him. The thought of it made him shudder.","“Why did Lady Houtu do that?” The Mermaid Queen was perplexed.","Yumen Beiqing’s eyes darted around as if she had a thought in mind, but she couldn’t confirm it.","Zu An asked out of curiosity, “Little sister Ling’er, what are your thoughts?”","“There’s too little information to work with.” Yumen Beiqing shook her head. She turned to the Mermaid Queen and asked, “What do you plan to do next?”","The Mermaid Queen had no answer. She knew too little about this world, and she vaguely sensed that the Fiend races’ Saintess was hostile to her. Is it because of big brother Zu...","Fortunately, Zu An interjected, “You should come with us. I’ll keep you safe.”","The Mermaid Queen nodded in relief. Now that she had his promise, nothing else was important.","Yumen Beiqing hesitantly spoke up. “The earlier clash showed that Yi is extremely strong. If he learns that his fiancée is with you, things will not end well.”","Zu An sighed. “I’ll explain it to him. If he can’t accept it, we’ll have no choice but to come to blows. I can’t turn a blind eye to Suyin.” He couldn’t bring himself to abandon the Mermaid Queen, whether it was due to his sense of responsibility, or the feelings he had for her.","When she heard Zu An calling her name, the Mermaid Queen’s eyes narrowed into tender crescent smiles.","Yumen Beiqing wanted to say more, but she suddenly thought of another possibility, and her eyes lit up. This development isn’t that bad either...","So, she grabbed the Mermaid Queen’s hand and said, “My queen, please forgive me for my harsh words. I was just worried about our circumstances; I don’t mean to leave you in a difficult situation. Pardon me for that.”","The Mermaid Queen was already in a good mood from her reunion with Zu An, and now, the Saintess was expressing her goodwill as well. There was no reason for her to mind it. “Don’t worry, Saintess. We should be standing on the same front and working together.”","Yumen Beiqing wasn’t used to this heartfelt sisterly interaction, but she knew it wouldn’t be apt for her to retract her hand now.","Fortunately, the Mermaid Queen changed the topic, asking, “How did the two of you get here?”","Yumen Beiqing took this chance to pull her hand away. “We’re heading to Kunlun Mountain to rescue Celestial Bao Jiang...” She quickly summarized the situation for the Mermaid Queen.","“Bao Jiang?” The Mermaid Queen frowned. “I have heard that name.”","“Where did you hear it?” Zu An was overjoyed. Kunlun Mountain was so massive that finding Bao Jiang there was as good as finding a needle in the ocean. Having some clues could greatly narrow their search radius.","“I remember it now!” The Mermaid Queen’s eyes lit up. “He stopped by and stayed at the Chang clan's residence for a few days. He was looking for a herb, and the clan elder guided him. Back then, I was too shaken up by this foreign world to pay much attention, so I only remembered it just now.”","“When did he arrive at the Chang clan?” Yumen Beiqing asked.","The Mermaid Queen spent a moment in thought before replying, “Around half a month ago.”","“What?” Zu An was astounded.","He'd been hoping to catch up with Bao Jiang to save his life, but even if that didn’t work out, it would be wonderful if he could get some clues about the Brilliant Pinflower’s whereabouts. But Bao Jiang had arrived at the Chang clan half a month ahead of them. There was just no way they could catch up with him anymore.","The schemers could have already killed Bao Jiang and obtained clues about the immortal medicine. Learning that their hard work was all in vain made Zu An slump in disappointment.","“There’s no need to be too disheartened. There’s a saying that a day in heaven is equivalent to a year on earth. Who knows? Bao Jiang might have just reported to the Celestial Court and started on his way back now,” Yumen Beiqing said. “When do you think would be the best time for the culprit to make a move? If Bao Jiang were killed on his way to report to the Celestial Emperor, the Celestial Court would swiftly notice something was amiss. But if Bao Jiang met the Celestial Emperor and received his orders, the Celestial Court would be unlikely to contact him again in the short term. If he died on his way back, the Celestial Court could fail to notice it for decades.”","Zu An’s eyes lit up upon hearing that analysis. “You’re sharp to have thought about that, little sister Ling’er!” If I were the culprit, I would have chosen to strike on Bao Jiang’s way back too.","Furthermore, with his current grasp of spatial transformations, he knew that the adage that a day in heaven was equivalent to a year on earth wasn't just hearsay.","He anxiously asked the Mermaid Queen, “Do you know where Bao Jiang headed when he left?” He figured that Bao Jiang could return via the same path.","The Mermaid Queen gave it some thought. A blue light glowed on her fingertip, and she drew a map on the table. “While planning my escape, I paid close attention to the terrain around the Chang clan's residence. I think he left from here.”","Zu An compared the Mermaid Queen’s map to the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s map. The maps were broadly similar, with the former having more details. Having confirmed the direction, he quickly steered the Crystal Boat over.","Just like that, they flew for days but didn’t find anything. The trio began to worry that they had gotten the direction wrong.","Out of the blue, however, Yumen Beiqing pointed in a direction and exclaimed, “I see movement there!”","Zu An looked over and saw a forest swaying. He didn’t sense anything unnatural about the movement, but he still decided to take a look. While they were heading there, he noticed a highly profound formation in the forest. He exchanged looks with Yumen Beiqing, and the two of them began hurling formation flags around. Soon, the surrounding space warped to reveal a white-bearded elder leaning against a big tree.","The white-bearded elder’s snowy-white robe was dyed red with blood. He looked to have suffered a severe blow to his ribcage. He had no doubt constructed the formation to conceal himself, yet he didn’t react to the breaching of his formation.","“Bao Jiang!” Recalling the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s description, Zu An could tell that the other party was the person they had been looking for at a glance.","When she saw Bao Jiang’s condition, Yumen Beiqing trembled. Her face turned pale, and her eyes became dazed. Has it all been decided? Is it impossible to change fate..."]},{"number":2576,"title":"Chapter 2576: Chapter 2528: Fate","paragraphs":["Bao Jiang was said to have white hair but a youthful face, but the severe injuries he had sustained made him look no different from an unkempt old man.","Seeing Bao Jiang’s shallow breathing, Zu An quickly took out a spirit medicine and fed it to him. It was a pity he had depleted his Feather Mountain Spring Water, and he didn’t know if the pills he had concocted in the future would work on a deity.","After swallowing the spirit medicine, Bao Jiang’s face regained some redness. His eyelids fluttered, and he weakly opened his eyes. “Did I just eat an immortal...”","Upon seeing Zu An’s group, he quickly stopped mid-sentence and asked, “You are?”","“Elder, we visited Treasure Origin Mountain under the Kaiming Six Shamans’ guidance to request a Brilliant Pinflower from you. However, we learned that someone was after your life, so we rushed over to aid you with the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s directions.” Zu An didn’t want to look so eager to claim credit, but Bao Jiang looked as if he would drop dead at any moment. They had worked so hard to save Xiaoxi, not hesitating to even travel across spacetime to gather the required materials. He didn’t even want to imagine what would happen if everything was in vain.","Those names brought some spirit back into Bao Jiang’s turbid eyes. He reached into his robe and took out a flower. “I harvested this flower a few days back. You may have it.”","Zu An looked at the flower; it had a glass-like transparency and resembled a pinflower. He didn’t need an introduction to know that this was what he was looking for.","After Zu An accepted the Brilliant Pinflower, Bao Jiang continued, “I have something I would like to ask of you, little brother...” He took out a gleaming golden pearl and passed it to Zu An. “Please hand this Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine to the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Have her entrust it to a fated someone to nurture it...”","Immortal medicine?","Yumen Beiqing and the Mermaid Queen looked at the golden pearl. Is this the legendary immortal medicine?","“The Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine!” Zu An shuddered.","No one was more familiar with the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine than him. He had found one in the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons in the future and used it to save Qiu Honglei. Mi Li had told him that the immortal medicines in this world were unique. This Divine Dragon Immortal medicine had to be the seed of the one he encountered in the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons in the future.","Zu An suddenly felt as if he was trapped in the constructs of fate, and it made him feel helpless and fearful.","“Who’s behind your injuries?” Yumen Beiqing asked.","Bao Jiang shook his head with a smile. “Knowing too much will only put you in danger. I’ll be grateful to you if you can fulfill my final wish...”","In the end, his voice faded away.","Alarmed, Zu An quickly checked on Bao Jiang. Seconds later, he shook his head at the two women and said, “He has passed on.”","“We’re still too late. Gu got to him before us,” the Mermaid Queen remarked with a sigh. Zu An had already filled her in on the details along the way. Even though she wasn’t acquainted with Bao Jiang, she could tell that he was a kind person from how he didn’t want to put them in danger despite already being at death’s door.","“Who are you, woman? Why do you know my name?” an eerie voice echoed from afar.","Zu An and the others were startled.","They looked over and saw a giant snake coiled around a colossal tree. The upper half of his body was that of a young man with red hair that fluttered with the wind, resembling little serpents. His irises were yellow slits, and his forked tongue flicked out now and then. He looked terrifying.","Zu An’s complexion turned awful. Yu Yanluo must have monopolized the beautiful genes of the Snake race. Why do all other snakes look so amazingly hideous?","A massive, bizarre bird resembling an eagle-owl hybrid landed on a nearby branch. It had a white head, a black spotted body, a red beak, and tiger-like claws. No one would doubt that a single swipe of its claws could tear through even a flood dragon.","It overheard Gu’s question and answered, “Milord, this woman appears to be the Chang clan’s Saintess.”","“The most beautiful woman in the world, Chang’e? She is indeed beautiful, and the woman beside her doesn’t pale much in comparison either. Looks like today is my day!” Gu eyed Zu An and the others before bursting into laughter.","Yumen Beiqing’s expression turned cold. The Mermaid Queen hid behind Zu An in fear.","“You must be here for the immortal medicine. Here, you may have it.” Zu An tossed the golden pearl toward the distant mountain valley.","At the same time, he grabbed Yumen Beiqing and the Mermaid Queen’s hands and fled in the opposite direction using Grandgale, not hesitating in the slightest. He didn’t bother to talk things out with Gu, knowing that the latter would choose to silence them regardless of the situation. Not to mention, Gu had expressed interest in Yumen Beiqing and the Mermaid Queen. That made it even less likely for him to spare them.","The words ‘immortal medicine’ caught Gu’s attention. He lunged at the golden pearl at a lightning-fast speed that seemed impossible for his massive body. As soon as he caught the golden item, however, his smile suddenly stiffened.","It was an ordinary piece of gold.","“How dare they fool me?” Gu gritted his teeth and crushed the piece of gold into dust. “Qin, capture them!”","Zu An executed a series of instantaneous movements, causing the scenery to swiftly retreat behind him. However, he didn’t look relieved in the slightest. The bizarre bird, Qin, was heading in his direction, and its movements were even faster than his. The other party was likely a subordinate deity similar to Wei Yueyan; it would be foolish to think of him as a simple beast.","Grandgale had a cooldown time. Knowing none of them would get away at this rate, Zu An pushed the two ladies ahead and shouted, “You two leave first! I’ll find you later!”","He drew his Tai’e Sword, turned around, and unleashed a burst of sword ki at Qin.","Qin’s eyes narrowed at the sight of the massive outburst of sword ki. A divine halo consisting of red, white, and black light enveloped its claws, and it swiped at the incoming sword ki. The energy was torn to shreds.","Zu An was stunned. He had expected Qin would be a formidable opponent, but he hadn't thought the other party would be this powerful. In particular, the celestials’ divine halo appeared to have a suppression effect on all other living beings.","In the blink of an eye, the other party’s claws were already right in front of him. Space seemed to freeze before it—the other party was guarding against his instantaneous movement. No matter where Zu An dodged, he couldn’t escape the fate of having his head split apart."]},{"number":2577,"title":"Chapter 2577: Chapter 2529: The Meeting of the Wind and Clouds","paragraphs":["Yumen Beiqing and the Mermaid Queen rode on the momentum of a powerful force for several kilometers before finally drifting to a halt.","The Mermaid Queen wanted to turn back, but Yumen Beiqing grabbed her. “Where are you going?”","“I can’t let big brother Zu brave danger alone!” the Mermaid Queen exclaimed.","Yumen Beiqing snorted in anger. “Can’t you tell that they are both celestials? They are many times stronger than you and me. You won’t be of any help to him; you’ll merely be marching to your death.”","The Mermaid Queen replied, “I am aware of my weakness, but my buffs should be able to help big brother Zu. Taking a step back, even if we lose the battle, I am content to die together with big brother Zu.” Ignoring Yumen Beiqing, she ran back.","Yumen Beiqing was left looking conflicted. Why are so many women so devoted to that fellow? She stomped her feet and followed the Mermaid Queen. She'd been planning to send the Mermaid Queen away before sneaking back to save Zu An, but given the current circumstances, she could only play along and see what she could do.","On the other hand, Zu An realized that he couldn’t dodge Qin’s claws, so he brandished his Tai’e Sword to parry the attack instead. It was a flesh body clashing against a divine weapon, yet sparks flew. With a loud clang, the two of them were knocked backward over a hundred meters away.","Qin circled the sky while eyeing the Tai’e Sword. “That’s a good sword.”","Zu An frowned. Even though the clash was a draw, he had the weapon advantage, and he had employed the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra to absorb the other party’s striking force to achieve this effect.","Qin was even stronger than Wei Yueyan. I wonder how the power levels of these celestials are determined.","However, Zu An didn’t panic. Over the years, he had accrued plenty of experience clashing with stronger opponents. It was only in recent days, after obtaining the Cultivation World’s World Law Beacon, that his battles had become much easier. He'd nearly forgotten how intense a battle could be.","Just then, two silhouettes rushed over from afar. “Big brother Zu, I’m here to help you!”","Hearing the Mermaid Queen’s voice and seeing Yumen Beiqing trailing behind, Zu An felt a headache settling in. It would have been much easier for him to slip away if they had left first. Now that they had returned, his only option was a fight to the death.","However, he didn’t blame them. How many men dreamed of a woman putting her life on the line to brave danger with them? That made him puff his chest outward, and he said, “Very well, let’s fight together!”","Even though the enemy was stronger than them, there was still a shot at victory.","“What arrogant words from a mere ant!” a cold voice echoed. A snake body slithered across the tree branches.","Zu An and the others were taken aback. By the time they looked up, the celestial named Gu had already enveloped the entire forest with his body, with his head loftily assessing them from above.","Inexplicable pressure bore down on Zu An and the others, causing their faces to turn pale. This suppression seemed to be caused by more than the disparity in their cultivation; it also felt as if a deity was exerting his dominion on mortals.","Zu An’s heart sank. He'd been confident he could dea with Qin even though the latter was a deity, but if the stronger Gu were to join the battle too, the chances of victory were slim even if he brought out all his trump cards.","The best I can do here is mutual destruction with the two of them. Hopefully I can save little sister Ling’er and the Mermaid Queen.","The Mermaid Queen racked her brain. We’re probably cornered here. I should find a chance to activate my founding ancestor’s forbidden art so big brother Zu has a chance of survival.","Yumen Beiqing was deep in thought. How can I save Zu An while hiding my identity? What a headache!","“A twat who struts around as if he’s a big shot just because he has a good bloodline thinks that he’s a deity?” A hearty laugh echoed.","A figure flashed over from afar. Gu tried to stop the figure with his snake body enveloping the forest, but the latter easily blasted through him with a punch.","Zu An was overjoyed. “Brother Yi, what brings you here?”","Yi clasped his fist at Zu An, only to be momentarily startled when he saw the Mermaid Queen. However, he quickly snapped out of it and replied, “I chased the pig head’s primordial spirit here when I sensed the jade I gave you shattering in the vicinity, so I came over to check things out.”","Zu An reached into his robe and retrieved a shattered piece of jade. It turned out that he had failed to properly neutralize Qin’s attack earlier. The shockwave wasn’t strong enough to hurt his resilient body, but the same couldn’t be said about Yi’s brittle jade.","“Yi?” Gu’s face darkened. He recognized the other party. This makes things troublesome.","“Gu, you’re getting from bad to worse. You’re a celestial, for heaven’s sake. Don’t you find it humiliating to be picking on a couple of mortals?” Yi sneered.","“You should worry about yourself,” Gu scoffed. “I heard you were betrothed to the Chang clan’s Saintess, so why is your fiancée with another man?”","Yi was taken aback. He turned to the Mermaid Queen and asked, “You’re Chang’e?” No wonder I felt something when I saw her earlier.","The Mermaid Queen was intimidated, but it was beneath her to hide behind a man and draw hatred for him. She took a deep breath and said, “It’s a misunderstanding. I’ll explain things to you when it’s all over.”","“All right.” Yi didn’t pursue the matter. It was enough for him that she was Chang’e.","Gu continued to provoke Yi, saying, “Hoh, I didn’t expect the renowned Yi to be a tortoise. I just saw Chang’e getting all chummy with that man, looking as if they would do a lover’s suicide.”","Yi’s cheeks twitched. “No one will think you’re a mute just because you stay silent.” He hurled a punch at Gu.","You have successfully trolled Yi for +119... +119... +119...","Small beads of sweat formed on Zu An’s forehead. Yi must be bothered by it. I’m glad that his rage is still within a manageable level.","Yi’s fist manifested into a massive avatar that descended upon Gu.","As he raised his hand to neutralize the attack, Gu unleashed a five-colored divine halo, but his body still shook under the blow. Yi’s punch must have been difficult for him to receive.","“Brother Necropolis, you escape with them first. I’ll look for you afterward!” Yi said grimly. He knew better than to underestimate a celestial’s strength, and he was worried that Chang’e would be injured by the shockwaves of the battle.","“Take care, Brother Yi!” Zu An bowed to Yi before fleeing with the two women.","Gu sneered, “Qin, I’ll leave them to you.”","Qin snickered, “Yes, milord!” It unfurled its wings and chased after Zu An and the others.","Yi wanted to stop Qin, but Gu quickly blocked him with his body. “I’m your opponent.”"]},{"number":2578,"title":"Chapter 2578: Chapter 2530: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["Yi eyed him coldly. “Your father is one of the Shaman races’ ancestors, so why do you lower yourself to be a celestial?”","Gu licked his lips as his face twisted in contempt. “What do you mean by lowering myself? With my noble bloodline, I don’t have to do anything myself for the Celestial Court to confer me as a celestial. All I hear are a loser’s words of envy.”","Then, he chuckled. “Ah, I heard you have done many things for the Shaman races in recent years, but the Celestial Court didn’t confer you any post. I guess the difference between us is a good father.”","Gu thumped his chest and ‘apologetically’ said, “Ah, I’m so sorry. I nearly forgot that you don’t have any parents. You’re an orphan!” His words were dripping with disdain.","Yi flew into a rage. “You’re courting death!”","He once again hurled a punch at Gu, but a thick snake tail coiled around his body and lifted him.","Gu stared coldly at the struggling Yi and sneered, “Little shaman upstarts like you wouldn’t know how noble our bloodlines are. How dare you challenge me? Today, I shall show you death!” He began to tighten his grip around Yi, squeezing the latter’s body so hard that veins began popping out.","Yi let out a howl, and his body swiftly expanded until he was a three-hundred-meter tall giant.","Gu was forced to release him. “Sss!”","Feeling humiliated, Gu’s body began to expand too. Soon, his body grew even larger than the massive dragon Zu An had seen in the future, looking almost like a small mountain.","Yi didn’t stop there either. His body continued to grow, soon crossing three thousand meters.","Both sides glared at each other. It was hard to tell who made the first move, but both sides released a furious roar and charged into each other.","The intense quake rattled Zu An and the others’ nerves. They turned around and saw a massive Yi brawling with a humongous snake. Wherever they passed, forests and mountains collapsed like tofu.","The Mermaid Queen’s face turned pale. “These ancient deities are shockingly powerful.”","The monsters who had invaded the Cultivation World were already strong enough to drive them to despair, but compared to the deities in this world, even they looked like children at play.","“I wonder if Brother Yi can escape.” Seeing the snake slowly coiling itself around the giant’s body, Zu An couldn’t help but be worried. Yi had only gotten involved to help him, and it would weigh on his conscience if something happened to him as a result.","“Rest assured, he’s strong. He withheld his strength for the earlier friendly duel,” Yumen Beiqing consoled as she looked at the choking giant with an unreadable face.","“Let’s hope so,” Zu An said.","A shrill laugh suddenly echoed from ahead. “You shouldn’t be worrying about others now.” A massive eagle-owl blocked their path.","Zu An released the hands of the two women and calmly looked at Qin. “Do you think we’re afraid of you?”","The only one he was worried about was Gu. Qin was formidable, but he had ways to deal with it.","Zu An’s impassive eyes made Qin’s heart skip a beat. This fellow is too composed. Does he truly possess the means to defeat me?","He quickly shrugged off that ridiculous thought and said, “Empty words. I just received orders from milord. The only fate awaiting you is death, though milord can consider sparing those two beauties beside you.”","Sensing Qin’s lustful eyes, Yumen Beiqing’s expression turned cold. She threw out the Emperor’s Suppression Talisman, and a golden aura billowed in the sky. Two golden-armored warriors emerged from the clouds.","Qin was taken aback. “You can summon celestial soldiers? How is that possible?!”","He frantically flapped his wings to flee, but it was too late. The golden-armored warriors stretched their hands down from the clouds, their movements clumsy but astonishingly fast. Before he knew it, they already had their grasp on his wings. Qin struggled with all his might, but he was unable to break free of the two golden-armored warriors.","Both the Mermaid Queen and Zu An were stunned. What’s going on? When did little sister Ling’er become this powerful?","More importantly, the pressure emanated by those two golden-armored warriors was so great that even Zu An felt insignificant. It wasn't his first time seeing the Emperor’s Suppression Talisman, but he had never seen it exert such incredible prowess before.","Yumen Beiqing noticed their shock and hurriedly feigned exhaustion. “Quick, I’m reaching my limit!”","The two golden-armored warriors began to dissipate, and it looked as if Qin would break free at any moment.","The Mermaid Queen quickly played a melody on her harp to stack buffs on Zu An.","Without any hesitation, Zu An unleashed the Star Shattering Imprint with its tenfold power! At the same time, he unleashed a barrage of sword ki with his Tai’e Sword.","Qin was unfazed. He scoffed at Zu An, “A mere mortal hopes to hurt me?”","The three-colored divine halo enveloped Qin once more. As long as he had his divine halo, Zu An wouldn’t be able to hurt his main body no matter how formidable his sword ki was.","Even so, Zu An had already expected that and activated the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra in advance. An invisible black hole appeared around Qin and devoured the three-colored divine halo.","“H-How is this possible?!” Qin finally panicked and screamed in shock.","But it was too late. The sword ki blasted through his celestial body with ease, slicing him in two. His two severed halves tried to reconnect, but the sword ki harnessed destructive energy that continuously tore through his body until it was reduced to dust.","Zu An was stunned. He felt an immense surge of ki rushing toward him.","His experience bar had been stuck at level 79 for the longest time, but he couldn’t make a breakthrough no matter how his ki grew. It was as if an invisible ceiling had been capping his growth. However, this rush of ki seemed to contain something that he couldn’t put his finger on, and it rattled the ceiling that had limited him thus far."]},{"number":2579,"title":"Chapter 2579: Chapter 2531: Undergoing Tribulation","paragraphs":["Clouds began covering the previously clear sky, turning it dark. Lightning crackled amid the clouds. An inexplicable air of heaviness and solemnity lingered in the surroundings. Countless birds and ferocious beasts in the nearby mountain forests fled in a fluster. Before this, no one had known that there were so many living beings residing in the vicinity.","Even the Mermaid Queen felt difficulty breathing. Her face paled in shock. “What’s going on?”","Yumen Beiqing grimly replied, “He’s about to undergo a heavenly tribulation.”","“Heavenly tribulation?” The Mermaid Queen was taken aback.","“It is a trial mortals have to overcome to become immortals.” Yumen Beiqing looked at Zu An’s silhouette with a deep gaze.","“I heard that most people die amid their heavenly tribulation. Will big brother Zu be fine?” the Mermaid Queen asked.","She came from the Cultivation World of thousands of years ago, when its ki was much stronger. She had heard legends about heavenly tribulation.","“It will be dangerous, but you don’t have to worry about him. He should be able to deal with it. Let’s leave this place first, lest we be implicated by his tribulation lightning,” Yumen Beiqing said as she grabbed the Mermaid Queen’s arm and flew away.","“Are you sure he can deal with it?” The Mermaid Queen was so worried that she wanted to find assurance from Yumen Beiqing.","“Let’s watch and see.” As she watched Zu An’s silhouette, Yumen Beiqing’s face flickered under the flashes of lightning.","She didn’t tell the Mermaid Queen the truth. Most people lost their lives while undergoing the heavenly tribulation, and that was considering how most challengers would have prepared pills, artifacts, and even had elders or daoist companions protecting them nearby.","But Zu An had abruptly encountered heavenly tribulation without any preparations. That would spell certain doom for anyone else.","With Zu An’s strength and his array of formidable methods, there was a good chance he could have overcome the heavenly tribulation had he encountered it in the real world. However, in this Celestial World, tribulation lightning would be at least two to three times stronger.","By now, Zu An had also sensed the anomaly too. The ki in his body had built up to a breaking point, and it felt as if it would shatter the space around him at any moment. He looked up at the tribulation lightning. There was an inexplicable connection between it and his body, and he could sense that it would descend on him at any moment now.","“A tribulation, huh...” He had previously read something similar in novels. He had also previously witnessed Zhao Han facing a tribulation, so it wasn’t hard for him to figure out his current plight.","But why does my tribulation feel much more difficult than Zhao Han’s?","The sky was completely covered in dark clouds, making it impossible to see even the towering Kunlun Mountain anymore.","Is it because of my strength, or just that this world is too powerful?","Zu An had no time to ponder that question, as the first bolt of tribulation lightning fell just then. A white streak that was thicker than a tree trunk fell from the clouds and instantly struck toward his head.","Zu An was already prepared for it, however. He sent his fist forth to crush the tribulation lightning. He didn’t dare to use the Tai’e Sword because Mi Li was inside. Heavenly lightning was the nemesis of soul entities, so he was worried that it could hurt her.","As soon as the lightning dissipated, Zu An felt traces of incredibly pure ki flowing into his body. This was the energy that had been contained within the lightning bolt.","It made him realize that even though tribulations were dangerous, they were also a fortuitous encounter. His clash against the tribulation lightning was also a chance for him to steal the lightning’s energy to temper his body.","Before this, he had considered using a Faraday Cage to avoid the heavenly tribulation. That method could work, but it would cost him an invaluable fortuitous encounter.","While he was deep in thought, another round of tribulation lightning descended. This time, nine bolts of brilliant lightning struck him consecutively.","The Mermaid Queen was horrified. The lightning bolts were so bright that they instantaneously enveloped Zu An’s entire body.","In contrast, Yumen Beiqing was much calmer. She watched the spectacle from afar.","A massive crater appeared in the region. Nearby trees were blasted into bits. Under the immense heat sparked by the tribulation lightning, even rocks melted into lava.","Even so, an upright figure stood at the center of the crater.","Yumen Beiqing’s face reddened. I have to admit that he has a good figure...","The nine consecutive lightning bolts had incinerated Zu An’s clothes into ashes, exposing his bare skin.","The Mermaid Queen also blushed furiously, but she was more concerned about another matter. “How many waves of tribulation lightning are there?” She had no idea why she was posing this question to the Fiend races’ Saintess, but somehow, she subconsciously thought that the latter would know these details.","“It’s hard to say. Some only undergo one wave, but some undergo nine waves or even more. Usually, the more waves of tribulation lightning one faces, the higher the limit is for their cultivation. Of course, more waves of tribulation lightning may fall on vile individuals who pique heaven’s scorn to decimate them too,” Yumen Beiqing answered smoothly, as if she already knew these things ahead of time.","The Mermaid Queen breathed a sigh of relief. “That’s good to hear. Big brother Zu has been doing good his entire life. Surely the world will not seek to destroy him.”","However, looking at his tattered clothes, she couldn’t help but worry. “His clothes are already destroyed even though it’s only the second wave. Things don’t look good.”","She was strong enough to be considered an expert in the Cultivation World too. She understood that Zu An’s clothes had only been destroyed because he was unable to fully neutralize the lightning. That meant he was already struggling a little on the second wave.","Yumen Beiqing could tell as much too. She calmly said, “Don’t worry, he's still enduring the lightning with his body alone. He hasn’t used his weapon yet.”","The Mermaid Queen breathed a sigh of relief.","Just then, another wave of tribulation lightning manifested in the sky, forming crimson lightning spheres.","Yumen Beiqing frowned.","“What’s wrong?” the Mermaid Queen asked nervously.","“The Planetary Tribulation Lightning should be far stronger than the earlier Barrage Tribulation Lightning, but I have no idea why it’s crimson.” Yumen Beiqing was confused.","“Is red lightning the most dangerous one?” The Mermaid Queen was horrified.","Yumen Beiqing shook her head. “It’s the opposite. Of the seven rainbow colors, red lightning is the weakest of all. It is a fearsome force to ordinary cultivators, but it is too weak for a cultivator of his caliber.”","The Mermaid Queen breathed a sigh of relief. “Isn’t that good news? It means that the odds of big brother Zu An surviving the heavenly tribulation are much higher.”","“It’s not necessarily a good thing,” Yumen Beiqing coldly pointed out."]},{"number":2580,"title":"Chapter 2580: Chapter 2532: Death","paragraphs":["“Ah? Why is that?” The Mermaid Queen was taken aback.","“The strength of the tribulation lightning is linked to the challenger’s future cultivation limit. The weaker the tribulation lightning, the lower their limit will be,” Yumen Beiqing replied.","Objectively speaking, the heavenly tribulation Zu An faced wasn't weak, but she still felt a little disappointed.","The Mermaid Queen smiled. “That’s nothing. I just need big brother Zu to be safe and sound.”","Yumen Beiqing glanced at her. This woman is a famous figure in that world, so why does it seem as if her mind turned to mush after meeting that fellow? What charm does he have, to leave so many women falling head over heels for him...","A crimson lightning sphere descended toward Zu An. It floated down slowly, but no matter how Zu An dodged, the sphere followed his movements.","He spent some time dodging the spheres to first calm the ki inside his body before hurling a series of punches at them. He was glad to have once possessed the Cultivation World’s World’s Law Beacon, which deepened his understanding of ki to a high level.","This confrontation with the lightning spheres could seem reckless, but he was capable of using the smallest force to unravel the latter’s weakest spot. Perhaps he'd look disorganized in others’ eyes, but in truth, he had minimized his ki depletion.","After Zu An shattered the nine crimson lightning spheres, the Mermaid Queen was about to cheer when her smile froze in place. She noticed that the tribulation clouds were still refusing to scatter, and orange tribulation lightning was starting to manifest.","Yumen Beiqing widened her eyes. “Ah, it’s the legendary Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation!”","“Is it dangerous?” The Mermaid Queen felt her heart clenching.","Yumen Beiqing nodded. “It’s very dangerous. Only two or three people have been known to have cleared this tribulation since ancient times. Others who encountered this tribulation were all decimated.”","She'd initially thought the tribulation lightning was too weak, but that wasn’t the case at all. If anything, it was too strong!","“Are there no solutions?” At this moment, the Mermaid Queen couldn’t care less why Yumen Beiqing knew so much; her attention was devoted to overcoming the current crisis.","Yumen Beiqing didn’t answer, but her gaze looked grim. Even those who have prepared for the Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation are likely to die, let alone the unprepared Zu An. Everything I have prepared and worked for has been futile anyway, so this isn’t that bad...","The orange tribulation lightning in the sky merged to form a terrifying whip. It lashed straight toward Zu An, slicing through space wherever it passed.","Yi was stunned to witness that. “The Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation? Brother Necropolis is indeed an extraordinary man!”","Angry rumbles echoed beneath him. Gu’s massive snake body was squirming under him, trying to get back up.","“Stay still!” While observing the heavenly tribulation, Yi hurled another series of punches at Gu’s head.","“How dare you humiliate me!” Gu’s eyes were spinning from the consecutive punches. Blood flowed from his mouth and nose. When had he, a celestial, suffered such grievance?","“Are you resorting to your mouth because your punches aren’t strong enough?” Yi sneered.","“My father is the Torch Dragon! You’ll have hell to pay for if you dare touch me!” Gu roared.","Given his lofty bloodline and his high standing as a celestial, he'd thought he could easily subdue an unaffiliated cultivator. Initially, everything went smoothly; he'd easily wrapped his body around his opponent’s neck.","Little had he expected his opponent to bite him, leaving a gaping hole in his steel-like body!","How the hell did he train his teeth? Are his teeth his soulbound artifact?","Yi’s face darkened. “I look down on those who rely on nepotism!”","He continued smashing his fist into Gu until the latter’s head swelled like a pig head. He had grown up as an orphan and gone through a lot from a young age, which was why he scorned those who only relied on their parents.","“I don’t believe that you would dare kill me!” Gu scoffed in anger despite being completely pinned down.","His father was one of the strongest experts in the world, and his mother was of exalted standing too. Given that this bastard was also from the Shaman races, he didn't think that the other party would truly dare take his life.","Yi’s gaze turned cold. “I shall purge you on behalf of our Shaman races!”","The suffering he'd gone through from a young age had nurtured a reckless, extreme personality. Faced with Gu’s provocation, he couldn’t withhold his killing intent anymore. He gathered immense destructive energy in his fist and hurled it at Gu’s head.","However, a beam of golden light suddenly shot down. Yi quickly changed the direction of the punch to strike the light.","Boom!","A loud explosion ensued, and Yi was jolted a hundred meters back. He looked in a certain direction with a grim expression.","Golden lights suddenly lit up the sky, and a dashing man emerged. He had a sharp hook nose, thin lips, and long eyes that gave off an air of cold authority.","Yumen Beiqing glanced at the golden lights in astonishment. “What is he doing here?”","The dashing man noticed the heavenly tribulation and remarked, “The Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation? To think someone in this world is capable of evoking such a heavenly tribulation!”","He was interested in taking a look, but he needed to settle the issue before him first.","Yi looked at the dashing man with a frown. “Dijun?”","The other party was of exalted status. Why would he suddenly appear here?","The dashing man shook his head at Yi. “What a pity.”","Despite knowing that the other party was stringing him along, Yi still asked, “What’s a pity?”","“You easily defeated Gu, a celestial. It was only a matter of time before you became a top-notch expert in the world. It’s a pity you won’t have the chance to do so,” the dashing man said with a sigh.","Yi narrowed his eyes in confusion. “You’re planning to kill me?”","Dijun was already the regent Celestial Emperor, and Zhuanxu was soon to officially step down from his position. Given that there was no grudge between them, why would Dijun want to take his life?","“You shouldn’t have appeared here.” Dijun slowly raised his finger.","Yi was taken aback. There was no time for him to ponder the reason; at this moment, he felt unprecedented danger. Without hesitation, he drew the bow he'd never touched during his battle with Gu. He pulled his bowstring and unleashed a brilliant arrow reminiscent of a shooting star at Dijun.","Dijun also released a golden light beam from his hand that collided with Yi’s arrow. The beam tore through the arrow, and Yi watched in bewilderment as it shot into his forehead.","At the same time, Dijun looked down and saw the two halves of the arrow lodged in his body. Two droplets of golden blood dripped from his wounds, causing the earth beneath to blaze into flames.","A divine light shone from his body, and the two arrow halves were reduced to ashes.","His voice was filled with commendation. “What exquisite archery. If you had a good bow, you would have been able to put up a fight against me. A pity indeed.”"]},{"number":2581,"title":"Chapter 2581: Chapter 2533: True Identity","paragraphs":["Yi stared at Dijun in disbelief. He opened his mouth as if to say something, but nothing came out before he collapsed on the ground.","Meanwhile, Gu was finally able to get back up. He felt exuberant at Yi’s death. He spat a mouthful of blood and sneered, “Pui! You deserve to die.” He turned to the dashing man and said, “Thank you for your aid, Milord. This brute would have killed me if it weren’t for your timely arrival.”","The dashing man eyed him coldly. “You have disappointed me.”","Gu smiled sheepishly. He was embarrassed that he, a celestial, had been pinned onto the ground and helplessly beaten up by a shaman.","“You didn’t tell anyone else what happened, right?” the dashing man asked.","“Rest assured, Milord. I wouldn’t talk about a matter of such great importance with others. Even my subordinate, Qin, doesn’t know about it.” Gu thumped his chest and gave his assurance.","“That’s good.” The dashing man slowly nodded before raising his finger.","Gu was horrified to see the other party’s expression and movements. “Milord, are you planning to silence me? Please be assured that I won’t share this matter with anyone!”","The dashing man had an utterly cold look on his face. “Only the dead tell no tales, but you don’t have to worry. I won’t kill you. You are still useful to me.”","His finger lightly tapped on Gu’s forehead. There was a flash of golden light, and the latter’s expression turned dull before he passed out. The dashing man then casually waved his hand, and a golden flame enveloped Yi’s corpse. Soon, his body was burned to ashes.","“No one should know now. All that’s left is the situation over there,” the dashing man murmured as he turned his sights toward the heavenly tribulation.","...","Seeing the imminent arrival of the orange lightning whip, Zu An quickly manifested the Tranquility Bell to shield himself. However, it only held for a second before shattering into pieces.","Tsk, that’s why pirated things can't be trusted. I don’t think it's ever succeeded in stopping the enemy’s attack before. Oh well, at least it can greatly weaken my enemy’s attacks.","At the very least, the whip did dim significantly after tearing through the Tranquility Bell.","Zu An channeled the White Lotus Flame into his Flame Blade before swinging it down on the whip, severing it into two. The massive lightning whip dissipated into sparks that flowed into Zu An’s body and tempered it.","The clouds in the sky bellowed furiously. Golden lights peeked through the clouds, dyeing the pitch-black sky yellow.","Sensing the increasing pressure from the tribulation clouds, Zu An didn’t dare to let his guard down. He channeled the Primordial Origin Sutra to heal his wounds. Despite his not preparing pills beforehand, the Primordial Origin Sutra’s recovery prowess was more useful than most pills.","The Mermaid Queen tried to rush over to Zu An’s side, only for Yumen Beiqing to stop her. “What are you doing?”","“I want to deliver some pills and offer him some buffs to help him tide through the heavenly tribulation,” the Mermaid Queen said anxiously.","“Don’t even think about going there. You will only put him in greater danger,” Yumen Beiqing warned. “If you step within a certain radius of it, the heavenly tribulation will grow even stronger. You will only be making things more difficult for him.”","The Mermaid Queen was horrified. “I’m glad that you’re here, Saintess. Otherwise, I would have made a grievous mistake.”","At the same time, she was curious to know why the Saintess was so familiar with heavenly tribulation. She was about to ask that when a golden light suddenly shone beside her.","A figure stepped out from the light. He extended a single finger toward her, looking as if he was going to crush her like a mere ant.","The Mermaid Queen tried to raise her hand and activate the Mermaid race's forbidden arts, only to realize that she couldn’t move. Time seemed to stop around her, causing even her thoughts to stall to a halt.","Yumen Beiqing was startled.","As she thrust her palm toward the figure, a blinding light shone around her too. The clash between the finger and the palm sent her flying a hundred meters back, whereas the golden figure merely swayed on the spot.","“Hm?” The dashing man didn’t continue his attack. Instead, he looked at Yumen Beiqing with questioning eyes. “It’s you. What are you doing here?”","Yumen Beiqing’s face darkened. She glanced worriedly at Zu An and the Mermaid Queen.","“Don’t worry. They can’t see what’s happening here,” the dashing man replied.","Yumen Beiqing still refused to speak a word. She stared intently at the dashing man.","The dashing man chuckled. “Why are you looking at me with such eyes? Is it because you haven’t seen me in a long while, my wife, Sun Goddess Xihe? What are you doing in this mortal body?”","Yumen Beiqing’s eyes turned cold. She didn’t display the slightest joy at this reunion. “Don’t disgust me by calling me that! What are you doing here?”","The dashing man smiled. “I sensed a phenomenon, and it was the legendary Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation at that, so I came here to have a look out of curiosity.”","“Do you think I’d believe that?” Yumen Beiqing sneered. “You, the Celestial Emperor, descending to the mortal world over such a triviality? I reckon you came to deal with Gu.”","The dashing man’s expression turned cold. “I don’t need to explain myself to you.”","Yumen Beiqing scoffed in contempt, “Of course. Who doesn’t know that the great Dijun has lovers everywhere? There’s no one you are accountable to.”","“Are you jealous?” The dashing man smirked. “This human body doesn’t look too bad, and that mermaid over there is quite a charmer too. Did you find them especially for me?”","“Your narcissism is as repulsive as ever.” Yumen Beiqing’s eyes were frigid. “If you can fool around, I can do the same too. I can now tell you that this woman and I are that man’s lovers.”","“That man...” The dashing man looked at Zu An with a frown. “So he’s the one who invoked the legendary Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation. I see potential in him, but his strength is lacking...”","Just then, his smile suddenly stiffened. He turned his gaze back to Yumen Beiqing and huffed. “Xihe, I know you're displeased by my womanizing ways, and that you’re saying those words to irk me. You wouldn’t fancy an uncouth man like that. What are you scheming?”"]},{"number":2582,"title":"Chapter 2582: Chapter 2534: What Should I Do Now?","paragraphs":["“I’m trying to irk you?” Yumen Beiqing laughed. “I shan’t question your affairs, so don’t bother questioning my affairs either.”","The dashing man frowned, but he chose not to argue with her. “Fine, I shan’t question you, but I’ll be killing that man. As for this woman...” Looking at the Mermaid Queen’s beautiful face, he murmured, “It would be a pity to kill her. I’ll bring her with me.”","Yumen Beiqing sneered, “You’re true to your character. You won’t be touching either of them, though. They are my people.”","The dashing man frowned. He eyed the man standing amid the tribulation clouds, and saw that the latter was more handsome than him and had a physique that would make women go crazy. He suddenly had an ominous feeling. “You couldn’t have truly fallen for that man, did you?”","His killing intent deepened.","“It has nothing to do with you. Don’t foil my plan.” Yumen Beiqing glared at him with cold eyes.","The dashing man breathed a sigh of relief. She’s scheming something after all.","“Forget it. Since you insist, I shall spare them on your account,\" he said. He walked closer to Yumen Beiqing to better admire her beauty. “Your current body looks so beautiful. Shall we get intimate like that? Perhaps we can find the passion we used to have.”","Yumen Beiqing stepped back to avoid his touch. With eyes as sharp as daggers, she bellowed, “Scram!”","The dashing man’s face twisted in anger. “I am the next Celestial Emperor, which makes you the next Celestial Empress. Are you going to snub me?”","Yumen Beiqing continued staring at him with cold eyes, not saying a word.","The dashing man harrumphed coldly. “Forget it!”","Feeling displeased, he flung his sleeves and morphed into a golden light. Before leaving, he took one last glance at the Mermaid Queen. She’s gorgeous. Why have I never heard about her before? I should look into her and approach her once Xihe is gone...","Following his departure, the Mermaid Queen’s perception of time reverted to normal. She anxiously scanned her surroundings while asking, “Where’s that golden man?”","Yumen Beiqing calmly replied, “What golden man? You must have been hallucinating because of the tribulation clouds.”","“Did I?” The Mermaid Queen rubbed her head in confusion. Was it a hallucination?","Yumen Beiqing wasn’t in the mood to deal with her. She fell into deep thought. Why was Dijun here? Could it be that he’s involved in everything too? But that doesn’t make sense! Why would he...","“Saintess, the tribulation lightning resembles the celestial warriors you summoned earlier.” The Mermaid Queen tugged at Yumen Beiqing, jolting her from her thoughts.","Yumen Beiqing looked over and saw that the tribulation lightning had morphed into an army of celestial warriors that charged straight at Zu An.","The Mermaid Queen was horrified. “There are so many of them! Do you have a way to control those celestial warriors?”","Yumen Beiqing looked at the golden-armored warriors in the heavenly tribulation with cold eyes. Even if I could control them, why would I do so?","Even Zu An was intimidated by the sight of so many massive warriors charging at him.","“Don’t worry. The Tai’e Sword is a deity-grade weapon, after all. I won’t be affected by the heavenly lightning in here,” Mi Li suddenly said.","“Master empress!” Zu An was delighted to hear her.","“You’re at the heart of the heavenly lightning, so I’ll be going into hibernation soon. Be careful, especially for the next few waves of heavenly tribulation. Make sure to remain steadfast to your true nature. If need be, ask that Saintess for help,” Mi Li quickly said before falling silent.","Zu An was confused. What does Mi Li mean by those words? Why did she tell me to ask little sister Ling’er for help? Her cultivation is beneath mine, and she knows less about the heavenly tribulation than me. How would she be able to help me?","But faced with the onslaught of the celestial warriors, he had no time to ponder these questions.","He brought out his Rune Weapon Chart. Golden ripples appeared behind him, and several weapons, including the Tai’e Sword and the Human Emperor Seal, drifted out from within. He sent those weapons hurtling toward the celestial warriors.","The celestial warriors brandished their blades to deflect the incoming weapons, but unfortunately, the Rune Weapon Chart could conjure unlimited weapons. By the time the celestial warriors deflected the first wave, the second wave had already arrived.","The weapons conjured by the Rune Weapon Chart included Gatling guns, bombs, attack helicopters, bombers, and fighter jets; things that no one here had ever seen before.","Even Yumen Beiqing was stunned. What are these things that man has brought out?","In contrast, the Mermaid Queen was overjoyed. Her eyes gleamed with excitement.","Zu An opened his hands and enjoyed the boundless ki around him. This world was even richer in ki than the time he entered this place in the future. Only such a colossal amount of ki could sustain his continuous generation of weapons.","Most cultivators feared going up against an army, let alone one of these celestial warriors' caliber. But Zu An’s Rune Weapon Chart could unleash unlimited attacks, making it the ideal weapon against armies.","The only downside to his Rune Weapon Chart was its terrifying ki consumption. Even with a colossal amount of ki to tap, he gradually approached his limit, resulting in a steadily decreasing number of conjured weapons.","It was a relief that the previous bombardments had destroyed most of the celestial warriors, and the few survivors’ golden lights had become dim.","So, Zu An decided to stow away his Rune Weapon Chart and instead charge at the celestial warriors with his Tai’e Sword. Sword ki rampaged amid the tribulation clouds. The remaining celestial warriors collapsed in the blink of an eye, turning into specks of golden light that lingered in the air; Zu An unleashed the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra to absorb the specks.","A formation that aided in the recovery of Zu An's life force and ki suddenly appeared beneath him. He glanced at the Mermaid Queen, who was playing her harp from afar, and acknowledged her with a smile before focusing on his recovery. Soon, his almost depleted ki became plentiful once more.","Yumen Beiqing watched their interaction with impassive eyes. A frown slowly formed on her face. What should I do now?"]},{"number":2583,"title":"Chapter 2583: Chapter 2535: The Four Great Beauties of History","paragraphs":["By this point, most of Yumen Beiqing's plans had already failed, and she was only holding on because of her reluctance to give up. She knew that the best course of action right now was to kill this fellow. Even if she didn’t do that, it would be best to reenter this point in spacetime and do things anew in hopes that something could be different.","And yet, she felt lost. She had planned everything out, and she'd been confident she could pull it off. However, she'd been a step late for everything. She couldn’t tell whether it was because she wasn’t doing well enough, or if everything had been decided by fate.","No matter how she struggled, the world was still able to pull everything back to its original trajectory.","She looked at the man amid the tribulation clouds with a flickering expression. I've made such a huge sacrifice. Am I supposed to give up just like that? Even if I have to give up, I should at least kill him to vent the humiliation I suffered.","She slowly raised her hand, but right as she was about to make her move, she suddenly hesitated. No matter what, this is the one time that I came closest to success. Should I give it one more try? But the Nature Jade Plate only has one last use. Should I still use it on him...","While she was hesitating, the Mermaid Queen exclaimed, “Hm? Why did big brother Zu suddenly turn green?”","Yumen Beiqing snapped out of her thoughts to look at Zu An. Indeed, his body had turned completely green. It started with just his thighs, but it quickly spread throughout his entire body. Even the light coming from his body became a little warped. It seemed to be the effect of the surrounding temperature.","“Big brother Zu is on fire!” The Mermaid Queen finally realized what was happening. She formed a hand seal and summoned a deluge of water onto Zu An.","But not only did the water fail to put out the fire, it even made it blaze with greater fervor.","“Why isn’t the fire going out?!” The flustered Mermaid Queen wanted to rush over to help.","Yumen Beiqing held her back. “Don’t go over. That’s not ordinary fire.”","“What do you mean?” The Mermaid Queen grabbed Yumen Beiqing’s hand so tightly that it hurt the latter a little.","But Yumen Beiqing didn’t blame her for it and even explained, “This should be another wave of the heavenly tribulation. That flame is neither heavenly flame nor mortal flame; it’s called the yin flame. It begins surging up from the leg’s Yongquan Acupoint up to the head. If he fails to overcome this ordeal, his organs will be burned to ashes, and his limbs will wither. If that happens, his years of cultivation will have been in vain.”","Yumen Beiqing was shocked as well. This was one of the Three Disasters that deities encountered once every five hundred years. Why would Zu An encounter that when he wasn’t even a deity yet?","Even deities had died to this tribulation before. A mortal encountering it was bound to die.","The Mermaid Queen was horrified. She anxiously asked, “Is there a way to deal with this yin flame?”","Yumen Beiqing looked at Zu An’s green figure and calmly replied, “That flame is fueled by desires. He can survive this ordeal if he holds to his heart. Otherwise, he will be reduced to ashes. Outsiders won’t be able to help him at all.”","The Mermaid Queen breathed a sigh of relief. “That’s good to hear. Big brother Zu has a strong heart. He’ll weather through this ordeal.”","Yumen Beiqing sneered. This woman doesn’t know how terrifying the yin flame is. Even deities have fallen prey to it, let alone that lustful fellow!","In the time they had spent together, she had witnessed how great his desires were. It was unknown what surfaced in her head, but her cheeks reddened, and her eyes narrowed in rage. Hmph, this works fine. It’s heaven’s will if he dies here. I won’t have to make a move.","Zu An was unaware of the situation outside. He thought groggily, What was I doing earlier?","He noticed thin veils hanging around him as he sat on a massive, soft bed. A subtle sweet fragrance lingered in the air, mesmerizing him.","While he was trying to make sense of the situation, he heard a melancholic pipa melody that sounded pleasing to the ears.","He looked over and saw a gorgeous woman wearing a red cloak. She was dressed like a nomad, giving her an air of valiance. And yet, she also carried the coyness of a woman from the Central Plains. Her hands lightly stroked the pipa, producing beautiful melodies that seemed to tug directly at Zu An’s heartstrings.","Moonlight shone through the window and bathed her in its cold radiance.","Zu An was suddenly reminded of a poem: In the Qin’s Han residence, the shadows illuminate Consort Ming.","He was amazed that such a ravishing woman could exist in the world. He was about to ask her what was going on when he suddenly heard a crisp, bell-like chuckle.","It turned out that two women were dancing gracefully in the room. One of them wore a graceful and dignified dress from the Qin-Han era. The other wore a fluttery red dress that looked as vibrant as a blossoming flower. They held hands while dancing lithely. It looked as if they were competing to be the most beautiful flower in the room, yet their movements harmonized into an enchanting performance. Their faces were reddened with embarrassment, and amid their dance, they looked at Zu An with amorous eyes. It was as if they were doing all these things to pleasure him, to receive his affirmation and love.","Zu An had to concede that he had been presumptuous. Only a moment earlier he'd wondered how there could be someone as beautiful as the red-cloaked woman playing the pipa, but two other equally gorgeous women appeared right after.","“What’s going on?” Zu An wondered, feeling disoriented. His normally quick mind felt bogged down as if it was trapped in a swamp, preventing him from thinking normally. All he could do was obey his instincts and admire the beauties before him.","“Hubby~” A seductive voice echoed from behind, accompanied by the sound of splashing water.","It was only then that Zu An realized there was a huge spring in the room, and a gorgeous woman was bathing in it. Her arms rested against the border, and she looked at him with an inviting smile. Glistening water droplets flowed down her neck, drawing one’s eyes to her cleavage.","Zu An gulped. To think that there are four beauties of such caliber here!","“Hubby, why are you still in a daze? Come here and bathe with me. Xi Shi, Diaochan, and Zhaojun, you must be exhausted too. Come and join us!” The beauty in the spring beckoned them over.","It took tremendous willpower for Zu An to keep his nose from spurting blood. He was shocked by the names of the women. Aren’t they the Four Great Beauties [1] of history? The woman inside the spring must be Imperial Consort Yang.","Who am I? Where am I? What am I going to do?","He felt as if insufficient blood was flowing into his head, possibly because it was charging into his other head.","Xi Shi chuckled. “That won’t do. He hasn’t chosen yet.” She looked at Zu An with amorous eyes. “Hubby, who do you want to serve you tonight?”","There was an inkling that something was off at the back of Zu An’s mind, but in his dreamlike state, he was unable to connect with his rationality. He instinctively laughed and said, “Only a child chooses. I want it all!”","1. The Four Great Beauties are four Chinese women who were renowned for their beauty. The four are usually identified as Xi Shi, Wang Zhaojun, Diaochan, and Yang Yuhuan. Diaochan is a fictional character, while the rest have been greatly embellished by legends. They gained their reputation from the influence they exercised over powerful men and, consequently, their impact on Chinese history. ☜"]},{"number":2584,"title":"Chapter 2584: Chapter 2536: Slave and Master","paragraphs":["Diaochan and Wang Zhaojun exchanged surprised looks before chuckling behind their hands. “Hubby, you shouldn’t be so greedy. Choose one of us. This is for your own good.”","“One is hardly enough. Who are you underestimating? Since it’s a dream, why should I have just one beauty?” Zu An thumped his chest as if to say that he could take it.","This was a weird situation, but his rational mind was no longer functioning. Everything was going according to his true heart. He couldn’t explain the current situation, so he instinctively assumed that it was just a dream. As for why he was having such a dream and what he'd been doing before it, he had no idea at all, and he didn’t think of asking those questions either.","At Zu An’s insistence, the four beauties exchanged looks.","“Since hubby insists on it, we will serve you well.”","The four women chuckled coyly. As they gathered around him, their dresses fluttered.","All Zu An could smell were their mesmerizing fragrances. How he wished that he had more hands and feet! He finally understood why there were so many tentacle comics in his previous world. It turned out that they were fueled by the experience of realistic limitations.","Before he knew it, they were all soaking in the spring. The women's thin dresses floated on the water like vibrant flowers competing for attention. Hearing their coy laughter and feeling their smooth skin, Zu An thought that there was no paradise greater than this.","The world scorns King Zhou, yet the world desires to be King Zhou [1] .","Imperial Consort Yang suddenly chuckled seductively before diving into the water like a mermaid. Zu An was confused as to what she was planning to do when he suddenly gasped.","He immediately understood what was going on as his restless body was comforted with tenderness.","...","Meanwhile, the Mermaid Queen nervously grabbed Yumen Beiqing’s arm as she asked, “Oh no, why is the green flame burning stronger and stronger?”","Looking at Zu An’s dogged expression, Yumen Beiqing’s face turned red. She spat, “He can only blame himself for his weak willpower. He became enslaved to his desires so easily. Not even the gods can save him.”","Her tone revealed her anger at his incompetence. He’s at least a hero. I thought he would be better than this, but how could he succumb so easily? I have misjudged him!","The Mermaid Queen found her tone peculiar. It doesn’t sound like she’s worried about big brother Zu’s life and death. However, she didn’t push the issue and instead asked, “Is there any way to save him?”","“None at all. We’re just waiting for his death,” Yumen Beiqing coldly scoffed. “I’ve already said it. He only has himself to count on for this tribulation.”","The Mermaid Queen bit her lip. Unable to remain still, she took out her Deep Sea Harp and gently stroked it. A cleansing song manifested as tangible music notes that drifted toward Zu An. She had no idea whether this would be helpful or not, but she could only do whatever she could.","What’s going on? How humiliating it would be if I can’t even withstand something of this extent! Taking a deep breath, Zu An channeled his ki to calm his emotions.","But Diaochan and Wang Zhaojun took this chance to kiss his chest, while Xi Shi sealed his lips. He immediately stiffened up. Even steel tempered a hundred times would be reduced to jelly under such tenderness!","His face reddened. No, I can’t admit defeat at a time like this. It might be unfair, but now that I’m outnumbered here, I have no choice.","He channeled his Primordial Origin Sutra and unleashed his Golden Phoenix ability.","Perhaps they were famed beauties in history, but they were still women. How could they withstand the combined prowess of the primordial ki and the Golden Phoenix’s skill? The tables were quickly turned.","These women were too formidable; they were the cream of the crop. Ordinary men wouldn’t hesitate to toss aside their armor for any one of them. While Zu An was extraordinarily talented, he was at a disadvantage going up against four of them at once. The situation was too precarious. If he let the four women claim the initiative, it would only be a matter of time before he succumbed.","So, he found an opportunity and went on the offense. Not only was he talented, but he also had plenty of experience with his lovers. He usually held back out of concern for his lovers, but there was no reason for him to do so here.","All of a sudden, the hunters had become the prey.","...","Looking at the four women lying weakly by the spring, showing expressions very similar to those from erotic doujinshis, Zu An suddenly felt a massive sense of triumph. He cried out, “Come, let’s go at it for another three hundred rounds!”","Seeing that Zu An was getting more and more excited, the four women turned pale and hurriedly fled. Zu An tried to give chase, but the four women were so fast that they quickly disappeared from his line of sight.","“What’s going on?” Zu An stood naked on the spot, feeling a little confused by the situation.","Just then, he heard a calming melody that gradually calmed his restless heart.","“Ah, I’m still undergoing my tribulation...” He finally remembered the plight he was in, which also explained the inexplicable situation he had just been through.","Slowly opening his eyes, he first looked at the tribulation clouds above, before looking at the green flames slowly receding from his body. He was a little confused. So, did I succeed or not?","Countless planets suddenly appeared out of a void in the universe. They were interwoven together in a way that resembled the opening of a massive eye. Those who approached these planets would feel a surge of desire and depravity, and if they were lacking in willpower, they could succumb right away. Only a few experts with steadfast minds could keep themselves together.","“Instead of being enslaved to your desires, you’re seeking to become the master of your desires? Interesting...”","The eye closed, and everything reverted to normal. But a commotion broke out amid the lifeforms dwelling in the region. They speculated fervently about why that being had suddenly opened its eyes.","Meanwhile, Yumen Beiqing was extremely shocked that Zu An had surprised the Fire Tribulation. She'd thought that lustful man would struggle the most here, and the outcome was beyond her expectation.","The tribulation cloud swirled once more, and a tinge of blue surfaced. A wind began to brew.","Yumen Beiqing’s face twisted in shock. She instinctively shouted to Zu An, “Be careful! The Wind Tribulation is up next! It’s not directional winds, seasonal winds, nor nature winds, but Crow Wind! It can blow into your body through your forehead and into your innards, dantian, acupoints, bones, and flesh, disintegrating everything along its path...”","Before she could finish her words, a terrifying wind had already entered Zu An’s body through his head. Despite his body being more resilient than a dragon’s, he couldn’t withstand it at all. His brawny body began to melt, turning into a withered skeleton in almost an instant.","1. The story of King Zhou became a cautionary tale on what could befall a kingdom if its ruler gave into corruption and moral depravity ☜"]},{"number":2585,"title":"Chapter 2585: Chapter 2537: Aiding in Secret","paragraphs":["“Ah?” The Mermaid Queen’s blood turned cold. Her breathing suddenly became difficult, and the world seemed to lose its color.","However, she wasn’t so weak as to cry helplessly in a predicament. She quickly recovered and cast a healing blessing at Zu An. Unfortunately, her musical notes instantly popped like bubbles upon falling on Zu An; they were ineffective.","“How can this be...” The Mermaid Queen’s heart sank. She wanted to rush to Zu An’s side, but Yumen Beiqing held her in place.","“You’ll only be struck to death if you head over right now,” Yumen Beiqing uttered coldly.","“If big brother Zu is dead, nothing else matters. I just want to send him off.” For the first time, the Mermaid Queen’s usually euphonious voice sounded hoarse.","“Who says he’s dead?” Yumen Beiqing huffed.","“He’s still alive?” Light returned to the Mermaid Queen’s dull eyes.","“This is the Wind Tribulation of the Three Disasters that deities encounter once every five hundred years. The Fire Tribulation tests one’s heart, whereas the Wind Tribulation tests one’s willpower and cultivation. Those who survive this ordeal will undergo metamorphosis, whereas those who fail will be reduced to shreds.” Yumen Beiqing’s eyes remained fixed on the man in the middle of the dark clouds. She harbored a tinge of hope that he would pull it through.","“What can we do to help him?” the Mermaid Queen asked anxiously.","Yumen Beiqing replied, “There’s nothing you can do to help him. This is a tribulation he needs to overcome by himself. The only thing you can do is to pray for his safety.”","The Mermaid Queen took a deep breath. She clasped her hands in front of her chest and earnestly prayed, “Esteemed Ocean Deity, please bless big brother Zu for this ordeal. I’m willing to earnestly pray to you every night under the emerald sea...”","Yumen Beiqing secretly snickered. This woman is a fool. She isn’t as close to that fellow as me, yet she’s willing to go this far for him.","But as she laughed, she soon fell silent. Looking at the furious swirling wind, she couldn’t help but wonder if her cynicism was because she had never experienced true love before.","Dijun had many women, but those women only loved his strength and high standing. None of them were like the Mermaid Queen. She was devoted to Zu An, and so were Xie Daoyun and Pei Mianman. Just what kind of sorcery had that lustful man cast on them?","Meanwhile, Zu An felt as if he was on the verge of death. A wind was blowing down from his forehead, and it scoured every single part of his body that it passed by. His body was supposed to be resilient enough to withstand any physical scouring, but this wind was intangible and attacked him from the inside, rendering his defenses ineffective.","He tried to channel the Primordial Origin Sutra to heal his injuries, but the wind hindered the flow of his ki, making it impossible for him to circulate it normally. The experience gave him a glimpse into the suffering of those who were sentenced to death by a thousand cuts. For a moment there, he even considered giving up, knowing it could save him from the pain.","However, there were too many people and matters that he couldn’t let go of, so he continued to hold on. Even so, under the excruciating pain, his mind was swiftly reaching its limit.","It was then that he heard a woman’s voice saying, “This is both a trial and an opportunity to undergo metamorphosis. It only depends on whether you can pull it through or not.”","Zu An vaguely thought that the voice sounded familiar, but he couldn’t put his finger on it, and he didn’t have the spare energy to think about it either. He was like a man who had been wandering the desert for a long time, but then suddenly stumbled upon a clear spring and rushed to greedily slurp it up.","In truth, most people weren’t afraid of suffering or exhaustion; what they feared the most was hopelessness. They didn’t want to persist in something that would bring them endless suffering and give them nothing in the end.","Those words gave Zu An a ray of hope. There was meaning to his persistence. The darkness was only temporary, and it would soon give way to light. Many of his hesitations disappeared. It’s just bearing the pain. You don’t know how much I've suffered since I transmigrated here and started with the worst possible hand! I am no stranger to pain!","Now that he had tossed everything aside to focus on the present, he began thinking of ways to alleviate or neutralize the pain. His Primordial Origin Sutra granted him formidable regenerative prowess, but the wind rampaging in his body prevented him from channeling it. The same went for his other skills too.","Since it’s an intangible wind, I should use something intangible to counteract it.","Why am I so fixated on circulation pathways? Take the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra for instance. I'vee previously succeeded in conjuring black holes around me. Black holes devour not just the tangible but also the intangible...","As such thoughts surfaced in his mind, his body slowly turned intangible like a black hole. These winds were formidable, but they weren't fast enough to escape the grasp of a black hole.","...","“Hm?” Yumen Beiqing narrowed her eyes in shock.","She was just wondering why she had secretly offered him some advice when the situation began to change. Sensing the black hole forming around Zu An, she couldn’t help but bite her lips. Even she felt a tinge of fear toward him. She was the Sun Goddess, but the sun feared a black hole too. Her fear was only alleviated by the knowledge that the other party was Zu An. As she looked at him, her expression slowly became fervent.","She hurriedly averted her gaze. Pui pui pui, I can’t be truly interested in him. It’s just that the black hole holds a tremendous attractive force toward everything in the world.","“Saintess, what’s happening to big brother Zu?” The Mermaid Queen also sensed the change in Zu An.","“Don’t worry, your big brother Zu will be fine very soon.” Yumen Beiqing harrumphed.","“Isn’t he your big brother Zu too?” the Mermaid Queen asked while heaving a sigh of relief. She was perplexed by the twist in their dynamics. Despite being younger than her, the Fiend races’ Saintess seemed to have somehow taken the role of the ‘big sister’ here.","“My big brother Zu...” Yumen Beiqing was dazed for an instant before quickly calming down.","At some point, Zu An noticed that the scraping pain had vanished, replaced by a gentle breeze. It nourished every cell in his body, and his blood and flesh regrew at a visible pace. His body looked as impeccable as the finest jade.","He felt as if he had become one with his surrounding ki; he could now tap into it freely. This sensation wasn't new to him, but he had previously only been able to achieve that level with the aid of the World Law Beacon. Yet now, he could achieve the same effect with just his body. His area of control over the surrounding ki was nowhere near the scale of an entire world, but he was no longer an ordinary mortal.","Yumen Beiqing looked at Zu An with an unnatural expression. He has good skin.","Upon seeing him safe and sound, the Mermaid Queen cried out in delight.","Zu An belatedly noticed his two spectators. His face reddened, and he quickly took out a shirt and clothed himself. But before he could say a word, the clouds in the sky suddenly turned indigo.","He looked up and was shocked to see the tribulation clouds parting open. A giant indigo planet was falling from the sky toward him."]},{"number":2586,"title":"Chapter 2586: Chapter 2538: A Breakthrough","paragraphs":["The indigo planet resembled his previous life’s Earth. It was deep blue and looked beautiful.","Had he seen it under any other circumstances, Zu An would have been impressed, but to see such a huge planet crashing down on him amid his heavenly tribulation caused immense fear that couldn’t be explained with words.","He had heard the term ‘megalophobia’ in his previous life, but since he had already gotten used to seeing something huge whenever he went to relieve himself, he'd never thought that he could suffer from it. However, he now felt as if he was a megalophobia patient.","How insignificant was an individual before an entire planet?","He didn’t have the time to think about why the planet was falling on him, or why the planet he was on wasn’t affected by this celestial body. Rather, he was more anxious to figure how he could overcome this ordeal.","The Mermaid Queen stared at the massive indigo planet with a pale face. While she wasn’t the main target of it, when it came to something as huge as that, it didn’t make a difference.","“Do others face such trials in their heavenly tribulation too?” she asked, stunned.","Yumen Beiqing stared at the falling planet in utter shock as well. “I’ve never heard of anyone undergoing this in their heavenly tribulation. This is bizarre.”","However, she quickly snapped out of it and said, “No, that’s not a real planet. It’s just an illusion conjured by the heavenly tribulation. It’s probably targeted at the challenger and not us.” She was the Sun Goddess, after all. She could tell whether the planet was real or not.","“But what about big brother Zu?” The Mermaid Queen had many questions on her mind. “Why are big brother Zu’s tribulations so much tougher than those of others? How is he supposed to survive this?”","Yumen Beiqing fell silent. I have already helped him once. Should I help him again? Why am I even here at all? It’d be for the best if he died here, but why am I not as happy as I thought?","Zu An stared grimly at the descending planet. With a wave of his hand, the red Sun Slaying Bow appeared in his grasp. He nocked an arrow onto the bow and drew the bowstring. It was as if he had turned into the bow himself, his bulging muscles pulsating with strength.","The Mermaid Queen squealed in glee. “Big brother Zu’s bow is formidable! I can sense a destructive energy building up on the tip of his arrow.”","There was no response from Yumen Beiqing, so she turned around and was shocked to see the latter with a livid expression. Yumen Beiqing was trembling, and the hands hidden in her sleeves were clenched into fists.","The Mermaid Queen was startled. “Is big brother Zu in danger?”","“It would be best if that was the case!” Yumen Beiqing clenched her jaw. She had plotted all these events to change the future of Yi shooting down the suns. That was the very bow that killed her nine sons in history! How could she not be furious?","The days she'd spent with Zu An weren't enough for her to fall in love with him, but they had changed her impression of him. Yet the bow reminded her of the last time she'd seen him shooting down the suns. Back then, she'd sworn to kill him, but she'd almost forgotten about the vow she made back then.","The Mermaid Queen was stunned. She had no idea why Yumen Beiqing was reacting in such a manner. She seems to have a deep grudge against big brother Zu. Aren’t they lovers?","She thought that it could be a misunderstanding, so she didn’t dwell on it. At the same time, the massive congregation of white light on Zu An’s side drew her attention.","A white arrow was released, and it flew across the horizon like a shooting star. In the blink of an eye, it struck the indigo planet.","Pah!","The planet instantly unraveled, shattering into starlight that scattered all over the sky.","“He overcame the tribulation so easily?” The Mermaid Queen rubbed her eyes. She couldn’t believe that the other tribulations were so difficult, but the scariest one thus far was overcome with such ease.","Yumen Beiqing sneered, “It’s all because he has a good bow. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have stood a chance in this trial.”","“Saintess, you don’t seem happy about his victory,” the Mermaid Queen said carefully.","Yumen Beiqing simply looked at the tribulation clouds coldly without answering.","With the shattering of the indigo planet, the tribulation clouds billowed once more and slowly turned violet.","“Why does his heavenly tribulation have so many phenomena?” Yumen Beiqing fell into deep thought. The Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation had happened before, but it was never to this ridiculous extent.","Every tribulation Zu An had encountered thus far could easily be the most dangerous one for other people’s heavenly tribulation, yet he faced them one after another in succession.","All of a sudden, Yumen Beiqing froze up before sneering. I don’t care whether he lives or not! It would be best if he died here.","The violet tribulation clouds slowly parted to reveal a brilliant universe in the sky. The Mermaid Queen and Yumen Beiqing had seen the starry sky before, but they had never seen one as beautiful as this.","The sky suddenly tilted, and the stars began pouring down. However, each of these stars was actually a planet. It was utterly insane to have all these planets simultaneously crashing down on one person.","The Mermaid Queen was flabbergasted. She didn’t even ask Yumen Beiqing about it, as she thought that it wouldn’t make a difference no matter who she asked. Even a single planet was already a terrifying force to behold, but here, Zu An was up against the countless planets of the universe.","How could Zu An shoot down so many planets? Even a deity would be helpless before such a force, let alone a cultivator.","Yumen Beiqing looked grim too. She had never heard of such a heavenly tribulation. Even Dijun would have died for sure if he had encountered this heavenly tribulation back then, let alone her.","Meanwhile, Zu An was exceptionally calm. After overcoming six tribulations, his body and mind were now sharpened to the fullest. In the face of the falling planets, he emptied his mind, and his body slowly became ethereal before finally morphing into a black hole.","He wasn’t planning to absorb all these planets, however. Even a real black hole would explode if it were to absorb all the planets in the universe! Rather, he was hoping to become a part of the universe as well as a black hole.","Even though Yumen Beiqing wished for his death after seeing the Sun Slaying Bow, she couldn’t help but admire him for the solution he had come up with.","If only this man wasn’t an enemy...","Zu An had already emptied his mind and become a part of the universe. Witnessing the birth and destruction of the universe and countless planets, he gained a profound understanding of the world.","With that, he finally overcame his bottleneck!"]},{"number":2587,"title":"Chapter 2587: Chapter 2539: Seven-Colored Divine Halo","paragraphs":["The dangerous tribulation clouds morphed into colorful auspicious clouds, and the sky rained flower petals. These weren’t real petals, however, but immense aggregations of ki manifested in the shape of petals.","Bathing in them, Zu An felt his cells cheering in exuberance. He had never been immersed in such rich ki before. It was unlike the usual surrounding ki. It was much purer and more soothing. Every breath he took reminded him of the sensation he'd felt when he first drank the Feather Mountain Spring Water.","“Is this the legendary immortal ki?” Zu An wondered.","His body was undergoing a massive change. It had already surpassed those of ordinary cultivators, perhaps even exceeding those of dragons, due to him previously tempering his body with the Primordial Origin Sutra. But now, it was still growing stronger. It wasn't just a simple stats enhancement, but a metamorphosis. His skin shone with a faint luster reminiscent of the moonlight, and he felt as if every part of his body was resonating with the surrounding ki without the slightest impediment.","It was as if he had become a part of the world.","Zu An realized that he might have achieved the legendary ‘Indestructible Body’. Not only did he now boast incredible defensive prowess, his body could also regrow without limits as long as his soul remained intact.","He had no way of knowing for sure, but he didn’t think most deities had reached this level. At the very least, Er Fu, Wei Yueyan, and Gu hadn't.","Just then, Zu An heard a divine symphony. A golden celestial palace appeared in midair. Its doors slowly opened, and a golden light shone down on him.","He thought that it was yet another tribulation and was about to put up his guard when he sensed no danger from the golden light. On the contrary, it felt comfortable to be basked in it.","The distant Mermaid Queen asked Yumen Beiqing, “What’s that ray of golden light?”","Somehow, she trusted the judgment of this woman even though the latter was younger than her.","“Those who achieve immortality manifest divine halos. The more colors or the purer their divine halos are, the stronger they will be, and the greater their potential as well,” Yumen Beiqing replied while keeping a close eye on Zu An. She was curious how many colors the latter’s divine halo would have.","The Mermaid Queen thought about how the celestial named Qin had a tricolored divine halo and nodded in partial understanding.","Meanwhile, Zu An’s attention was on a phenomenon inside his body. He sensed a formation inside his mind slowly lighting up, forming a peacock imprint. He was overjoyed. He had cultivated the Phoenix Nirvana Sutra for many years, and he would usually unlock a divine bird ability with each major breakthrough. However, despite having made several breakthroughs, he hadn’t unlocked a new divine bird ability since the Kun Peng.","That had made him wonder if his skill was incomplete, and if it was impossible for him to reach the legendary ninth level. It was only now that he realized that the Phoenix Nirvana Sutra’s scaling was different from ordinary cultivator skills.","It was rumored that it was possible to achieve immortality through the Phoenix Nirvana Sutra, but who could have thought that it would be true?","He sensed circles of different colors forming around him. He was curious to know what ability he would receive from the peacock.","“Three, four, five... six, seven?!?!” Yumen Beiqing counted his divine halo colors in shock.","They had spent enough time together for her to know that Zu An was anything but ordinary. There was no way he would manifest just one or two colors for his divine halo when he became a deity. However, she hadn’t expected his divine halo to manifest that many colors!","Isn’t the limit for divine halo five colors? What the heck is a seven-colored divine halo?","It was also at this time that the Keyboard System’s voice echoed in Zu An’s head. “Congratulations on unlocking the Peacock’s ability. The five-colored divine halo allows you to neutralize anything within the Five Elements.”","Zu An’s breathing quickened. Could this be Master Kong Xuan’s Five-Colored Divine Halo from Investiture of the Gods? He could sweep through anyone except for the saints! Thanks to that ability, fans deem him the strongest character beneath the saints!","With this ability, I will be undefeatable!","Just then, the Keyboard System continued, “During the awakening of your ability, you underwent the legendary Seven-Colored Divine Tribulation, causing your Five-Colored Divine Halo to mutate with this world’s origin dao and become a Seven-Colored Divine Halo. You will have to uncover its ability by yourself.”","Zu An was stunned.","Huh? What’s going on? Where’s my Five-Colored Divine Halo? Give me back my Five-Colored Divine Halo!","Even though the Seven-Colored Divine Halo sounded more formidable, given that it had two more colors, there was no way to say whether it followed that logic for sure. What if his ability had become even weaker after the mutation?","There was no way he could be happy when a guaranteed god-level skill pick suddenly turned into another round of gacha draw, where he could end up getting something trashy instead.","However, there was nothing he could do. The only silver lining was that he had finally leveled up. He didn’t stop at level 80—the experience points he had accumulated all this time pushed his level all the way up to level 83! The experience points he needed for each level up had reached a terrifying amount, but fortunately, he had devoured many experts’ energy and had received an immense amount of ki from the heavenly tribulation.","“So this is what power feels like...” Zu An quivered in excitement as he felt the changes in his body. Not only was his ki many times stronger than before, even his grasp of energy had reached a completely new height. If he acquired the World Law Beacon once more, he would be able to exert far greater power than before.","“Big brother Zu, you have reached immortality?” the Mermaid Queen exclaimed in delight. She flew over, looking like she wanted to leap into his embrace, but was hesitant to do so.","Beside her was a conflicted-looking Yumen Beiqing.","“I think so.” Zu An looked at his hands. He still felt like he was in a dream.","“You smell really good now.” The Mermaid Queen’s face reddened.","“An immortal’s body is pure and impeccable. The heavenly tribulation has cleansed all filth; that’s why I smell good now. Do you want to come closer to smell it better?” Zu An regretted those words right away. Under normal circumstances, he would have avoided saying such suggestive words to the Mermaid Queen, but his breakthrough had made him overexcited.","The Mermaid Queen was moved, but with Yumen Beiqing around, she didn’t dare to go too far. Instead, she quickly changed the topic and asked, “Is there any difference now that you have achieved immortality?”","“Other than my deep grasp of ki, the way I see this world is also different now,\" Zu An replied.","Somehow, the world now looked much more vibrant to him. He could now clearly see many things that he 'd overlooked before, such as the wind trails and the flow of ki. He had gained a deeper insight into the fundamentals of the world.","The Mermaid Queen wanted to ask more questions, but Yumen Beiqing interjected, “How is your divine halo seven-colored? Does it have a special ability?”"]},{"number":2588,"title":"Chapter 2588: Chapter 2540: Vengeance","paragraphs":["Zu An was perplexed too. “I also don’t know what’s going on...”","Yumen Beiqing quickly added, “You should try releasing it to see what it’s capable of. The divine halo is extremely important for those who have reached immortality. You can think of it as a special domain that ensures complete domination against those without it. Even among deities, those with a stronger divine halo can suppress those with a weaker one.”","Zu An took her advice and unleashed his divine halo. Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet—his body was completely covered by seven-colored lights, so much so that it was impossible to make out his appearance.","Yumen Beiqing wanted to take a closer look when she and the Mermaid Queen suddenly disappeared in a flash.","Zu An frowned. He willed them to return. There was a flash of seven-colored light, and the two women returned to where they were.","The Mermaid Queen’s face gleamed with excitement. “I think I entered a seven-colored space earlier. I felt groggy, and I couldn’t move at all. Big brother Zu, how did you do it?”","In contrast, Yumen Beiqing looked horrified. Even though her guard was down, the thought that she could be so easily transported into another space chilled her heart.","“That could be the effect of my divine halo.” Zu An thought that this was similar to the effect of Master Kong Xuan’s Five-Colored Divine Halo in Investiture of the Gods[1]. So what’s the point of me having two more colors?","“You have a unique divine halo.” Yumen Beiqing seemed to have a lot on her mind.","“Little sister Ling’er, how do you know so much about deities?” Zu An was intrigued. Despite having become a deity himself, his understanding of deities was incomplete, yet the other party seemed to know far more than him.","Yumen Beiqing replied with a strained smile, “I learned about all these things through the Fiend races’ records, though I didn’t know whether they were true then.”","“I see.” Zu An thought that the records had to have been lost in time. He had never heard the future Fiend Empress mentioning them.","The Mermaid Queen widened her eyes in realization. No wonder the Saintess knows so much.","Zu An suddenly recalled something and exclaimed, “Oh no, Brother Yi was fighting with Gu earlier. I wonder what the situation on his side is.”","Yumen Beiqing looked conflicted. Zu An grabbed the two ladies and flew over to where Yi had been previously. A rainbow formed in his wake.","In the blink of an eye, they arrived where Yi and Gu had previously fought.","Zu An was stunned. How am I so fast? This distance should be beyond the limits of my instantaneous movement.","Yumen Beiqing was shocked. “Rainbow Morph!”","“What’s Rainbow Morph?” the Mermaid Queen asked in confusion.","“As its name suggests, it allows one to surge across the sky like a rainbow. This is a movement technique that only top powerhouses can pull off. It is exceptionally useful for escape.” Yumen Beiqing paused for a moment to stare at Zu An before adding, “But your earlier execution looks rough. If you master it fully, practically no one will be able to catch you.”","Zu An’s eyes lit up in delight. “I like this skill. I guess I’ll have to practice it more in the future.”","He eyed their surroundings before exclaiming, “Hm? Why don’t I see Brother Yi? That big snake is gone too.”","His tone was initially relaxed, but his expression slowly turned grim. Marks of Yi and Gu’s fight could be seen all around, from the collapsed trees to the blood splattered all over the mountain. Judging from the scales mixed into the blood, Zu An could deduce that Yi had claimed the upper hand in the battle.","But why did the battle suddenly halt?","Zu An stopped before a giant pit. The nearby trees were bent, and the nearby stones had been reduced to rubble. Marks of struggle could be seen on the ground. Judging from these clues, he could form a picture of what had happened then. Yi had to have been riding on Gu’s body, beating him up, but something suddenly happened that caused Yi to stop.","He soon moved to another spot in the distance. Heat lingered in the surroundings, and the nearby stones and dirt on the ground had crystallized. There had to have been an intense blast of heat earlier.","“Big brother Zu, did you notice something?” the Mermaid Queen walked up to Zu An and asked.","“Brother Yi might be dead,” Zu An said grimly. As the lord of the underworld, he was extremely sensitive to death, and he could feel an aura of death looming. The vibrant fire ki lingering in the vicinity didn’t belong to Yi, so there had to have been a third party here.","Yumen Beiqing’s eyes widened. It went without saying that she knew what had happened here, but she hadn’t expected Zu An to be so sharp as to figure out the situation despite Dijun erasing his trail and destroying the corpse.","“Did you see anything earlier?” Zu An asked the two ladies. Earlier, he'd been focused on dealing with the heavenly tribulation, so he hadn’t had the energy to observe his surroundings.","“There was a ray of golden light here earlier, then a terrifying aura descended. However, it quickly disappeared afterward.” The Mermaid Queen felt apologetic that she wasn’t of much use. “I was too focused on you, so I didn’t pay attention to this place.”","Yumen Beiqing noticed Zu An’s gaze falling on her and replied, “It’s the same for me as well. I was too focused on you. We were also too far away to keep an eye on Yi.”","Had it been any other circumstance, she wouldn’t have minded exposing Dijun. Despite being a couple, the two of them were already estranged anyway. The problem was that she would risk exposing her true identity, and she was worried that Zu An’s wrath would implicate her sons along with Dijun...","All of a sudden, her face paled. Could that be the reason he shot the suns in history?","She tried to console herself. No no, that’s not right. Yi is already dead. History might have changed.","Zu An stared at the crystallized ground. A golden light. Strong fire ki. Capable of overpowering Yi. Could it be...","Seeing his contemplative look, Yumen Beiqing quickly interjected, “This matter should have nothing to do with us, and it might be good news too. The Mermaid Queen has taken the identity of the Chang clan’s Saintess, Chang’e, which means that she is betrothed to Yi. Now that things have unfolded the way they did, we don’t have to worry about that anymore.”","The Mermaid Queen frowned. “I don’t want to marry him, but I didn’t wish for his death either.”","“Indeed.” Zu An nodded. “Brother Yi intervened to save us. We're indebted to him. If not for him, I could have been the one to die here. I have to avenge him!”","“But how can we avenge him when we don’t even know who our enemy is?” the Mermaid Queen asked worriedly.","Zu An fell into deep thought. Behind him, Yumen Beiqing narrowed her eyes as the fingers hidden beneath her sleeves gradually turned sharp.","1. Kong Xuan had five different rays of light that would sweep his enemy into a void. ☜"]},{"number":2589,"title":"Chapter 2589: Chapter 2541: Marriage","paragraphs":["While pondering about this issue, Zu An told the Mermaid Queen, “I intend to first return to Wu Mountain to inform the Kaiming Six Shamans and the Goddess of Wu Mountain about Bao Jiang’s death. They're Bao Jiang’s friends, so I reckon they should have a way to redress his grievance. The Celestial Court will have to investigate this matter, and they should figure out who Yi’s murderer is in the process. If the Celestial Court refuses to punish Yi’s murderer, I’ll do it on their behalf.”","By now, Yumen Beiqing was ready to make a move. Looking at Zu An from behind, she could tell that he wasn’t on his guard. He wouldn’t have time to unleash his bizarre Seven-Colored Divine Halo. If she went all out, there was a chance that she could kill him in a single strike.","But looking at him from the side, she was reminded of the time they had spent together, and that made her hesitate. The real Yi is dead. Do I have to kill him over a mere possibility? But why did I see him shoot the suns back then... Something must have gone wrong in history!","As she thought about her sons, her expression stiffened. She discreetly positioned her finger behind Zu An’s head, and she was about to make a move when footsteps suddenly became audible.","As Zu An turned around, Yumen Beiqing anxiously retracted her hand and pretended to turn around as well to look in the direction of the footsteps.","A group of people resembling the barbarians from TV dramas emerged from the nearby forest. Their bodies were mostly exposed, revealing their bulging muscles. They were far more muscular than most humans.","Unlike barbarians, however, their clothes were exquisite. Primitive tribes wouldn’t be capable of weaving such beautiful textiles.","They first assessed the three of them before their gaze finally fell on the Mermaid Queen. “Saintess!” They quickly rushed over and danced in delight. “We have finally found you, Saintess!”","When he saw them rushing over, Zu An was initially wary of them, but their words surprised him. He instinctively turned to the Mermaid Queen.","The Mermaid Queen looked back at him with an awkward smile as she softly explained, “They are from the Chang clan.”","Zu An nodded in realization. So they think that the Mermaid Queen is Chang’e.","“Chieftain, you’re mistaken! I am not Chang’e,” the Mermaid Queen explained.","The old man leading the group looked at the Mermaid Queen sternly. “Saintess, what nonsense are you spouting? How can so many of us mistake you for someone else? We took turns carrying you while you were younger. I know that you are reluctant to marry a fiancé you have never seen before, but this was a promise our clans made a long time ago. The Youqiong clan might have fallen from grace, but we can’t turn our backs on them!”","The Mermaid Queen was usually eloquent, but she had no idea how to explain this situation. Was she to tell them that she'd transmigrated here?","Putting aside whether she could convince them of it or not, she also had to take into consideration that this world had deities and the Celestial Court. If they were to learn that it was possible to travel across spacetime, they could decide to capture the group for research. It wasn't a risk worth taking.","Seeing her panic, Zu An took a step forward and said, “Elder, I’m afraid that there’s a little hiccup here. It might not be possible for your Saintess to marry Yi anymore.”","The old chieftain was stunned. “What do you mean?”","Zu An told him what had happened here together with his deductions.","The old chieftain’s orange-skinned face showed many interesting expressions. “Bao Jiang and Gu... Should we be hearing these secrets?! How did Yi get roped into this matter? We’re done for... It’s all over!”","Zu An was confused. Why is he reacting so dramatically? Is Bao Jiang so powerful that it frightens even a chieftain like him?","All of a sudden, the old chieftain kneeled on the ground Yi had died on and pinched some of the crystallized stones. His expression slowly turned grim. “This is...”","“Chieftain!” The other Chang clansmen quickly stopped him from speaking further.","The old chieftain raised his head and alternated his gaze between the Mermaid Queen and Zu An. He couldn’t help but notice how unnecessarily close they were standing to each other, and he narrowed his eyes. “Saintess, is he the reason you don’t want to marry your fiancé?”","“Ah?” The Mermaid Queen’s face reddened. There was nothing wrong with those words, but there was just something about the phrasing that felt off.","Zu An helped her answer the question, “Elder, we're good friends. I won’t let her marry someone she doesn’t want to. Besides, that’s not the point here. Brother Yi has already...”","Before he could finish his sentence, the old chieftain raised his hand to stop him. “Young man, do you wish to marry Chang’e?”","“Chieftain!” The Mermaid Queen stomped her feet shyly. “It’s not like that between us!” She was worried that big brother Zu would misunderstand that she was exploiting this situation to coerce him. That’s not my intention at all!","The old chieftain harrumphed as he closely assessed Zu An. “You eloped for him. Shouldn’t he do something for you too?”","“But...” The Mermaid Queen wanted to explain the matter, but Zu An stopped her and gently smiled.","“Of course I’m willing to marry her,\" he said, thinking this was a good opportunity to resolve the Mermaid Queen’s marriage issue once and for all.","A mini explosion broke out in the Mermaid Queen’s head, and she fell completely still. It was hard to tell whether it was out of excitement or shock.","Yumen Beiqing looked at Zu An in scorn. This fellow is so lecherous.","As she looked at the man she loved with adoring eyes, the Mermaid Queen blushed furiously. Regardless of his intent, those words were more than enough for her.","“Good, good!” The chieftain asked, “Which major clan are you from?”","“I’m not from any major clans.” Zu An figured it wouldn’t be easy to explain his identity in this era.","“Do you have any masters?” the chieftain further probed.","“I’m afraid not.” Zu An figured he couldn’t tell the chieftain about Mi Li when he didn’t even know her true identity.","“That’s wonderful!” The chieftain clapped his hand in delight.","Zu An was speechless.","The chieftain loudly declared, “What a coincidence! On top of finding the Saintess, we have also found Yi! And it turns out they have feelings for each other! What joyous news!”","Everyone was speechless.","Someone from the Chang clan whispered doubtfully, “Chieftain, are you sure he’s Yi? They don’t look alike.”","Not many people had seen Yi when he came to ask for Chang’e’s hand in marriage, but there were still a number of people who had seen him.","The chieftain nodded affirmatively. “Of course! I personally received him back then. There can be no mistake about this!”","Some remained doubtful, but they swallowed down their words of skepticism. The majority, who had never met the real Yi, quickly offered words of congratulations.","Zu An stared at the chieftain in absolute shock. “Chieftain, I’m not...”","Before he could finish speaking, the chieftain pulled him to the side and whispered, “This is the only way you can marry Chang’e. There’s an old prophecy in the Chang clan stating that the Saintess Chang’e can only marry Yi!”","Zu An was so shocked that he didn’t notice Yumen Beiqing’s trembling body. Her hands and feet had turned cold, and her eyes blazed with killing intent."]},{"number":2590,"title":"Chapter 2590: Chapter 2542: Condition","paragraphs":["Yumen Beiqing had never thought that there would be such a twist in the situation. She had gone back in time to change some important events in history in hopes of changing the fate of the ten suns being shot down. \\And yet, she realized that no matter what she did, every major event along the way had still happened.","She had already fallen into despair when she stumbled upon the legendary Yi, but then the latter actually died here. For a moment, she'd felt hope. Even when Zu An vowed to avenge Yi and she began feeling a tinge of unease, she'd still remained optimistic on the whole.","Yet this Chang clan’s chieftain had just proposed for Zu An to become Yi, making her feel goosebumps. In truth, she had been confused as to why she had seen Zu An as Yi in history when he clearly wasn’t Yi, but now, the answer was finally apparent to her.","It turned out that she hadn’t changed anything at all. Remembering everything she had done along the way gave her a profound sense of helplessness.","Zu An was flabbergasted too. “This won’t do...”","The old chieftain gestured for his clansmen to wait on the spot before leading Zu An and the others elsewhere. As soon as they were out of the sight of the Chang clansmen, the chieftain dropped to his knees in front of Zu An.","“What are you doing, chieftain?! Please, get up!” Zu An was bewildered.","The Mermaid Queen also rushed forward to pull the old chieftain to her feet. The latter had treated her well while she was in the Chang clan.","“I’ll kneel here forever if you refuse to accept my request!” The old chieftain looked at Zu An with a stubborn expression.","Zu An was silent. He didn’t like how the latter was threatening him here, so he waved his hand and supported the chieftain back up with gentle but firm force.","The chieftain was shocked to realize that Zu An was so unfathomably powerful. He wasn't the Chang clan’s chieftain for no reason. If he refused to get up, most people wouldn’t be able to move him. “Do you find my actions laughable?” he asked. Seeing through Zu An’s thoughts, he sighed. “I didn’t want to do this either, but I guess I have no choice but to be honest with you now. It’s not that we old fogeys obstinately want Chang’e to marry someone she doesn’t love, but this matter concerns an old prophecy. Our Chang clan’s greatest priest once prophesied that our clan would one day encounter a crisis that might spell the end of our clan. Only the matrimony of a saintess named Chang’e and a Youqiong clan hero named Yi could resolve this disaster.”","Zu An frowned, replying, “That’s pure superstition. How can a clan’s rise and fall be tied to a single individual? And for the man and the woman to be so specifically named at that!”","“You can’t say that!” The chieftain anxiously waved his hand. “He’s our Chang clan’s greatest priest. His prophecies have always been accurate. We were initially skeptical too. How can someone from a long time ago know that we'd have a clanswoman named Chang’e, and the Youqiong clan would coincidentally have a clansman named Yi in the same generation?”","A hint of fear appeared on the chieftain’s face as he continued, “But fifteen years ago, a clanswoman of ours returned severely injured. Before she died, she gave birth to a child, and not knowing about the prophecy, she named her child Chang’e.”","He sighed. “Do you know how shocked we elders were when we first heard the name? We initially shrugged it off as a coincidence, though we sent someone to the Youqiong clan to check on things. Little did we expect there to truly be a young man named Yi on their side too. Furthermore, he carried a token similar to Chang’e’s. A Youqiong clan elder said that his father had betrothed him to another woman, and the other token was with his future fiancée.”","Noticing the old chieftain’s gaze, the Mermaid Queen reached for her waist token, which resembled the Deep Sea Harp. “This...”","The old chieftain scoured the crystallized grounds where Yi had died and found a token in it. This token was identical to the one the Mermaid Queen carried; the two complemented each other! The Mermaid Queen instinctively grabbed it and put them together.","They were a perfect fit!","She suddenly fell into a daze. It was said that she'd had this token in her mouth when she was born, and it was later discovered to be a special artifact—it could transform into the Deep Sea Harp. Thanks to that, she was viewed as the unquestionable successor of the Mermaid Queen.","When they called her their Saintess, she'd thought that the Chang clan had gotten the wrong person, but it appeared now that she had some ties with Chang’e after all.","Zu An took the two tokens. Individually, they were Deep Sea Harps, but when put together, they formed a complete round moon. It reminded him of the legends surrounding Chang’e and the moon, and his eyes widened.","The chieftain continued, “When I heard about Yi’s death, I fell into despair. I couldn’t watch the Chang clan being destroyed like that, which is why I came up with this ploy.” Noticing Zu An’s silence, he turned to the Mermaid Queen and asked, “Chang’e, has our clan treated you well over the years?”","“Yes, the clan has treated me well.” The Mermaid Queen pursed her lips. From her residence and environment, which had been arranged down to the fine details, she could tell that Chang’e had to have been pampered like a princess.","“Since that’s the case, I humbly ask you to save our clan in view of that!” The chieftain began to kneel to her and kowtow.","The horrified Mermaid Queen quickly supported him back up. She then walked over to Zu An’s side and whispered, “Big brother Zu, what do we do now?”","Zu An spent a moment in thought before replying, “Let me ask a few more questions.” He turned to the old chieftain and said, “It’s not that easy to impersonate someone. A few people in your Chang clan have already met Brother Yi, and his own clan can’t possibly mistake him for me.”","He could use his Myriad Transformations to assume Yi’s appearance, but he didn’t want to marry the Mermaid Queen in the form of another man.","The old chieftain was overjoyed to hear Zu An’s tone softening. “Don’t worry. Not many in the Chang clan know his true identity, and I have my ways to curb them. As for the Youqiong clan, Yi’s remaining kin died while he was on his way to our Chang clan. He was the only one left in the Youqiong clan. There’s no one to expose you.","“But I heard that in order to become qualified for Chang’e. Yi has made a resounding name for himself over the years. There are many in the world who recognize him,” Zu An said. Considering how Yi had even triumphed over Celestial Gu, the chances were that his reputation had spread far and wide.","The old chieftain replied, “I have been keeping an eye on Yi over the years. Most of his battles were just small squabbles; the more reputable powers don’t know him. Besides, your physique and disposition resemble his. With a bit of disguise, you should be able to fool most people.” Once again, he bowed to Zu An and said, “I implore you to save our clan in view of your ties with Chang’e and Yi.”","Zu An found those words weird. Does marrying Yi’s fiancée count as helping him?","He quickly expelled that thought from his mind. This is the Mermaid Queen, not Yi’s fiancée Chang’e.","Sensing Zu An’s hesitation, the old chieftain added, “Don’t you want to know who Yi’s murderer is? I found a clue about that.”","“Oh?” Zu An quickly asked about it, only to be met with the old chieftain’s enigmatic smile. Clearly, the latter would only talk if he accepted his conditions. In the end, he nodded and said, “I’ll accept your terms.”","The old chieftain was overjoyed. He quickly called his clansmen over. “Come, escort the Saintess and our son-in-law back!”","The Chang clansmen danced in joy, delivering their own earnest blessings. Many of their younger clansmen looked at Zu An with envy. All of them were fond of the beautiful Chang’e.","Zu An took this opportunity to ask the old chieftain about the murderer. The old chieftain slyly blinked and said, “I’ll tell you after you get married.”","Zu An was speechless."]},{"number":2591,"title":"Chapter 2591: Chapter 2543: I’m Willing","paragraphs":["This chieftain is such a sly dog! As if I’d renege on my promise if he told me in advance. I can’t possibly torture the chieftain just because he’s unwilling to speak, right?","While Zu An was dumbstruck, the old chieftain had already called his clansmen over and tossed an artifact on the ground.","To Zu An’s bewilderment, the artifact was an orange, club-like object. No matter how I look at it... In’t this a carrot?","The carrot instantly grew many times until it became enormous. The Chang clansmen ushered Zu An and the Mermaid Queen onto it.","Judging from the formation pulsating from the carrot, Zu An could tell that it was a flying artifact. He suddenly recalled Yumen Beiqing and beckoned her over. “Little sister Ling’er, come here.”","But Yumen Beiqing had an awful expression. She stared at him coldly.","Zu An thought to himself that no woman wouldn’t be upset to see her lover marrying another woman. While they were in another world, it wouldn’t be good for there to be a conflict between them now. If they lost each other here, he would regret it for life.","So, he walked over and grabbed her hand. He was shocked by how cold it was. He quickly sent her a telepathic message, “Little sister Ling’er, this is just a temporary measure to resolve the current issue. Don’t pay it any mind.”","Yumen Beiqing scoffed, “Do you really have to be Yi?”","Zu An was taken aback. Held thought that she was angry because he was marrying Chang’e, but it turned out that she was angry because he was becoming Yi?","He thought about it and figured that she could just be finding another excuse to grumble about this issue, so as to not directly offend the Mermaid Queen. After all, he wouldn’t be able to marry the Mermaid Queen if he wasn’t Yi.","“Brother Yi died while helping me. I have to get to the bottom of Brother Yi’s murder, so I have no choice but to accept the chieftain’s request first,” he explained. At the same time, he was intrigued by Yumen Beiqing’s temperament. It’s unusual for the gentle little sister Ling’er to react in such a way.","Upon hearing his answer, Yumen Beiqing’s expression turned even colder, but she didn’t shake free of his grip and instead followed him onto the carrot.","The enlarged carrot had plenty of space for dozens of people. It was unknown how the chieftain controlled it, but it rose into the air and shot forth like a rocket. The people on the carrot didn’t even feel the wind blowing against them; it was extremely stable.","Zu An was amazed by the artifact-forging skills of the seemingly primitive Chang clan.","The old chieftain walked over and assessed Yumen Beiqing. “Our son-in-law, who is this lady?”","Quite a few youths also looked at Zu An with hostile gazes.","“She’s my little sister,” Zu An replied. A second later, he added, “As well as my lover.”","The youths initially sneered. What little sister? See how tightly you’re holding each other’s hands! There must be something more between the two of you.","Who could have thought that Zu An would admit their relationship outright? That further stoked their anger, and they complained, “Audacious! Why are you flirting with our Saintess when you already have other women?”","“Aren’t you being too greedy right now?!”","...","Looking at the surge of Rage points in his system, Zu An also felt distressed. It showed just how well-respected Chang’e was as the Chang clan’s Saintess.","The chieftain quickly raised his hand to stop the crowd. “Son-in-law, you are betrothed to our Saintess. I’m afraid you can’t get together with other women...”","Before the chieftain could finish speaking Zu An interjected, “Little sister Ling’er and I have mutual feelings for each other. I can’t do anything as heartless as abandoning her!”","His words further angered the Chang clan’s youths. Many roared for the engagement to be annulled, and in the blink of an eye, Zu An received over 100,000 Rage points.","Yumen Beiqing looked at the man standing in front of her calmly. Had it been in the past, she would probably be moved by his attitude, but now...","The Mermaid Queen stepped forward to stop the crowd. “Don’t put him in a tough spot! He knew big sister Ling’er first...”","She directed an apologetic glance at Yumen Beiqing. Even though she was very fond of big brother Zu, she knew she was the third wheel here. Ever since she first found out, she'd thought that there was no chance between her and big brother Zu anymore. She would already be very satisfied even if this was just a marriage in name only. She didn’t want to harm anyone else, and she didn’t want big brother Zu to misunderstand her too.","Seeing their beautiful Saintess protect Zu An made the Chang clan’s youths go mad with envy. Once again, they contributed another huge wave of Rage points.","The chieftain stepped forward to resolve the situation. “Hahaha, our son-in-law is indeed a sentimental person. I can only marry Chang’e off to someone as reliable as you!”","The other clansmen were flabbergasted. “But he already has another woman! How can he marry our Saintess on top of that?”","“It’s normal for a man to have multiple wives.” The chieftain was unfazed. “Don’t I have multiple wives too?”","The other clansmen couldn’t refute that, but some indignant ones argued, “Even so, our Saintess has to be the main wife! The other woman can only be the concubine!” They even directed a taunting look at Yumen Beiqing right after.","Yumen Beiqing sneered. Her killing intent started to flare.","The chieftain stepped forward to mediate. “What do you mean by main wife and concubine? It’s only natural to treat all wives the same!”","Seeing that some of the clansmen still wanted to stir up trouble, the old chieftain angrily hollered, “That’s a matter between them! They don’t need outsiders like you to worry about their affairs. Stop running your mouth here and focus on the upcoming wedding!”","The Chang clansmen were dumbfounded.","Zu An understood where the chieftain was coming from. His impersonation of Yi was a desperate attempt to save the Chang clan from doom. If this marriage was ruined, the chieftain wouldn’t be able to face his ancestors.","The ‘carrot’ flew extremely fast and soon arrived at the Chang clan manor.","Zu An looked at the Chang manor and was shocked by the fanfare beneath. There were red lanterns and congratulatory red papers plastered everywhere. He asked, “Has there been a joyous event in your clan recently?”","“What are you saying? It’s your wedding with Chang’e! Today is an auspicious day. There is no better time for you two to get married!” the chieftain said as he gleefully stroked his goatee.","Zu An was dumbfounded.","Yumen Beiqing was dumbstruck too. Why are they in such a hurry?","The Mermaid Queen’s face reddened. She secretly glanced at Zu An with a mix of embarrassment and nervousness.","Many youths who had a crush on her felt their hearts shattering into pieces.","The ‘carrot’ landed in the Changmanor. A large group of Chang clansmen rushed up to Zu An and the Mermaid Queen to escort them to private rooms and doll them up. Before they knew it, they were already wearing wedding outfits.","A pleasant harp melody drifted to Zu An’s room before turning into the Mermaid Queen’s voice. “Big brother Zu, please don’t feel burdened. We’re doing this to uncover the culprit. This isn’t a true marriage.”","The Mermaid Queen would have preferred to personally explain things to Zu An, but due to her history of escaping from the marriage, the Chang clan was more uptight than usual. Nearly all the Chang clan’s ladies were gathered in her room to doll her up; there was no chance for her to slip out at all. She could only play the harp to relay her words.","She was happy enough to have this wedding, even if it was all fake...","Zu An was initially hesitant, but after hearing the melancholic tinge and overwhelming feelings contained in the harp melody, he made up his mind. “Why should it be a mere show? If we’re going to marry, let’s make it the real thing. Or are you unwilling to marry me?”","“Ah?” Happiness came so fast that the Mermaid Queen’s mind was hurled into a tailspin. She wasn't a young, demure girl anymore, and she knew that she had to grasp the perhaps fleeting happiness presented to her. Thus, she replied, “I’m willing!”","They had kept a distance from each other because they were from different periods in spacetime and didn’t have a future together. But since they were both strangers to this world, she figured that they might as well have a passionate romance in this foreign world.","While their feelings were ripening, Yumen Beiqing stood on the rooftop, looking at the joyous atmosphere that had suffused the Chang clan. Her face darkened.","These damned people deserve to die!"]},{"number":2592,"title":"Chapter 2592: Chapter 2544: Something Happened","paragraphs":["Zu An was dressed up by the people around him like a puppet. He had never thought that marriage could be this complicated. In particular, the bridegroom's robe was astoundingly complicated. All kinds of gold accessories were put on him. If not for him being stronger than ordinary humans, he would have been crushed under their sheer weight.","He had heard from the Chang clansmen that the more accessories the bridegroom wore, the more earnest he was in marrying the bride. Since this symbolized the Chang clan’s sincerity, he respected their tradition and went along with whatever they wanted.","Soon, it was evening. He was dragged out for the marriage rites.","Much to his surprise, the marriage rites weren't conducted inside a room, but rather at a square. Chang clansmen, from the old to the young, were gathered in the square, each dressed in celebratory clothes. The women had beaming smiles as they eyed Zu An with curiosity.","In contrast, the men looked depressed. They glared at Zu An with envious and hateful eyes.","Looking at the Rage points surging into his system, Zu An was awed by the Mermaid Queen, or rather Chang’e’s, popularity once more. Do they like her that much? We’re getting married. Shouldn’t they let it go?","A few of them tried to screw with him while dressing up, but Zu An was no longer the type of person to lose his temper at a couple of youths.","Just then, he heard exclamations. A commotion broke out among the youths as they turned to look in the same direction.","The crowd opened up, and a beautiful figure slowly emerged under the support of the Chang clan’s ladies. Her figure looked like a sculpted masterpiece. Not even the majestic bridal clothes could conceal her beautiful curves. Her waist lightly swayed as she walked, bringing a spring breeze to the hearts of the youths and elders present. The crowd was mesmerized.","In the Chang clan’s traditions, the bride wore a tiara with bead curtains obscuring her face instead of a red veil. This made her look even more alluring. Her fair skin, contrasted against her red bridal gown, looked so dewy that it could leak water. She shyly eyed Zu An with eyes overflowing with bliss.","When Zu An met her gaze, he felt as if flowers had blossomed all over the world. Even the moon wanes in shame when compared against such beauty. Idioms to describe beauty surfaced in his head, but he lamented his lacking literary ability to relay just how enchanted he was.","Before they knew it, they were already standing before each other. The thought of being a couple with her loved one filled the Mermaid Queen with so much bliss that she didn’t think there was a need for her to return to her previous world anymore. This is fine too.","Zu An looked at the blush on her fair skin, which looked as if someone had applied a layer of rouge on smooth jade. What beauty.","The old chieftain hosted the ceremony. Marriage ceremonies in this era were much simpler. There was no need to bow to the heaven and the earth; the only one they had to pay respect to was Lady Houtu.","It could be her overthinking it, but when she was paying respect to the latter, the Mermaid Queen seemed to see a smile on Lady Houtu’s face.","Zu An couldn’t help but think that Lady Houtu’s standing in the Shaman races was much higher than that of the other Ancestral Shamans.","Next, they paid respect to their respective clans’ totems.","The Chang clan’s totem was a full moon. Zu An thought that explained the pictures of full moons throughout the Chang clan. He was reminded of the legend regarding Chang’e and the moon and frowned. I wonder if Chang’e will elope to the moon in this world.","The Youqiong clan’s totem was a giant bow. Known for their archery prowess, they naturally worshiped the bow and arrow. That wasn't too surprising.","Zu An thought the next step was for the couple to bow to each other, but that wasn't part of the rites. Instead, the two of them were told to link their hands together and dance for the crowd.","Being asked to dance before a crowd all of a sudden was extremely awkward, but fortunately, the Mermaid Queen was highly skilled at dancing. She naturally guided him to the campfire at the center of the square and began dancing. Cheers erupted from the crowd.","Feeling the Mermaid Queen’s tender eyes and the vibrant atmosphere, Zu An gradually immersed himself in the dance and matched her movements impeccably.","That drove the atmosphere to a new high. Young men began approaching the ladies they were interested in to ask them for a dance. Joy radiated from the entire Chang clan.","After the dance, the Mermaid Queen was escorted into the consummation room. Zu An wanted to follow her there, as there were too many things he wanted to say to her.","However, the Chang clan’s youths didn’t let him off the hook and swarmed him with toasts instead.","Zu An was at a loss for words. It was one thing for the men to hinder him out of jealousy, but why were the women joining the commotion too? Some of the bolder ones even used intoxication as an excuse to throw themselves at him and touch him. He would have exploded in rage had he not known that the Chang clan meant no malice.","One bowl after another, he drank a lot of wine. The Chang clan’s wine was much stronger than anything he had ever drunk before. He secretly used his ki to expel the alcohol from his system, but even so, he still remained mildly intoxicated. These wines were made for cultivators; if not for him having undergone the heavenly tribulation, he would have been knocked out here.","One after another, the Chang clan’s youths collapsed after having drunk too much.","Zu An was finally free. He first looked for the mildly intoxicated chieftain to ask about Yi’s murderer, but the latter replied with a chuckle, “Today is a joyous occasion. Let’s not talk about inauspicious things. Go to the consummation room. I’ll talk to you tomorrow.”","The chieftain then continued chatting up a group of older women with thick makeup, making them burst into laughter.","Black streaks appeared on Zu An’s face. This old fellow is so wild... Looks like he’s still worried about me turning my back on the Chang clan after learning about the culprit. He wants to make sure that the deal is sealed first. Knowing that the Mermaid Queen was waiting for him in the consummation room, his mind heated up. He decided to stop holding back and make his way there.","When he opened the door, the Mermaid Queen was sitting upright on the bed. His staggering movements prompted her to quickly rush over to support him. “Why did you drink so much?”","“Those men went all out to make me drunk because they don’t want me to share the night with their dream lover. Too bad they underestimated me,” Zu An said gleefully. But as he leaned on the Mermaid Queen’s soft body, he suddenly felt drunk once more.","“Suyin, you’re so beautiful,” he said as he gently pried open her bead curtains.","The Mermaid Queen averted her gaze out of shyness. “Are you still going to call me Suyin now...”","Zu An understood what she was getting at. “My wife!”","“My husband~” The Mermaid Queen’s voice was coy and sugary sweet.","It numbed Zu An’s mind. Unable to take it anymore, he leaned in for a kiss.","As she lay weakly in his arms, the Mermaid Queen moaned.","All their previous hesitations about them being from different worlds and not having a future together were tossed to the back of their minds. Right now, they just wanted to vent the passion in their hearts and become one.","After kissing for a long time, Zu An’s hands began scaling the snowy mountain to explore the scenery that countless experts only dreamed about. As his hands slid down to her belt, however, he suddenly thought of something and stopped. It looked as if he was going to retract his hand.","The Mermaid Queen grabbed his hand and quietly looked at him with a reddened face.","She didn’t have to say a word; her gaze said it all. Zu An cast aside his final sliver of hesitation and lightly tugged on the belt, causing her red bridal gown to unravel like a blossoming rose, revealing the most beautiful sight in the world.","Zu An’s breathing quickened. The two of them naturally embraced...","A dull harrumph suddenly echoed. Zu An immediately straightened up and vigilantly looked outside the window.","“What’s wrong?” The Mermaid Queen shyly tugged his arm, not knowing why he had suddenly stopped at this juncture. For a moment there, she even doubted her own charm. How could he stop now? Am I that unattractive? Do I have to take the initiative each time? But it’s so embarrassing!","She consoled herself by thinking about how intimate they already were. She could already feel the manifestation of his lust. It can’t be because of my lack of charm. Could he be concerned about something else?","Ah, now that I think about it, I haven’t seen the Fiend races’ Saintess. Is it because of her...","While she was feeling disheartened, Zu An took a deep breath and said, “Something happened!”"]},{"number":2593,"title":"Chapter 2593: Chapter 2545: Misunderstanding","paragraphs":["“What happened?” The Mermaid Queen’s mind turned blank.","Zu An quickly draped her bridal gown over her body. “Quick, put on your clothes. Something seems to have happened to the Chang clan.”","The situation outside unnerved him, but he didn’t dare to leave the Mermaid Queen alone in here, fearing that something could happen to her. His grim expression relayed the severity of the situation to the Mermaid Queen. Her lust faded, and she quickly put on her clothes. Only then did Zu An lead her out of the room.","The Mermaid Queen took a sniff, and her expression warped in shock. “Blood stench!”","The Mermaid race revered nature, so they were exceptionally sensitive toward such smells.","Zu An didn’t say a word. He grabbed her hand and led her outside to further investigate the situation. Several ladies were sprawled in the courtyard; these were the people who had escorted the Mermaid Queen into the consummation room earlier. They were beautiful, but all of them had stopped breathing.","“They're dead?!” The Mermaid Queen was appalled. It was not long ago that these people were cheerfully dolling her up, and some even teased her about Zu An. It was shocking to see them as corpses just hours later. Tears brimmed in her eyes.","Zu An nodded grimly. He continued heading out to investigate the situation. Most of the Chang clansmen had been gathered in the square. It was still bustling there when he slipped off to the consummation room, and youths had still been dancing merrily together.","But by the time he arrived there, the whole place had fallen silent. All that could be heard was the crackling of burning firewood. The Chang clansmen were sprawled out on chairs, tables, and the ground. There was a strong alcohol smell in the air. Were it not for what they'd seen earlier, perhaps they'd have just shrugged it off as the Chang clan being drunk. But now, this silence just felt eerie.","Zu An inspected some of their bodies; they had no pulse.","Soon, he found the old chieftain. He was lying amid a couple of older women, and they were embracing one another comfortably. But there wasn't the slightest smile on his face. His face was twisted in fear as if he had seen something utterly horrifying.","The Mermaid Queen squatted down to check their pulse. Soon, her face twisted in shock. “Why are they all dead? What happened?”","“I don’t know either.” Zu An’s face clouded over. He had already spread his divine sense, and there didn’t seem to be a single survivor in the Chang clan.","Even though he'd been distracted by the consummation, given his current cultivation, it should have been impossible for someone to kill all the Chang clansmen without alerting him... unless they all died at the same time, leaving him no time to react.","But who could possibly do that?","His expression suddenly warped in shock. “This is bad!”","He began scouring the Chang clan as he got increasingly anxious.","“What’s wrong, hubby?” The Mermaid Queen followed him.","“Little sister Ling’er is missing!” Zu An’s heart sank. Given that the Chang clansmen were all dead, it was unlikely that Yumen Beiqing was still alive. He didn’t dare to entertain that thought, however.","The Mermaid Queen was stunned as well. If something happened to the Fiend races’ Saintess here, she would be a sinner. However, she didn’t lose her bearing and quickly took charge of the situation. “It’s also good news in a way that we haven’t found the Saintess’. Let’s continue searching together.”","Zu An understood what she was saying. As long as they hadn’t found Yumen Beiqing’s corpse, there was hope. He continued searching the premises while expanding his divine sense.","All of a sudden, he grabbed the Mermaid Queen and flew eastward. They soon arrived at the entrance of town, where they saw Yumen Beiqing slowly returning from outside.","Relieved, Zu An rushed forward to embrace her. “Where did you go earlier?”","Yumen Beiqing didn’t expect such a forceful embrace. She instinctively tried to push him aside, but it was to no avail. In the end, she coldly replied, “I don’t need to report my whereabouts to you.”","“Of course you don’t have to. I’m just glad that you’re safe and sound.” The feeling of having found someone he thought he had lost filled Zu An with relief. He had been seriously worried about the worst-case scenario earlier.","“Saintess, something huge happened on our side. The Chang clansmen are all dead,” the Mermaid Queen helped to explain. She wasn't angry to see the two of them hugging each other; she was only glad to see Yumen Beiqing safe.","“Oh?” Yumen Beiqing’s response was surprisingly calm.","The Mermaid Queen frowned. She was extremely sensitive to emotions, so she keenly noticed how cold the other party’s response was. Even though she didn’t consider herself a true member of the Chang clan, the care and concern they had showered her with over the days had left her with some feelings for them. It hurt her to see something so tragic happening to them.","However, the Chang clan had also warmly welcomed the Fiend races’ Saintess. The latter’s attitude was overly cold in comparison.","“What were you doing outside?” Zu An asked.","“Was I to cheer you on while the two of you were having fun consummating your marriage?” Yumen Beiqing coldly retorted.","The Mermaid Queen felt awkward. Zu An was also rendered speechless. Little sister Ling’er feels different from before.","While silence loomed among the trio, powerful auras suddenly surged from afar. Several towering figures rushed across the ground outside, heading in their direction.","A deafening voice rumbled, “Why don’t we compete in terms of leg strength?”","“Sure!”","The two tallest figures suddenly accelerated. Despite only taking a few strides, they instantly arrived at the town’s entrance.","The man carrying a giant axe and shield was slightly slower, and he muttered in frustration, “Kuafu, your speed is truly incredible.”","The other man held a green snake in his right hand and a yellow snake in his left. He burst into laughter. “Xingtian, that’s only because your axe and shield weigh you down. That gave me an advantage.”","The man named Xingtian brandished his axe and shield, causing a powerful wind to blow. “A loss is a loss. There’s no need for so many excuses! These weapons have long become a part of me; they can’t possibly slow me down!”","Zu An was stunned. Both Xingtian and Kuafu were renowned mythological figures in his previous life. Could these truly be them?","It was then that the two men noticed Zu An’s group. They were initially mesmerized by the Mermaid Queen and Yumen Beiqing’s beauty, but they quickly recovered and asked, “This is the Chang manor, right? Where’s your chieftain? Call him out to meet us.”","Zu An frowned. “I’m afraid he can’t meet you now. He...”","Before he could finish his sentence, the two men frowned.","“I smell an overwhelming stench of death.”","“There’s no one alive in there.”","The two of them widened their strides and instantly arrived at the square. They gasped upon seeing the corpses lying all around. They exchanged looks before returning to Zu An and the others. With hostile eyes, they asked, “Were you the ones who massacred the Chang clan?”"]},{"number":2594,"title":"Chapter 2594: Chapter 2546: Suspect","paragraphs":["“Of course not!” Zu An was rendered speechless. “We're also investigating their abrupt deaths.”","“Abrupt deaths?” The man holding snakes frowned. “What do you mean?”","“They were still fine moments ago, but all of a sudden, all of them died,” Zu An explained.","“The Chang clan is filled with experts. Who has the strength to discreetly kill all of them at the same time?” the other man wielding a shield and an axe pointed out in a deep voice. He eyed the three of them and asked, “Who are you? What are you doing here?”","The Mermaid Queen knew it would be hard to clarify their true identities, so she said, “I am the Chang clan’s Saintess Chang’e. Today was the day I would marry my fiancé, so the Chang clan was more bustling than usual. But moments after we entered our consummation room, we sensed something amiss and rushed out to investigate, only to find that my clansmen had lost their lives.”","“Saintess Chang’e?” the man holding two snakes murmured contemplatively. “I have heard about you. Your fiancé is the Youqiong clan’s Yi...” He turned to Zu An and asked, “You are Yi?”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He knows about Chang’e and Yi’s engagement. This will be tricky.","It would be tough to explain the underlying reasons, so he said, “The old chieftain has indeed officiated my marriage with Chang’e.”","The man wielding an axe and a shield scoffed, “That’s impossible. I have heard of Yi. He’s a rising star in the Shaman races, but you don’t have the slightest shaman blood in you.”","The Mermaid Queen anxiously clarified, “He’s indeed the Yi acknowledged by the old chieftain and the entire Chang clan. The reasons are complicated...”","The man holding the two snakes interjected, “Given how lovey-dovey you are, you two are obviously together. Speak! Did you plan to impersonate Yi to marry the Saintess, only for the Chang clan to find out about your ploy and for you to massacre them out of anger?”","By now, their other companions had also arrived at the town. They were nowhere as muscular as Kuafu and Xingtian, but their massive statures made it clear that they were from the Shaman races. They surrounded Zu An and the others and focused their auras on them.","Zu An sneered, “The first thing you did upon arriving here is to accuse me without evidence. Now that I think about it, you suddenly appeared here while we were investigating the Chang clan’s massacre. That makes you people suspicious too!”","The snake-holding Kuafu harrumphed. “The Chang clan’s chieftain invited us to witness the newlyweds’ marriage ceremony, but we faced some issues on our way here and were delayed by several days. That’s why we only arrived now.”","The axe and shield-wielding Xingtian nodded.","Zu An asked, “Where’s your evidence?”","The two giants were at a loss for words. Kuafu raged, “What evidence can I offer for that?!”","You have successfully trolled Kuafu for +114... +114... +114...","Zu An nodded. I didn’t hear wrong. This is Kuafu, and the other one is Xingtian. Knowing that they were dealing with two mythological powerhouses, he felt troubled.","Xingtian said, “We’re on close terms with the Chang clan’s chieftain; why would we bother leaving any evidence? Besides, the chieftain relayed the message to us using his skill... Hold on! We're the ones asking questions here, so why are you questioning us now?”","Sensing the hostile gazes from all around, Zu An asked, “Can you ask your companions to back down first? There’s something confidential I need to discuss with you.”","Xingtian and Kuafu exchanged looks before gesturing for their companions to step away. Then, they turned to Zu An and said, “Hurry up and say your piece. I advise you not to try anything. Even if it’s just us, you won’t be able to escape.” As powerhouses of the Shaman races, they weren’t worried about anything going awry.","Zu An spent a moment in thought. Since the Chang clan’s chieftain invited them, they're likely friends with the Chang clan. As powerful as they are, given their huge physiques, I doubt they could massacre the Chang clan without me noticing.","So, Zu An told them about the Chang clan’s chieftain’s plan to have him impersonate Yi and marry Chang’e to prevent the ancient prophecy from being made impossible. He spoke with a controlled cadence with clear logic, so it didn’t take long before the duo understood what he was saying.","“What? The real Yi is dead?”","“The Chang clan has such a prophecy?”","Kuafu and Xingtian were astounded.","“Who killed Yi?” Xingtian asked.","Zu An shook his head. “I wanted to ask the old chieftain, but he insisted on only telling me after the ceremony. I didn’t expect such a mishap to happen in the meantime.” He had a guess, but he had no evidence, so he didn’t dare to run his mouth.","“You’re saying that the culprit might have killed them to silence them?” Kuafu stroked his lower jaw, allowing the snake he was holding to coil intimately around his neck.","Looking at that, the Mermaid Queen had goosebumps.","“That could be possible.” Zu An reserved his skepticism about that, as he hadn’t sensed the same unique energy present where Yi was killed.","“Why did the culprit spare you?” Kuafu’s suspicion still wasn’t dispelled.","“I don’t know.” Zu An frowned. “At this rate, if we continue dawdling here, the true culprit might escape.”","“You don’t have to worry about that.” Xingtian harrumphed. “I scanned the vicinity, and there are no living beings in the area except for us.”","“So, you still suspect that we’re the culprits?” The Mermaid Queen frowned.","“The two of you were in the consummation room. What about her? Where was she?” Kuafu pointed to the quiet Yumen Beiqing.","Yumen Beiqing eyed him coldly, not bothering to answer the question.","The Mermaid Queen anxiously spoke up. “She was with us!”","“With you?” Kuafu and Xingtian were stunned. Their gazes went back and forth among the three of them. He brought another woman into the consummation room? Both the bride and this woman are ravishing beauties, and yet they agreed to such an arrangement?","They looked at Zu An in awe.","Yumen Beiqing harrumphed. “Drop those filthy thoughts! I was strolling outside the town!”","“Strolling? Alone?” Kuafu and Xingtian’s expression turned vigilant once more.","“Of course I was alone!” Yumen Beiqing stood upright as if she wasn't afraid of causing any misunderstandings.","Kuafu and Xingtian exchanged looks. Looking at each other, they verified their conjecture. This woman isn’t as simple as she looks. She has a power that makes us uncomfortable.","“You are the biggest suspect! Come with us!”","The green snake on Kuafu’s right hand shot toward Yumen Beiqing and coiled around her body."]},{"number":2595,"title":"Chapter 2595: Chapter 2547: Meeting Houtu Once More","paragraphs":["Zu An’s eyebrows twitched, but he didn’t move right away, as if he was awaiting something.","Yumen Beiqing looked as if she was stunned. Before she could react, the green snake wrapped itself around her and dragged her toward Kuafu.","Zu An couldn’t wait anymore. He dashed over and slashed his blade down on the green snake.","The green snake winced in pain as it anxiously released Yumen Beiqing. Zu An pulled her into his embrace as he punched the other yellow snake, which had darted in to attack. Then, he took advantage of the opening to bring Yumen Beiqing back to the Mermaid Queen’s side.","“Are you fine?” Zu An quickly inspected her body.","Yumen Beiqing shook her head. Her icy eyes looked conflicted.","“How dare you hurt my beloved snakes!” Kuafu roared.","He took out a staff to strike Zu An. A brilliant light and the sound of crashing waves emanated from the staff as it was swung with terrifying might that could crush a small mountain.","Zu An was about to fight back when he suddenly remembered the mysterious Seven-Colored Divine Halo. He released a seven-colored light ahead of him, and the charging Kuafu vanished into thin air.","Everyone present was stunned. Kuafu should have had the upper hand there, so why did he suddenly disappear?","Some of Kuafu’s brethren brandished their weapons to attack Zu An, hoping to rescue Kuafu. However, they also vanished in a flash of seven-colored light.","“What sorcery did you use?!” Xingtian didn’t dare to let his guard down. He placed his shield in front of him while preparing his axe; he was ready to launch a fatal blow at any moment.","His shield was imbued with tremendous defensive prowess. It could withstand most spells, forcing his enemy to engage him in close-quarters combat, which happened to be the strength of the Shaman races.","It was a pity that such an ability was useless. With a flash of a seven-colored light, he also vanished.","Seeing the previously bustling surroundings suddenly become empty bewildered the Mermaid Queen and Yumen Beiqing.","“Hubb... Big brother Zu, where did they go?” The Mermaid Queen didn’t think it was appropriate to call Zu An 'hubby' in Yumen Beiqing’s presence.","Yumen Beiqing reacted faster. “Is that the ability of your Seven-Colored Divine Halo?”","Zu An nodded. He sensed that Kuafu and the others had been put inside a peculiar seven-colored space. The weaker shamans had fainted on the spot, and only the strongest Kuafu and Xingtian were still holding on.","Kuafu’s two snakes grew until they were over a thousand meters long, and as they attempted to break free from the peculiar seven-colored space, they rampaged like massive dragons. Even so, no matter where they went, the two snakes couldn’t find a way out.","Xingtian roared as his body became incomparably huge. He furiously chopped at the seven-colored space like the great Pangu who had severed heaven from earth. Terrifying force rippled through the space, causing it to shake.","Zu An thought, The Seven-Colored Divine Halo is similar to Kong Xuan’s five-colored divine halo in Investiture of the Gods. I can stow anything I want inside it, but there’s a limit. If the enemy is too strong, it might be possible for them to break free.","Even though Xingtian was causing a huge commotion, most of the force he used was absorbed by the special laws of the seven-colored space to reinforce it. In other words, he couldn't break free.","But Zu An didn’t dare to assume the results would be the same against an enemy far stronger than Xingtian.","In Investiture of the Gods, Kong Xuan had dragged one of the strongest characters in the series, Zhunti of the Two Western Saints, into his five-colored divine halo; but Zhunti was able to break free from inside.","I wonder if my Seven-Colored Divine Halo is any stronger than his five-colored divine halo...","Zu An sensed that Xingtian and Kuafu were getting desperate inside the seven-colored world, and were preparing to use secret arts that demanded a hefty price to activate. He didn’t want to become the Shaman races’ mortal enemy in the first place, so this battle had no meaning.","The seven-colored light flashed once more, and the shamans appeared again. The weaker shamans collapsed onto the ground, while Kuafu landed on his butt. Only Xingtian maintained a firm footing, looking fierce like a war god.","“I could have taken your lives, but it’s not my wish to become your enemy. All I wish to say is that I’m not the culprit behind the Chang clan’s massacre. Someone else is behind it,” Zu An said, although he was bluffing to an extent. It was easy for him to control them, but it wouldn’t be as easy for him to kill them.","Even so, Xingtian and Kuafu were intimidated. They thought that Zu An truly had the power to kill them, but he'd chosen to patiently talk things out. There had to be a misunderstanding here.","Xingtian undid his transformation and apologized. “Forgive us for our earlier offense.”","Kuafu apologized as well.","Yumen Beiqing scoffed. These shamans oppress the weak, but fear the strong.","“I don’t know what tricks the culprit used to massacre the Chang clan within such a short time, and I don’t know why they spared us either.” Zu An fell into deep thought. Xingtian and Kuafu’s doubts made perfect sense; he couldn’t make sense of the situation either.","Xingtian chimed in. “Someone capable of such a feat can’t be nameless.”","“Do you have any suspects?”","“Not at the moment, but we can consult the Ancestral Shamans,” Xingtian replied.","Zu An was overjoyed. “You’re able to contact the Ancestral Shamans? May I know which one?”","Some said there were ten Ancestral Shamans, whereas others said there were twelve. Regardless, there had to be quite a few of them around. But those were legendary figures. Zu An didn’t think that Xingtian could contact them directly.","“Lady Houtu!” Xingtian replied with a look of reverence.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Houtu again! What role does she play in this matter?","Xingtian made an incision on his finger, and fresh blood oozed out. He flicked the blood droplets toward the sky and quickly drew a series of mysterious runes. Each finger stroke he made contained a peculiar, arcane power.","The blood-colored runes slowly diffused to form a thin portrait. A woman's impassive voice echoed from it. “Who calls me...”","Everyone present suddenly felt insignificant, as if a lofty god was judging them.","Xingtian and Kuafu quickly kneeled and bowed. “Junior Xingtian (Kuafu) pays respect to Lady Houtu!”","Zu An tried to widen his eyes to take a better look at Houtu’s appearance, but the only thing he could see in the portrait was a blurry figure. He could vaguely tell that the other party was a woman, but he was unable to make out her facial features. Even though the latter was just an avatar, he felt tremendous pressure. She seems stronger than the Houtu I met in the future.","“What’s wrong?” The woman’s voice remained placid.","Xingtian hurriedly explained the situation.","“Oh?” Houtu’s avatar turned her eyes toward Zu An. “The Chang clan’s chieftain told you to become Yi?”","Xingtian and Kuafu were perplexed. They were here to request information about the culprit, but why was Lady Houtu more interested in this matter?","Zu An instinctively nodded. He was about to probe further into it when an aura flew out from the portrait and fell on him, infusing a wild power into his bloodline. This aura wasn't foreign to him. It was that of the Shaman races.","“From now on, he’s Yi. You can testify on his behalf,” Houtu’s voice echoed.","Xingtian and Kuafu trembled. They could feel the purest shaman bloodline coming from Zu An. Other shamans wouldn’t be able to tell that anything was wrong with him. They had no idea why Lady Houtu was doing this, but they didn’t dare to defy her orders.","Zu An was dumbstruck. Yumen Beiqing’s hair fell over her lowered head, making it impossible to make out her expression."]},{"number":2596,"title":"Chapter 2596: Chapter 2548: Heavenly Punishment","paragraphs":["Zu An had only promised the old chieftain he'd impersonate Yi to learn about Yi’s murderer. But not only had he failed to uncover the identity of the murderer, the Chang clan had even been massacred. He hadn't thought there was a need for him to continue this act.","Little had he expected Lady Houtu to call the shots and decide that he would continue being Yi. She'd even bestowed him with a droplet of shaman blood essence so his act would be more convincing. That blood essence was none other than the aura he'd felt, and he could feel the tremendous power contained within it as it fused with his body. Fully assimilating it could bring his prowess up another level.","Judging from Xingtian and Kuafu’s envious looks, he could tell how valuable the blood essence was, but he still had doubts about this development. He looked at the blurry figure in the sky and asked, “Lady Houtu, why do you want me to impersonate Yi?”","Houtu’s ethereal voice rang out, “It is fate’s arrangement. You’ll know in the future.”","Zu An was mystified. Riddle after riddle.","He wanted to ask more, but Xingtian interjected, “Milady, do you know the culprit behind the Chang clan’s massacre?”","“Too much is involved in this matter. It is beyond your jurisdiction.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. What's involved here for her to answer in such a manner?","“As for Bao Jiang’s murder, inform the Goddess of Wu Mountain of the matter. It is most apt for someone of her lofty standing to deal with it,” Houtu said before the portrait in the sky faded.","“Yes!” Despite Houtu’s disappearance, Xingtian and Kuafu didn’t drop their etiquette. Their respect for Houtu came from the bottom of their hearts.","Then, they bowed to Zu An and asked, “Will you accompany us to Wu Mountain to explain things to the Goddess of Wu Mountain? You are, after all, a witness to Bao Jiang’s murder.”","Zu An had been planning to make a trip back to Wu Mountain anyway, so he accepted the offer.","Xingtian and Kuafu were overjoyed. They slit their fingers to draw runes resembling ancient characters with their blood. Soon, the surrounding spatial ki began to congregate into a unique formation.","Xingtian explained, “This is our Shaman races’ secret art. We can use our bloodline to perform long-distance teleportations to locations where we have established teleportation coordinates. Now that you have shaman blood running through your veins, you should be able to use this secret art too.”","Zu An made sure to remember those ancient characters. All of a sudden, he asked, “Can this secret art teleport those without shaman blood too?”","“This...” Xingtian and Kuafu glanced at Yumen Beiqing. “We can definitely bring Chang’e along, but this lady...”","The future Houtu was likely the one who had transmigrated the Mermaid Queen into this world. Houtu would have granted her the shaman bloodline while she was at it, or else the Mermaid Queen would have been exposed as a fake right away.","Yumen Beiqing suddenly spoke up. “You can go on ahead. I won’t be following you.”","Her mind was in chaos. This was an opportunity for her to separate from Zu An to do what she wanted. Zu An and the Mermaid Queen’s marriage was the perfect excuse for her to do so.","And yet, Zu An grabbed her hand and said, “How can I leave you behind?”","Yumen Beiqing didn’t protest, knowing she could give herself away if she said too much. She figured that Zu An would have to give up, since they wouldn’t slow their journey to Wu Mountain because of her.","But Zu An turned to Xingtian and asked, “What are the teleportation coordinates of Wu Mountain?”","Even though he had been to Wu Mountain, each world had its own unique considerations when determining the coordinates. Without a deep understanding of the world, it was easy for one to get such a thing wrong.","Stunned, Xingtian reflexively told Zu An the coordinates. He didn’t know what Zu An was going to do with them since there was no way he could bring that woman along using their Shaman races’ secret art.","Zu An closed his eyes and began overloading his mind with calculations. Being well-versed in spatial transformations, he had a bold idea in mind. He said, “Give me a moment. I’ll try it out first.”","He morphed into a seven-colored light, forming a massive rainbow across the sky.","Yumen Beiqing was shocked. The last time he employed this skill, Zu An’s mastery of Rainbow Morph had been severely lacking, so how had he improved so quickly? She could sense that the rainbow stretched to a very faraway place, so much so that she had no idea where the endpoint was.","Thinking about Zu An’s earlier question, she couldn’t help but wonder. Could it be...","The rainbow flickered out of existence, and Zu An reappeared before the crowd. “There was a small discrepancy earlier, but there should be no problem now.”","He grabbed Yumen Beiqing and the Mermaid Queen’s hands and dashed away as a rainbow. Before he disappeared, a distant voice echoed, “I’ll see you at Wu Mountain!”","Xingtian and Kuafu exchanged confused looks, but they decided to go through with it. They tapped their fingers on the floating blood character, causing the surrounding space to ripple. One after another, they and their shaman companions vanished into thin air.","When they reappeared, they were at Wu Mountain. But much to their shock, Zu An’s group was already waiting for them with smiles.","“How did you do it?” Kuafu was certain that Zu An had utilized the energy of the Shaman races’ secret art, but how could that secret art work on a non-shaman?","Zu An chuckled. He had used his shaman blood as the foundation and roughly deciphered those ancient characters using his understanding of spatial transformations. He'd combined those with his recently-learned Rainbow Morph and experimented several times.","It had worked out perfectly. This was much better than arduously constructing teleportation formations between two locations, since the enemy wouldn’t give one the chance to construct teleportation formations beforehand. He could now freely use his Rainbow Morph to travel anywhere he had the teleportation coordinates for. He no longer had to worry about his enemies catching up to him.","That being said, it was easier said than done. Many key factors had to be in place. Had he not acquired all these abilities by coincidence, Zu An wouldn’t have been able to pull this feat off either.","Just then, those who were gathered heard the sound of jade pendants clanging. A majestic mountain peak in the distance transformed into a beautiful figure, who gracefully descended next to the group.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at Zu An and asked, “You’re looking for me?”","Somehow, she felt something inexplicable toward this man who had embraced her in their first meeting, but she couldn’t put her finger on it.","Zu An had to suppress his urge to rush forward to embrace the woman who looked identical to Pei Mianman. “Bao Jiang has been murdered...” He roughly explained the situation to her.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. “Gu dared to kill Bao Jiang!?”","Bao Jiang was one of her few friends. This terrible news introduced a tinge of rage to her usually composed state of mind. She took a deep breath and asked, “Do you have evidence?”","This was a huge matter. She couldn’t just take Zu An’s word for it.","Zu An spent a moment in thought before taking out the Brilliant Pinflower and the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine’s seed. “Before his death, Bao Jiang handed these two things to me.”","Upon seeing the two items, the others widened their eyes, especially after seeing the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine’s seed.","With a wave of her sleeves, the Goddess of Wu Mountain cast a spell on the two items. Soon, a portrait appeared in midair. It was the sight of Bao Jiang right before his death.","Only now did Zu An believe that the other party wasn’t Pei Mianman. The power to trace an object’s origin was indeed a formidable ability.","By the time the Goddess of Wu Mountain was done watching the projections, her beautiful face was clouded with frost. She waved her hand, and the projected images swirled into the air as if they had become tangible. A cloud drifted over and carried the projected images into the sky.","Zu An stared at the sky. Is the Celestial Court in the sky? But why didn’t I see it while I was flying through the sky earlier? Ah, come to think of it, there was a faint spatial pulsation right before the images vanished. Could it be concealed by a special formation?","Soon, the sky lit up with a five-colored auspicious light. A beam of light descended upon a distant mountain. An authoritative voice boomed across the lands. “Gu coveted an immortal medicine and killed Celestial Bao Jiang! His crime warrants death!”"]},{"number":2597,"title":"Chapter 2597: Chapter 2549: Conflict","paragraphs":["The voice contained inexplicable authority. All living beings in this world heard it and felt an overwhelming urge to kneel and kowtow.","The weaker shamans had already caved in and fallen to their knees. Meanwhile, Kuafu was barely holding on, but his creaking bones and trembling muscles showed that he was barely stopping himself.","As for Xingtian, he stared at the sky with an air of valiance. This hinted that he was significantly stronger than Kuafu.","Zu An initially felt compelled to kneel too, but his Seven-Colored Divine Halo suddenly shone, and the pressure he felt lightened. He quickly pulled the collapsing Mermaid Queen behind him. He was taken aback to see Yumen Beiqing standing calmly, but he still reached out to protect her with his divine halo.","As for the Goddess of Wu Mountain, she stood completely unfazed by the pressure.","There was no need for introductions; it was obvious to Zu An that the person who had just spoken was the legendary Celestial Emperor, though the other party’s aura felt weirdly familiar. It feels like the person who bestowed me with the Sun Slaying Bow the last time I was here.","“That is?” Zu An glanced at the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain approached him with a surprised look. She appeared to be curious about his Seven-Colored Divine Halo. “That is Zhong Mountain, where Gu lives.”","Xingtian remarked with a frown, “Zhong Mountain is Ancestral Shaman Zhulong’s territory, and Gu is Zhulong’s son. Isn’t the Celestial Emperor going overboard here?”","Many believed Zhulong to be the strongest Ancestral Shaman. He had many legends surrounding him, such as daybreak being the moment he opened his eyes, and nightfall being the moment he closed them...","Unsurprisingly, a terrifying aura suddenly flared from Zhong Mountain, as if a formidable being had been jolted awake. Unlike the Celestial Emperor’s authoritative and dignified aura, this aura was wild and terrifying. In comparison to the Celestial Emperor's, however, the latter didn’t pale at all.","Cheers came from the nearby mountains. They were likely shamans, standing in a united front against the Celestial Court.","“Zhuanxu, you have overstepped your boundary,” a deep voice boomed, shaking the earth.","The incumbent Celestial Emperor is indeed Zhuanxu. It was Zhuanxu who gave me the Sun Slaying Bow back then, Zu An thought.","He couldn’t resist the urge to look beneath his feet with a shaky gaze. It was rumored that Zhulong was an indescribably massive snake, and thanks to ‘One Drop of Heaven’s Essence’[1] Zu An was extremely sensitive to mountainous leylines.","Zu An had felt the entire mountain range slowly moving earlier. Could the entire Spirit Mountain be Zhulong? How humongous must he be then?","A ray of golden light pierced through the clouds and scattered over the mortal world. A massive golden figure appeared in midair, emanating an air of authority, divinity, and power...","Countless adjectives flashed through Zu An’s mind, but nothing felt apt here. He could clearly see the golden figure’s appearance, but as soon as he turned away, he forgot about the other party’s physical details. All he could remember was the other party’s overwhelming air of authority and divinity.","This was the Celestial Emperor’s aura!","Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu said impassively, “Gu, as a celestial, violated the celestial rules by killing Bao Jiang to steal an immortal medicine. Such a crime cannot be condoned!”","A series of images showing Gu murdering Bao Jiang appeared in midair.","Zu An was stunned. These projected images were more detailed than what the projection conjured by the Goddess of Wu Mountain had revealed. Does the Celestial Emperor have the ability to see everything that happens in this world?","A commotion broke out across the mountain range. The crowd had only spoken out in support of Zhulong because they didn’t know about Gu’s deeds.","Bao Jiang had a good reputation on Spirit Mountain for his amicable and kind-hearted personality. He had never turned down anyone who requested medicine or treatment from him, so many people were fond of him. Those who had previously received Bao Jiang’s help criticized Gu for his cruelty.","Those images stunned Zhulong, and he fell into a prolonged silence.","Just then, a green-robed woman on Zhong Mountain said, “My son must have fallen for Qin’s deception out of folly. Celestial Emperor, I implore you to spare my immature son!”","Even though her face was concealed by her unkempt hair, her physique suggested that her appearance could be unflattering. Her very presence caused the surrounding trees to wither and the ground to crack.","Zu An could feel a powerful heat wave even from a distance away.","The last time he was here, the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans had told him that Zhulong’s wife was the Yellow Emperor’s daughter. She'd lost her divine powers while aiding her father in his fight against Chiyou, resulting in her inability to return to the Celestial Court. Forced to stay in the mortal world, she'd turned into a Ba that was shunned and feared by everyone. Lands would be scorched wherever she appeared.","That should be her.","The Celestial Emperor fell silent, but he eventually shook his head and declared, “Such a grievous sin cannot be overlooked. If Gu isn’t killed, the celestial laws will be undermined!”","He slowly raised his finger. A ray of golden light fell on Zhong Mountain, and it dragged Gu, who was hiding in one of the caverns, out.","Gu panicked. He struggled with all his might, but he couldn’t break free of the golden light. He screamed, “Mother, save me!”","The green-robed woman panicked. She flew over to save her son, only for the golden light to ricochet her away. Knowing she was no match for the Celestial Emperor, she shouted, “Zhulong, hurry up and save your son!”","Zhulong didn’t answer. Zhong Mountain was silent.","Before the green-robed woman could say anything, Gu cried out miserably. He was pinned against Zhong Mountain’s eastern cliff, his life force severed for good. His bloodshot eyes were filled with disbelief.","Zu An was intrigued. The Celestial Emperor sure is domineering, to kill Zhulong’s son on his turf.","The Celestial Emperor continued his declaration, “Celestial Er Fu has murdered Yayu. Considering that he was incited by Gu and Wei Yueyan, I’ll spare him from death and instead imprison him at Shushu Mountain's cliff for three thousand years.”","A woman screamed. Wei Yueyan, who had been hiding in Er Fu’s palace, was vanquished by a divine light falling from the sky, not even leaving a corpse behind. Another ray of divine light transported Er Fu to the distant Shushu Mountain.","“What airs from the Celestial Emperor! Have you forgotten the agreement for the Fiend races to manage heaven while we, the Shaman races, manage earth? Why are you kicking up a fuss on our turf now?” a cold voice echoed.","Dozens of massive water dragons surged over from the distance. The deluge of water caused the golden light in the sky to dim a little.","“It’s Ancestral Shaman Gonggong! Gonggong is here!” The shamans cheered.","What happened earlier had felt like a slap to the Shaman races’ face. Many of the hardliners among the Shaman races were dissatisfied with Zhulong’s concession to the Celestial Emperor. Now that Gonggong was here, they felt as if they'd finally found their backing.","1. This is a book written in the Song dynasty about predicting the future using one’s Eight Birth Characters. ☜"]},{"number":2598,"title":"Chapter 2598: Chapter 2550: Slave","paragraphs":["Zu An raised his eyebrows upon hearing the name ‘Gonggong’. He had met Gonggong the last time he was here, and the other party’s major boss vibe had left him with a deep impression.","A figure with a human face and a snake body stood above a whirlpool, his red hair fluttering with the wind; he had an open and carefree air.","Zu An frowned. This wasn't the Gonggong he had met the last time. He belatedly recalled Gonggong’s subordinate, Xiang Liu, telling him that Gonggong was a position, so there had been many Gonggongs over the generations.","Given how the shamans addressed the current Gonggong as an Ancestral Shaman, could he be the very first Gonggong?","But what’s with the Shaman races? Why do so many of them have human faces and snake bodies?","With Gonggong taking the lead, more figures emerged from the mountains, each of them emanating powerful auras. They were powerhouses of the Shaman races. They hadn’t dared to step forward and backed down because they were intimidated by the Celestial Emperor’s aura, but with Gonggong taking the lead, they decided to join him.","They weren’t close with Bao Jiang, and they didn’t care about the details of this matter either. What they were concerned about was the Shaman races’ reputation. They felt that the Celestial Emperor had gone overboard by intruding on Ancestral Shaman Zhulong’s territory and publicly sentencing his son to death. Zhulong, for some reason, had chosen to tolerate it, but that didn’t mean that the others would take it lying down!","Over the years, there had been too many conflicts between the Celestial Court’s Fiend races and the Shaman races to determine who had done what wrong first. The accumulated grudges had grown so great that both sides viewed each other as an eyesore.","The Celestial Emperor coldly glanced at Gonggong. “Gonggong, what do you want?”","As he rode on a huge wave, Gonggong’s red hair fluttered. His aura was no weaker than the Celestial Emperor’s golden avatar. “Gu is a shaman. Even if he deserves to be punished, you should have let us deal with him internally. You’re undermining our agreement by executing him publicly.”","“Since Gu took on a position in the Celestial Court, he was obligated to follow celestial laws. It is within the scope of our agreement to punish him,” the Celestial Emperor calmly pointed out.","A shaman powerhouse exclaimed, “Hah! I was wondering why the Celestial Court was conferring us with titles. Turns out it was a trap all along! Since that’s the case, there’s no reason for us to continue holding onto those positions!”","Many shaman powerhouses voiced their agreement. “Indeed! So many of our people fought with each other to get positions in the Celestial Court. Little did they know that they were just shackling themselves.”","“I don’t need a post if it means that the Celestial Court can arbitrarily sentence me to death!”","...","Those words riled up the crowd.","Zu An was surprised. The Celestial Emperor must be disturbed that so many people are outright defying him. Looks like the conflict between the Fiend races and the Shaman races is creeping toward its climax.","He turned to Xingtian and Kuafu. “You also witnessed the events. What do you make of this matter?”","Kuafu replied, “Gu deserves to be punished, but their words make sense too. The one to punish Gu should have been Lady Houtu and not the Celestial Emperor.”","Xingtian scraped his axe against his shield. “Fight, fight! My axe thirsts for blood!”","Zu An was at a loss for words. This fellow doesn’t care about the truth at all. He just wants to fight.","He turned to the Goddess of Wu Mountain. He naturally felt goodwill toward her because she resembled Pei Mianman. Ah, our Manman is so beautiful!","“Is there something on my face? Why are you looking at me?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain calmly asked, but her eyes remained fixated on the distant Zhong Mountain.","Yumen Beiqing sneered. This man is a breeding horse. His mind is filled with nothing but filth.","The Mermaid Queen frowned as well. Big brother Zu is too lustful! But she quickly remembered how he'd initially kept his distance from her despite his nature, and that made her feel that he was a gentleman instead.","Feeling the two ladies’ sharp gaze, Zu An’s face heated up. “I was wondering about the Goddess’ take on this matter.”","“What can you see?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain calmly asked.","Zu An had to concede that despite their identical appearances, their personalities were vastly different. One was passionate and seductive, whereas the other was as cold as ice. The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s personality was closer to Chu Chuyan’s instead.","Remembering Chuyan made Zu An’s heart hurt. He said solemnly, “It doesn’t look as if you care about how this matter unfolds.”","Sensing the change in his mood, the Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at him before answering, “Yes, I have nothing to do with this matter.”","She had only intervened because Bao Jiang was her friend. Now that the culprit had been punished, she couldn’t care less about what happened afterward.","Zu An was surprised. Even though the Goddess of Wu Mountain lives on Spirit Mountain, she's more aligned with the Celestial Court than the Shaman races. Is she not worried that if she maintains a nonchalant attitude, the Celestial Court might suffer a setback here?","In a cavern amid the mountain range, the Lord of Slaughter and Salamay stood respectfully behind a black-robed man. “Master is indeed wise! You were able to turn the fiends against the shamans with just a little ploy!”","It felt as if many things had happened since they arrived in this world.","One morning, they'd woken up to find Mojard missing. This came as a huge shock to them, as Mojard was no weakling, and he had rested alongside them that night. And yet, he'd disappeared without them noticing, leaving not a trace behind. The person behind it had to have been terrifyingly powerful for neither the Lord of Slaughter nor Salamay to have noticed a thing.","Salamay had wanted to search for the missing Mojard, but the Lord of Slaughter had dragged her elsewhere. They'd begun making their way toward the towering Kunlun Mountain, which could be seen from all parts of this world.","Be it Kunlun Mountain’s towering peak that pierced through the clouds, or the words of the indigenous population, the Lord of Slaughter had become convinced that Kunlun Mountain was linked to the Celestial Court. He wanted to find the Celestial Court’s secret and awaken his bloodline, so he could return to his world and exact vengeance on the Monster Lord.","Along the way, they'd encountered a mysterious man. The latter had spent a long time sizing them up, occasionally murmuring words like ‘slave’ and ‘pet’.","The Lord of Slaughter, being the hot-tempered man he was, couldn’t tolerate such an insult and decided to kill the other party to vent his anger.","Howevver, what happened next had driven him to despair. He'd been defeated before he could touch the other party. It was a completely one-sided battle.","He could still remember the other party looking down on him while saying, “I never expected to stumble upon such a rare spirit beast. I happen to be lacking underlings. Are you willing to be my mount?”","The humiliation he'd felt then permeated his entire being. To think that he, the Lord of Slaughter, was only worthy of being a mount to the other party!","Even so, he had no choice but to submit. The other party was so strong that when going up against him, the Lord of Slaughter was completely helpless. Furthermore, the other party’s words suggested that he knew about the Lord of Slaughter's bloodline origin. That sparked the Lord of Slaughter’s hopes of becoming stronger. So, he'd decided to accept the offer. Naturally, Salamay had no choice but to follow her father too.","As a result, both the father and the daughter had become the mysterious man’s mounts.","Over time, the Lord of Slaughter witnessed the mysterious man’s methods of wreaking havoc in the world. That reduced the indignation he felt, and he thought that he'd likely made the correct decision then.","“The fiends and the shamans have been fighting for a long time now. I am merely giving them a push. Besides,” the black-robed man said with a chuckle, “I’m not the only one fanning this conflict.”"]},{"number":2599,"title":"Chapter 2599: Chapter 2551: Isolation of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Others are fanning this conflict too?","The Lord of Slaughter and Salamay exchanged looks. It sounds like others are playing on this chessboard as well, and master appears to be wary of them. To think there are other beings as terrifying as master! This world is a scary place!","Salamay’s eyes darted around in contemplation. She approached the black-robed man and coyly asked, “Master, master! Who are the others hiding in the shadows?”","After saying those words, she couldn’t help but shiver. This was her first time speaking like that. She had never thought that a day would come when she would have to resort to a honey trap.","The black-robed man harrumphed as he shoved her aside. “That’s not a question you should be asking. Also, don’t even think about seducing me. Would you be interested in your pets?”","He was already being considerate by not calling them ‘livestock’.","Salamay’s face reddened in anger. She had never been humiliated in such a manner before. However, she quickly reined herself in and hid her displeasure under a beaming smile. “Yes, master is right to reprimand me. I will reflect on my mistake.”","The black-robed man turned his attention back to Zhong Mountain. Over there, more and more shaman powerhouses were abandoning their posts in the Celestial Court. The situation was spiraling out of control.","Even the Celestial Emperor couldn’t help but frown. “Calm down; it’s meaningless to act in a fit of rage. We agreed that the fiends and the shamans would govern their own jurisdictions. If you abruptly abandon your posts, the world will be plunged into chaos.”","Gonggong sneered, “The agreement was for the Fiend races to govern heaven while the Shaman races governed the earth, but you overstepped your boundary to kill our people on our turf. Since our agreement means nothing to you, there’s no reason for us to continue wearing these shackles.”","The other shamans cheered in agreement. Shamans had unbridled personalities, and the grudge between both races was simply too deep. At this point, they weren’t rioting just over Gu’s execution anymore.","A shaman powerhouse roared, “A few years back, someone proposed the isolation of heaven and earth. Why is there suddenly no further word on that? We don’t want to see you celestials descending to earth as and when you like to wreak havoc!”","“That’s right! This is the only way to resolve our conflicts!”","...","With someone taking the lead, a huge uproar broke out. It looked as if a huge battle would break out if the Celestial Emperor didn’t agree to the isolation of heaven and earth.","Zu An clicked his tongue.","There are several troublemakers among the shaman powerhouses. Each time the matter is finally about to be put to rest, someone jumps out to further muddy the waters. It feels like someone is intentionally stoking this conflict.","They're brave to dare scheme against the Celestial Emperor and the Ancestral Shamans.","While the Celestial Emperor’s avatar at Zhong Mountain was placating the shamans, his main body was at the Celestial Court, discussing this matter with the other celestials.","It was chaos in the Celestial Court. The Celestial Emperor had conjured a huge screen above the hall to project the situation at Zhong Mountain. The celestials felt indignant, as they thought that the Shaman races were going too far.","To them, Gu was at fault, and it was the Celestial Emperor’s prerogative to punish him. And yet, the Shaman races made it sound as if the Celestial Court was in the wrong. It was out of goodwill that the Celestial Court had offered the Shaman races positions, yet the Shaman races made it sound like a malicious attempt to tie them down. Some of the hardliner celestials were so infuriated that they cursed the shamans.","It didn’t take long for hawkish propagandists to claim the upper hand in the discussions.","In the first place, the conflicts between the fiends and the shamans hadn't ceased for many years now. If the Celestial Court bowed to the shamans despite having the moral high ground, they would become a joke to the whole world. No one would submit to the Celestial Court anymore!","There were also celestials who pushed for peace, but their voices were drowned out by the hawkish faction’s saliva. After so many years of conflict, which celestial didn’t have a personal vendetta against the shamans? Under such circumstances, it was difficult for the celestials to think rationally.","In truth, Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu had publicly executed Gu for more than just his vile deed. He'd intended to use this opportunity to punish the shamans and vent the suppressed emotions of the Fiend races’ hawkish faction as well. Otherwise, the situation could spiral out of control if feelings of discontentment continued seething. Despite being the Celestial Emperor, he couldn’t act as he pleased and neglect the interests of his subordinate celestials.","Zhuanxu looked at Dijun, who stood at the forefront of the other celestials. Most people recognized him as the next Celestial Emperor, so many celestials were gathered by his side. Dijun’s harsh stance against the Shaman races was welcomed by most celestials. He hadn't said a word thus far, but his aides had already spoken up on his behalf, relaying whatever he wanted to say.","No one knew what would happen if a war truly broke out.","Just then, Fire Celestial Zhongli stepped forward and said, “War is not the only way to resolve this problem. There’s another option.”","Zhuanxu’s heart sank. Zhongli was his grandson; he could already guess what the other party was going to say. However, that was too heavy of a price to pay.","“May I know what Fire Celestial’s solution is?” a celestial asked.","“The separation of heaven and earth!” Zhongli replied with a calm but firm gaze.","The noisy hall fell silent.","Dijun, who had been silent all this while, finally spoke up. “Fire Celestial, do you know the price we’d have to pay for separating heaven and earth? Is there a need to sacrifice our Fiend races’ great celestials for mere shamans? Who is willing to put their lives on the line?”","Celestials averted their eyes wherever Dijun looked. The separation of heaven and earth was simple in theory; it involved pushing up heaven and pushing down earth, thus severing the link between both places. That would allow the independent governance of heaven and earth. Once interactions between the shamans and the fiends stopped, their intense conflicts would naturally be resolved.","But that was easier said than done.","Even the great Pangu, to stop heaven and earth from converging back together after severing them apart, had to hold up the sky while stepping on the earth. He'd continued this grueling feat for countless years before finally taking his last breath. His body had turned into mountains, rivers, forests, and other such terrain. There were rumors that the towering Kunlun Mountain was a bone that Pangu had left behind.","Thanks to Pangu’s sacrifice, a new equilibrium between heaven and earth had formed. Building on Pangu’s foundation, the difficulty of completely separating heaven and earth was much lower than what Pangu had done back then, but it would still require the strongest Fiend races deities to put their lives on the line to achieve the feat.","Very few fiends could cultivate to that level, so who would be willing to sacrifice themselves to save a bunch of shaman barbarians?","“I’ll do it if no one else is willing to!” Zhongli declared.","A horrified Zhuanxu quickly stopped him. “Zhongli, you mustn’t be reckless...”","But Zhongli interjected, “Grandfather, you taught me that all cultivators must find their path. I had no idea where my path was for the longest time, but now I know it’s to prevent this world from being destroyed.”","Right after he finished speaking, his body pulsated in enlightenment. This was a sign that he had been recognized by the heavenly dao.","Dijun bowed deeply to Zhongli. “I am in awe of Zhongli’s grand wish.”","The others in the hall, regardless of factions, also bowed to Zhongli. They were also in awe of his selflessness.","Zhuanxu sighed. To a cultivator, their dao was more important than their life. He couldn’t stop Zhongli, even for the latter’s good; otherwise, Zhongli’s dao heart could unravel, causing him to descend into despair. That would make him no different from a cripple.","“It would be best if this could resolve the war between the fiends and the shamans. It would bring tremendous karma to Zhongli.” Zhuanxu tried to console himself, but he was still disheartened.","He had many offspring, but not many of them had achieved anything great. The same went for his descendants, too. Zhongli was the only one who had displayed outstanding talent. He'd intended to nurture Zhongli as the next Celestial Emperor, or the one after that, or even the one after that, but it looked as if his hope was going to be dashed.","On Zhong Mountain, another golden avatar slowly manifested and declared, “To prevent the further escalation of conflict between the shamans and the fiends, Fire Celestial Zhongli shall completely separate heaven and earth under the Celestial Emperor’s order!”","The golden avatar morphed into a giant that was as tall as the sky. With a roar, he stomped his foot on the ground and propped up the sky with his hand. The surrounding ki was immediately plunged into chaos. The earth quaked and mountains collapsed. The ground undulated nonstop, as if it had been liquefied. Everyone struggled to maintain their footing.","Zu An quickly grabbed the Mermaid Queen and Yumen Beiqing. Much to his shock, he realized that the earth was sinking downward while the sky was being propped higher and higher up.","Even powerhouses like Xingtian and Kuafu were caught off guard and fell on their butts.","In contrast, the Goddess of Wu Mountain firmly stood her ground as if there was a stake beneath her body, keeping her in position no matter how the ground moved.","Feeling the rampaging spatial ki around him, Zu An looked at the golden avatar in utter shock. Pangu severing the sky had always been a legend to him; he'd never thought he would see something similar in his lifetime.","How powerful did that golden avatar have to be to pull off such a feat?","Yumen Beiqing’s hands and feet turned ice-cold. In the end, things still ended up like this!"]},{"number":2600,"title":"Chapter 2600: Chapter 2552: Vengeance","paragraphs":["Xingtian looked at the massive golden avatar with an admiring gaze. “To think there were such valiant heroes amongthe Fiend races too!”","Kuafu nodded in agreement. \"Looks like not all fiends are despicable and shameless. There are noble souls among them too.”","Zu An could tell that the shamans and the fiends were extremely prejudiced toward each other. “I’m surprised that you acknowledge him.”","“The separation of heaven and earth is easier said than done. Back then, Pangu sacrificed his life to sever heaven from earth. What Zhongli is trying to achieve is nowhere as difficult as what Pangu did, but he is nowhere as strong as Pangu either. The only fate awaiting him is death by exhaustion,” Kuafu explained.","The Shaman races were said to be created by Pangu’s blood essence, so they naturally carried great respect for Pangu.","Upon hearing those words, Zu An looked at the golden avatar once more with a melancholic gaze. He had a greater grasp of the world now, and he could sense the golden avatar dissipating, as if fusing with the world. In due time, it would become a part of the world’s laws.","“He is a true hero!” the other shamans in the mountains remarked as well.","The Celestial Emperor remained silent. In the end, he let out a sigh and dissipated his golden avatar.","Even the previously infuriated Gonggong also looked conflicted. He clasped his fist at the massive golden avatar before leaving on a water wave.","“He’s leaving like that? He acted as if was going to pick a fight with the Celestial Emperor!” Zu An was perplexed. He'd thought that Gonggong was going to make a move, but the latter hadn't gone through with it.","“The Celestial Emperor killed Ancestral Shaman Zhulong’s son, but now the Celestial Emperor is sacrificing a grandson for this cause. The Shaman races are meticulous in settling scores. Things are even now, so there’s no reason to continue pursuing this matter,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain explained.","“Zhongli is the Celestial Emperor’s grandson?” Zu An was surprised. It was his first time hearing about this.","“Indeed. He is the Celestial Emperor’s most outstanding grandson, and there was a chance he could have become the next Celestial Emperor,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said.","Zu An took this chance to gather more information. “You mentioned earlier that the Celestial Emperor’s name was Zhuanxu, and that Zhongli is in line to become the next Celestial Emperor. What’s the deal with Dijun then?”","Yumen Beiqing’s face twitched at the mention of ‘Dijun’.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain answered his question. “Strictly speaking, he is only the appointed successor and has yet to take the throne, so we should address him as ‘Jun’ instead of ‘Dijun’.","“Jun is likely to become the next Celestial Emperor, but Zhongli is outstanding too, not to mention that he’s Zhuanxu’s grandson, whereas Jun is only Zhuanxu’s nephew. Due to that, Zhongli has many supporters too. Even if he didn’t become the next Celestial Emperor, there was a huge chance he could become the subsequent one after Jun.”","At this point, the Goddess of Wu Mountain sighed. “But now that Zhongli has sacrificed himself to separate heaven from earth, that is all for naught.”","Zu An was at a loss for words. He hadn't thought that deities engaged in nepotism too, though it was hard to think badly of Zhongli after the latter had selflessly sacrificed himself for others.","“Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu looks to be at the peak of his power. Why is he stepping down all of a sudden? Is he nearing the end of his lifespan?” Zu An was confused.","“Deities do have limited lifespans, but that’s not why the Celestial Emperor is stepping down. He has merely reached the end of his term. By letting go of secular responsibilities, he can go into seclusion and focus on achieving enlightenment.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s voice was cold, but she gave off an inexplicable charm.","“Achieving enlightenment?” Zu An was surprised by the huge burden that came with being the Celestial Emperor. “Isn’t the Celestial Emperor already the strongest person in the world?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain eyed Zu An. “I see you have become a deity too, so why don’t you know the basics? Being the Celestial Emperor can accelerate one’s accumulation of faith and hasten one’s cultivation growth, but that only works to an extent before the effectiveness starts to wane.","“On top of that, being too entrenched with the world’s karma can get someone stuck, preventing them from advancing any further. That is why the Celestial Emperors of every generation step down when they feel their time has come, purge the karma they have been afflicted with, and focus on grasping the greater dao so that they can eventually achieve Sainthood.”","“Sainthood?” Zu An recalled a phrase from a popular web novel in his previous world—’All beings beneath saints are mere ants’. I wonder if it’s the same for this world too. To verify his conjecture, he asked, “What saints are there in this world?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain rolled her eyes. “That’s not something you should concern yourself with.”","Zu An was speechless. She's scorning me, right?","He wanted to ask more when he noticed the nearby flora and fauna withering swiftly. Even the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s straight black hair had begun curling up.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. A mist enveloped her body, and her hair regained its straightness and smoothness.","A terrifying heat wave surged. Even breathing left one with a stinging sensation in the chest.","Zu An quickly protected the Mermaid Queen and Yumen Beiqing. With their current cultivation, they wouldn’t be able to withstand this heat wave.","Just then, a hoarse female voice echoed, “Yaoji, return my son’s life to me.”","A terrifying heat wave surged toward the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","Even Xingtian and Kuafu had no choice but to retreat three hundred meters away to avoid the brunt of the attack. Zu An was also worried about the two ladies, so he took them elsewhere to avoid the heat wave.","Much to his astonishment, the Goddess of Wu Mountain stood her ground, not bothering to dodge. Alarmed, he shouted, “Be careful!”","Soon, a green-robed woman slowly walked over from afar. Wherever she passed, lush grass and fresh flowers withered at a visible pace. She left giant footprints that looked to be crackling with flames on the ground.","Wu Mountain was a verdant mountain shrouded in fog, but the woman’s presence dissipated the fog and withered the forests. All beings residing on Wu Mountain felt their mouths becoming dry as sweat rained from their bodies.","Beads of sweat appeared on the usually cool Goddess of Wu Mountain’s forehead. In response, she waved her sleeves with a harrumph, and the fog reappeared around Wu Mountain.","The green-robed woman stopped not too far away from the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Somehow, it felt as if two forces were clashing against each other, especially given the stark difference in the sceneries behind the two women.","One had a backdrop of scorched earth, whereas the other had a verdant mountain.","Zu An recognized the green-robed woman to be Gu’s mother. Just earlier, she'd begged the Celestial Emperor to spare her son’s life.","Yumen Beiqing’s eyes narrowed. She came at a good time.","“Were you the one who reported this matter to the Celestial Court?” The green-robed woman’s appearance was concealed by her unkempt hair, but she was glaring at the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","“Indeed. Gu deserves punishment for what he did,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied.","“You’re courting death!” Furious, the green-robed woman swiped her pitch-black fingernails toward the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s neck. If her attack landed, the latter’s neck would be covered in bloodied holes."]}]);
